                new (
                    "00TQx0000050vOUMAY",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: FW: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-09").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FW: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine",
                        Description = "To: uuni@novonordisk.com\nCC: rifa@novonordisk.com; DAFL@novonordisk.com; eleneag@unops.org; janphilipk@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; timl@unops.org; valentynp@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine\nBody:\nDear Ulrik,\nThank you very much for your update - and apologies for my belated response. \nThere is no doubt that we would easily be able to help procure and deliver mobile health clinics. This is something we have already done with great success as part of the Ebola and COVID responses. We would suggest that these mobile clinics are tied to a hospital, so that the clinics can be utilised even during a post-war scenario. \nWe would absolutely align this effort with the Ukrainian healthcare reform. All that we do in Ukraine on behalf of donors (such as Novo Nordisk and Denmark) obviously needs to underpin and be aligned with Ukrainian wishes. \nAn approach where we procure and deliver mobile health clinics in connection to the reconstruction of a hospital / health clinics would also align well with the transition from humanitarian and emergency response to recovery and longer term development interventions. \nI am pleased to hear that you are still open to include in a possible new engagement the reconstruction / modernisation of a hospital or minor health clinics. We now have a few locations and scopes that we can consider together: We need to revalidate if Snihurivka and other primary healthcare centres that we discussed initially are still available (they have likely received funds for some of them). Bucha could be a new option where there is a need to modernise a mental health facility plus construct a multi-disciplinary hospital. Procurement of lacking radioactive components to fully enable the Mykolaiv Cancerclinic treatment is also an option that we could discuss depending on your budget level. \nFinally I just want to flag that it would be very likely that mobile clinics would be in a situation of offering health services to wounded soldiers with \"dual use\" implications that you should be aware of - as these units may contribute to soldiers returning to the battlefield and the overall combat readiness. This is something we can mitigate on paper - and discuss further. \nI have looped in my colleagues from Ukraine to ensure transparency and ease communication. We would be very happy to meet as soon as possible at your convenience to discuss how to take this forward. \nCould you let me know when you are available for an online meeting? \nThank you in advance. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 18 Dec 2023 at 13:59, UUNI (Ulrik Uldall Nielsen) <uuni@novonordisk.com> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n \nI very quick update from our side in relation to Novo Nordisk support to reconstruction of health infrastructure in Ukraine.\n\n \nI had meeting last week with MoFA and the Danish Embassy in Ukraine. The main item of the meeting was a discussion around the different options which we have been looking at in terms of support\n to the reconstruction of a hospital versus primary healthcare centres. In that connection there was according to MoFA also another possible option which could be to create mobile clinics serving as primary care facilities. The mobile clinics cost 50’000-100’000\n a piece depending on which equipment you put inside and gives a flexibility in providing services as close as possible to the frontline even when it is moving.\n\n Is this something that you would also consider as an option in UNOPS that can be pursued? If so, it would still need to be integrated into the Ukrainian health services. But it could potentially\n also be integrated to our support to a hospital where patients are referred to from the mobile services. If the mobile clinics is a possible solution, it would be interesting to investigate whether we would be able to give support to both a hospital and mobile\n health service as an integrated part of our support. \n \nAnother theme which is recurring in the conversations is the Ukrainian healthcare reform. The reconstruction of healthcare facilities should of course in any case be part of the healthcare reform\n which I realise is more long term but nevertheless important to ensure sustainability of our support.\n\n \nIt would be great to have your feedback on above and happy to set up a meeting in first week of January to further discuss the possible options.\n\n \nKind regards\nUlrik\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUlrik Uldall Nielsen\n\n\nHealth Equity Lead\nGlobal Public Affairs and Sustainability\n\n+4530754738 (direct) ǀ \nUUNI@novonordisk.com \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 13. november 2023 11:05\n\nTo: UUNI (Ulrik Uldall Nielsen) <uuni@novonordisk.com>; DAFL (Daniel Flentø) <DAFL@novonordisk.com>\n\nCc: RIFA (Rikke Fabienke) <rifa@novonordisk.com>; Jan Philip KLEVER <janphilipk@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine\n\n\n \n\nCaution: This email originated from outside of the Novo Nordisk email system. Use caution when clicking on links or\n opening attachments. \n\n \n\n\n\nDear Ulrik and colleagues,  \n\n \n\n\nThank you very much for the update and your work in taking this project forward. I fully understand the need to be aligned with your relevant stakeholders - both internally and externally. \n\n\n \n\n\nSimilarly, we have had to engage in dialogues with local Ukrainian stakeholders to assemble the list of potential engagement for you. In light of this I also hope that we will soon hear back from you with regards to the way forward on this\n project. \n\n\n \n\n\nI look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible. \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you in advance. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn  \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 26 Oct 2023 at 14:13, UUNI (Ulrik Uldall Nielsen) <uuni@novonordisk.com> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n\n \nI want to let you know that we are working on the internal lines to get a decision on what direction we should go in moving forward.\n hopefully by the end of next week we should be able to have more clarity on what we would like to o ahead with.\n\n \nAs Daniel mentioned we are also in dialogue with our affiliate in Ukraine and it is important for us to be aligned on the way forward.\n\n \nIn the meantime thank you for your patience.\n\n \nKind regards\nUlrik\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUlrik Uldall Nielsen\n\n\nAccess to Care Lead\n\nGlobal Public Affairs and Sustainability\n\n+4530754738 (direct) ǀ \nUUNI@novonordisk.com \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: DAFL (Daniel Flentø) <DAFL@novonordisk.com>\n\n\nSent: 22. oktober 2023 23:05\n\nTo: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; RIFA (Rikke Fabienke) <rifa@novonordisk.com>;\n UUNI (Ulrik Uldall Nielsen) <uuni@novonordisk.com>\n\nCc: Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>;\n Jani Matti LEIVO <janil@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>;\n Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ <teresam@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine\n\n\n \nDear Asbjørn\n \nMany apologies for the late reply from our side. We’ve been a bit floored last week by several\n issues hitting us at the same time so we’re a bit behind schedule. \n \nPlease allow us to get back to you with an ETA early next week. It’s been dragging out partially\n because of the above mentioned reason, but also because the project has had larger internal interest (and thereby also requirements on co-ordination) than we initially expected. We hope to be able to conclude as soon as possible and move ahead with you as\n we have on the previous project. \n \nBest,\n\nDaniel\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest regards\n\nDaniel Flentø\n\n\nAssociate Director\n\nGlobal Public Affairs and Patient Relations\n\n+4530795544 (direct) ǀ \ndafl@novonordisk.com \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 17. oktober 2023 10:27\n\nTo: DAFL (Daniel Flentø) <DAFL@novonordisk.com>; RIFA (Rikke Fabienke) <rifa@novonordisk.com>;\n UUNI (Ulrik Uldall Nielsen) <uuni@novonordisk.com>\n\nCc: Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>;\n Jani Matti LEIVO <janil@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>;\n Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ <teresam@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Optioner for samarbejde vedr. genopbygning af sundhedsinfrastruktur i Ukraine\n\n\n \n\n\nCaution: This email originated from outside of the Novo Nordisk email system. Use caution when clicking on links or opening attachments.\n\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Daniel, Rikke and Ulrik\n\n\n \n\n\nCould I kindly inquire about the status of your internal deliberations on the preferred way ahead? As we are internally preparing to deliver on time on the projects by allocating\n and hiring staff, we would greatly appreciate if your could let us know as soon as possible where you are in the process. \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you very much in advance. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n \n\n\nOn Sun, 17 Sept 2023 at 17:31, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nKære Daniel, Rikke og Ulrik\n\n\n \n\n\nArun har siden nedenstående fremsendte mail indhentet yderligere data vedr. de mindre sundhedsklinikker (option 2). Vi har derfor opdateret de tidligere fremsendte\n slides med gnst. antal patienter behandlet årligt på hver af klinikkerne, omfanget af skaderne, skønnede genopbygningsomkostninger, adresser og billedemateriale (se slide 5-12 i vedlagte). \n\n\n \n\n\nJeg håber de yderligere information kan hjælpe med jeres interne beslutningsproces. \n\n\n \n\n\nMvh\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 13 Sept 2023 at 17:41, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nKære Daniel, Rikke og Ulrik\n\n\n \n\n\nSom opfølgning på vores dialog tidligere i dag, vedlægger jeg her de slides vi gennemgik med henblik på jeres stillingtagen til, hvilke optioner I ønsker at arbejde\n videre med.\n\n\n \n\n\nBl.a. af hensyn til tilbagemelding til de ukrainske myndigheder og da situationen udvikler sig hurtigt på jorden, håber vi meget på jeres tilbagemelding senest mandag\n d. 18. september. \n\n\n \n\n\nDermed kan vi låse os fast på en af tilgangene, melde dette til de ukrainske myndigheder og få håndteret den kontraktuelle del med jer snarest. Dette også med henblik\n på hurtigst muligt at komme i gang med det konkrete arbejde på jorden.  \n\n\n \n\n\nSom drøftet ses grundlæggende to optioner for den videre vej frem:\n\n\n\n\nGenopbygning og evt. modernisering af Snigurivska City Hospital, Mykolaiv\nGenopbygning og evt. modernisering af en håndfuld mindre sundhedsklinikker i Mykolaiv\n\nSom drøftet på mødet er der en række fordele hhv. ulemper ved de to optioner, som jeg på bedste vis har forsøgt at opsummere nedenfor - idet jeg bemærker at der\n ikke er tale om en udtømmende liste. \n\n\n \n\n\nAd 1) Snigurivska City Hospital i Mykolaiv\n\n\n\n\nDe ukrainske myndigheder (særligt Sundhedsministeriet) foretrækker at dette hospital genopbygges. \nDer er tale om et velanerkendt hospital med relativ stor bevågenhed, herunder fordi hospitalet har været under russisk besættelse i 8 måneder. Se fx\ndenne artikel. \nGenopbygning af dette hospital vil få relativ stor positiv effekt. \nSelvom hospitalet ligger relativt tæt på frontlinjen (ca. 40 km) vurderes der ikke at være større risiko for, at dette hospital igen rammes af russiske angreb end andre hospitaler i fx Mykolaiv området. \nDer er angiveligt militært personale til stede på visse dele af hospitalet. Det vil skulle afklares - og der vil være behov for klare skriftlige garantier fra de ukrainske myndigheder om, at hospitalet ikke har nogen form for militær anvendelse\n - men fortsat alene fungerer som et civilt hospital (som naturligvis også kan behandle såret militært personel). \nDen nuværende militære tilstedeværelse øger risikoen for en længerevarende periode med forudgående papirarbejde mhp. at sikre de nødvendige garantier for at kunne gennemføre arbejdet. \nAdgang til hospitalet er besværliggjort af den relativt korte afstand til frontlinjen. \n\n \n\n\nAd 2) Genopbygning af en række mindre sundhedsklinikker i Mykolaiv\n\n\n\n\n\nBruttoliste på ca. 25 mindre sundhedsklinikker i Mykolaiv by og i landdistrikterne i regionen. Opdateres løbende. \nUd af de 25 klinikker udvælger vi sammen de klinikker som vurderes mest hensigtsmæssige at genopbygge/renovere - efter en umiddelbart besigtigelse af vores ingeniører. \nRelativ stor fleksibilitet i udmøntningen, og mulighed for løbende at vise fremskridt på jorden efterhånden som de enkelte klinikker genopbygges. \nMindre bevågenhed på de mindre klinikker - idet der dog også er stor reel efterspørgsel i fx landdistrikterne. \nMulighed for at udstyre de fleste af klinikkerne med relevant udstyr til håndtering af ikke-smitsomme sygdomme - efter dialog med de lokale ukrainske myndigheder. \n\nJeg håber det nogenlunde opsummerede vores samtale. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nVi er helt til jeres rådighed for evt. opfølgende spørgsmål, behov for afklaring eller andet. \n\n\n \n\n\nJeg ser meget frem til at høre fra jer snarest muligt. \n\n\n \n\n\nPå forhånd tak. \n\n\n \n\n\nMvh\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\nPS - kunne I hjælpe med koordinater på jeres medarbejder i Kyiv? \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 |",
