                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx0000057FSaMAM",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Denmark Infrastructure Mykolaiv - monthly update meeting Dec '23",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-11").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Denmark Infrastructure Mykolaiv - monthly update meeting Dec '23",
                        Description = "To: janphilipk@unops.org\nCC: eleneag@unops.org; TimL@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; svitlanaz@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Denmark Infrastructure Mykolaiv - monthly update meeting Dec '23\nBody:\nHi Philip, \n\nThanks a lot for this elaborated debrief. Super to hear that you guys will lead the monthly meetings - and I would super much appreciate if you could let me know how they go - like below. \nAs always - thanks for the great and close collaboration!\nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Tue, 19 Dec 2023 at 12:46, Jan Philip KLEVER <janphilipk@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Asbjorn,\nA quick update as we just come out of the (newly established) monthly update meeting with donor (Embassy: Olga, CPH: Jasmin and Torben), and stakeholders (city - Sergey Kohiniiv and Andrii, and oblast - deputy governor Mykola Marinov, and Andrii) on the project progress.\nThe government stakeholders' sense of urgency that things need to happen faster, is palpable. This position they have taken and will continue to take in every meeting, and it is a justified one, considering the context.\nOur, as justified, position on the required quality in the process (Design Review, effective procurement in a high corruption environment, etc) to achieve long-term results, is often mistaken for bureaucracy and too slow processes.\nWhilst - internally - there of course always are ways to improve process efficiency, they are instrumental to our mandate and directly contribute to sustainable outcomes.\nConcerns by the city were raised also on the costing of bomb-shelters for which we have preliminary figures following the feasibility studies, but will only have exact amounts once the respective designs are finalized. \nThe city thinks to hold comparative shelter construction information from other oblasts which are more economical and quicker to construct. We remind them that no single shelter is the same, and that cost benchmarking needs to compare same with same.\nValue for money is an underpinning principle for all our interventions, so if there are real and significant costing discrepancies between similar shelter projects, we will analyse why that would be the case. But, frankly, costing is very comparable across similar projects, we find.                 \nThe above points were again raised by a single participant, Andrii, who uses the setting, with superiors and donor in the meeting, to repeat the same points - that he is fully briefed on from the weekly project interaction with him. \nIt is clear that going forward we will be more tactical in our communication, specifically for this format meeting, and focus on marketing the progress (of which there is a lot, though not yet tangible on the ground).\nFor 2024 we will be leading the monthly update meetings and are now scheduling the next for the end of January. It is all our interest to move to construction as soon as possible, but also to note that this is a three year project for a quality reason.\nThis briefback to you, in case a conversation should come again from the UKR ambassador, who obviously is closely connected to Mykolaiv.\n@Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ @Arun NARAYANAN @Elene AGLADZE please complement as needed.\nAsbjorn, if I don't speak to you prior: Happy Holidays and happy end of year!\nBest,\nPhilip   Jan Philip Klever | Head of Programme | Ukraine Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel. (+380) 95 278 4072  | Email: janphilipk@unops.org",
