                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000005KVhmMAG",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Concept note on the reconstruction of Gaza",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-16").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Concept note on the reconstruction of Gaza",
                        Description = "To: marijab@unops.org\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Concept note on the reconstruction of Gaza\nBody:\nHi Marija, \nWould you be OK with me sharing this document + the below message with the UK - and subsequent other Northern European donors? \nThank you very much for your help! \n/Asbjørn\nDear Agnes, \nFollowing up on our recent conversation, I wanted to confirm that the office of the new Senior Coordinator (Ms. Sigrid Kaag) is currently developing a reconstruction strategy - involving all the relevant parties. There is no timeline as to when this will be finalised. Therefore I am unfortunately unable to share this with you for now. \nAs you know, following the recent approval of Security Council Resolution 2720, the UN Secretary General appointed Ms Sigrid Kaag as Senior Humanitarian and Reconstruction Coordinator for Gaza (see news flash here). The UN SG has tasked UNOPS to 1) supporting the full operationalization of the Office of Senior Humanitarian and Reconstruction Coordinator for Gaza; and 2) the establishment of the UN mechanism to facilitate, coordinate, monitor, and verify humanitarian relief consignments to Gaza.\n\nI know there is already a good contact between the FCDO and our local office in Amman that coordinates the work (Marija Bateman - marijab@unops.org). Don't hesitate to have your team on the ground reach out to her for any detailed info etc. \nFor your information I am attaching a brief overview of UNOPS' work so far in Gaza as well as our capacity to rapidly procure and deliver much needed items for the population. \nCurrently we have a strong presence on the ground to implement life saving projects. UNOPS' office in Egypt supports the management and oversight of the logistics chains required for delivery of humanitarian assistance into Gaza. Our UNOPS team in Gaza stands ready to support delivery of humanitarian assistance and early recovery responses. \nSo far during the ongoing crisis, UNOPS has been - and continues to - supply fuel for humanitarian operations. UNOPS procures the fuel from Egypt and delivers it through the Rafah Crossings, and ensures that the fuel is only distributed to the humanitarian locations.  We have established a coordinated communication with DSS to ensure the deconfliction and safety of the deployed staff on the ground.\nIn addition, UNOPS continues to support the operations of the Access Support Unit with its key role in access of humanitarian actors, evacuation of staff and rotation of humanitarian staff.\n\nFinally we are currently delivering various humanitarian supplies into Gaza including NFIs, health items and others.\n\nPlease feel free to relay this information to the relevant FCDO team as we would be happy to support the implementation of the UK's much needed help in Gaza. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 11:42, Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Asbjørn, \nLara shared this document with us in November 2023 and I have created this table based on the document. But I would not categorize this as a concept note but rather an overview. \nBest, Naimo \nOn Mon, Jan 15, 2024 at 11:26 AM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nNaimo: Do you have the link for that?\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 11:25, Marija BATEMAN <marijab@unops.org> wrote:\nYou can share with them what Lara shared earlier this year for now.Marija Bateman\nSenior Regional Advisor, Partnerships and Planning\nMarijaB@unops.org\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 1:17 PM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Marija,\nI will relay info to the FCDO HQ, which naturally are also requesting info in writing on the development strategy. Even though the UK Permanent Representative met with this \"Special Representative\", we should be able to provide info to the FCDO HQ when they ask for it as an interested donor. \nThe FCDO does not have any specific questions. But the HQ based team working on Gaza are of course interested in knowing which organisation they could use to channel aid through.To do so, they naturally ask for written information about our work there. \nDo we have anything in writing we can share with the UK about UNOPS' work in Gaza? A concept note or similar? \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 10:51, Marija BATEMAN <marijab@unops.org> wrote:\nHi AsbjornThe Senior coordinator is now leading the discussions with all the parties, including the Member States. She met with UK PR in New York so they should be fully aware. There is no timeline as of yet; and we should not be promoting it on our own to the donors, as it is very sensitive and political and requires buy in from many parties. At this time, the Office of the Senior Coordinator is fully in the lead. If any donors have please refer them to me as I am working closely with her team and can provide answers to their questions.\nAll the best,MarijaMarija Bateman\nSenior Regional Advisor, Partnerships and Planning\nMarijaB@unops.org\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 12:42 PM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nWhen will it be ready? \nThere is a huge demand for it. \nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 10:40, Marija BATEMAN <marijab@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Naomi,\nThis is not ready yet.We will share once the Senior Coordinator receives agreement from all the parties.Should FCDO have specific questions you can connect them with me.\nThanks,MarijaMarija Bateman\nSenior Regional Advisor, Partnerships and Planning\nMarijaB@unops.org\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jan 2024 at 12:37 PM Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Marija, \nA kind reminder of the concept note concerning the reconstruction of Gaza. As previously mentioned, the FCDO has expressed interest in both the concept note and our strategy for the reconstruction efforts in Gaza.\nBest regards, Naimo \nOn Thu, Jan 11, 2024 at 3:53 PM Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Marija, \nI hope you're doing well. Best wishes for 2024! I understand that you are currently working on a concept note for the reconstruction of Gaza. Could you kindly share the concept note with us, as the FCDO has requested a copy?\n\nBest regards, Naimo\n-- \n\nNaimo Hassan Hirsi | Partnerships Analyst | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 26 83 48 78  | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
