                new (
                    "00TQx000005Nya8MAC",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: UNOPS in Gaza",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-16").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: UNOPS in Gaza",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS in Gaza\nBody:\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you very much, Asbjorn – I’ll pass this on.\n \nOn another note – my colleagues in Mexico City mentioned to me today that our Ambassador there is due to meet the Mexico UNOPS team soon.\n \nAll the best,\n \nAgnes\n \n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> \n\nSent: Tuesday, January 16, 2024 4:16 PM\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS in Gaza\n\n\n \n\n\nDear Agnes, \n\n\n \n\n\nFollowing up on our recent conversation, I wanted to confirm that the office of the new Senior Coordinator (Ms. Sigrid Kaag) is currently meeting with all the relevant parties to discuss the implementation of the SCR2720(2023).\n There is no timeline as to when this will be finalised. Therefore I am unfortunately unable to share this with you for now. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs you know, following the recent approval of the above mentioned Security Council Resolution 2720, the UN Secretary General appointed Ms Sigrid Kaag as Senior Humanitarian and Reconstruction Coordinator for Gaza (see news flash here).\n The UN SG has tasked UNOPS to 1) support the full operationalization of the Office of Senior Humanitarian and Reconstruction Coordinator for Gaza; and 2) the establishment of the UN mechanism to facilitate, coordinate, monitor, and verify humanitarian relief\n consignments to Gaza.\n\n\n \n\n\nI know there is already a good contact between the FCDO and our local office in Amman that coordinates the work (Marija Bateman - marijab@unops.org). Don't hesitate to have your team\n on the ground reach out to her for any detailed info. \n\n\n \n\n\nFor your information I am attaching a brief overview of UNOPS' work so far in Gaza as well as our capacity to rapidly procure and deliver much needed items for the population. \n\n\n \n\n\nCurrently we have a strong presence on the ground to implement life saving projects. UNOPS' office in Egypt supports the management and oversight of the logistics chains required for delivery of humanitarian assistance into Gaza. Our UNOPS\n team in Gaza supports delivery of humanitarian assistance and early recovery responses. \n\n\n \n\n\nSo far during the ongoing crisis, UNOPS has been - and continues to - supply fuel for humanitarian operations. UNOPS procures the fuel from Egypt and delivers it through the Rafah Crossings, and ensures that the fuel is only distributed\n to the humanitarian locations.  We have established a coordinated communication with DSS to ensure the deconfliction and safety of the deployed staff on the ground.\n\n\n\n\nIn addition, UNOPS continues to support the operations of the Access Support Unit with its key role in access of humanitarian actors, evacuation of staff and rotation of humanitarian staff.\n\n\n\nFinally we are currently delivering various humanitarian supplies into Gaza including NFIs, health items and others.\n\n\n\nPlease feel free to relay this information to the relevant FCDO team as we would be happy to support the implementation of the UK's much needed help in Gaza. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000005Nya8MAC",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "asbjornb@unops.org", "agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk", "marijab@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org" },
