                new (
                    "00TQx000005bA5gMAE",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Fwd: Framework Arrangement update",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-22").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: Framework Arrangement update",
                        Description = "To: naimoh@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: Framework Arrangement update\nBody:\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>\nDate: Mon, 22 Jan 2024 at 09:37\nSubject: RE: Framework Arrangement update\nTo: Anne Lubell <alubell@unicef.org>, Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>, Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\nCc: Leona Barusya <lbarusya@unicef.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you Aasa and colleagues,\n \nOur legal team has reviewed the document and will continue to coordinate with your legal teams for the next steps.\nHappy to meet to further discuss, maybe when Anne is back?\nBest,\nRafael \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Anne Lubell <alubell@unicef.org> \n\nSent: Friday, January 19, 2024 2:45 PM\n\nTo: Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>; Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>; Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nCc: Leona Barusya <lbarusya@unicef.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Framework Arrangement update\n\n\n \nHi Aasa and all,\n \nNice to read you and happy 2024.\n \nThanks for following up on the FA and DDA annex – we have reviewed from a partnerships perspective but given the scope of the documents, it will need to be further consulted internally. \n\n\n\nI am out of the office for next couple weeks but would be happy to touch base and get a temperature on where we are at and share some initial thoughts if useful.\n \nBest wishes\nAnne\n \n \n\nFrom: Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, January 19, 2024 12:44 PM\n\nTo: Anne Lubell <alubell@unicef.org>; Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>; Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>;\n Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Framework Arrangement update\n\n \n\nDear colleagues, \n\n \n\n\nHappy Friday, hope you've had a good start to the new year!\n\n\n \n\n\nI wanted to reconnect on the FA and the due diligence piece in particular to hear if you have had a chance to look at it and if we should get together to discuss?\n\n\n \n\n\nI understand our legal colleagues have taken a first look, but it may take a little time still before we are ready to get back to the FCDO.\n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best, \n\n\nAsa\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Nov 28, 2023 at 10:52 AM Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear colleagues, \n\n \n\n\nPlease see attached the FA  with comments from the FCDO as well as the DDA. And below a table summarising the edits. \n\n\n \n\n\nI have asked our legal office to share with your legal colleagues and to advise on how they wish to proceed. While these documents are linked, the legal advisors have led on the FA and the partnerships teams have led on the DDA annex. \n\n\n \n\n\nFCDO has asked for a call in January to go over the comments, while recognising we will need time to review and discuss, perhaps we can pencil something in preliminarily, for example on the 23rd or 24th?\n\n\n \n\n\nBest, \n\nAsa\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\n\nFrom: Louise Beynon <Louise.Beynon1@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nDate: Mon, Nov 27, 2023 at 11:50 AM\n\nSubject: Framework Arrangement update\n\nTo: dahlvik@unfpa.org <dahlvik@unfpa.org>\n\nCc: Rebecca Holderness <rebecca.holderness@fcdo.gov.uk>, Stephen Berwick <stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk>, Ellie Young <ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk>,\n Roomana Mahmud <Roomana.Mahmud@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Åsa,\n \nI hope this email finds you well.\n \nWith sincere apologies for the delay in getting this over to you, I am pleased to say that after a lot of internal coordination\n FCDO is now in a position to share an updated draft of the Framework Arrangement with you. I would be grateful if you could share with the leads for the other UN Agencies.\n \nIn the updated draft we have cleaned up the track changes for the areas that were previously agreed between FCDO and the\n Agencies, and we have also provided some proposed language and comments on the outstanding issues. For ease of reference, please see a table of FCDO’s latest updates below.\n \nAs discussed over the summer, the Framework is a high priority piece of work for FCDO and we are looking forward to working\n with you to finalise the new version. It would be great if we could schedule a tentative call in January once you have had a chance to review the latest version, and in the meantime please let me know if you have any questions.\n \n \n\n\n\n\nSection\n\n\nAmendments/comments\n\n\n\n\nIntroduction/Competent Authority\n\n\nWe have made some amendments to reflect updated policy on using the Framework Arrangement across the UK Government.\n\n\n\n\nEntry into operation and termination\n\n\nPara 5 amended for clarity.\n\n\n\n\nProvision of grant\n\n\nPara 7 addition of FCDO standard language.\nPara 8 deletion reversed.\n\n\n\n\nStatus and compliance with the law\n\n\nPara 10 minor insertion.\n\n\n\n\nEligible expenditure\n\n\nPara 13 inserted in place of prior provisions on eligible expenditure.\nPara 15 coordination levy guidance inserted.\n\n\n\n\nDigital spend\n\n\nPara 17 added language.\n\n\n\n\nUN reform\n\n\nPara 20 updated.\n\n\n\n\nDisbursement\n\n\nPara 22 clarifications needed.\nPara 27 added language.\nPara 29 deletion reversed.\n\n\n\n\nReporting\n\n\nPara 41-42 added language.\n\n\n\n\nDue diligence\n\n\nAttached separately.\n\n\n\n\nRisk management\n\n\nPara 60 deleted.\n\n\n\n\nAid diversion\n\n\nPara 63-64 added language.\nPara 70 insertion deleted.\nPara 71 added language.\n\n\n\n\nTerrorism\n\n\nLanguage updated.\n\n\n\n\nAssets and inventory\n\n\nPara 81-83 deletion reversed.\n\n\n\n\nEnvironment and climate\n\n\nPara 86-88 language added.\n\n\n\n\nCommunication and branding\n\n\nLanguage added to reflect the new FCDO logo.\nAid Visibility Annex re-inserted.\n\n\n\n\nIntellectual property\n\n\nClarification needed.\n\n\n\n\nProgramme information and collaboration\n\n\nPara 103 clarification needed.\n\n\n\n\nTermination and closure\n\n\nPara 107 new proposed paragraph.\nPara 108 insertion deleted.\nPara 110 clarification needed.\n\n\n\n\nAnnex 1\n\n\nAmended reporting currency.\n\n\n\n\nAnnex 3\n\n\nRe-inserted.\n\n\n\n\nAnnex 4\n\n\nAttached separately.\n\n\n\n\n \nBest wishes,\n \nLouise\n \nLouise Beynon\n | Commercial Specialist – Multilaterals and Grants\n| Commercial\n | \nForeign, Commonwealth & Development Office | Tel: +44 (0) 7788 227 119 | Email:\nlouise.beynon1@fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \n\n\n \nFollow us online: \nwww.gov.uk/fcdo\n \nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n    <img border",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000005bA5gMAE",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "lbarusya@unicef.org", "dahlvik@unfpa.org", "louise.beynon1@fcdo.gov.uk", "alubell@unicef.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk", "roomana.mahmud@fcdo.gov.uk", "rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org", "rebecca.holderness@fcdo.gov.uk", "stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk", "asbjornb@unops.org", "stephan.ulrich@undp.org" },
