                new (
                    "00TQx00000629qDMAQ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: [EXT] OpenWHO & Uzbekistan tailored training",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-31").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: [EXT] OpenWHO & Uzbekistan tailored training",
                        Description = "To: utunenh@who.int\nCC: allegrea@who.int; pirouxc@who.int; dominiquef@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: [EXT] OpenWHO & Uzbekistan tailored training\nBody:\nDear HeiniI have sent a placeholder in case we can meet on Friday at 10.30 Geneva time.Please feel free to suggest an alternative if this does not work for you.Looking forward to discussingBest wishesLouise \n\nOn Thu, 25 Jan 2024 at 15:12, UTUNEN, Heini <utunenh@who.int> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise, Dominique, \n \nNice to stay connected Louise and please to e-meet Domonique. We would be most interested in this joint pursuit. It aligns with WHO’s strategic focus on country capacitation.\n\n \nWe will craft more detailed answer on the below and get back to you, best next step would be to call with Dominique and anybody in the workflow.\n\n \nBests\nHeini \n \n \n \nHeini UTUNEN, PhD (she,her)\n| Unit Head\n| \nLearning and Capacity Development\n| \n\nOffice of the Executive Director | \nHealth Emergencies Programme\n| \n \nWorld Health Organization\n| \nAvenue Appia 20 \n| 1211 Geneva\n| Switzerland\n| \nMobile: +41 79 5933476\n|  \n*\nutunenh@who.int\n| \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Thursday, January 25, 2024 11:49 AM\n\nTo: UTUNEN, Heini <utunenh@who.int>\n\nCc: Dominique FREIRE <dominiquef@unops.org>\n\nSubject: [EXT] OpenWHO & Uzbekistan tailored training\n\n \n\n\nDear Heini - great to see you briefly yesterday! \n\n\n\n\n\n\nWishing you and the team a happy and healthy 2024!\n\n\n\nMy colleague Dominique, in copy, is currently working as Senior Technical Advisor in Public Health to our UNOPS Project Team in Tashkent who are managing a large infrastructure and procurement project for the MOH, and working with Asheena WHO Rep.\n \nDominique reached out regarding a training programme that is being discussed in country, as part of the current Laboratory Project (\"COVID-19 Emergency Response\n Project. Duration: December 2022 - January 2025\", Partners/Donors: Ministry of Health, Asian Development Bank, Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank)\n \n\nHaving heard about the great OpenWHO learning platform, Dominique was wondering if we can have a conversation with you on the following concept:\n\nDescription: UNOPS is supporting the Government of Uzbekistan in enhancing\n resilience to COVID-19 and other pandemics / epidemics by upgrading 54 laboratory and treatment facilities nationwide. This includes infrastructure assessment, procurement of diagnostic equipment, and establishing an ICT-based surveillance system. Considerable\n training is needed including on new equipment. For the public health aspects approximately 3.5 million lab staff will be targeted\n (training budget is USD 3M) in three core courses: Biosafety, Pandemic Preparedness, and Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).\n\n\nTraining Concept Design:\n\n\n\nUNOPS Uzbekistan envisions creating a “lifelong learning” environment for underserved staff by complementing in-person courses with WHO's online educational platform, OpenWHO (https://openwho.org/).\n The platform is free, self-paced, offers courses in Russian language and allows offline access, ideal for low-internet speed regions which exist across the country.\n\n\n\n\nNext Steps:\n\n\n\nFollowing high-level discussions between Brendan Keirnan of UNOPS and Asheena Ahkaladina, WHO Rep in December 2023, UNOPS is eager to engage with WHO counterparts at country / regional level\n and with the Learning and Capacity Development Unit within WHO's Health Emergencies Programme, at HQ that developed the OpenWHO platform.\n\n\n\nOur Request:\n\n\n\nWe seek to raise awareness of this valuable learning resource as well as train local lab staff in its use. We have some questions:\n\n\n\n1. How can we collaborate to enhance our joint training using this platform for a more comprehensive and sustainable experience? (Note- UNOPS and WHO have a pre-existing cooperation agreement\n which includes “project management and training-related activities” (Article 2.1.4)) While the platform is free, there may be translation costs, etc.\n\n\n\n\n2. Are there paid online or in-person courses (e.g Biosafety) that UNOPS can utilise?\n\n\n\n3. Is there potential to translate more courses, including into Uzbek?\n\n\n\nNote our training plan is devised in close collaboration with the Sanitary and Epidemiological service of Uzbekistan, our client.\n\n\n\nThank you for considering this collaboration to strengthen preparedness and resilience, and build capacity in Human Resources for health by enabling such partnership. We look forward to hearing\n from you shortly.  \n\n\nBest wishes,\n\nLouise and Dominique\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000629qDMAQ",
