                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006L6lTMAS",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: FCDO comms collab",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-06").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FCDO comms collab",
                        Description = "To: peterb@unops.org; tomco@unops.org\nCC: sophien@unops.org; banak@unops.org; laraas@unops.org; marijab@unops.org; taranehd@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; kelseyl@unops.org; luker@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FCDO comms collab\nBody:\nDear Pete, Tom, Sophie and colleagues, \n\nThank you very much for the elaborated feedback from the FCDO on their thoughts on communications regarding our work in Gaza. \nConsidering that Jorge has spent a considerable amount of time in the margins of the EB talking about and promoting our work in Gaza - I am confident that he would be very keen to go further with this project - incl. all the great ideas from the FCDO listed below. \nFor your information, there was a very strong interest from a multitude of donor countries to learn more about the concrete work we do in Gaza - and many asked for us to communicate more about it externally. \nI also support Tom's suggestion to establish a team working on this. Considering our developing relationship with the FCDO - I would be very happy to participate in this team. \n@Tom COLLINS: Please do advise however I can aid in taking this forward as soon as possible. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 5 Feb 2024 at 11:26, Peter BROWNE <peterb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Sophie, colleagues\nJust following up on the below.\n\n Following consultations on your side, could you advise if either of the two FCDO asks may be possible? We committed to get back to them last week so it would be ideal if we could respond today to clarify. \n\nIf this is not possible, perhaps a simpler option would be some form of website piece that has been shared with all parties for no objection, and the first couple of press points which Jorge could potentially follow up independently.\n\nOver to you to advise\nBest, Pete\n\nOn Thu, Feb 1, 2024 at 10:45 AM Tom COLLINS <tomco@unops.org> wrote:\nDear colleagues, \nI just wanted to follow up on my message below. \nYour guidance would be greatly appreciated as we would like to get back in touch with colleagues at FCDO soon. \nBest wishes, \nTom. \nOn Tue, 30 Jan 2024 at 10:24, Tom COLLINS <tomco@unops.org> wrote:\nHi all, \nYesterday afternoon, Luke, Kelsey and myself met with Joe Lightfoot and Hannah Mozley from FCDO communications team. \nIn short, FDCO is keen to do a joint-communications effort on the work of the Access Support Unit (ASU). \nWe highlighted that while we too are keen, that we would have to seek guidance from OCHA on any final product and also that we could not focus solely on a single donor on what is a multi-donor project. This point was accepted (with some caveats)\nFCDO’s ideas were in two areas: digital and press. \nDigitalProduce a video to be shared across FCDO social media channels as well as their minister’s own social media channels;UNOPS would also post footage across our social media channels;The video would focus on telling the story of how the project is helping on-the-ground. Although, specifics will have to be developed further once we know what footage we can gather;This could include b-roll footage from our work together in Gaza (but this would need to be gathered by UNOPS team on the ground);This could be mixed with a piece-to-camera of one or more individuals working directly on the project or similar project spokesperson close to the operationPotentially, it could also include comment from key people in FCDO (such as the British Foreign Secretary) and UNOPS Executive Director - especially focussing on Jorge’s thoughts following his recent mission to Gaza but their primary focus is on what is happening on the groundFCDO already has some footage, but this is only up until the border. They do not have any footage from inside Gaza;\nPressFCDO would like a key UNOPS spokesperson (suggested Jorge) to potentially be available for interviews on flagship UK television and radio shows (such as BBC Breakfast and ITV’s Good Morning Britain);We highlighted that this could be possible, but would depend on the exact subject and we also made the point that if  the ASU project and the UK’s contribution to it should be referenced, then this would likely require endorsement from the multi-donor group as part of an agreed comms planFCDO also asked what the appetite would be to organise an international press team to come and visit the project on the ground for a tour. We highlighted the immediate sensitivities and challenges around such a visit, but we agreed we would bring it back to colleagues for further discussion. (It may be possible, for example, to connect a local spokesperson with a BBC correspondent on the ground)\nTimelineFCDO are keen to move quicker rather than slower. They asked if we could provide an update to them by the end of the week? \nWe would suggest developing a comms plan that includes a set of potential deliverables and key messages that the multi-donor group + OCHA could provide feedback on and hopefully agree to, but of course we will leave any discussions around next steps with donors to your team. \nOverall, we got the impression that FCDO are keen to push visibility on this project - not just at the FCDO level, but they also mentioned that Number 10 (the UK Prime Minister’s office) could potentially be involved. However, no promises were made on that point. \nIt should also just be noted that while FCDO accepted the need for endorsement from the other donors for any external comms on the project, and the need for it to be referred to as a multi-donor project, they are eager to highlight the UK’s contribution through the various comms they will produce. \nLooking forward to hearing your feedback from our discussions. \nBest, \nTom. \n\nOn Mon, 29 Jan 2024 at 16:31, Sophie NYIRABAKWIYE <sophien@unops.org> wrote:\nDear AsbjornThanks for our call.As discussed, UNOPS is implementing this Access Project on behalf of OCHA. Due to the nature of the Access in Palestine, we would wish to check with the Humanitarian Coordinator, to see if we can organise a joint interview and his overall point of view. Having OCHA (HC), UNOPS, and the Project Manager would be beneficial. As it was mentioned, other donors who have been supporting the project, didn't ask for their visibility since they started supporting the project. I think at this level we may consider consulting them. We are also very careful when discussing \"access\" in Palestine as the perception of the access is not positive. Lara and Dana are available for the meeting with FCDO.Best regardsSophie\n\nOn Fri, Jan 26, 2024 at 3:00 PM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Sophie,\n\nThis is truly excellent news! \nI would suggest that we set up a meeting on Monday with CG colleagues to discuss how to concretely take this forward. I will try to find a workable timeslot. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Fri, 26 Jan 2024 at 02:40, Peter BROWNE <peterb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Sophie\nMany thanks for your message.\n\nWe'd be happy to explore media opportunities and look into developing content with UK counterparts. Copying colleagues in CG to take this forward.\n\nBest, Pete\n\nOn Thu, Jan 25, 2024 at 10:08 PM Sophie NYIRABAKWIYE <sophien@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Peter,Greetings from Palestine. I would like to share with you the below communication from FCDO/HQ. They want to have an interview with UNOPS on the ongoing work (UNOPS & FCDO). From November 2023, they have committed 1M£ pounds to support the Access Support Unit.  Also from our meetings with their Senior Managers on ground, they are aware of UNOPS work in Gaza and we are planning to explore the possibility to mobilise their support for the early recovery project. \nCould you please take this communication forward and inform  the right person to talk to them.My suggestion would be ED and RD Bana to talk to them. I see this request as a great opportunity to strengthen our UNOPS/FCDO partnership. \nMeantime, I will put you in touch with them. Please note that myself and Lara can prepare talking points as soon as requested.\nBest regardsSophie\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Joe Lightfoot <Joe.Lightfoot@fcdo.gov.uk>\nDate: Thu, Jan 25, 2024 at 6:59 PM\nSubject: FCDO comms collab\nTo: sophien@unops.org <sophien@unops.org>\nCc: Hannah Mozley <Hannah.Mozley@fcdo.gov.uk>, Chloe Barry <Chloe.Barry@fcdo.gov.uk>, James Toole <James.Toole@fcdo.gov.uk>, William Archer <William.Archer@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Sophie,\n \nI’m getting in touch from the UK Foreign Office’s comms team – good to make contact with you!\n \nFCDO is keen to give the work that we’re doing with UNOPS to help those in Gaza more of a comms push. We’re thinking particularly in terms of digital content that could be shared across our ministerial and departmental channels, showcasing\n all the great work that you’re doing on the ground and the difference it’s making.\n \nIf possible, we’d also be interested in working with you on press opportunities (in particular interviews with UK broadcast media) to profile these projects.\n \nWould you be available for a quick call to discuss?\n  \nThanks,\nJoe\n \nJoe Lightfoot | Senior Communications Officer – MENA Taskforce |\n Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office | Email: joe.lightfoot@fcdo.gov.uk\n \n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nSophie Nyirabakwiye OIC-Country Director | Head of Programme  | Jerusalem Operations Centre | Cell: +972 545318782 |  www.unops.org | \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\n-- \nPete Browne | Director | Communications | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 3017 7526 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn<span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(6",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006L6lTMAS",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "taranehd@unops.org", "kelseyl@unops.org", "banak@unops.org", "marijab@unops.org", "james.toole@fcdo.gov.uk", "sophien@unops.org", "william.archer@fcdo.gov.uk", "peterb@unops.org", "hannah.mozley@fcdo.gov.uk", "laraas@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "chloe.barry@fcdo.gov.uk", "asbjornb@unops.org", "luker@unops.org", "tomco@unops.org", "joe.lightfoot@fcdo.gov.uk" },
