                new (
                    "00TQx000006LG9iMAG",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: FYI - communication efforts on work in Gaza",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-06").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: FYI - communication efforts on work in Gaza",
                        Description = "To: Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: FYI - communication efforts on work in Gaza\nBody:\nDear Agnes, \nI hope you have returned well to Glasgow and that your jet lag has passed. It was really good to briefly meet you in NYC - and I hope that I can soon come to visit you in the UK. \nAs mentioned we are in a dialogue with your communication team (Joe Lightfoot and Hannah Mozley) on the work we do in Gaza in connection to the Access Support Unit (ASU). \nI thought it might be useful to give you an overview of the talks we have had so far. \nAlso I just wanted to flag that while we are very keen on a joint communication effort, we would need some guidance from OCHA on the final products and we would need to not solely focus on one of the donors (FCDO) as there are several. I understand that this has been accepted by your communication colleagues. \nThe communication ideas fall in two categories: digital and press: \nDigitalProduce a video to be shared across FCDO and UNOPS social media channels as well as your minister’s own social media channels;UNOPS would also post footage across our social media channels;The video would focus on telling the story of how the project is helping on-the-ground. Although, specifics will have to be developed further once we know what footage we can gather;This could include b-roll footage from our work together in Gaza (this would need to be gathered by UNOPS team on the ground);This could be mixed with a piece-to-camera of one or more individuals working directly on the project or similar project spokesperson close to the operationPotentially, it could include comment from key people in FCDO (such as the British Foreign Secretary) and UNOPS Executive Director - especially focussing on Jorge’s thoughts following his recent mission to Gaza FCDO already has some footage, but this is only up until the border. FCDO do not have any footage from inside Gaza, which UNOPS would provide;\nPressA key UNOPS spokesperson (suggested Jorge) to potentially be available for interviews on flagship UK television and radio shows (such as BBC Breakfast and ITV’s Good Morning Britain);Potentially organise an international press team to come and visit the project on the ground for a tour. There are a number of sensitivities and challenges around such a visit, but we agreed to explore further.\nBest,Asbjørn\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006LG9iMAG",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk", "naimoh@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
