                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006LQPGMA4",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Status on Denmark proposal for mine action in Mykolaiv, Ukraine?",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-06").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Status on Denmark proposal for mine action in Mykolaiv, Ukraine?",
                        Description = "To: aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org\nCC: amiro@unops.org; timl@unops.org; andreas.hansen@wfp.org; eleneag@unops.org; michela.carucci@wfp.org; guy.rhodes@wfp.org; davidnm@unops.org; charlesf@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Status on Denmark proposal for mine action in Mykolaiv, Ukraine?\nBody:\nDear Aleksandra, \nThank you for your reply - and good to hear your mission to Mykolaiv went well. I look forward to catching up with Andreas to get his direct impressions from the visit and I hope that we can soon visit Mykolaiv together to kickstart this engagement. \nI fully understand the need to align this engagement with your overall and broader engagement with FAO. That seems very reasonable and important. \nConsidering that we together promised to get back to the Danes weeks ago and the symbolic nature of this project showcasing the OneUN approach - I hope that we can accelerate efforts to draft a common proposal for the engagement. \nI understand that David and Charles have shared a draft proposal from our side some time ago and that we are waiting for your input to the proposal. Would it be possible for you to insert your suggested parts of the proposal during this / early next week? Would be forever grateful - and reduce risks of us together missing this opportunity. \nFinally - I just wanted to remind about the ask from the Danes: That we consider how the engagement could potentially be split into a number of phases - where they provide funding for the first part now - and then potentially more at a later stage. Just for your consideration when drafting the proposal. \nThank you so much in advance for your attention. \nBest regards,Asbjørn\n\nOn Thu, 1 Feb 2024 at 20:46, Aleksandra KRAJCZYNSKA <aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn,\n \nThanks for the message and sorry for my delayed response.\n\nWe just had an internal meeting where we discussed the recent missions to Mykolaiv. The part of the team is still in the south, returning to Kyiv over the weekend.\n\nWe’ll need at least another two weeks or so to finalize the plans from our side. I know this is not ideal and that there is a momentum from the donor side, but we want to ensure that the overall\n project framework for Mykolaiv is clear for us and FAO before closing in on this discussion and how it fits into a bigger picture. Hope this can be conveyed to the MFA colleagues.\n \nIn the meantime, yes – I do believe it’s more efficient to ask for two separate disbursements to remain co-efficient.\n \nAll the best,\nAleksandra\n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, January 31, 2024 6:42 PM\n\nTo: Guy RHODES <guy.rhodes@wfp.org>; David McMahon <davidnm@unops.org>; Charles FRISBY <charlesf@unops.org>; Aleksandra KRAJCZYNSKA <aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org>\n\nCc: Amir OMERAGIC <amiro@unops.org>; Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org>; Andreas HANSEN <andreas.hansen@wfp.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Status on Denmark proposal for mine action in Mykolaiv, Ukraine?\n\n\n \n\nPlease be careful when opening emails that originate from outside WFP\n\n\n\nDear Guy, David, Charles and Aleksandra,  \n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well and that your mission to Mykolaiv went well. \n\n\n \n\n\nI was wondering where we are with drafting a common proposal with budget estimates, timelines, etc. for the potential engagement with Denmark on mine clearing in Mykolaiv? \n\n\n \n\n\nAs I recall, we promised the Danes to get back with a detailed proposal after your mission to Mykolaiv. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe also promised to look into costs of channeling the funding via the RC in Ukraine. Based on conversations with Andreas,. I understand that the MPTF takes 1% and the General Management Support fee is 7%. So I gather it would cost the Danes\n 8% to channel the funds through the RC (which will then come on top of WFP's and UNOPS' management fees...). If that is correct, we can easily recommend to the Danes to channel the funds directly to WFP and UNOPS. \n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe information contained in this electronic message and any attachments is intended for specific individuals or entities, and may be confidential, proprietary or privileged. If you are not the intended recipient, please notify the sender immediately, delete\n this message and do not disclose, distribute or copy it to any third party or otherwise use this message. The content of this message does not necessarily reflect the official position of the World Food Programme. Electronic messages are not secure or error\n free and may contain viruses or may be delayed, and the sender is not liable for any of these occurrences. The sender reserves the right to monitor, record and retain electronic messages.",
