                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: LCM-312 FCDO Framework Arrangement Negotiation",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-06").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: LCM-312 FCDO Framework Arrangement Negotiation",
                        Description = "To: lcm@unops.atlassian.net\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: LCM-312 FCDO Framework Arrangement Negotiation\nBody:\nDear Maryam and Naimo\nApologies for my lack of responses to this. \nI met with the partnership focal points from the other UN agencies last week to discuss the approach. All are keen on moving this forward as quickly as possible - but expecting the FCDO to be the slow part (as they have shown so far, and as they have very limited administrative capacity). \nWith regards to the due diligence annex, I understand that this is something separately negotiated by the partnerships people from the other UN agencies. It would therefore be good to touch base on UNOPS' collected suggestions and approach to the due diligence annex. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Tue, 6 Feb 2024 at 14:08, Maryam Gul KHALID <jira@unops.atlassian.net> wrote:\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n —-—-—-—\n \n \n Reply above this line.\n \n \n \n Maryam Gul KHALID commented:\n Hi Naimo,\n Yes, it’s unfortunate; on the bright side, this means that we will have a better draft to review that accounts for everything that was previously agreed to. Regarding the meeting, UNFPA is attending as the lead negotiator on behalf of the rest of the agencies, but I can ask them to raise the question of timeline and let us know what FCDO says. Is that ok?\n Best regards,\n Maryam\n \n \n View request · Turn off this request's notifications\n This is shared with Maryam Gul KHALID, Naimo HASSAN HIRSI, Asbjorn BRINK, and Devorah Flax-Davidson.\n Powered by Jira Service Management\n \n Sent on 06 February 2024 14:08:07 CET",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006M3AJMA0",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "jira@unops.atlassian.net", "lcm@unops.atlassian.net" },
