                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006PK3dMAG",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-07").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps",
                        Description = "To: gboko@worldbank.org\nCC: skokoricha@mail.smu.edu; adanhossou@worldbank.org; pngouagouni@worldbank.org; frusso@worldbank.org; jonathanbi@unops.org; anahilariae@unops.org; christinebo@unops.org; entelas@unops.org; saraho@unops.org; terrar@unops.org; marko@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps\nBody:\nDear Joachim, \nLooking forward to the discussion tomorrow. I have attached the blog posts with some further minor edits.  \nIn terms of where to publish, I would be happy to reach out to Aaliyah Madyun in the FCV group about publishing the community infrastructure piece on their Development for Peace blog in the run up to the Fragility Forum. Happy to discuss the best approach tomorrow.\nBest,\nAlistair \n \n\nOn Mon, Feb 5, 2024 at 12:56 PM Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Alistair and colleagues, \nThank you very much for this. Apologies for late reply to this. I have been swamped. I have reviewed it and found it good. Please find attached the draft with some suggestions. Please do share the final draft with me before it is further\n processed for publication.\nI understand UNOPS will not be able to produce the photobook. We will see with the Ministry how to do that before the closing of the project. We will be in touch with our colleagues in Washington, DC.\n\nI’m happy to chat later this week. Would Thursday 11 a.m. DC time work for you?\nBest,\nJoachim \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 8:20 PM\n\nTo: Kokoricha, Suvwe <skokoricha@mail.smu.edu>\n\nCc: Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org>; Athanase Danhossou <adanhossou@worldbank.org>; Pisteurpits Boris Martial Ngouagouni <pngouagouni@worldbank.org>; Ana Hilaria ESPIN SANCHEZ <anahilariae@unops.org>; Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>; Entela\n SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Franco Russo <frusso@worldbank.org>; Jonathan BIGOMOKERO <jonathanbi@unops.org>; Sarah O’Neill <saraho@unops.org>; Terra ROBINSON <terrar@unops.org>; marko@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps\n\n\n \n[External]\n\n\nDear Joachim, Suvwe, colleagues, \n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached a first draft of the second blog post, focused on community infrastructure and drawing on beneficiary quotes from the recent mission to Bambari. We would welcome your thoughts on which blog site within the World Bank\n (perhaps an Africa regional platform) would be most appropriate, and how we can support the further development of the piece before publication. \n\n\n \n\n\nSimultaneously, UNOPS corporate communications is working on a feature story for the main\nunops.org website, which will present a similar key message in a more visually immersive way. Following some internal consultation, we consider this a better alternative to the production of a brochure/photobook.\n However, as was the case in South Sudan, UNOPS would be happy to ensure that the World Bank has access to all necessary visual materials to produce a similar product to the example you shared. However, we would not be in a position to support the actual compilation\n and production of a brochure. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe would also welcome the chance to discuss  with you how we can continue to work together to publish these pieces, and also to elevate the shared results of this project to the global level in the run-up to the Fragility Forum and the\n all-important Spring Meetings in April. \n\n\n \n\n\nIn the meantime, wishing you a great weekend ahead.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Jan 19, 2024 at 5:32 PM Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Suvwe, \n\n \n\n\nThanks very much for taking this forward. Please find attached with some minor additional suggestions from our side. The substantive data evidence and the addition of beneficiary quotes make for a strong draft, I think! \n\n\n \n\n\nWe look forward to hearing from your ECR team regarding which WB blog platform would be most appropriate for this piece, and whether our Country Manager or Regional Director would be more appropriate as a potential byline alongside a WB\n official.\n\n\n \n\n\nIn the meantime, we are continuing work on the community infrastructure draft blog. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest wishes,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jan 16, 2024 at 3:33 PM Kokoricha, Suvwe <skokoricha@mail.smu.edu> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nGood afternoon everyone,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope you all are doing well. My apologies for the delayed response; I took off MLK day yesterday. Kindly find attached two revised versions of the blog post. Both\n copies are identical except for the introduction. On one, I used the exact language Ms. Robinson and Mr. Somerville suggested, and on the other I ran with the suggestion, but the language is different. Otherwise, I accepted the in-text  language edits and\n added quotes from beneficiaries from the Key Messages document. Please let me know if there were any additional changes you would like to see.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\n \n\n\n\nSuvwe Kokoricha\n\n\nskokoricha@smu.edu | (575) 749-9292\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\nSent: Monday, January 15, 2024 2:41 PM\n\nTo: Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org>; Athanase Danhossou <adanhossou@worldbank.org>;\n Pisteurpits Boris Martial Ngouagouni <pngouagouni@worldbank.org>; Kokoricha, Suvwe <skokoricha@mail.smu.edu>\n\nCc: Ana Hilaria ESPIN SANCHEZ <anahilariae@unops.org>; Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Franco Russo <frusso@worldbank.org>; Jonathan\n BIGOMOKERO <jonathanbi@unops.org>; Sarah O’Neill <saraho@unops.org>; Terra ROBINSON\n <terrar@unops.org>;\nmarko@unops.org <marko@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nalistairs@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Joachim, Athanase, Boris, and Suvwe, \n\n \n\n\nThanks for the call on Friday. Please find attached the draft blog post with inputs and comments from UNOPS side. Thank you, Suvwe, for helping us move this piece forward! In addition to the suggestions in track changes, here are few other\n questions/reactions:\n\n\n\n\nSome of the information about the two towns presented in paragraph 2 might be better placed at the opening of the piece to create an attention-grabbing intro, before moving to the background about the country context. We have suggested a way to do this in the\n document. \nA number of our suggestions are designed to refine the language, but we understand there will be a further editorial process too before publication.  \nWhile of course the government needs to be in the lead in terms of credit for implementation in the piece, we also need to include reference to UNOPS work in the piece as well, which we have added in track changes. \nWe also suggest the addition of some of the beneficiary quotes in the attached message grid, to complement the data about the project. We'd welcome your views on which ones would be most appropriate. \nQuestions for World Bank ECR team: Which WB platform would be best placed to run the blog? Whose name would appear on the byline? On UNOPS side, we would propose either CAR Country Manager Mark Ohanian or our Regional Director (a.i.) for Africa Dalila Goncalves,\n depending on the level on the Bank's side. \n\nI am following up internally on the photobook and on what a feasible path forward would be, particularly from a funding/resources perspective. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nIn the meantime, we will begin work on a community infrastructure blog post, using the (updated) message grid attached, to which we have added more beneficiary quotes since we last shared this document before the break. \n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to the next steps.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest wishes,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Jan 10, 2024 at 12:11 PM Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nThanks -- I look forward to receiving it. \n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Jan 10, 2024 at 11:24 AM Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks very much Alistair. The proposed time works well for me. Let me send an invite now.\nBest,\nJoachim\n \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, January 10, 2024 5:01 PM\n\nTo: Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org>\n\nCc: Ana Hilaria ESPIN SANCHEZ <anahilariae@unops.org>; Athanase Danhossou <adanhossou@worldbank.org>; Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Franco Russo <frusso@worldbank.org>; Jennifer Sharon ALIMA <jenniferal@unops.org>;\n Jonathan BIGOMOKERO <jonathanbi@unops.org>; Marie Anne Gael PERPIGNAND <marie-annegp@unops.org>; Pisteurpits Boris Martial Ngouagouni <pngouagouni@worldbank.org>;\n Sarah O’Neill <saraho@unops.org>; Terra ROBINSON <terrar@unops.org>;\nmarko@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps\n\n\n \n[External]\n\n\n\nHi Joachim,\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for sharing the draft. We will take a look and provide feedback. Does Friday at 7:15 am DC time work for you? If so I will send a calendar invite.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlistair Somerville\n| Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office, 1775 K Street NW,\n Washington, DC 20006, USA | www.unops.org |\n +1 (229) 586-9792\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 10 Jan 2024 at 03:58, Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nThanks Alistair.\nI have a team retreat Monday-Thursday next week, so I am afraid it might be too late. So, if we can touch base Friday, that would be great. In the meantime, please see attached the draft blogpost.\n\n\n\n\nBest,\nJoachim\n \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 9, 2024 11:47 PM\n\nTo: Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org>\n\nCc: Ana Hilaria ESPIN SANCHEZ <anahilariae@unops.org>; Athanase Danhossou <adanhossou@worldbank.org>; Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Franco Russo <frusso@worldbank.org>; Jennifer Sharon ALIMA <jenniferal@unops.org>;\n Jonathan BIGOMOKERO <jonathanbi@unops.org>; Marie Anne Gael PERPIGNAND <marie-annegp@unops.org>; Pisteurpits Boris Martial Ngouagouni <pngouagouni@worldbank.org>;\n Sarah O’Neill <saraho@unops.org>; Terra ROBINSON <terrar@unops.org>;\nmarko@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS - PACAD communications next steps\n\n\n \n[External]\n\n\n\nDear Joachim,\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for the speedy response. I agree it would be great to move quickly and I’m glad there is already a draft in the works. I am technically on leave this Thursday and Friday but am as keen as you are to move this forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nSo may I propose: \n\n\n\n \n\n\nEither a) a call on Monday and for you to share the draft with us in the meantime to share feedback and add our thoughts or b) if that doesn’t work I can find a moment for a call on Friday morning D.C. time. \n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for the cooperation.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlistair Somerville\n| Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office,\n1775 K Street NW, Washington, DC 20006, USA\n | www.unops.org |\n +1 (229) 586-9792\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jan 9, 2024 at 4:38 PM Joachim Boko <gboko@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Alistair,\nThanks for your message and happy new year to you too. Please accept my apologies for not getting back to you earlier. The end of last year was quite hectic.\n\nNow that we are all back, let’s move fast on this. We do have already a draft post prepared by our intern. Let’s try to talk this week to agree on how to proceed. I am quite flexible on Thursday and Friday morning DC time. Feel free to send a calendar invite\n and we shall proceed.\nBest,\nJoachim \n \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 9, 2024 10:33 PM\n\n<",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006PK3dMAG",
