                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS Gavi partnership",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS Gavi partnership",
                        Description = "To: alatrielle@gavi.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi partnership\nBody:\nDear Amy\n\nThanks so much for this helpful update. I understand and appreciate the timing issues and am grateful for all your support.If we could set up brown bag and/or some bilaterals with SCM/teams for Cameroon, DRC, Ethiopia, Nigeria, Madagascar, CAR, Angola, and Burundi my colleague from Senegal multi country office (covering 18 N/NW AFR) and DRC multi country office (covering 15 countries) would be most appreciative!\nOn the Framework contract, I am on it, following up and will revert asap. \nThanks again for your support during this busy time.Best wishes Louise\n\nOn Fri, 9 Feb 2024 at 17:06, Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nDear Louise,\n \nI wanted to follow up on your request to let you know we are speaking internally on dates and opportunities and I’ll come back to you. It’s a really busy time with the development of 6.0 in full swing thus I apologies I am not more timely\n in communication. \n \nI also wanted to let you know that legal sent the contract to your UNOPS legal dept this week. I hope we can keep this moving quickly as there are many in the Secretariat keen to use this to engage on critical activities with UNOPS.  Grateful\n for your follow up. \n \nHave a great weekend\nAmy\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Monday, February 5, 2024 3:51 PM\n\nTo: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Per your previous email\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nHi Amy, please see the original email chain below. \n\n\nTarget date would be 29 February - the\nmorning for the brown bag with country teams, and the afternoon for bilaterals. \n\n\nHere's a short blurb in case it is useful to capture the concept / share with colleagues / save the date.\n\n\nLooking forward to hearing back from you\n\n\nBest wishes Louise \n\n\n \n\n\nEvery year, UNOPS delivers\n around USD 3 billion in projects in over 80 countries, more than 30% of these projects are focused in the Health sector\nand more than 40% of all our projects are implemented in FCVs.  In 2023, UNOPS delivered 2 projects for Gavi, valued at USD 3 million - less than 1% - in procurement and financial\n / project management in DRC and Ethiopia.\n \nPlease join us on 29th February (add\n time/location) for a Brown Bag session with UNOPS colleagues representing over 30* African countries for an engaging discussion on\n\n\nhealth procurement (UNOPS manages\n\nUN WebBuy+ the UNs \"Amazon\") \nhealth Infrastructure (warehouses / health facilities / IPC / solarisation / WASH) and \nhealth programme management (last mile delivery, multi donor fund management / community led health work).\nCome and meet the team, to connect,\n share ideas, and build valuable connections. Don't miss this informative session!\n \n*Angola, Benin, Burkina Faso, Burundi, Cabo Verde, Cameroon, the Central African Republic, Chad, the Comoros, Congo, the Democratic Republic of the Congo,\n Equatorial Guinea, Ethiopia, Gabon, Guinea, Guinea Bissau, Madagascar, Mali, Mauritania, Mauritius, Morocco, Libya, Niger, Nigeria, Rwanda, and São Tomé and Príncipe, Senegal, Seychelles, South Sudan, Togo and Tunisia\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nDate: Wed, 31 Jan 2024 at 14:18\n\nSubject: Fwd: In person meetings UNOPS Gavi the week of 26 February\n\nTo: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\n \n\n\nDear Amy\n\n\nHope all well with you. Can we have a quick catch up by phone or in person soon? I would love to get your thoughts on the brown bag, perhaps we can do that in parallel with the\n Framework discussion, as I am trying to help plan the programme for my AFR colleagues that are travelling to Geneva.\n\n\nMany thanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nDate: Wed, 24 Jan 2024 at 12:35\n\nSubject: Re: In person meetings UNOPS Gavi the week of 26 February\n\nTo: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>, Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>, Sara Fetouh (Consultant) <sfetouh@gavi.org>,\n Thabani Maphosa <tmaphosa@gavi.org>, Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\n\n \n\n\n\n\nDear Amy\n\n\nGreat to hear from you and thanks so much to you and Jack for moving forward the Framework Agreement process. We look forward to receiving the latest version. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs we have a bit more information about the travel plans of our regional colleagues, can we please pencil in some hours in the morning and afternoon of Thursday 29th February\n for brown bag & bilaterals with SCMs. I have shared some preliminary background with our colleagues about Gavi mandate strategy and work so we can focus our discussions on addressing specific challenges through enhancer collaboration \n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to h working with you and the team on this.\n\n\nBest wishes \n\n\nLouise  \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 16 Jan 2024 at 14:01, Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nThanks for reaching out and a very happy new year to you.  Noted on UNOPS Regional Director and Director for DRC being in town. Let’s have a side chat on setting up meetings and\n you and Tokunbo should link up directly on anything concerning DRC specifically. \n\n \nIn terms of a brown bag, I might suggest we first work through the contract framework between our institutions and then we could use a brownbag occasion to announce the simplified\n contracting process as we discuss engagement in these countries and potential synergies with UNOPS.  I’ve followed up with legal and will do so again to ensure the contract negotiations move forward expeditiously.  \n \nSincerely,\nAmy\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 16, 2024 11:15 AM\n\nTo: Thabani Maphosa <tmaphosa@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Almaz Tessema <atessema@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>;\n Sara Fetouh (Consultant) <sfetouh@gavi.org>; Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: In person meetings UNOPS Gavi the week of 26 February\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Thabani \nThanks for your message. Great - will continue to work with Amy and team to prepare for the AFR mission, and with your office for bilat. \n\n\nThanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 16 Jan 2024 at 09:30, Thabani Maphosa <tmaphosa@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nI believe that Amy is well placed to coordinate with Tokunbo, Colette and their teams, please keep working through her and with her. I have copied Colette. If I am in town I would\n be happy to meet the Regional Director.\n \nBest Regards,\n \nThabani\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, January 15, 2024 5:49 PM\n\nTo: Thabani Maphosa <tmaphosa@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Almaz Tessema <atessema@gavi.org>; Sara Fetouh (Consultant) <sfetouh@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>;\n Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: In person meetings UNOPS Gavi the week of 26 February\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Thabani\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nWishing you a happy and healthy 2024 - and congratulations to you and Gavi colleagues on the appointment of your new\n CEO!\n\n \n\n\nI would like to follow up on my previous email regarding the mission to Geneva next month of our Regional Director\n for Africa, Ms Dalila Goncalves and the Director of our DRC multi country office Dr Tatiana Wah.  I am working with Amy and Anne on the FCV portfolio, and would welcome your guidance to convene a discussion with AFR SCMs for the following countries, including\n DRC where we have ongoing collaboration:\n\n\nAngola, Burundi, Cameroon, Cape Verde, CAR, Chad, Comoros, Equatorial Guinea, Ethiopia, Gabon, Kenya, Libya, Madagascar,\n Nigeria, Republic of Congo, Rwanda, São Tomé and Príncipe, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Uganda, Zambia. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nWe were thinking of a \"Brown Bag\" type meeting to hear from the SCMs on operational challenges, and also share some\n examples of relevant UNOPS country projects that could help accelerate the achievement of Gavi 5.0.  In 2023, UNOPS implemented USD 877 million in health projects on behalf of our government and international partners, addressing country needs and priorities\n with a focus on climate resilient health infrastructure, health procurement and programme management.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe anticipate a productive meeting to build on and potentially scale up some existing collaborations.\n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you in due course.\n\n\nWith thanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
