                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi",
                        Description = "To: kfendler@gavi.org\nCC: alatrielle@gavi.org; lgabus@gavi.org; areynolds@gavi.org; smueller@gavi.org; ipetkova@gavi.org; devorahfd@unops.org; jnichols@gavi.org; ekaterinapo@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\nBody:\nDear KateThanks very much for sending this through. Devorah and Ekaterina have looked extensively at the document you sent, but cannot detect any further changes, other than the addition of \"classified as internal\"!   I have set up a separate Google sheet which I have just shared with Kate, Jack, Ekaterina and Devorah to please use in order to clarify the issues still under discussion.  I suggest we meet as soon as possible to clarify remaining issues so we can move forward. Look forward to hearing from youBest wishes Louise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Thu, 8 Feb 2024 at 17:01, Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Devorah and colleagues,\n \nWith my apologies for the delay, I have attached a new draft template agreement for discussion, which reflects in tracked changes the edits we have made when compared to the draft you shared on 26 January. I have left the prior comments\n for completeness but have added a few new comments flagging new points we have raised.\n\n \nPlease let us know if you would like to schedule a call to discuss the initial draft or send comments back in the first instance.\n\n \nBest regards,\nKate \n \n\n\nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org> \n\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 4:08 PM\n\nTo: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>; Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Kate and colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for confirming. Looking forward to our discussion.\n\n\n \n\n\nHave a nice weekend,\n\n\n \n\n\nDevorah\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n|\nLegal Specialist |\nIPAS\n Legal | HQ |\nCopenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Jan 26, 2024 at 4:02 PM Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n \nDear Devorah and colleagues,\n \nThank you for sharing this draft. We were able to open and review and are now compiling internal comments on Gavi’s side and will aim to send back an updated draft for further discussion\n next week. \n \nBest regards,\nKate\n \n\n\nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 9:57 AM\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nCc: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>;\n Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>; Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Jack, Kate and colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for your patience. I spoke with my colleague, Katya, and for ease of reference, please find the December 2023 version\n that represents for us the most recent version that I believe Louise sent a month ago. \n\n\n \n\n\nPlease let me know if you have any issues opening up the document.\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks!\n\n\n\n\nDevorah\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n|\nLegal Specialist |\nIPAS\n Legal | HQ |\nCopenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Jan 26, 2024 at 9:53 AM Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Kate and team\n\n\nI believe you have the latest version, the one I sent a month or so ago. I am 99.9% sure, but will re confirm my side;\n until then pls consider this version the latest one.\n\n\nThanks and best wishes Louise\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 26 Jan 2024 at 09:46, Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Devorah and colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for engaging with us in developing a template. I am following up on Jack’s request, below, for UNOPS to share the late 2023 version of the agreement with additional\n comments so we can try to respond to the most recent comments and proposed terms.\n\n \nBest,\nKate\n \n\n\nFrom: Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 23, 2024 1:32 PM\n\nTo: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nCc: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>; Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n\n \nDear Devorah\n \nThe draft as it stood on our side in Q1 2022 had comments from UNOPS (Daniel Elliott, David Ssali and Mesfin Hailu) with only a couple dating from 16 December 2021, and most would\n therefore be within the draft you have from November 2021. Any later comments in the draft were internal to Gavi and while they may have arisen from ongoing discussions with UNOPS at the time, related to our review of UNOPS’ position, so we cannot share that\n with you at this point. \n \nWould you be able to share with this email chain the version that Katya worked on late 2023, so that we can review and take account of your proposals as we update the draft?\n \nMany thanks and kind regards\n \nJack\n \n\n\nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, January 19, 2024 4:42 PM\n\nTo: Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>; Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Jack and colleagues, \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you so much for reaching out relating to the finalization of the GAVI-UNOPS model agreement. A big thanks to Amy and Louise\n for putting us all in touch!\n\n\n \n\n\nI note in your email you mention the version last negotiated between GAVI and UNOPS is from Q1 2022. Unfortunately, the legal colleague who\n had been undertaking the negotiation back in 2022 is no longer with UNOPS and the last version that we have in our possession is dated from 5 November 2021. Would you be able to provide the Q1 2022 version so we may compare this document with our last recorded\n version from Nov 2021? Additionally, my colleague, Ekaterina (Katya) was most recently involved in a discussion with GAVI colleagues at the end of 2023 where she updated the 5 November 2021 with some comments from UNOPS's side. Have you seen this document\n and if so, would this be a good starting point on which to engage?\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease let us know if setting up a meeting in the next coming weeks would be helpful; we can not only identify which version to\n which we should consider and refer as a starting point but also we may introduce ourselves.\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you so much and looking forward to working with you and your colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nDevorah\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n|\nLegal Specialist |\nIPAS\n Legal | HQ |\nCopenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Jan 17, 2024 at 2:57 PM Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Devorah, Ekaterina\n \nIt is good to be in contact with you, and Louise, on this. I and the other members of the legal team copied (Kate Fendler and Laurent Gabus) are looking forward to supporting colleagues\n in the process and drafting to finalise the template.\n \nAs Amy mentioned, in Gavi we are currently initiating the process of looking at the draft grant agreement template as it stood in Q1 2022, to ensure it remains consistent with Gavi’s\n current requirements and best practice, in line with the expected operational scope and requirements of the envisaged project/programme interventions, and to close out the open comments as the draft stood. Once we conclude that process we can come back to\n you with a draft for your further consideration. \n \nWe trust that fits your expectations, and that we would not be cutting across any process you are currently running on the document. However, please do let us know if you are working\n on the draft template grant agreement now in which case we will await your revised draft before we review.\n \nKind regards\n \nJack\n \nJack\n Nichols \n \n\nHead, Legal\n \n\nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners.\n\n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy\n the e-mail or any attachment.\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, January 17, 2024 9:22 AM\n\nTo: Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>; Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>\n\nCc: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n\n \nDear Jack, Devorah and Ekaterina,\n \nHappy 2024 to you all (I’ve been told I can say that until 31 Jan).  I’m pulling our respective UNOPS and Gavi legal teams into one thread to help us progress in finalizing a “Template\n Grant Agreement” between our institutions.  The goal of this exercise is to have a standardized grant agreement with will have negotiated terms and conditions thus allowing us to contract more expeditiously without having a back and forth on every contract. \n Thank you for your efforts to make this happen. \n \nJack Nichols will lead the process from Gavi and will follow this up with an email laying out the proposed process to move this forward.\n\n \nLooking forward to closer engagement in 2024.\n\n \nSincerely,\nAmy\n \n\nAmy LaTrielle (she/her/hers)\n\n \n\n\n \n\nDirector, Fragile and Conflict Segment, Country Programmes Department\n\n\nMobile: +41 79 201 50 33\n\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / X\n (Twitter) /\nLinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n \n\n \nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create\n any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners. \n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy\n the e-mail or any attachment.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006cxv0MAA",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "areynolds@gavi.org", "devorahfd@unops.org", "ekaterinapo@unops.org", "kfendler@gavi.org", "louisel@unops.org", "ipetkova@gavi.org", "lgabus@gavi.org", "jnichols@gavi.org", "smueller@gavi.org", "alatrielle@gavi.org" },
