                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006d9o1MAA",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: THANK YOU & Next Steps - finalizing the new WHO Strategy (GPW14 - 2025-28)",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: THANK YOU & Next Steps - finalizing the new WHO Strategy (GPW14 - 2025-28)",
                        Description = "To: aylwardb@who.int\nCC: pfeifferm@who.int\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: THANK YOU & Next Steps - finalizing the new WHO Strategy (GPW14 - 2025-28)\nBody:\nDear Bruce \nThank you so much for the invitation to join the VC last week and provide some additional feedback on the excellent current draft GPW 14.\nAttached please find a few comments (and rationale) for your consideration. These primarily reflect (i) recognising UNOPS current and potential role to help WHO and partners expand delivery and impact for health (ii) emphasising health infrastructure and health procurement as key enablers to improving inclusive, accessible health and wellbeing, and (iii) reflecting Scaling Up Nutrition inputs (one of our hosted partnerships).\nLooking forward to the next phase, and working towards that all important alignment (and coordination!).\nThanks and best wishesLouise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Fri, 9 Feb 2024 at 16:03, AYLWARD, Raymond Bruce J. <aylwardb@who.int> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear partner colleagues,\n\nTHANK YOU!  \n\nWe are simply indebted for the superb participation, feedback and suggestions in \nyesterday’s VC on the working draft of WHO’s new strategy (‘GPW14’).  \n\nThis was even more than we’d hoped for.\n\nTo recap the next steps we discussed:\n\n\nRevising current GPW14 draft: next week we will revise the EB version of GPW14 to reflect inputs received from our Member States and partners as of today.  While we worked hard to capture all your rich feedback in our call, I’m sure we missed some things\n and would really appreciate any written comments ASAP to try & capture them in this iteration;\nNext opportunity to comment: we will also issue the next (and final) ’pre-WHA’ version of the draft strategy in WHO’s 6 official languages in early-March, with another 10 day opportunity for you to review and comment – thx you in advance for your stamina!;\n\nImpact measurement & outcome indicators: as Samira explained, as this part of the consultation process moves forward her team will send a separate email with further details on how you can engage in the upcoming Global Technical Consultation on the impact\n measurement aspect of the GPW14 Results Framework.\n\nThank you all again so much for your tremendous interest, engagement, and very constructive input into this joint vision for global health over the vital 4 year period 2025-2028 – the world will be a better place if we are aligned\n😊.\n\nBest regards and looking forward to our continued exchanges as this work progresses.\n\nBruce, on behalf of our WHO GPW14 SteerCo and my co-chairs Samira and Jeremy\n\nPS - for those of you who were not able to join us yesterday, please find attached the presentation we used to frame our conversation.\n \n\n\nFrom: AYLWARD, Raymond Bruce J. <aylwardb@who.int> \n\nSent: Friday, February 2, 2024 5:51 PM\n\nTo: 'Juan Pablo Eusebiq Uribe Restrepo' <juribe@worldbank.org>; Michael Kent Ranson <mranson@worldbank.org>; Bruno Rivalan (brivalan@worldbank.org) <brivalan@worldbank.org>; Katie Kampf <Katie.Kampf@theglobalfund.org>; David Marlow <dmarlow@gavi.org>;\n Aurelia Nguyen (ANguyen@gavi.org) <ANguyen@gavi.org>; Ms H. Burris (hburris@gavi.org) <hburris@gavi.org>; Johannes Ahrendts <jahrendts@gavi.org>; Kelechi Ohiri <kohiri@gavi.org>; Mandeep Dhaliwal <mandeep.dhaliwal@undp.org>; GOMEZ, Efraim <gomeze@unaids.org>;\n onabanjo@unfpa.org; Nazneen Damji (nazneen.damji@unwomen.org) <nazneen.damji@unwomen.org>; giancarlo.cirri@wfp.org; Mr B. Syme Van Ameringen (benjamin.syme@wfp.org) <benjamin.syme@wfp.org>; jsi@cepi.net; Saul Walker <saul.walker@cepi.net>; Karishma Saran (karishma.saran@finddx.org)\n <karishma.saran@finddx.org>; Sergio Carmona <Sergio.Carmona@finddx.org>; PEREZ CASAS, Carmen <perezcasasc@unitaid.who.int>; arai@ilo.org; Kieran Daly <kieran.daly@gatesfoundation.org>; S.Birks@wellcome.org; Dr C. Elias (Chris.Elias@gatesfoundation.org) <Chris.Elias@gatesfoundation.org>;\n Ted Chaiban <tchaiban@unicef.org>; oaabdi (oaabdi@unicef.org) <oaabdi@unicef.org>; Richard Hatchett <richard.hatchett@cepi.net>; DUNETON, Philippe <dunetonp@unitaid.who.int>; O GLOBAL FUND - Mr P. Sands (peter.sands@theglobalfund.org) <peter.sands@theglobalfund.org>;\n Willibald Zeck <zeck@unfpa.org>; Monique Vledder <mvledder@worldbank.org>; Hajime Inoue <hinoue@worldbank.org>; jorge.moreiradasilva@unops.org; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Igor Oliynyk <igor.oliynyk@theglobalfund.org>; francesca.colombo@oecd.org;\n JA.Rottingen@wellcome.org\n\nCc: FARRAR, Jeremy <farrarj@who.int>; ASMA, Samira <asmas@who.int>; HAJJEH, Rana <hajjehr@who.int>; PFEIFFER, Michaela V. <pfeifferm@who.int>; KASOLO, Francis Chisaka <kasolof@who.int>; FREEMAN, Richard <freemanr@who.int>; KASAPI, Evis <kasapie@who.int>;\n SERHAN, Fatima <serhanfa@who.int>; PRASAD, Amit <prasada@who.int>; VOLK, Susanna <volks@who.int>; LUKSCH, Niklas <lukschn@who.int>; NAKARI, Taina Tea Irmeli <nakarit@who.int>; NIE, Jiangang <niej@who.int>; KELLY, Linda <kellyl@who.int>; LONNQUIST, Fabia <lonnquistf@who.int>;\n MASON, Clarisse <masonc@who.int>; PENDSE, Razia <pendsera@who.int>; URSU, Pavel <ursup@who.int>; HOLLO, Imre <holloi@who.int>; PENDERGAST, Scott Douglas <PendergastS@who.int>; BROSTRØM, Søren <brostroms@who.int>; KASONDE, Mwenya <kasondem@who.int>\n\nSubject: Finalizing the new WHO Strategy (GPW14 - 2025-2028) - Thurs, 8 Feb 2024, 16-17hr CET\n\nImportance: High\n\n\n \nDear Colleagues,\nOn behalf of my Co-Chairs, and WHO’s GPW14 SteerCo, I would like to extend our sincere thanks for your incredibly constructive feedback on\nour draft Global Health Agenda (the ‘GPW14’) in the run-up to last week’s WHO Executive Board (EB) meeting.\nI am delighted to report that we had very positive feedback on and strong support for this draft Strategy from our 194 Member States.  \nCountries were particularly appreciative of your direct engagement and inputs in this process, and affirmed that the strategic objectives and major outcomes align with our shared priorities for global health over\n the crucial four year period in front of us.\nAs we embark on the final phase of this process,\nwe would like to invite you to join us on Thurs, 8 February 2024, from 16:00-17:00h CET to discuss how we can capture your further inputs as we develop a final version of GPW14 for the 77th World Health Assembly. \n\nA calendar invitation with zoom details will follow.\nAttached again – if helpful – is a link to the\nlatest draft of the 14th GPW as presented to our Executive Board.\nPlease feel free to forward this invitation to appropriate focal points in your organizations.\nWith best regards\nBruce\n \nAssistant Director-General and\n  Co-Chair GPW14 Steering Committee\nWorld Health Organization",
