                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006esJBMAY",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UNOPS Portfolio",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS Portfolio",
                        Description = "To: rswami@worldbank.org\nCC: christinebo@unops.org; mfikre@worldbank.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Portfolio\nBody:\nDear Rajeev,\nI hope all is well with you. We have completed the requested review of UNOPS WB-financed operations. \nPlease find attached the spreadsheet. Duplicate projects are marked in yellow. \nBelow is a list of projects we have assessed to be missing from the sheet, all on the borrower contracting side. Project names without numbers are UNOPS project names, which often differ from the WB name when we are only implementing one component of a project. Please let us know if you think these projects may be reflected somewhere I have missed, or if you need any further information. \nMozambique: P172350 Digital Governance Economy Project - (signed Oct 2023 – could be too recent), $17.4MThere are also multiple instances of procurements on behalf of the Ministry of Health that I don’t see reflected in the portfolio overview. Similarly, our Building Emergency Response Capacity at Hospitals Project for $12.5M does not appear to be reflected in the WB portfolio overview. Cameroon: PATNUC - Digital Transformation Project for $1.5M seems to be missing. Liberia: Ebola Emergency Response Project for <$1M does not appear.Senegal: PAFS - Projet d’Appui aux Filets Sociaux for <1M does not appear.Sierra Leone: P126733 West Africa Regional Fisheries Program - (UNOPS 22885-001) - $650K (Construction of a Fisheries Landing Site at Konakridee) does not appear.Freetown Disaster Preparedness (UNOPS #21200) - $263.6K does not appear. Nepal: Household Registration for the Nepal Housing Reconstruction Program - $7.25M in 2016. \nWe will also follow up separately regarding our inactive accounts, and have a few questions for George. We look forward to tomorrow’s FM meeting and are happy to answer any questions about either of these exercises.\nBest wishes,\nAlistair \n\nOn Tue, Jan 9, 2024 at 5:52 PM Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org> wrote:\nThanks — this is very helpful!\nAlistair Alistair Somerville | Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office, 1775 K Street NW, Washington, DC 20006, USA | www.unops.org | +1 (229) 586-9792Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\nOn Tue, 9 Jan 2024 at 17:13, Rajeev K. Swami <rswami@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Alistair, thank you so much for looking into this.  Our only priority is to make sure we have our records aligned with yours.  If the additional details do not pose too much additional burden on you then that\n would be great as well but only if that is not too much headache at all.\n \n\nbest, Rajeev\n \n\n\n\n\nRajeev K. Swami\n\n\n\n\nLead Specialist\nOperations Policy & Country Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nT\n\n\n+1 (202) 458-9610\n\n\n\n\nE\n\n\nrswami@worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\nW\n\n\nwww.worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nrajeevkswami\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 9, 2024 12:53 PM\n\nTo: Rajeev K. Swami <rswami@worldbank.org>\n\nCc: Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Portfolio\n\n\n \n[External]\n\n\nDear Rajeev, \n\n \n\n\nI hope you also had a chance to relax over the holidays. Many thanks indeed for sharing this document with us. We will review it and get back to you with suggested additions. In addition to checking if any operations/contracts are missing,\n do you also want us to fill in the empty cells where dates and other information are missing? \n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks,\n\n\n\n\nAlistair \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Jan 8, 2024 at 9:49 AM Rajeev K. Swami <rswami@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Christine and Alistair,\n \nFirst, happy new year to you both (and to Andrea as well), and hope you had a chance to enjoy the holiday break.  I wanted to reach out to you regarding\n the portfolio that UNOPS has had with the Bank.  The data set is from July 2015 (our FY2016) through the end of 2023.\n \nAs with anything IT related these days, we are in the middle of some system upgrades.  We noticed that some of the data in the various systems was slightly\n incomplete – and as we are putting in a series of fixes, we wanted to take the opportunity to make any adjustments that are needed so that we have a completely accurate data set across all our operational systems.\n \nSo, I am sharing with you the portfolio data that we have pulled – both indirect and direct financing.  If I could ask you to review this and let me\n know what operations/contracts may be missing from the list, then we can make sure that the adjustments are correctly entered in the system.\n \nAppreciate your review and help on this.\n \nbest, Rajeev\n \n\n\n\n\nRajeev K. Swami\n\n\n\n\nLead Specialist\nOperations Policy & Country Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nT\n\n\n+1 (202) 458-9610\n\n\n\n\nE\n\n\nrswami@worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\nW\n\n\nwww.worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nrajeevkswami\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\nAlistair Somerville\n| Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office, 1775 K Street NW,\n Washington, DC 20006, USA | www.unops.org |\n +1 (229) 586-9792\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nAlistair Somerville | Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office, 1775 K Street NW, Washington, DC, 20006, USA | www.unops.org | +1 (229) 586-9792Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
