                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000006gSmCMAU",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: 🇯🇵 Official launch of the UNOPS Japan Parliamentary Association 🇯🇵",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: 🇯🇵 Official launch of the UNOPS Japan Parliamentary Association 🇯🇵",
                        Description = "To: jorge.moreiradasilva@unops.org; sonjalk@unops.org; hilaryb@unops.org; sanjaym@unops.org; dalilag@unops.org; banak@unops.org; TimL@unops.org; DionyssiaG@unops.org; fabriziof@unops.org; anneclaireh@unops.org\nCC: plg.personnel@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: 🇯🇵 Official launch of the UNOPS Japan Parliamentary Association 🇯🇵\nBody:\nColleagues,\nIn Tokyo, earlier this week, we held the inaugural meeting of the UNOPS Parliamentary Association in Japan. The main objective of this bipartisan group is to raise UNOPS’ profile with key decision makers (Parliamentarians and senior officials) and demonstrate how we can contribute to advancing Japan’s foreign policy objectives. The President of the Association is Mr. Gen Nakatani, former Defense Minister of Japan and the PM’s former advisor on international human rights issues. The Secretary-General is Mr. Kiyoto Tsuji, State Minister for Foreign Affairs. \nOn the bureaucracy side, we were pleased to see that all major ministries were represented: Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA), Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare (MHLW), and Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry (METI).\nThis inaugural meeting allowed us to present UNOPS’ business model and value proposition and update the group on our recent work in Gaza, Ukraine and Myanmar. There was particular interest when we highlighted that, for the last three years, UNOPS is the UN agency that procures the most products from Japanese companies. There were several interventions and questions from parliamentarians asking MOFA why UNOPS was not used more regularly by the Government in order to fulfill Japan’s foreign policy and international development priorities. \nThe next meeting is planned for June 2024, and we aim to have official meetings every six months. In this regard, we are hoping DEDs, RDs and other UNOPS leaders will be able to share their work with the group- depending on interests.\nUNICEF, UNHCR, WFP and the World Bank (to name a few) established parliamentary associations in Japan several years ago and they have become key forums for discussion. We are confident this new association will allow us to better position UNOPS with this important partner. Finally, this  milestone for us in Japan comes as a result of the Tokyo Liaison Office’s two years of engagements with parliamentarians which culminated with Jorge’s visit last November. \nThank you Yuko and the TLO team for getting us here! Thank you Jorge for coming last November to ensure we were able to seal the deal! \nÉmilie\n-- \nÉmilie S. Potvin | Director, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
