                new (
                    "00TQx000006gi9IMAQ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Follow-up Corporate Agreement UNOPS - AIIB",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-01-03").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Follow-up Corporate Agreement UNOPS - AIIB",
                        Description = "To: emiliep@unops.org\nCC: ping.cheah@aiib.org; bwang@aiib.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Follow-up Corporate Agreement UNOPS - AIIB\nBody:\n*OFFICIAL USE ONLY\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*OFFICIAL USE ONLY\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Emilie, \nI hope you had great beginning to 2024. \nFollowing COP, G20 and our own Board session in December, we are now ready to follow-up on the corporate agreement between AIIB and UNOPS.\n@Ping Yean Cheah is our relationship manager for UNOPS and together with\n@Bin Wang our expert in partnership agreements, will be leading the negotiations and drafting of the document.\n They will be making all the necessary connections with our relevant internal teams (LEG, Procurement) to ensure a smooth process.\n\nPing has been so far engaging with Akira Moretto from your SE region so let me know whether he would be the right focal point for this as well or there are other UNOPS colleagues that should be engaged.\n\nIn terms of timing, we can have an early assessment once the teams connect but the WB/IMF Spring Meetings in April could be one (assuming George will be in DC). Otherwise, we can think on our own Annual meetings in September in Uzbekistan,\n WB/IMF Annual Meetings or the FICS Summit which we will be hosting in Chengdu in October.\n\nLooking forward to working together in landing this relevant engagement which will unlock great synergies between our institutions,\n\nAll the best, \nR\nRodrigo Salvado\n\nDirector General, Operational Partnerships Department (OPD)\nAsian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB)\nAIIB Headquarters, Tower A, Asia Financial Center\nNo. 1 Tianchen East Road, Chaoyang District, Beijing 100101, China\nrodrigo.salvado@aiib.org\n\nwww.aiib.org",
