                new (
                    "00TQx000006i1D9MAI",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: World Bank and UNOPS blog post on CAR to highlight around Fragility Forum",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-14").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: World Bank and UNOPS blog post on CAR to highlight around Fragility Forum",
                        Description = "To: amadyun@worldbankgroup.org\nCC: gboko@worldbank.org; christinebo@unops.org; anahilariae@unops.org; terrar@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: World Bank and UNOPS blog post on CAR to highlight around Fragility Forum\nBody:\nDear Aaliyah,\nI hope you are well. I am writing from the Washington office of UNOPS, where I am leading our engagement at the forthcoming Fragility Forum. \nWe have been working with the Task Team for the PACAD project to highlight results of the collaboration between the government of CAR, the World Bank and UNOPS as the project reaches its conclusion. (The TTL Joachim Boko is in copy.) One of the communications products we have been working on is the attached blog post, which we think would be a great fit for the Development for Peace blog in the run up to the Forum. We would need to agree still on a byline from the WB side and from UNOPS leadership as well (either our CAR Country Manager or Africa Regional Director) but I was wondering if the piece would be of interest to you and your team as you consider content to highlight around the Fragility Forum. \nI look forward very much to hearing from you (and was glad to see that you also worked for UNOPS!). \nBest wishes,\nAlistair -- \nAlistair Somerville | Senior Officer | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Washington Liaison Office, 1775 K Street NW, Washington, DC, 20006, USA | www.unops.org | +1 (229) 586-9792Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
