                    "00TQx000006kkviMAA",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Update",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-14").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Update",
                        Description = "To: Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org\nCC: Sidharth.Rupani@theglobalfund.org; rainerf@unops.org; fitsumberhanw@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Update\nBody:\nDear Scott and SidharthPlease find enclosed the revised SOW adding the additional clarification on LTAs and technical support your request for review.There are a few remaining questions regarding procurement / additional tech assistance to clarify, so I have copied Rainer and Fits in order to set up a call for you all to clarify these finer points (I am out of office the next few days)Over to you and looking forward to getting closer to finalising this collaboration!\nAll best wishesLouise\n\nOn Thu, 11 Jan 2024 at 16:49, Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Scott\nGood to hear from you and thanks for the update.\nOn the Agreement, yes indeed. I need to explore how we have dealt with this in other (already signed) GF Agreements - this is part of my discussion with my legal team on Monday.\nIn the meantime, regarding SOW please see attached for your review. We can set up a call with the Kenya technical services unit for any clarifications next week if that works for you.\nSee you soonBest wishes Louise\n\nOn Thu, 11 Jan 2024 at 08:38, Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nThank you for the update. Sorry I missed you yesterday. I have my regular check in with Francesco today so I will check in with him on this.\n \nWill be interesting to see if that agreement could help in getting something signed. It seems that the GF and UNOPs agreement has yet to be signed due to language around sexual exploitation,\n and this is what we’ve been waiting for to work off to have an agreement for the type of engineering support we discussed with you and your team.\n\n \nWe are still waiting for approval to receive funding for that initiative, but once we do, I’ll need to circle back to you about what we discussed with your engineering colleagues\n around the SoW for seconding people to GF and providing technical expertise through your LTAs.\n \nI will be around next week to talk.\n\n\nRegards,\nScott\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScott Dubin\nAdvisor, Supply Chain Private Sector Engagement\nIn-Country Supply Chain Management\nSupply Operations\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41764701538\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nscott.dubin@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, January 10, 2024 2:19 PM\n\nTo: Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: Update\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Scott - Happy New Year!  Hope you had a restorative break.\n\n\n \n\n\nJust to update you on a few things since our last conversation about Warehouses. I found a generic global agreement dating from 2015 - so a bit out of date, but I will be reviewing\n it on Monday with my legal colleagues and will update you on the outcome.\n\n\n \n\n\nRelated to this, our Regional Director for Africa, Ms Dalila Goncalves and our Director of DRC multi country office Dr Tatiana Wah will be coming to Geneva for a \"health mission\"\n the week of 26 February 2024.  I am working with Francesco Moschetta (GF official focal point for UNOPS partnership), to set up brown bag & follow up meetings with a number of GF country teams.  \n\n\n \n\n\nWe will be focused on the following countries  - Angola, Burundi, Cameroon, Cape Verde, CAR, Chad, Comoros, DRC, Equatorial Guinea, Ethiopia, Gabon, Kenya, Libya, Madagascar,\n Nigeria, Republic of Congo, Rwanda, São Tomé and Príncipe, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Uganda, Zambia.  \n\n\n \n\n\nWe plan to share updates and challenges from GF and UNOPS side with a focus on how UNOPS can provide the most impactful operational support to these portfolios and associated\n strategic initiatives (e.g. including warehouses). Francesco and I also discussed the possibility of signing a new global agreement on that occasion.\n\n\n \n\n\nI am at GF now - just finished a meeting to plan this health mission. Are you in the office today? If not, let's catch up on the Warehouse conversation next week some time?\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to speaking soon,\n\n\nThanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000006kkviMAA",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "scott.dubin@theglobalfund.org", "rainerf@unops.org", "louisel@unops.org", "sidharth.rupani@theglobalfund.org", "fitsumberhanw@unops.org" },
