                new (
                    "00TQx000006w5qSMAQ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Fwd: Invitation: Kick-off: Regeringens arbejde med styrket engagement i Afrika 11. marts 2024",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-19").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: Invitation: Kick-off: Regeringens arbejde med styrket engagement i Afrika 11. marts 2024",
                        Description = "To: sarahdg@unops.org; waingchita@unops.org\nCC: emiliep@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; annag@unops.org; oonaa@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: Invitation: Kick-off: Regeringens arbejde med styrket engagement i Afrika 11. marts 2024\nBody:\nDear Sarah and Waing, \nPlease see below an invitation to the launch of a debate on The Danish Government’s revised approach to strengthened engagement in Africa. \nThe event takes place on March 11 at 10.15-12.15 at The Black Diamond in Copenhagen C and will be conducted in Danish but with simultaneous interpretation to English. \nAt the event the Danish Prime Minister, the Foreign Minister and the Minister for Development and Global Climate will present their reflections on Denmark's future engagements in Africa - with a special emphasis on how it should complement the EU engagement. The event will also feature high-level representation from African countries. \nCould you kindly let me know if Jorge would be available and would like to participate in this event? As the event is very much focused on Danish development policy and as we do not have an active role, I do not think that it warrants a high priority in Jorge's already busy schedule. However, it would be an opportunity to greet some high level decision makers in Denmark, the diplomatic corps and some African representatives. I could also try to secure an active role for Jorge at the event - but obviously can't promise anything. \nNo matter what - I will naturally participate in the event. \nBest,Asbjørn\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: event@altinget.dk <event@altinget.dk>\nDate: Fri, 16 Feb 2024 at 15:47\nSubject: Invitation: Kick-off: Regeringens arbejde med styrket engagement i Afrika 11. marts 2024\nTo: Jorge.moreiradasilva@unops.org <Jorge.moreiradasilva@unops.org>\nCc: sarahdg@unops.org <sarahdg@unops.org>, davidc@unops.org <davidc@unops.org>, asbjornb@unops.org <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nINVITATION \n\nKick-off: Regeringens arbejde med styrket engagement i Afrika\n11. marts 2024\n  \nVerden er i hastig forandring, og partnerskaber og dialog er vigtigere end nogen sinde før i en geopolitisk brydningstid. Regeringens udenrigs- og sikkerhedspolitiske\n strategi fremhæver, at Europas vægt i verden mindskes, mens andre lande og regioner vokser både økonomisk, befolkningsmæssigt og teknologisk. Det gælder også i Afrika, et kontinent i vækst, som både rummer et stort potentiale og omfattende udfordringer.\n\n \nOver de kommende måneder vil regeringen derfor stille skarpt på hvordan Danmarks og EU’s engagement med afrikanske partnere kan styrkes. Regeringen vil udarbejde\n en plan for dansk engagement i Afrika, der skal styre Danmarks indsats, og analysere hvordan der kan sikres stærkere samtænkning og styrkelse af danske tiltag gennem EU. Planen forventes lanceret i sommeren 2024. Målet er stærkere og mere ligeværdige partnerskaber\n for en bedre fælles fremtid. \n \nI den forbindelse inviterer Udenrigsministeriet til et kick-off arrangement, som vil finde sted\nmandag d. 11. marts kl. 10:15-12:15 i Dronningesalen, Den Sorte Diamant.\n \nHer vil statsministeren, udenrigsministeren og ministeren for udviklingssamarbejde og global klimapolitik præsentere overvejelserne for arbejdet. Afrikanske partnere\n forventes også at deltage i dialogen under arrangementet. \n \nIssa Jeppesen vil moderere arrangementet, herunder en paneldebat, der vil berøre, hvordan Danmark kan arbejde for ligeværdige partnerskaber med afrikanske lande,\n herunder gennem EU. Der forventes deltagelse fra en bred kreds af relevante aktører, herunder erhvervslivet, internationale organisationer, interesseorganisationer, tænketanke og civilsamfundsorganisationer. \n\n \nDette er ikke en personlig invitation, og der vil således være mulighed for at sende én stedfortræder til arrangementet, såfremt man er forhindret i at deltage.\n\n\nProgram vil kunne findes på \ndette tilmeldingssite i dagene op til arrangementet. \nUdenrigsministeriet samarbejder med Altingets Live-afdeling ARENA om afvikling af konferencen.\nVenligst bekræft deltagelse\n\nher senest den 4. marts.\n \nVenlig hilsen,\nKontor for Afrika, Policy og Finansiering (AFRPOL)\nUdenrigsministeriet\n\n \n_______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\n \nINVITATION\n \nKick-off: The Danish Government’s approach to strengthened engagement in Africa\n11 March 2024\n \nThe world is rapidly changing, and partnerships and dialogue are more important than ever in a new geopolitical reality. The government’s foreign\n and security policy emphasizes that Europe’s weight in the world is decreasing while other countries and regions are growing economically, population-wise and technologically. This also applies to Africa, a continent in growth with both great potential and\n extensive challenges. \n \nDuring the course of the coming months, the Danish government will undertake work to determine how Denmark’s and the EU’s engagement with African\n partners can be strengthened. This will lead to the establishment of a plan for strengthened Danish engagement with African partners, which will guide Denmark’s efforts going forward, including by analysing how stronger synergies between strengthened Danish\n actions and EU actions can be promoted. The plan is expected to be launched in the summer of 2024 with the aim of supporting stronger and more equal partnerships for a better shared future.\n\n \nIn relation to this, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs invites you to a kick-off event, which will take place on\nMonday, March 11, from 10:15-12:15 in Dronningesalen, The Black Diamond. \n \nThe Prime Minister, the Minister for Foreign Affairs, and the Minister for Development Cooperation and Global Climate Policy will present the Government’s\n reflections on the work ahead. High-level representation from invited African partners is also expected at the event.\n\n \nThe event will be moderated by journalist Issa Jeppesen, which will include a panel debate that will reflect upon how Denmark can work for strengthening\n equal partnerships with African countries, including through the EU. Participants are expected to include a wide range of relevant actors, including international organizations, business representatives, think tanks and civil society organizations. \n\n \nThis is not a personal invitation, and it will thus be possible to pass the invitation to a colleague, if you are prevented from participating.\n\n \nThe program will be available\n\non this site in the days leading up to the event.\n \nKindly confirm your attendance\n\nhere at the latest on 4th of march.\n \nThe Ministry of Foreign Affairs is collaborating with ARENA, the event department of Altinget on the organization of the conference.\n \nSincerely,\nDepartment for Africa, Development Policy, and Financing (AFRPOL)\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs of Denmark",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
