                new (
                    "00TQx0000075qy4MAA",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Follow-up on UNOPS/WFP/FAO mine action project proposal",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-21").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Follow-up on UNOPS/WFP/FAO mine action project proposal",
                        Description = "To: mrasmu@um.dk\nCC: aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org; annkah@um.dk; guy.rhodes@wfp.org; olgpob@um.dk; pjerik@um.dk; sahadn@um.dk; andreas.hansen@wfp.org; charlesf@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; janphilipk@unops.org; timl@unops.org; davidnm@unops.org; amiro@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Follow-up on UNOPS/WFP/FAO mine action project proposal\nBody:\nDear Marianne, \nThank you very much for your questions and your patience with us. \nPlease find below responses to your queries. If you have time, I would suggest that you and I briefly touch base tomorrow on the next steps. When would it be convenient for you? \n\nQ1: Will this project be registered as a separate project through the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine or whether it has already been registered as part of a multi-donor program.UNOPS registers projects following signing of a donor agreement; WFP does not register separately but the project will sit within the WFP/Gov Interim Country Strategic Plan (ICSP).\nQ2: Since our meeting in January, we have decided to allocate DKK 40 million to a multilateral partner and DKK 35 million as part of a civil society call for proposals. We consider this to be an initial allocation to a multi-annual engagement in mine action. Please let us know whether the allocation size for 2024 would result in any changes to the received proposal.The figure of DKK 40m is less than anticipated and therefore the project will have a scaled back ambition of outputs in the short term. We welcome the consideration that this may be multi-year engagement and therefore this reduced allocation will provide a strong platform for further implementation which will be more effective in terms of measuring mine action outcomes.\n\nWe would suggest to provide you with an updated and concrete proposal with scaled back output based on the reduced allocation, in which we can lay the foundation for a multi-year engagement with increased outputs as a result. \n\nQ3: Kindly let us know whether there would be any reservations at your end in terms of allocating funding through the UN Community Fund, which we are currently considering.While we greatly appreciate the idea of channelling funds via the UN Community Funds, this would add timelies, administrative burden and management fees. As a donor you would therefore end up paying a higher fee. Therefore we would suggest channeling the funds directly to UNOPS and WFP thereby getting more value for your money.\n\nQ4: What is the anticipated geographical split between Mykolaiv and other regions (Kharkiv) for this project?Implementation will be in Mykolaiv only for this specific project but can of course be widened in a multi-year engagement upon your requests. \n\nQ5: Are there any updates with regards to funding from other donors?We suggest that this specific engagement will only be sponsored by Denmark - contributing to Denmark's visibility and engagement in the Mykolaiv region. \n\nUNOPS will soon sign an agreement with Italy for Explosive Ordnance Disposal (EOD) capability in Mykolaiv region, to include a capacity development component with the National Police of Ukraine (NPU). \n\nWFP and FAO have several donors at the national level, including Croatia, France, Finland and Norway. These funds are not earmarked for a specific oblast but funds will be drawn on to complement Danish support to address objectives under this proposal. How this will be specifically allocated is yet to be defined.\n\nQ6: Could you provide for further details as to how this programme will align to agricultural cycles and seasonal deadlines (sowing, harvesting etc.). When is clearance of contaminated land expected to be cleared for farming and at what stage are involved farmers informed of the de-mining timeline? When do you expect that land confirmed as being uncontaminated to be released?The mobilisation and implementation of the project will not see benefits for the spring planting season; the outputs from the land release components will be generated in Q4 2024 and Q1 2025 (subject to the signing of the agreement during Q1 2024). This will benefit winter crops in 2024. Targeted households and farms may also receive cash and other context-specific support under Phase 3 to off-set losses caused by explosive contamination and help to prepare for the resumption of cultivation activities. Targeted households and farms will be informed of the mine action timelines according to priorities established under Phase 1.\n\nQ7: We understand that the FSD will be the main implementing partner. Kindly confirm that this understanding is correct and to what extent they are accredited to carry out the various stages of mine action.No. FSD is an implementing partner in Kharkiv Oblast under the wider WFP/FAO project. WFP will engage a separate international partner for mine action in Mykolaiv as well as a partner for the livelihood component. In addition, UNOPS will be considering other national partners for the mine action component.\n\nQ8: Who are the national NGOs/companies mentioned as preferred partner to deliver on selected land release priorities?WFP are considering the accredited international NGOs HALO Trust, MAG and/or Norwegian People’s Aid but are open to deconflict with any decisions regarding Danish support through the civil society component of your planned support. UNOPS are viewing national implementing partners to include Demining Solutions (DS), Ukrainian Demining Association (UDA) and Ukroboronservice.\n\nBest regards,Guy, Charles, David, Aleksandra and Asbjørn\nOn Wed, 21 Feb 2024 at 11:24, Marianne Rasmussen <mrasmu@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn, dear all,\n\n \nThank you very much. In addition to below questions we would be grateful if you could clarify whether this project will\n be registered as a separate project through the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine or whether it has already been registered as part of a multi-donor program. Also, if at all possible, we would welcome your initial feedback by tomorrow COB as we plan to move\n forward with a final decision on Friday. \n \nSincerely,\n\n \nMarianne\n \n \n\n\nFra: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSendt: 19. februar 2024 15:33\n\nTil: Marianne Rasmussen <mrasmu@um.dk>\n\nCc: Aleksandra KRAJCZYNSKA <aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org>; Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Charles FRISBY <charlesf@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Guy RHODES <guy.rhodes@wfp.org>; Jan Philip KLEVER <janphilipk@unops.org>; Olga Poberezhna\n <olgpob@um.dk>; Poul Jacob Erikstrup <pjerik@um.dk>; Sahil Adnan <sahadn@um.dk>; Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org>; andreas.hansen@wfp.org; davidmn@unops.org\n\nEmne: Re: Follow-up on UNOPS/WFP/FAO mine action project proposal\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply,\n click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Marianne\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you very much for your feedback and questions. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe will discuss internally between WFP and UNOPS and revert to you asap. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\nAsbjørn \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS\n HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, 19 Feb 2024 at 15.25, Marianne Rasmussen <mrasmu@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear David, Asbjørn and Andreas\n \nThank you again for a fruitful meeting and solid proposal some three weeks ago and for\n the subsequent follow up with Danish colleagues in Kyiv and Mykolaiv. Since our meeting in January, we have decided to allocate DKK 40 million to a multilateral partner and DKK 35 million as part of a civil society call for proposals. We consider this to be\n an initial allocation to a multi-annual engagement in mine action. Please let us know whether the allocation size for 2024 would result in any changes to the received proposal. Also, kindly note that we have yet to take a decision with regards to your request\n to split funds equally between UNOPS and WFP. Kindly let us know whether there would be any reservations at your end in terms of allocating funding through the UN Community Fund, which we are currently considering.\n\n \nIn addition, we have inserted a few questions to the received proposal and would welcome\n your comments in this respect:\n \n-     \nWhat is the anticipated geographical split between Mykolaiv and other regions (Kharkiv) for this project?\n-     \nAre there any updates with regards to funding from other donors?\n\n-     \nCould you provide for further details as to how this programme will align to agricultural cycles and seasonal deadlines (sowing, harvesting etc.). When is clearance\n of contaminated land expected to be cleared for farming and at what stage are involved farmers informed of the de-mining timeline? When do you expect that land confirmed as being uncontaminated to be released?  \n-     \nWe understand that the FSD will be the main implementing partner. Kindly confirm that this understanding is correct and to what extent they are accredited to carry\n out the various stages of mine action. \n-     \nWho are the national NGOs/companies mentioned as preferred partner to deliver on selected land release priorities?\n-     \nPhase 1 of the project is scheduled for implementation in Q1 – is the proposed project timeline on track? If not, we would be grateful to have an updated version?\n \n@Andreas – grateful if you could forward to Guy, as I do not have his contacts.\n\n \nWe look forward to hearing from you,\n\n \nAll the best,\n\n \nMarianne\n \n\n_______________________________________________________\n\n \n\nMARIANNE RASMUSSEN  /\nMRASMU@UM.DK\n\nSPECIALKONSULENT / EUN\n\nDIREKTE +4533920788\n\n \n\nUDENRIGSMINISTERIET\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 KØBENHAVN K\n\nTLF. +45 3392 0000",
