                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-22").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS - Gavi Africa Health Mission to Geneva - Bilateral Meetings",
                        Description = "To: mibrahim@gavi.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; eblanco@gavi.org; pdimattei@gavi.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS - Gavi Africa Health Mission to Geneva - Bilateral Meetings\nBody:\nDear MagdiGood to be in touch again! It has been a while since I left Gavi but great to keep in touch with old colleagues!Thanks for confirming that you would be happy to discuss Madagascar and Burundi with members of our AFR team who will be travelling to Geneva next week.Would 9.30 am on Thursday 29th February be convenient for you to meet at the Global Health Campus?Looking forward to hearing from youWith best wishesLouise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>\nDate: Tue, 20 Feb 2024 at 08:27\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>, Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\nCc: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>, Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>, Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>, Pietro Di Mattei <pdimattei@gavi.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n\n\n\nOur SCM Magdi Ibrahim is happy to discuss Madagascar and Burundi. Feel free to follow up with him directly. Copying Pietro who is the Regional Head for East and Southern Africa.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, we don’t have the bandwidth for a special session for the Core Countries team. It would be great if you could share a couple of slides on the work in the regions and potential opportunities, which I will share with the team. If\n there is interest to learn more and explore further we can connect you with the country teams accordingly. \n\n\n\nBest regards,\nColette \n\n\n\n\n\nSent from Outlook for iOS\n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSent: Monday, February 19, 2024 7:48 PM\n\nTo: Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n \n\n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Tokunbo and Amy\nThanks for confirming these three bilaterals - I have added Elena to work with Elodie to set these up. \n\n\n\n@Colette - Will we also be able the schedule a short “brown bag” session to cover the other 25 or so countries covered by our Senegal and DRC multi country offices ? \n\n\n\nThanks for letting us know asap\n\n\n\nThanks and best wishes \nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 19 Feb 2024 at 07:00, Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Amy,\n \nThis is to acknowledge receipt of your email and to confirm my interest in scheduling UNOPS bilateral meetings with my DRC, Ethiopia and Nigeria country teams. I have copied Elodie to directly follow-up with Louise in scheduling the proposed\n bilateral meetings. Thanks for the update on the Grant Agreement template.\n \nBest wishes,\nTokunbo\n \n\n\nFrom: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, February 13, 2024 7:41 AM\n\nTo: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>; Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \nDear Colette and Tokunbo,\n \nI’m reaching out to you as our UNOPS focal point, Louise Leech, would like to set up bilateral meetings with your teams to include the following countries: DRC, Ethiopia, Nigeria, Madagascar,  Angola, and Burundi.  I’ll let you all schedule\n as useful. \n \nAs an aside, we are working with UNOPS currently on a Grant Agreement template to ensure rapid contracting between our agencies moving forward and hope to have this finalized at the soonest.  It’s currently going back and forth between\n lawyers to engage and finalize the Terms and Conditions.  I’ll keep you updated as it nears finalization.\n\n \nSincerely,\nAmy\n \nAmy LaTrielle (she/her/hers)\n\n \n\n\n \nDirector, Fragile and Conflict Segment, Country Programmes Department\n\nMobile: +41 79 201 50 33\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / X\n (Twitter) /\nLinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n \n\n \nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or\n its partners. \nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail,\n and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy the e-mail or any attachment.",
