                        Description = "To: toshin@gavi.org\nCC: cselman@gavi.org; eblanco@gavi.org; elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\nBody:\nDear TokunboGreat to hear from you and hope you are well!For the DRC discussion, would Thursday 29th Feb at the Global Health Campus from 10.30 - 11.15 be convenient for you?Thanks for letting me knowBest wishes Louise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Mon, 19 Feb 2024 at 08:00, Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Amy,\n \nThis is to acknowledge receipt of your email and to confirm my interest in scheduling UNOPS bilateral meetings with my DRC, Ethiopia and Nigeria country teams. I have copied Elodie to directly follow-up with Louise in scheduling the proposed\n bilateral meetings. Thanks for the update on the Grant Agreement template.\n \nBest wishes,\nTokunbo\n \n\n\nFrom: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, February 13, 2024 7:41 AM\n\nTo: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>; Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \nDear Colette and Tokunbo,\n \nI’m reaching out to you as our UNOPS focal point, Louise Leech, would like to set up bilateral meetings with your teams to include the following countries: DRC, Ethiopia, Nigeria, Madagascar,  Angola, and Burundi.  I’ll let you all schedule\n as useful. \n \nAs an aside, we are working with UNOPS currently on a Grant Agreement template to ensure rapid contracting between our agencies moving forward and hope to have this finalized at the soonest.  It’s currently going back and forth between\n lawyers to engage and finalize the Terms and Conditions.  I’ll keep you updated as it nears finalization.\n\n \nSincerely,\nAmy\n \nAmy LaTrielle (she/her/hers)\n\n \n\n\n \nDirector, Fragile and Conflict Segment, Country Programmes Department\n\nMobile: +41 79 201 50 33\nFollow us:\nFacebook /\nX (Twitter) /\nLinkedIn /\nInstagram /\n#VaccinesWork\n \n\n \nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners.\n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please\n do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy the e-mail or any attachment.",
