                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Ghana Global Fund",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-02-22").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Ghana Global Fund",
                        Description = "To: ifeomacm@unops.org\nCC: dalilag@unops.org; elenage@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Ghana Global Fund\nBody:\nDear IfeomaHope all is well with you? Can you please advise the status of the Global Fund engagement in Ghana. I heard today from GF side that \"there may be an issue\" - can you advise me on this?  We want to be ready / get ahead of any potential difficult conversation here in Geneva next week.Thanks and best wishesLouise \n\nOn Wed, 8 Mar 2023 at 05:56, Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nDear IfeomaThanks for the additional information, this is really helpful. Would you like me to speak with the Geneva Ghana team or Regional Head to see what the problem is with the funding ?  Are you already in touch with the Fund Portfolio Manager ? Looking forward to hearing from you Best wishes Louise \n\nOn Tue, 7 Mar 2023 at 21:31, Ifeoma Esther Charles-Monwuba <ifeomacm@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Louise,\nThanks for reaching out. \nWe have two GF’s funded procurement of HIV test kits Projects currently being implemented by the Ghana office. The first: Procurement of 476,100 units of test kits for the Christian Health Association of Ghana (CHAG). That has been running since September 2022.\nThe second, which one signed in February 2023, to procure 2,060,000 units of test kits for the Ghana Health services. That project is currently in its operational phase. Our major hold-back now has to do with funds transfer which appears to be taking a while. The GF has therefore requested UNOPS to pre-finance in the interim. In this regard, we will be submitting an application for advance financing soon to allow us to take off asap in view of the urgency around the items.\nWe will continue to push for greater engagement with GF. We are looking to explore engagement with them in the Tuberculosis space.\nBest RegardsIfeoma \n\n Ifeoma Charles-Monwuba | Director/Representative | Africa Region| Ghana Multi-Country Office- Gambia, Ghana, Liberia, Nigeria, Sierra Leone | Accra, Ghana | Tel: +233 501 516 156, +233 59 386 8084 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\nOn Mon, Mar 6, 2023 at 8:27 AM Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Ifeoma!I hope this finds you well and congratulations on your new LDG5 video - great stuff!  shared widely :)\nOn Global Fund, I see a procurement of HIV kits project dating from September - is all going OK with this - anything I can do to support?Here is the GF overview of the Ghana portfolio, if not already seen: \n\nLooking forward to speaking again soon!\nBest wishes LouiseLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  | Global project overview here  | Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n-- \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  | Global project overview here  | Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
