                        Subject = "Email: Re: [EXT] WHO GPEI geographies of concern - UNOPS update",
                        Description = "To: olearya@who.int\nCC: elenali@unops.org; fouste@who.int\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: [EXT] WHO GPEI geographies of concern - UNOPS update\nBody:\nDear AidanGreat thanks duly noted.For E DRC meeting, the plan will be for you to outline the needs and for our team to share their current, related activities - zero dose / last mile, then discuss how we can support your priorities in this area.All best wishesLouise\n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 13:03, O'LEARY, Aidan <olearya@who.int> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks Louise,\n\n\n\nWell copied and understood, I will be happy to do five meetings rather than if this is more helpful - I copy Eva who is best placed to assist with scheduling.  For tomorrow, it would be helpful to confirm the focus of the meeting  currently\n scheduled.\n\n\n\nBest regards\nAidan \n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 11:52 a.m.\n\nTo: O'LEARY, Aidan <olearya@who.int>\n\nCc: Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>\n\nSubject: [EXT] WHO GPEI geographies of concern - UNOPS update\n \n\n\n\nDear Aidan\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAhead of our meeting tomorrow on Polio Eradication efforts in eastern DRC, I wanted to provide a short update:\n\n\n\n\n\nI would like to set up 5 meetings (unless you want to tackle all geographies together?) for Pakistan, S. Somalia, NW Nigeria, Myanmar and Angola, where our UNOPS country teams have confirmed capacity / expertise and are keen to work with you/GPEI\n\n\n\n\n\nAs background, attached please find a short update from Myanmar (understandably vague, pls don't share widely) and from Pakistan.\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease suggest a few times / dates that work for you and we can set up the call(s).\n\n\n\n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you\n\nBest wishes Louise \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
