                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS Gavi - Benin / Cote d'Ivoire",
                        Description = "To: mdaget@gavi.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; elenage@unops.org; jakobt@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi - Benin / Cote d'Ivoire\nBody:\nDear Morgane\nGreat to meet you last week and good you are in touch with our regional / multi country team now - here in copy.  Sorry we missed Komi Ahawo and Alain, but we would be happy to reconvene online to continue the discussion on the outcomes / recommendations of the full portfolio planning exercise in Benin. \nIn the meantime, please find below some additional capacity statements for the areas we discussed for your background. For information, we are currently discussing with Gavi Legal team, a bilateral framework agreement that should be ready soon, this should help provide the enabling environment for UNOPS to provide some additional support and capacity as needed esp in Benin.\nFeel free to reach out any time and we look forward to reconnecting soon.\nAll best wishesLouise\nUNOPS_Capacity_Statement_Health_ProcurementUNOPS capacity building for Health ProgrammesHealth Facilities Capacity Statement UNOPSHealth Supply Chain management Capacity Statement \n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 11:58, Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi again,\nIt will be in GHC-L1-6-Ashoka\nAll other room onL2 are fully booked that morning.\n \nMorgane\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 11:39 AM\n\nTo: Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Souad Hesse <shesse@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Gavi bilaterals / Thu 29 Feb 2024 / UNOPS and Core Countries (Gavi)\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Morgane\n\n\nThanks this should be fine. Please confirm if meeting room L2 13 a is still available!\n\nBest wishes Louise\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 11:30, Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks Louise.\nCan we make it 10 am if possible?\nMorgane (Benin)\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 10:33 AM\n\nTo: Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org>; Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Souad Hesse <shesse@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi bilaterals / Thu 29 Feb 2024 / UNOPS and Core Countries (Gavi)\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Morgane and Danielle - and San (sorry I don't seem to have San's email - pls kindly transmit)\n\n\n \n\n\nWould it be possible to meet around 09.30 to 10.30 to discuss Guinea\n / Benin / Guinea Bissau ?\n\n\n \n\n\nWe can share a bit of our work on Zero Dose / last mile we are doing for MOH / Gavi in DRC to see if\n our support in health system strengthening (health infra / procurement / solarisation etc) can be of use to you.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe are meeting Thierry before you in room L2-13b if this would still be available to save some time\n :)\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you / meeting tomorrow.\n\n\n\nBest wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 10:19, Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nI will be in the office tomorrow.\nMorning would work best for me as we have our team meeting in the afternoon (same for San and Danielle actually as we are on the same team).\n \nAwaiting to hear from you, Morgane\n \n\n\nFrom: Souad Hesse <shesse@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 9:53 AM\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nCc: Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Aideen Bolger Imparato (Consultant) <abolger@gavi.org>;\n Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>; Souad Hesse <shesse@gavi.org>; Marius Keller <mkeller@gavi.org>;\n Seydou Mohamed Ouedraogo (Consultant) <souedraogo@gavi.org>; Morgane Daget <mdaget@gavi.org>; Komi Ahawo <kahawo@gavi.org>;\n Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>; Marthe Essengue Elouma <messengue@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS Gavi bilaterals / Thu 29 Feb 2024 / UOPS and Core Countries (Gavi)\n\n\n \n\nDear Louise, \n\n \n\nI am pleased to e-meet you. \n\n \n\nProgram Managers and Senior Country Managers for Core Countries are:\n\n \n\n\nGuinea : PM\nSan M. Njona / SCM: Marius Keller\nBenin: PM: Morgane Daget / SCM: Komi Ahawo\nGuinea-Bissau: PM Danielle Rosset / SCM: Seydou Ouedraogo\n \n \nKindly note that Marius, Seydou and Komi are not available this week. I suggest you reach out to San, Morgane and Danielle and check their availability to attend the bilateral tomorrow.\n \nWith best regards,\nSouad\n \n \n \nSouad Hesse\n(Sue-Ad Hess-Seh) (she/her)\n\n \n\n\n \n\nSenior Administrative Assistant, Core Countries, Country Programmes Delivery\n\nMobile: +41 78 605 84 06\n\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / Twitter\n / LinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n\n \n\n \n\nGlobal Health Campus\n\nChemin du Pommier 40\n\n1218 Le Grand-Saconnex\n\nSwitzerland\n\n \n\nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners.\n\n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy\n the e-mail or any attachment\n \n \n\n\nFrom: Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, February 23, 2024 3:56 PM\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>;\n Aideen Bolger Imparato (Consultant) <abolger@gavi.org>; Souad Hesse <shesse@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS Gavi bilaterals\n\n\n \nGood afternoon Louise,\n \nThank you for your email.\n \nAs I support Tokunbo Oshin and his team of the High Impact countries, I am putting you in contact with me colleagues who support the Directors of the other two teams and their team\n members. Here there are:\n \n\n\nConflict and Fragile countries – Amy La Trielle (Director) > Aideen Bolger (assistant)\nCore countries – Colette Selman (Director) > Souad Hesse (assistant)\n \nI believe they will be able to put you in contact with the SCM and the PM of the following countries for a possible meeting next week:\n\n\n\nGuinea : PM\nSan M. Njona / SCM: Marius Keller\nNiger:\n\nBenin: PM: Morgane Daget / SCM: Komi Ahawo\nChad \nGuinea-Bissau: PM Danielle Rosset / SCM: Seydou Ouedraogo\n \nThank you\n@Aideen Bolger and\n@Souad Hesse for your help with this. For your information,\nUNOPS team is hoping to come to the GHC on Thursday 29th for a meeting with Jean Bernard on DRC. So maybe if the SCM/PMs are available on those days we could group all the meetings one after the other.  \n Thanks for passing the information to your colleagues.\n \nThank you\n \n\nElodie Blanco\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, February 23, 2024 3:44 PM\n\nTo: Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi bilaterals\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nHi Elodie\n\n\nAny chance you can help us also set up bilats with SCMs for Guinea Niger Benin Chad and Guinea-Bissau - or group some together if that's\n more convenient? Could we target Wednesday afternoon from 3.30 pm onwards\n\n\n\nThanks so much for your support! Best wishes Louise\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / United Nations Office for Services Project Management Unit\n\n\nGlobal project overview here|  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx000007mNOBMA2",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "eblanco@gavi.org", "abolger@gavi.org", "messengue@gavi.org", "jakobt@unops.org", "shesse@gavi.org", "elenali@unops.org", "mdaget@gavi.org", "drosset@gavi.org", "kahawo@gavi.org", "elenage@unops.org", "louisel@unops.org", "souedraogo@gavi.org", "mkeller@gavi.org" },
