                new (
                    "00TQx000007mQYzMAM",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS Gavi DRC follow up",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS Gavi DRC follow up",
                        Description = "To: jlegargasson@gavi.org\nCC: eblanco@gavi.org; toshin@gavi.org; elenali@unops.org; cnogier@gavi.org; tatianaw@unops.org; fionam@unops.org; elenage@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi DRC follow up\nBody:\nDear Jean-Bernard\n\nGreat to meet you last week in Geneva with the team - and sorry to miss @Tokunbo Oshin ! (saw him fleetingly yesterday :)  \nI was really happy to hear that UNOPS was able to help diagnose some of the cold chain problems and help the roadmap of what needs to be done. It will be good to see the outcomes of the FPP - on that - were you able to connect Fiona with the subgroup to feed into that session?Hope we can also progress the conversation around all those health centres that desperately need equipment!\n\"Courage\" for the next phase and do keep in touch. In the meantime pls find below a few capacity statements that may be of interest - feel free to share with your colleagues :) \nFinally, we met with Amy and your legal team this morning, we are close to finalising a bilateral framework agreement that should greatly facilitate our collaboration across countries in future. Will keep you posted on that one.\nWishing you all a restful weekend and thanks again for your time and hospitality last week :) Best wishes Louise \nUNOPS_Capacity_Statement_Health_ProcurementHealth Supply Chain Management Capacity Statement UNOPS Health Facilities Capacity Statement UNOPS Solar for health capacity statement UNOPS \nDigital Health Capacity Statement \n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 10:58, Jean-Bernard Le Gargasson <jlegargasson@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi colleauges\n10.30 am tomorrow at GHC works for a meeting with UNOPS team\nAll best,\nJean-Bernard\n \n\n\nFrom: Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org> \n\nSent: Friday, February 23, 2024 10:57 AM\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Jean-Bernard Le Gargasson <jlegargasson@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Cyril Nogier <cnogier@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \nDear Louise,\n \nActually Cyril and Jean Bernard are both on leave this week.\nJean Bernard is back on Monday so he can get back to Elena with his availabilities. In a separate email Elena had suggested the 29th February for an in person meeting. Is this date still an option?\n \n@Jean-Bernard Le Gargasson When I look at your calendar it seems that on 29th\n February, anytime between 9h and 12h would work but please get back to Louise Leech/Elena Librino with your availabilities.\n \nThank you very much and kind regards,\n \n\nElodie Blanco\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, February 23, 2024 10:18 AM\n\nTo: Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Cyril Nogier <cnogier@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nHi Elodie\n\n\nThanks for your update and shame we will miss Tokunbo.\n\n\nPlease can you set up the meeting with Cyril and Jean Bernard to discuss DRC as we have not heard back from them. \n\n\nWe revert on ETH and Nigeria as our UNOPS country directors for these countries are not coming to Geneva, so we can fix these calls up separately.\n\n\nThanks so much for your help!\n\n\nBest wishes Louise and Elena \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 22 Feb 2024 at 17:50, Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nGood afternoon Louise,\n \nUnfortunately Tokunbo will not be available for this call next week as he will be on duty travel in Togo along with several other members of the leadership team of Gavi.\nI have been in touch separately with Elena and provided her the names and emails of the Senior Country Managers and Programme Managers of DRC, Ethiopia and Nigeria.\n \nTokunbo has agreed the discussion can take place without him and I believe Elena has already been in touch with them.\n \nDo not hesitate to reach out if I can help any further with those meetings.\n \nKind regards,\n \n\nElodie Blanco\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, February 22, 2024 1:44 PM\n\nTo: Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>; Elodie Blanco <eblanco@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Tokunbo\n\n\nGreat to hear from you and hope you are well!\n\n\nFor the DRC discussion, would Thursday 29th Feb at the Global Health Campus from 10.30 - 11.15 be convenient for you?\n\n\nThanks for letting me know\n\n\nBest wishes Louise \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, 19 Feb 2024 at 08:00, Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Amy,\n \nThis is to acknowledge receipt of your email and to confirm my interest in scheduling UNOPS bilateral meetings with my DRC, Ethiopia and Nigeria country teams. I have copied Elodie\n to directly follow-up with Louise in scheduling the proposed bilateral meetings. Thanks for the update on the Grant Agreement template.\n \nBest wishes,\nTokunbo\n \n\n\nFrom: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, February 13, 2024 7:41 AM\n\nTo: Colette Selman <cselman@gavi.org>; Tokunbo Oshin <toshin@gavi.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS Bilateral Meetings\n\n\n \nDear Colette and Tokunbo,\n \nI’m reaching out to you as our UNOPS focal point, Louise Leech, would like to set up bilateral meetings with your teams to include the following countries: DRC, Ethiopia, Nigeria, Madagascar, \n Angola, and Burundi.  I’ll let you all schedule as useful. \n \nAs an aside, we are working with UNOPS currently on a Grant Agreement template to ensure rapid contracting between our agencies moving forward and hope to have this finalized at\n the soonest.  It’s currently going back and forth between lawyers to engage and finalize the Terms and Conditions.  I’ll keep you updated as it nears finalization.\n\n \nSincerely,\nAmy\n \n\nAmy LaTrielle (she/her/hers)\n\n \n\n\n \n\nDirector, Fragile and Conflict Segment, Country Programmes Department\n\n\nMobile: +41 79 201 50 33\n\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / X\n (Twitter) /\nLinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n \n\n \nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create\n any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners. \n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy\n the e-mail or any attachment.",
