                    {
                        Name = "Email: Catch up UNOPS/ Global Fund",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Catch up UNOPS/ Global Fund",
                        Description = "To: Helene.GaudinDeVillaine@theglobalfund.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Catch up UNOPS/ Global Fund\nBody:\nDear Hélène\nThank you so much for your message and reaffirming GFA commitment to get the LFA agreement over the line. Yes indeed this has been a protracted negotiation due to a number of reasons which we have been discussing, and some additional reviews on our side related to the unfortunate PNG situation.\nNotwithstanding you should receive our proposed revisions on the draft today in order for us to regroup next week and hopefully finalise the discussion!\n\nI will revert shortly on the regular meeting update that we agreed when we came to see you at GHC on 1 February so we can kick 2024 off with a more holistic view / review across our engagements! \nAll best wishesLouise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Wed, 6 Mar 2024 at 14:30, Hélène Gaudin De Villaine <Helene.GaudinDeVillaine@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nThanks again for the discussion yesterday.\n\n \nI just wanted to follow up on the meeting that we were suggesting organizing between 17 and 30 April and check if you have been able to coordinate with your colleagues so that we\n can agree on a date. \n \nFollowing yesterday’s discussion and the comments on the time that this negotiation is taking, I wanted to take the opportunity to re-affirm our commitment to get this LFA agreement\n over the line as showed throughout our constant engagement and follow up to finalize this contract before the end of the extension.\n \nAs you will recall Maia sent the LFA agreement with our comments on 17 January and a meeting had been scheduled on 19 January but was canceled by UNOPS.\nWe then met on 1 February at the GHC and the following day Maia sent an email with several slots to discuss the content of the agreement. We got a response from UNOPS on 6 February\n offering to discuss on 13 February. After the 13 February meeting, Maia sent an invite to set up another meeting on 16 February and shared a revised draft contract on 15 February. The meeting was cancelled as Maryam was sick, and Maia followed up on 26 February\n to reschedule the call, which took place yesterday. Unfortunately, no revised draft has been shared by UNOPS since 15 February and the travel policies deviations were only shared on 5 March.\n \nFor UNOPS and the Global Fund to finalize the agreement shortly, we would be very grateful if UNOPS could share their proposed revisions on the draft agreement ASAP (ideally today\n or by tomorrow COB), and at any rate before we set up another meeting, so that we can expedite the review from our end.\n \nThanks again for your collaboration and support.\n \nBest,\n \nHélène\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHélène Gaudin De Villaine\nLegal Counsel\nLegal & Governance\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41 76 396 27 86\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhelene.gaudindevillaine@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, February 14, 2024 8:55 AM\n\nTo: Hélène Gaudin De Villaine <Helene.GaudinDeVillaine@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Natacha Heffinck <Natacha.Heffinck@theglobalfund.org>; Maia Okruashvili <Maia.Okruashvili@theglobalfund.org>; Shevone Corbin <Shevone.Corbin@theglobalfund.org>; Alexander Andwati <Alexander.Andwati@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: Catch up UNOPS/ Global Fund\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Hélène\n\n\n \n\n\nLikewise! and apologies I had to leave the LFA discussion before it ended, but I understand the team is regrouping this Friday.\n\n\n \n\n\nRegarding regular catch ups, absolutely, I will coordinate with local and HQ colleagues and we will set these up regularly going forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nFor your further information, we have a small delegation from two of our Africa multi country offices coming to Geneva, and I am working with Francesco Moschetta and his team\n to organise a 90 minute interactive \"brown bag\" session, and a few country specific bilaterals where we have ongoing collaborations. This is scheduled for the morning of 27th February, in case you see this information around, and please feel free to join us\n :)\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to a productive collaboration in 2024 and beyond!\n\n\n \n\n\nBest wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 14 Feb 2024 at 08:28, Hélène Gaudin De Villaine <Helene.GaudinDeVillaine@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nI hope you are doing well. It was nice to see you yesterday and we are glad that the negotiations are making good progress.\nAs agreed in January, regular meetings between UNOPS and the Global Fund would be helpful to strengthen our partnership and to resolve\n issues.\n \nWe were thinking of April for the first meeting – between the 17 and 30 April ( that is after the school holidays in Geneva).\nOur Finance colleagues, cc to this email, will be attending as well.\nOur preference would be to meet in the morning if possible and to avoid Wednesdays.\n\n \nCould you kindly liaise with the relevant colleagues within UNOPS and propose a few dates?\n\n \nMany thanks\n \nKind regards,\n \nHélène\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHélène Gaudin De Villaine\nLegal Counsel\nLegal & Governance\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41\n 76 396 27 86\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhelene.gaudindevillaine@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nGlobal Health Campus | Chemin du Pommier 40 | 1218 Grand-Saconnex | Geneva, Switzerland",
