                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Gavi UNOPS meeting - Angola",
                        Description = "To: jeitokpah@gavi.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; anader@gavi.org; mariscaljorge@gmail.com; nnathani@gavi.org; elenage@unops.org; rodriguespaulon@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Gavi UNOPS meeting - Angola\nBody:\nDear JemimahGreat to hear from you and thanks so much to you and Narayan your time and hospitality at GHC last week!Sorry we could make the technology work, but it is great the teams are connected with Nuno now!Please see below capacity statements as discussed - feel free to share with colleagues - and thanks so much for the slide deck - very much appreciated and great to see how the MIC team works a bit differently!Happy to catch up any time - feel free to reach out.Thanks and best wishesLouise \nUNOPS Capacity Statement - Health supply chain managementUNOPS capacity building for health UNOPS_Capacity_Statement_Health_ProcurementHealth Facilities Capacity Statement UNOPS\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Mon, 4 Mar 2024 at 19:04, Jemimah Eitokpah (Consultant) <jeitokpah@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louis, colleagues,\n \nI hope this email finds you well. \n \nIt was a pleasure meeting you and the team on Thursday. Thank you once again for the time dedicated to considering possible areas of collaboration with UNOPS for Angola.\n \nPlease find summary meeting notes from our discussion and agreed next steps also included below. I have also attached the presentation from Thursday as requested and a document summarising our current support to Angola.\n\n \nLooking forward to a continued conversation, and to also receive UNOPS capacity statement.\n \nNext Steps \n\n                    \nI.UNOPS will connect Nuno (in-country Angola) with the Gavi MIC Country Liaison Officer based in Angola (done via email). \n\n                 \nII.UNOPS will share a capacity statement with Gavi. \n\n                \nIII.Gavi to share Presentation Slides with UNOPS and context on support covered by Gavi for Angola (see attached)\n\n               \nIV.Partnership possibilities to be considered towards 6.0 (consider a follow-up meeting soon online). \n \n \nThanks, and Kind regards,\nJemimah Eitokpah\n\n \n\n\nProgramme Manager, Middle Income Countries\nEmail:\njeitokpah@gavi.org\nWeb: Gavi.org\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / Twitter\n / LinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n \n\n \nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may\n be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners.\n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately\n by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy the e-mail or any attachment.\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 12:31 PM\n\nTo: Jemimah Eitokpah (Consultant) <jeitokpah@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Alice Nader (Consultant) <anader@gavi.org>; Jorge Mariscal Padilla <mariscaljorge@gmail.com>; Narayan Nathani <nnathani@gavi.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Caitlin Longden <clongden@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Gavi UNOPS meeting - Angola\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDuly noted, many thanks Jemimah. We look forward to meeting you tomorrow.\n\n\nBest wishes Louise \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 28 Feb 2024 at 12:26, Jemimah Eitokpah (Consultant) <jeitokpah@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise, colleagues,\n \nThank you very much for your reaching out and for your proposition to meet tomorrow.\n \nI, as well as two of my colleagues in copy working on the Angola portfolio would be able to make out time for the proposed meeting at 11:15 am tomorrow. However, please note that\n the Senior Country Manager for Angola \n@Alice Nader (Consultant) is out of office for the proposed time.\n \nI have secured the\nGHC-L2-20-Room for the meeting- please do not hesitate to reach out for directions in accessing the meeting room location if needed.\n \nAdditionally, as we are unaware of earlier emails sent in this regard (referred to below), further insight for us will be useful.\n \n \nThanks, and Kind regards,\nJemimah Eitokpah\n\n\n \n\n\n\nProgramme Manager, Middle Income Countries\n\nEmail:\njeitokpah@gavi.org\n\nWeb: Gavi.org\n\nFollow us:\nFacebook\n / Twitter\n / LinkedIn\n / Instagram\n / #VaccinesWork\n \n\n \n\nNOTICE: This e-mail, including any attachments to it, may be confidential and does not create any binding contract on behalf of Gavi or its partners.\n\n\nIf this e-mail was sent to you in error, please notify the sender immediately by reply e-mail, and please do not use, distribute, retain, print or copy\n the e-mail or any attachment.\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, February 28, 2024 11:10 AM\n\nTo: Jemimah Eitokpah (Consultant) <jeitokpah@gavi.org>; Caitlin Longden <clongden@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Gavi UNOPS meeting - Angola\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Caitlin and Jemimah\n\n\n \n\n\nYou may have seen earlier emails and we were wondering if you are available for a short meeting tomorrow at GHC around\n 11.15 with my Africa Regional colleagues who are covering around 35 countries between them including Angola?\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you and apologies for late notice!\n\n\n\nThanks and Best wishes \n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
