                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Mine action event in the UN City",
                        Description = "To: sarahdg@unops.org\nCC: waingchita@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; paulom@unops.org; hilaryb@unops.org; oonaa@unops.org; annag@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; amiro@unops.org; charlesf@unops.org; stellairinik@unops.org; nadiamo@unops.org; timl@unops.org; peterb@unops.org; tomco@unops.org; janil@unops.org; aikaterinis@unops.org; hannahsr@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Mine action event in the UN City\nBody:\nHi Sarah,\nAs previously mentioned, we are aiming to organise a demining event here at the UN City together with the WFP before the summer holiday. \nWe hope that the event could take place late May or early June. Would it be possible for you to provide me with a few dates that I could relay to the Danes to see when the Minister for Development Cooperation and Global Climate (Dan Jørgensen) would be available?   \nFor Jorge's review, please find here a draft concept note for the event, that we have coordinated with WFP at working level. \nThe objective of the demining event would be to:Announce a new demining engagement in Ukraine funded by Denmark and implemented by WFP and UNOPS. Raise awareness of the extensive challenges in mine action, illustrate the profound repercussion of mines on civilians with a specific focus on Ukraine.\nIncrease awareness of UNOPS' and WFP's demining capacities. Jorge would have a key role as the host by opening the event, signing the new engagement with the Danish minister and providing the closing remarks. We also hope for some media interests given the tangible stories, a new engagement and being able to showcase our demining capacities. This should make it possible to organise eg. a common interview with Jorge and the Danish minister. \nWe hope that we will be able to bring a survivor of a mine incident to the event to tell that person's story. We also aim to bring in a UNOPS demining expert who could showcase a dummy version of a mine. Finally we hope to bring in a bomb sniffing dog from one of our teams in the field.\nBut first things first: We need to settle on a date. Once we have some suggested dates, we will coordinate with the Danes to book their minister. \nAs always - happy to discuss! \nBest,AsbjørnAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
