                new (
                    "00TQx000007zHRUMA2",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: Revised UNOPS/WFP mine action project proposal",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-13").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: Revised UNOPS/WFP mine action project proposal",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: guy.rhodes@wfp.org; stellairinik@unops.org; andreas.hansen@wfp.org; aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org; michela.carucci@wfp.org; luke.irving@wfp.org; charlesf@unops.org; davidnm@unops.org; amiro@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; timl@unops.org; janphilipk@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; ejonab@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; annkah@um.dk\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Revised UNOPS/WFP mine action project proposal\nBody:\nDear Asbjorn, dear all\n \nThank you for your effort and time in drafting the attached proposal, answering questions and meeting with us. After careful\n consideration we have decided to proceed with another option. As previously communicated, we envision the present allocation to be an initial contribution to mine action and hope to be able to continue support to this important field in the years to come.\n Once materialized, we would be happy to share our forthcoming plans in this regard and look forward to continuing our excellent cooperation in Ukraine.   \n \nSincerely,\n\n \nMarianne\n \n_______________________________________________________\n \nMARIANNE RASMUSSEN  /\nMRASMU@UM.DK\nSPECIALKONSULENT / EUN\nDIREKTE +4533920788\n \nUDENRIGSMINISTERIET\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 KØBENHAVN K\nTLF. +45 3392 0000\n \n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 11. marts 2024 13:45\n\nTo: Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Marianne Rasmussen <mrasmu@um.dk>\n\nCc: Guy RHODES <guy.rhodes@wfp.org>; Charles FRISBY <charlesf@unops.org>; Stella Irini KABURIS <stellairinik@unops.org>; David McMahon <davidnm@unops.org>; Amir OMERAGIC <amiro@unops.org>; Andreas HANSEN <andreas.hansen@wfp.org>; Aleksandra KRAJCZYNSKA\n <aleksandra.krajczynska@wfp.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org>; Michela CARUCCI <michela.carucci@wfp.org>; Jan Philip KLEVER <janphilipk@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Ejona BAKALLI <ejonab@unops.org>;\n Luke IRVING <luke.irving@wfp.org>; Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ <teresam@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Revised UNOPS/WFP mine action project proposal\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply,\n click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Anne and Marianne,  \n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached to this email an updated and elaborated common WFP/UNOP project proposal for mine action in rural communities in Mykolaiv. \n\n\n \n\n\nI apologize sincerely for the delay in transmitting the updated proposal based on the revised budget. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs you will see from the attached, we have updated the budget to be 5.8 million USD split evenly between WFP and UNOPS. We have also summarized the intended outcome into three groups (see page 9 and 13ff in the attached): \n\n\n\n\nOutcome 1: Prioritisation of which rural communities and farms should be prioritised for project support. \nOutcome 2: Prioritised rural communities will receive extensive mine action operational responses to identify and clear mines, education, equipment etc. \nOutcome 3: Assistance to rural households to reassume agricultural production. \n\nWe estimate that approx. 50,000 individuals will benefit from the mine action activities and that approx. 1,000 will benefit from the livelihood support. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nAs requested we have drafted the proposal in such a way that the project can be expanded to a multi-year project via potential future budgetary allocations. If so - the number of estimated beneficiaries would of course increase.  \n\n\n \n\n\nWe are very proud to present this common proposal showcasing the OneUN approach and utilizing the synergies of WFP's food security capacities and UNOPS' infrastructure and development capacities to the benefit of the citizens of Mykolaiv.\n\n\n \n\n\nCould I suggest that we touch base at a meeting for the next steps once you have read the proposal? In the meantime we obviously remain at your entire disposal to answer any questions. \n\n\n \n\n\nOn behalf of the WFP and UNOPS teams. \n\n\n \n\n\n/Asbjørn  \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS\n HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
