                    new List<string> { "naimoh@unops.org" },
                    new List<string> { "B0047" }
                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000008ZPIIMA4",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Draft Framework Agreement btwn UNOPS and Gavi",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-03-27").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Draft Framework Agreement btwn UNOPS and Gavi",
                        Description = "To: lgabus@gavi.org\nCC: ipetkova@gavi.org; elenali@unops.org; ekaterinapo@unops.org; alatrielle@gavi.org; devorahfd@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Draft Framework Agreement btwn UNOPS and Gavi\nBody:\nDear Laurent, colleaguesThanks again for the review and updates.  Would you all be available during the morning of 3 April for a follow up meeting? If not, please kindly provide some alternative options. Looking forward to hearing from youWith thanks and best wishesLouise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Fri, 22 Mar 2024 at 15:20, Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Ekaterina,\n\n\n\n\n\nAfter internal review and confirmation, please find enclosed a revised draft template. I have cleaned agreed wording/comments and the open issues are highlighted, notably on financial reporting. We have done our best to accommodate UNOPS, but Gavi cannot agree\n on all points (see our track changes and remarks).\n\n\n\n\n\nHave a nice weekend!\n\n\n\n\n\nLaurent \n\n\nDe : Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>\n\nEnvoyé : jeudi, 14 mars 2024 13:31\n\nÀ : Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\nCc : Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nObjet : Re: Draft Framework Agreement btwn UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\n\n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear\n Laurent and Collegues \n\n\nThank\n you for the meeting last week. We finally managed to get relevant inputs from internal practices and are kindly sharing with you the UNOPS marked-up version of the draft framework agreement template. In addition, as briefly discussed last week, below is additional\n background information on UNOPS red lines. Once Gavi has a chance to consider UNOPS comments, we would be happy to receive Gavi revised version, pending which it would be good to have a call to hopefully resolve outstanding issues, if any. \n\n\nOverall\n comment\n\n\nWhile\n UNOPS always intends to collaborate with its funding sources and and partners to ensure that funds are used in a principled manner, UNOPS, due to its status as a self-financed (not receiving UN assessed budgetary contributions), UN system organization, and\n its obligation to follow the UN Principles in harmony with its other UN system organizations,\nit\n cannot agree to be bound to the GAVI rules and regulations and policies.\n The edits made to the document reflect these limitations which in particular impact the Annexes C and E and the Audit and Investigation requirements, including obligations relating to Misuse of funds and liability in relation to third parties. It is to be\n also noted that current tripartite agreements between UNOPS, GAVI and Governments, whereas UNOPS implements projects in Africa, are subject to UNOPS Standard Project Terms and Conditions. \n\n\nSpecific\n comments \n\n\n\n\n\nAnnex C and E:\nReference to GAVI-specific\n templates and policies are difficult for UNOPS to automatically follow as UNOPS has its own UN Principles and obligations to follow that stem from its legal status as a subsidiary organ of the United Nations. UNOPS has a requirement to harmonize its approach\n under the UN framework, but also cannot agree to be bound to comply with every funding sources’ policies and framework as it would limit UNOPS ability to independently and autonomously work and operate in fragile contexts. Additionally by agreeing to follow\n every funding sources’ policy/framework, there is a great possibility that it will be in breach with another funding source’s framework. For this reason, UNOPS has established its own Financial Rules and Regulations and legislative framework, which includes\n its own Environmental and Social Safeguard requirements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.8:\n As permits, licenses, consents, approvals and authorizations are under the ownership of the Government/Host Country, UNOPS cannot take full responsibility or liability for duties/obligations that are outside of its own control. UNOPS is more than happy to\n engage with the Government to receive all of the required approvals and authorizations, but it cannot ensure or own the process of receiving such approvals. \n\n\n2.9:\n UNOPS has agreements in place with third party contractors and subcontractors that put into place the terms and conditions in line with the UN requirements/principles for contracts. UNOPS is more than happy to engage with GAVI to identify necessary obligations\n that should be flown down as mandatory terms and conditions for its third party vendors where they are in line with UNOPS rules and regulations. However, UNOPS cannot flow down obligations “on the same terms as those imposed on UNOPS” due to the fact that\n UNOPS has a very specific status as a UN system organization with Privileges and Immunities, thereby making it impossible for UNOPS to bestow the terms and conditions identically to non-UN, non-state entities (NUNSE). All terms and conditions would need to\n be adjusted to match the status of the NUNSE third parties with whom we engage. Additionally, due to UNOPS privileges and immunities, UNOPS is unable to be responsible for the acts and omissions of its subcontractors nor remain responsible for the performance\n of the obligations. UNOPS is responsible for the identified obligations under the Agreement and has rules and regulations, and terms and conditions in place with its third party contractors to ensure that if there are any breaches to the contractual obligations\n or acts/omissions which rise to the level of a proscribed practice, to take action to remedy such situation. UNOPS is happy to go further into what remedies UNOPS has in place where a contractor has breached a contract and/or has acted in a way that rises\n to the level of a proscribed practice.\n\n\n2.10:\n UNOPS has inserted our standard language on legal coverage to ensure that all Parties are aware of UNOPS right to implement within the borders of the Host Country.\n\n\n4.1 and 4.3:\n UNOPS, in line with the IAIG MOU with GAVI counterparts, is able to provide reasonable supplementary information as long as it is provided subject to its privileges and immunities and rules/regulations. This is carried forward into the 4.3 request on capacity\n assessments for implementing partners - noting that UNOPS’s due diligence assessments are confidential, but we may be able to give relevant information subject to our rules/regulations. Additionally, UNOPS has a Due Diligence Operational Instruction which\n states that UNOPS performs DD only on non-UN, non-state entities.\n\n\n4.10:\nAny reference to an\n audit must be undertaken in line with the UN single audit principle. \n\n\n4.11 and 4.12:\nThese are the IAIG\n requirements that I believe are supported and referenced by the MOU between GAVI and UNOPS. Due to the due process rights of individuals involved and the protection to not jeopardize an ongoing investigation, UNOPS promptly informs of any non-frivolous allegation. \n\n\n4.13, 15:\n UNOPS, due to its legal status under the Convention on Privileges and Immunities and due to the fact that it is a self-financed organization (not receiving assessed budget from the United Nations), cannot agree to repay funds that have been misused as UNOPS,\n under its financial rules and regulations, can only trigger disbursements where project activities, defined under our legislative framework, has been identified and committed for that purpose. UNOPS will take reasonable measures to recover the funds and will\n repay any funds that have been duly recovered.\n\n--\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regard \nKatya \n\n\n\n\n\nEkaterina Ponomareva\n| Legal Senior Analyst  | HQ | Copenhagen,\n Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Mon, Mar 11, 2024 at 2:03 PM Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n\nDear Devorah,\n\n\n\n\n\nIt was great to talk to you last week. I have just discussed with Irina (cc.) and we note that Article 5.1\nin fine of the last draft on financial reporting that states the following comment:\n\n\n\n\n [The above reports shall be the\n combination of UNOPS standard financial reporting template with an annex of budget vs expenditures reporting in line with Gavi grant cost and activity categories.]\n\n\n\n\n... is incorrect, as Gavi insists on using its own budget reporting template. Please find attached said template.\n\n\n\n\n\nCan you please confirm your understanding with the foregoing? We could then amend Article 5.1\nin fine as follows: \"All financial reports shall be issued by UNOPS using Gavi's standard budgeting and reporting template and guidelines as set forth in Annex C\", and add both the enclosed template and the already existing link to those guidelines\n under Annex C.\n\n\n\n\n\nWe apologize for this further amendment. \n\n\n\n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\nLaurent \n\n\n\n\n\nDe : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nEnvoyé : mardi, 5 mars 2024 12:41\n\nÀ : Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\nCc : Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>;\n Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>\n\nObjet : Draft Framework Agreement btwn UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\nDear all\nJust sent a Google invite for Friday at 11.00 CET. Hope you can all make it.  Please let me know if Google is a problem, we can also handle MS Teams if you wish to resend :)\nLooking forward to this discussion\nBest wishes Louise\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 5 Mar 2024 at 12:33, Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org> wrote:\n\nDear Louise,\n \nThank you and agreed a meeting would be most useful.  The key participants from our side are Irin and Laurent and if I can join that would be great, but not essential given my agenda might delay us. \n Friday might be a more quiet day to try and if we could do this week, better to ensure we are moving this forward?\n \nKind regards,\nAmy\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 5, 2024 12:19 PM\n\nTo: Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>;\n Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Amy\nwelcome back - I hope the 6.0 mission to Togo was good :)\nThanks so much for getting back to us on the Framework Agreement - I am about to convene an update later this week.\nIt will be good to regroup given the new folk on both sides, in addition to a number of issues re-opened that had previously been settled\n (as I understand it).\nAre there any times/days to avoid from your perspective?\nMany thanks and speak soon\nLouise\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \nOn Mon, 4 Mar 2024 at 14:15, Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nDear Louise,\n\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I’m just back from mission and trying to calibrate where key deliverables stand.  I have quite a few Gavi colleagues keen to have us finalize the UNOPS contract. I know these are never straightforward and take a lot of effort\n on each side and it seems your team is pushing this ahead.  I also know your voice carries weight so am reaching out in hopes you can help see if this continues to move through the channels on your side.\n \nI’m also putting in copy Irina, Senior Manager Programme Support Team, so is taking the lead on all contracting from a process perspective and will help me by continuing to engage with you.  Also in\n copy is Laurent, my legal colleague, who is leading from Gavi side.\n \nWarmest\nAmy\n \n\nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nSent: Monday, February 26, 2024 12:49 PM\n\nTo: Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Laurent and colleagues,\n \nUnfortunately we were unable to finalize the review prior to your leave. We still have a few more internal stakeholders that we are consulting and\n will send the draft to this email chain once we have finished the review process from our end. \n \nThanks for your understanding,\nDevorah\n \n \nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n| Legal Specialist | IPAS\n Legal | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n \nOn Tue, Feb 20, 2024 at 3:54 PM Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\nDear Laurent,\n \nThanks for letting us know. We are still working on the draft internally, which requires engaging with several subject matter experts, so I'm not certain\n if we'll be ready for a meeting on Thursday or Friday. Let me check with my colleagues and will try to get back to you as soon as I get some sense of timing.\n \nThanks for your patience,\nDevorah\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n| Legal Specialist | IPAS\n Legal | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n \nOn Tue, Feb 20, 2024 at 3:48 PM Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nDear Devorah, dear Louise,\nJust to let you know that I will be out of office next week, so I am very happy to talk to you (either on Thursday or on Friday\n morning) if that helps and/or to receive a revised template by Friday morning if that is possible. If not, I will review your draft upon my return early March. \nMany thanks,\nLaurent \n\n\n\nDe : Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n\nEnvoyé : jeudi, 15 février 2024 14:27\n\nÀ : Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nCc : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nObjet : RE: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \nHi Devorah,\nAttached please find a revised template as well as a comparison document highlighting my further amendments and comments to the\n last draft circulated by Kate on Monday. New changes should be self-explanatory. I have also deleted a few Gavi's comments that are no longer relevant and cleaned some formatting issues. Please get back to us on open points at your earliest convenience. \nAll the best,\nLaurent  \n\n\n\nDe : Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nEnvoyé : jeudi, 15 février 2024 12:11\n\nÀ : Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n\nCc : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nObjet : Re: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Laurent,\n \nThanks for letting us know.  For the additional modifications, would you please send the updated draft, identifying the new changes/modifications in\n highlight as soon as you are able. This will allow us to incorporate the additions into the document that we are currently reviewing and we can flag these changes to the relevant internal units.\n \nHave a good rest of your day,\nDevorah\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n| Legal Specialist | IPAS\n Legal | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n \nOn Thu, Feb 15, 2024 at 12:03 PM Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nHi Louise, hi Devorah,\n \nI have been through the draft rapidly this morning and I do have further amendments. Please let me know whether I should circulate\n a revised draft today or tomorrow or wait for your feedback before adding my suggested changes.\n \nAll the best,\n \nLaurent \n\n\n\nDe : Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n\nEnvoyé : mercredi, 14 février 2024 14:27\n\nÀ : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nCc : Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>;\n Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nObjet : Re: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \nThanks so much for your email, Louise. I was suggesting that 1:1 call based on your email to Kate below to clarify some open issues if need be, but please feel free to circulate a revised draft instead\n (that we will need from UNOPS in any case for any remaining points and internal review). Happy to talk to Devorah meanwhile (@Devorah please let me know based on my suggested time slots below) and/or to you upon your return. It would be great if we could finalize\n this template as soon as possible.\nAll the best,\nLaurent \n \nEnvoyé à partir de \nOutlook pour iOS\n\n\n\nDe : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nEnvoyé : mercredi, février 14, 2024 1:38 PM\n\nÀ : Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n\nCc : Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>; Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>;\n Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nObjet : ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Laurent\n\n\nMany thanks for your message and for keeping this moving. We confirm receipt of the latest version, and note the addition of a number of new provisions, as well as comments on issues that had previously been discussed (unfortunately by staff members on both\n sides who have moved on/out). This means we will have to go back to the relevant UNOPS teams for their additional inputs (finance, PSEAH, audit, risk). As a UN agency, there are obviously UN system policies that we have to adhere to and\n\n@Devorah Flax-Davidson in copy is ready and available to speak with you asap to clarify some of these (I am out for the next few days). Please coordinate with Devorah to have that call, and I will look forward to reconnecting with you towards the end of\n the week. \n \nWith thanks and best wishes\nLouise \n \n \nOn Wed, 14 Feb 2024 at 11:41, Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nHi Louise,\n \nReference is made to your email below? \n \nI will take over this matter as Kate is backed up with other projects. May I kindly suggest to call you either tomorrow afternoon or on Friday afternoon (Swiss time) to discuss our last draft and remaining\n open issues? If not possible, what about next Monday? Please let me know a convenient time and phone number. \n \nAll the best,\n \nLaurent \n \n \nEnvoyé à partir de \nOutlook pour iOS\n\n\n\nDe : Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nEnvoyé : mardi, février 13, 2024 9:41 AM\n\nÀ : Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n\nCc : Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>; Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>\n\nObjet : Re: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Kate\nThanks very much, confirming receipt of your latest marked up version. \nPlease find attached Feedback document (if helpful...), and please suggest an expedient date/time for us to meet to finalise the Agreement.\nThanks and best wishes\nLouise \n \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview\nhere  | \nFollow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube \n\n \n \nOn Mon, 12 Feb 2024 at 14:50, Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nDear Louise and colleagues,\n \nThank you for reaching out. I did not attach the correct document and am re-attaching the correct version here.\n \nThank you for sharing the spreadsheet. I have not had a chance to review but it would not capture the most up to date input from Gavi colleagues.  \n \nBest,\nKate\n \nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSent: Monday, February 12, 2024 12:57 PM\n\nTo: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>; Irina Petkova <ipetkova@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: ! Urgent - Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Kate\nThanks very much for sending this through. Devorah and Ekaterina have looked extensively at the document you sent, but cannot detect any further\n changes, other than the addition of \"classified as internal\"!   I have set up a separate Google sheet which I have just shared with Kate, Jack, Ekaterina and Devorah to please use in order to clarify the issues still under discussion.  I suggest we meet as\n soon as possible to clarify remaining issues so we can move forward. \nLook forward to hearing from you\nBest wishes Louise\n \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview\nhere  | \nFollow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube \n\n \n \nOn Thu, 8 Feb 2024 at 17:01, Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\nDear Devorah and colleagues,\n \nWith my apologies for the delay, I have attached a new draft template agreement for discussion, which reflects in tracked changes the edits we have made when compared to the draft you shared on 26\n January. I have left the prior comments for completeness but have added a few new comments flagging new points we have raised.\n \nPlease let us know if you would like to schedule a call to discuss the initial draft or send comments back in the first instance.\n \nBest regards,\nKate\n \nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 4:08 PM\n\nTo: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Kate and colleagues,\n \nThanks for confirming. Looking forward to our discussion.\n \nHave a nice weekend,\n \nDevorah\nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n| Legal Specialist | IPAS\n Legal | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n \nOn Fri, Jan 26, 2024 at 4:02 PM Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>\n wrote:\n\n \nDear Devorah and colleagues,\n \nThank you for sharing this draft. We were able to open and review and are now compiling internal comments on Gavi’s side and will aim to send back an updated draft for further discussion next week.\n \nBest regards,\nKate\n \nFrom: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>\n\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 9:57 AM\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nCc: Kate Fendler <kfendler@gavi.org>; Jack Nichols <jnichols@gavi.org>;\n Amy LaTrielle <alatrielle@gavi.org>; Ekaterina PONOMAREVA <ekaterinapo@unops.org>;\n Laurent Gabus <lgabus@gavi.org>; Alexa Reynolds <areynolds@gavi.org>;\n Sylvia Mueller (Intern) <smueller@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Template Grant Agreement with UNOPS and Gavi\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Jack, Kate and colleagues,\n \nThank you for your patience. I spoke with my colleague, Katya, and for ease of reference, please find the December 2023 version that represents for\n us the most recent version that I believe Louise sent a month ago. \n \nPlease let me know if you have any issues opening up the document.\n \nThanks!\n\n\nDevorah\n \n \nMrs. Devorah Flax-Davidson,\nJ.D.\n| Legal Specialist | IPAS\n Legal | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n \nOn Fri, Jan 26, 2024 at 9:53 AM Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n wrote:\n<blockquote style=\"margin:5pt 0in 5pt 4.8pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6pt;border-top:",
