                        Subject = "Email: Haiti follow up meeting",
                        Description = "To: Daniel.DeLaTorre@theglobalfund.org\nCC: Philippa.DobreeCarey@theglobalfund.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Haiti follow up meeting\nBody:\nDear Daniel\nThanks so much for your message and consideration. Unfortunately Dabagai our Haiti Country Director is chairing a UN partner meeting so cannot change this. You probably remember she kindly joined at 7am for our first meeting at Jaimes request during our brown bag session, so I do hope we can find a mutually convenient time - perhaps Monday? Any time from 14h30 CET onwards is workable, given the Haiti team is 6 hours behind us.\nYou are aware of the extremely challenging operating environment in Haiti, even though the team had to relocate, and the Agreement for this work has expired, the country team has still run and finalised an RFP process for the two warehouses (bids will be opened today), and they are also consolidating the final narrative and financial report for the Govt. which we look forward to discussing with you, including some options for a way forward. \n\nThanks for your understanding and speak soon!Best wishes, Louise \n\nOn Tue, 9 Apr 2024 at 15:40, Daniel De La Torre <Daniel.DeLaTorre@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\nHi Louise,I’m sorry but every Friday 14.00 – 15.30 the CT and PRs have the crisis committee. Since they’re all working on the program adaptations, it’s not possible to shorten the call this time. Do you think the UNOPS team could be flexible this first meeting? From there both teams can agree on the next meetings.Hope it’s possible. Daniel DE LA TORRE AYORAAdvisor, Partnerships, Challenging Operating EnvironmentsImplementation and Challenging Operating EnvironmentsGrant Portfolio Solutions and SupportGrant Management Division M: +41764309531Daniel.Delatorre@theglobalfund.orgtheglobalfund.org From: Google Calendar <calendar-notification@google.com>On Behalf Of Louise Jocelyn LEECH\nSent: Tuesday, April 9, 2024 3:06 PM\nTo: CT Haiti <CT_HTI@theglobalfund.org>; Daniel De La Torre <Daniel.DeLaTorre@theglobalfund.org>; Francesco Moschetta <Francesco.Moschetta@theglobalfund.org>; Philippa Dobrée-Carey <Philippa.DobreeCarey@TheGlobalFund.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\nSubject: UNOPS - TGF project in Haiti CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. UNOPS - TGF project in Haiti   Hello, please can we schedule this ONE HOUR EARLIER to ensure our Haiti team is available. UNOPS - TGF project in HaitiFriday 12 Apr 2024⋅ 15:30– 16:30 (Central European Time - Zurich)Thanks Louise,\nI’m sending the link for the meeting.\nWould you please share with the colleagues at UNOPS office in Haiti, and the team managing the project?\nThanks a lot.\nBest,\nD ________________________________________________________________________________\nMicrosoft Teams Need help?\nJoin the meeting now\nMeeting ID: 239 565 460 890\nPasscode: KvRZfZ\n________________________________\nDial-in by phone\n+41 43 430 76 18,,610745566# Switzerland, Zurich/Zürich/Zurigo (Zurich)\nFind a local number\nPhone conference ID: 610 745 566#\nJoin on a video conferencing device\nTenant key: teams@vc.theglobalhealthcampus.org\nVideo ID: 119 446 257 7\nMore info\nFor organizers: Meeting options | Reset dial-in PIN\nNOTICE: This meeting may be recorded, including video and audio recording and automatic transcription. By joining the meeting you consent to the meeting being recorded and/or transcribed.\n________________________________________________________________________________Locationhttps://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_MTFlY2NhMzAtMTA2Ny00MWE1LTlhZWMtNGYzODU1NDA4ODkz%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%2277920909-8782-4efb-aaf1-44ac114d7c03%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%22b62a749b-85d4-4d3e-a6a5-6f0469e6d412%22%7d\nView mapGuestsDaniel De La Torre- organizerLouise Jocelyn LEECH- creatorCT HaitiPhilippa Dobrée-C