                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx000009DNHtMAO",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Recording of yesterday's informal update to the EB",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-04-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Recording of yesterday's informal update to the EB",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: plg.lo@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; arnauds@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Recording of yesterday's informal update to the EB\nBody:\nThanks so much Asbjørn - this systematic communication and forward planning around EO / EB engagements is extremely helpful.\nIs the Q&A document a \"living\" document?  This might be useful given we know the member states talk together about these issues. This will ensure PLG retains a \"one stop shop\" of consistent responses to evolving questions...  ie Regarding question 1 by the Swiss - do we have a clear answer on the \"how\" of performance management? (I don't see a \"response\" reflected in the slide deck).  \nRegarding further sharing - I would plan to share with Geneva Office colleagues in current negotiations with the Swiss on the Santiago Network financial contributions, as well as colleagues with projects funded by the Swiss.  Will you share with MT / RDs?\nThanks again!!All best wishes Louise\n\nOn Fri, 12 Apr 2024 at 09:03, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear PLG colleagues,\nPlease find here for your information the recording of yesterday's informal update to the EB. To watch the recording please insert the password 5^g+KF02. \nAlso please find here a written overview of the questions posed by the Netherlands, Sweden, Switzerland and Canada. As you will notice, the questions were quite elaborate and very technical which was due to the detailed and technical nature of the content presented. \nFor ease of reference you can see the slides presented here (the ones I sent yesterday). \nJune EB sessionTogether with the EO and NYBER we have started the planning of the next June EB session. I will soon send you the draft documents for the session, timelines, key topics etc. to get your inputs and to kickstart liaison offices' informal briefings of key partners. \nWithin the next two weeks we will also convene all relevant internal UNOPS stakeholders to kickstart the process, coordinate approach and most importantly ensure that EB members maintain a positive view of UNOPS' ability to conduct an EB session.  \nBest,Asbjørn\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
