                    "00TQx000009ECozMAG",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: WHO Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series - 2024 Schedule",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-04-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: WHO Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series - 2024 Schedule",
                        Description = "To: sanjaym@unops.org; simonettas@unops.org; dalilag@unops.org; elenage@unops.org; fabriziof@unops.org; banak@unops.org; leyres@unops.org; marijab@unops.org; timl@unops.org; sophiedj@unops.org\nCC: franciscob@unops.org; daniele@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; arnauds@unops.org; kajsah@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: WHO Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series - 2024 Schedule\nBody:\nDear Regional Directors and regional partnerships colleagues,\nPlease see below information and links to WHOs upcoming Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series. \nPlease share this with your MCO and CO colleagues for their information, and to help us increase our understanding and opportunities to engage / support WHO, governments and broader partners in this key agenda moving forward. \nNB: Agendas / speakers will be shared with registered participants in advance of the webinars - so please register!!\nThanks and best wishesLouise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: healthclimate <healthclimate@who.int>\nDate: Thu, Apr 11, 2024 at 6:51 PM\nSubject: Join the WHO Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series - 2024 Schedule\nTo: \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHO Climate Change and Health Technical Webinar Series 2024\n\nWHO is conducting a series of technical webinars on various climate change and health topics with the aim of building capacity for implementation at country level. These webinars will integrate training, experience sharing,\n interactive activities and group discussion. \n\nThe first series of webinars will explore specific topics related to:\n\n\nConducting a climate change and health vulnerability and adaptation assessment\nDeveloping a Health National Adaptation Plan\nAccessing climate finance for health\nClimate resilient and environmentally sustainable health care facilities\nEach webinar will be conducted twice to accommodate different time zones and interpretation will be available as follows (Geneva time/CET):\n\n\nMorning sessions: English, French and Arabic\nAfternoon sessions: English, French and Spanish\nPlease register for the webinars of interest using the links below.\nSchedule of Webinars: \n\n\n\n\nDate & time (CET)\n\n\nTopic*\n\n\nRegistration links\n\n\n\n\n24th April 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nGetting started: climate change and health vulnerability & adaptation assessments\n\n\nMorning session (9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEud--urjkjE9Tw5NEgRFtiMaoeMtknvcMC\n \nAfternoon session (15:00 – 16:30):\nhttps://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJUufuCorT4uEta5klx1L1Tf3L6_SLnT8k09\n\n\n\n\n30th April 2024\n09:00 – 10:30 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nWHO as an Accredited Implementing Entity of the Adaptation Fund; Accessing AF funding for Climate Change and Health\n\n\nMorning session \n(9:00 – 10:30):\nhttps://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0qfuGhqz8oGNT1euDMlJoc5s-ZWpIgw5t6\n \nAfternoon session \n(15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJclcu-gqjwuEtRExaK0aWnsRjWhbmO8bO-6\n\n\n\n\n12th June 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nDeveloping a Health National Adaptation Plan: Introduction\n\n\nMorning session (9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJAkdOCrqzMuEtW54HWifd6U31qliMwc9CfN\n \nAfternoon session (15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0qdOqvqD0iGtV-Ofj0LT_AFNDMVMe12HBx\n\n\n\n\n19th June 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nGIS and risk mapping in climate change and health vulnerability & adaptation assessments\n\n\nMorning session \n(9:30 –11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJAscOqsqzktHdSDRlVfAW1D7bkJB1erENOK\n \nAfternoon session \n(15:00 – 16:30):\nhttps://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJIpdO-vrTIsG9CZYlm2_QMwTsOQJITIKTap\n\n\n\n\n10th July 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nClimate resilient and environmentally sustainable health care facilities\n\n\nMorning session (9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJYsdu-hrzorGtek1ZaccPRU8qzX2Aowx1J4\n \nAfternoon session (15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJYodeurrT4rH9bDAKyFTnRXbLu_xdghIgvB\n\n\n\n\n17th July 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nQuantitative approaches for vulnerability & adaptation assessments: sensitivity analyses and projecting future health risks of climate change\n\n\nMorning session \n(9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEtduirqjwiHtw3nXTe_fz6h7wghpF3puVo\n \nAfternoon session \n(15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0rfuyrrTguE9Fbs1hCmm7mMN1_SHivhceh\n\n\n\n\n18th September 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nIntegrating health in NDCs and LT-LEDS\n\n\nMorning session (9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMqf-6hpj8vGdOZ-uNOf7MS7LrjZgEnp7of\n \nAfternoon session (15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJElf-yqrjIqH9Y_RbQoI-XsCTN9U5CdAhPa\n\n\n\n\n25th September 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nDeveloping a Health National Adaptation Plan: Quality criteria for HNAPs\n\n\nMorning session \n(9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJYld-mqqz8qHtOJQowZ4mgUb6-PKniXKqTJ\n \nAfternoon session \n(15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJIkcu2rpz4jG9IWidgJZhz6FsxIh-DKawAy\n\n\n\n\n16th October 2024\n9:30 – 11:00 &\n15:00 – 16:30\n\n\nConducting a gender analysis for climate change and health vulnerability & adaptation assessments \n\n\nMorning session (9:30 – 11:00): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0uc-Curz4uE9QqaHGSBY5N7PmuMGbMhaeB\n \nAfternoon session (15:00 – 16:30): https://who.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0oduGpqzkuGNE5me_Q56VXnVHoXyxJLVgl\n\n\n\n\n23rd October 2024 (TBC)\n \n\n\nAccessing GCF Readiness funds with WHO as the Delivery Partner  (TBC)\n\n\nTBC\n\n\n\n\n\n*Topics may be subject to change",
