                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-02").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Santiago Network: PRA by the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation",
                        Description = "To: duediligence@unops.org\nCC: shuoy@unops.org; lilyas@unops.org; benf@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Santiago Network: PRA by the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation\nBody:\nDear Gilda\nThanks for your message. I am delighted to hear from you on this subject, as I have been discussing with several colleagues the need for a coordinated / aligned response and approach. Several colleagues (Ana, but also Eda Kraja and the hosted entities you mentioned) have been through this process, to date I had put them in touch with each other,to share experience and responses to ensure some level of alignment. \nAna is on leave until tomorrow but she's previously advised me of the Partner Risk Assessment in November 2022, performed by a local auditing firm in Belgrade (I believe they're called DFK). It took about two months, covering key areas like governance, legal, procurement, HR, PM, Finance, IT, Assets, etc. Typically SDC hires a 3rd party to do the work and therefore do not have access to the reports etc.  \nAs you know, we now have a list of questions submitted by SDC regarding our new role in the Santiago Network with UNDRR.  Ben Ford, in copy, is coordinating this project on behalf of UNOPS. The questionnaire is here.\n\nI have reached out to Eda to share any data she has - did you request this from Hosted Entities?Happy to discuss a structured way forward, but seems the pieces are getting into place!Thanks and best wishesLouise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Thu, 2 May 2024 at 12:06, RCG Due Diligence UNOPS <duediligence@unops.org> wrote:\n\nDear Louise, Shuo and Lilya, \nHope all is well with you. I am writing to you all in relation to a request we got from SDC for UNOPS to complete a Partner Risk Assessment in relation to the upcoming Santiago Network. \nAs the DD Unit in HQ is now supporting with such requests (for organisational-wide type of questions, not the programmatic part), we would like to know if you happen to have in your files a PRA from SDC already responded to, and if YES, if you could share it. \nJudging from our internal Drive's documents, it seems that both Cities Alliance and the Sanitation and Hygiene Fund have had such PRAs requested from SDC in the past. There is also a project in RSMOC (Serbia Multi Country Office) which seems to have also completed a PRA by SDC (PRO - Local Governance for People and Nature). I have already reached out to Ana Nedeljkovic, the Programme Manager, but if you, @Louise Jocelyn LEECH could please give us a hand (or if you would know), it would be much appreciated. \nHaving those prior PRAs would help us a great deal, as we want to keep our responses both accurate and consistent. It would also help our DD HQ database needs, so that other country teams, when asked to do this from SDC or other partners, have a basis from where to start and avoid duplication. \nThank you and best regards,\nGilda Senties Portilla (she/her), PhD | Due Diligence Specialist | Risk and Compliance Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen | www.unops.org \n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>\nDate: Wed, May 1, 2024 at 9:03 PM\nSubject: Re: Due diligence by Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation\nTo: RCG Due Diligence UNOPS <duediligence@unops.org>\nCc: Ben FORD <benf@unops.org>, Gilda SENTIES PORTILLA <gildasp@unops.org>, Marianne HOVE HILDEBRANDT <marianneho@unops.org>, Julia Charlotte KEIL <juliack@unops.org>, Hannah MILDE <hannahm@unops.org>, Katrin LICHTENBERG <katrinl@unops.org>\n\nThanks, Gilda.  \nFor the Serbia office, Louise (PLG liaison in GVA) is to ask Ana\nNEDELJKOVIC BELJA about it.  You can follow up with her as well and/or try Daliborka KOLAR (HoSS) and/or Marko VUJACIC (HoP). \nFor Cities Alliance, you can ask Shuo Yang, Partnership and Resource Planning Officer. \nFor RMB, you can ask Lilya BOARON, Executive Associate to the CEO. \nBest regards, Guillaume\n\n-----------------------------Guillaume Lemenez | Legal Advisor, Team Lead for GVA/ECR/AFR, Legal Group | Geneva, Switzerland | Tel: +41791359187 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nOn Wed, May 1, 2024 at 5:01 PM RCG Due Diligence UNOPS <duediligence@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Ben, dear all, Thanks for sharing the SDC questionnaire. I can see it contains very similar questions to the ones in the others that I shared with you, for instance PSEAH-related responses are quite well-covered. Usually it is the teams who input the content for programmatic-related questions; the DD Unit reviews and/or coordinates with HQ relevant units to validate entity-wide (UNOPS-wide) questions. \nI ran a search in all of UNOPS Drives and judging from the documents I found, it seems that SDC has already requested Partner Risk Assessments (PRA) to at least two hosted entities (Cities Alliance and the Sanitation and Hygiene Fund, SHD). @Guillaume LEMENEZ would you know who to contact there to inquire/request those prior PRA? I also noticed that a project in RSMOC (Serbia Multi Country Office) makes reference to a PRA by SDC. I have already reached out to the Programme Manager; will let you know once she replies. \nJulia-Charlotte (DD Advisor) and I have no problem joining a meeting, wherever you find a spot (preferably tomorrow afternoon or Friday morning).\nAll best,Gilda\nOn Wed, May 1, 2024 at 12:15 PM Ben FORD <benf@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Gilda & Marianne,\nMany thanks for your support on this matter. I have saved the Swiss questionnaire here so we can collaborate on its completion.\nWith regard to the questions (or documents) for the main text of the “credit proposal”, unfortunately we don't currently have a log frame/theory of change for the Santiago network. This is something we are planning on developing in Q2 as part of the strategy development in advance of the next Advisory Board scheduled for 9-11 July so we will need to see if this can be fast tracked. I am working on the development of the 4 year budget and in kind contributions are also in touch with UNFCCC regarding details of pledges made by the donors.\nPerhaps we could have a brief call tomorrow or Friday to discuss the completion of the questionnaire further?  I'll put some time in the diary but please suggest another time if not convenient.\n\nThanks,\nBen\nOn Wed, May 1, 2024 at 11:06 AM Gilda SENTIES PORTILLA <gildasp@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Marianne, \nThanks for your email. Yes, the DD Unit is now supporting other units and country teams with partner's assessment requests on us, UNOPS. I haven't come across a prior partner risk assessment carried out by SDC, but I can certainly do a quick search in our Drives and let you know later today. \nHaving said that, this year we have received a good number of both \"entity-wide\" and programmatic (hosted entities) DD assessment requests from FCDO. Although I would expect SDC questions to be somewhat different, geared to fund management, I am opening access to you here, which contains the questionnaires we have so far supported with, in case you find some responses useful. The one entitled TB Reach (dated March 2024) is the most complete, where HQ units got to verify and validate most entity-wide responses.\nAll best,Gilda Senties Portilla (she/her), PhD | Due Diligence Specialist | Risk and Compliance Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Wed, May 1, 2024 at 9:54 AM Marianne HOVE HILDEBRANDT <marianneho@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Gilda, \nI hope all is well. \nIn the context of the Santiago network secretariat co-hosted by UNOPS and UNDRR, UNOPS is acting as project and fund manager. The Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) is willing to give $2 million to the Santiago network, to be administered by UNOPS. In this regard, SDC first needs to prepare a credit proposal for internal approval, which includes conducting a Partner Risk Assessment (\"PRA\") of UNOPS.\nWe have received a questionnaire to be completed in this regard. As we understand that RCG handles due diligence requests of UNOPS, we were wondering if you are aware of any other UNOPS offices having gone through SDC Partner Risk Assessments in the past? If so, it would be useful if the questionnaire could be shared to identify; i) whether this was UNOPS-wide or project specific; and ii) whether we could use previous responses to ensure consistency and avoid duplication of effort. \nBen and Guillaume in cc may be able to provide more information if required. Thank you for any insights you may have.Kind regardsMarianne\nMarianne Hove Hildebrandt | Management Specialist | Legal Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n-- \nBen Ford (he/him) | Fund Management Advisor | Tel/WhatsApp: +44 (0) 7707 536898 | www.unops.org",
