                        Subject = "Email: SDC - Risk Dialogue documents",
                        Description = "To: gildasp@unops.org\nCC: benf@unops.org; elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: SDC - Risk Dialogue documents\nBody:\nDear Gilda\nPlease see below email from Eda, including her comprehensive response to SDC \nDaliborka also contacted me to say Serbia MCO had a rather light assessment in the form of an interview and a couple of documents shared. The Embassy in Skopje was prior to that looking into assessment we went through in Serbia back in 2022 (before latest developments with Swiss)\n\nHope this adds a few more pieces to help our puzzle evolve \nbest wishesLouise\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Eda KRAJA <edak@unops.org>\nDate: Fri, 3 May 2024 at 10:00\nSubject: Fwd: SDC - Risk Dialogue documents\nTo: Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nFYI as requested. We also had an interview with them which lasted a couple of hours. The questions were mostly on the project/country office structure, DOAs, project monitoring and assurance.   \n\nBest regards,\n\n \n\nEda\n\n \n\nEda Kraja (she/her) | Country Manager Cambodia and Lao PDR | South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) | Phnom Penh Cambodia | Mob. +855 89 555 786 |  www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Kannikar WANTHANA <kannikarw@unops.org>\nDate: Thu, Jan 18, 2567 BE at 7:03 PM\nSubject: Re: [EXTERNAL] Fwd: SDC - Dashboard contribution for 2024 - documents risk dialogue\nTo: Ohanyan Sirun EDA OHASI <sirun.ohanyan@eda.admin.ch>\nCC: Lackner-Häfliger Denise EDA LAC <denise.lackner@eda.admin.ch>, Engler Christian EDA ECH <christian.engler@eda.admin.ch>, Eda KRAJA <edak@unops.org>, Sonja Bachmann <bachmanns@un.org>, Gonnet Hélène EDA GOH <helene.gonnet@eda.admin.ch>\n\nDear Sirun,\nApologize for the delay as we were getting internal clearance to share the information. \nKindly find for your reference, the requested documents for risk assessment.Some internal information, especially what is related to our partners, should not be disclosed without their acknowledgement.Therefore, if you need any specific additional information apart from this, please let me know. The legal structure, setup, and organizational chart of UNOPS in general and the office in BangkokOrganizational Principles and Governance ModelOrganizational StructureOrganogram - Bangkok is under Regional Office Asia - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country OfficeBinding agreements with your partnersProjects and locationsPrimary funding sources of UNOPS in general and the office in BangkokOur PartnersBangkok Liaison OfficeUNOPS internal compliance policies and proceduresDue Diligence Framework at UNOPS \nUNOPS guidelines on PSEAH (e.g., procedures, Code of Conduct (CoC), training internal and partner organizations, etc.)PSEAHPSEAH Strategy 2023Mandatory PSEAH training for UNOPS personnel (internal document)Written guidelines or policies of the project management cycleProject ManagementGuidelines for a systematic risk management process (ongoing monitoring and re-evaluation)OD Risk ManagementOI Risk ManagementUNOPS internal control systemsInternal Control FrameworkBudgeting and financial management proceduresFinance and Assets ManagementBudgeting and Internal Investment ManagementIPSASProcedures for cash paymentsTreasury and Cash ManagementEstablished procurement policies and procedures that have been approvedProcurement FrameworkProcurement ProceduresVendor SanctionsProcedures for the Acceptance and Management of Pro Bono Goods or ServicesFinancial accounting and reporting proceduresEngagement Financial Management and ReportingFinancial Accounting and ReportingOthers relevant documentsAnti-Bribery and Anti-Corruption Policy Due Diligence Framework at UNOPSQuality ManagementContribution to SDGsFor the risk assessment dialogue, if you need to conduct this with the team, it would be great to provide the scope so we can arrange specific focal points for you. If it is a general topic, would one or two people from the project team be sufficient? If this deems to be a rather formal process, it will be great if you can share with us the procedure of the assessment, how the results of the assessment will be used, and whether the results shall be shared with UNOPS, as this will help us with the arrangement and serve as internal records, \nThank you and best regards,\nKannikar WANTHANA, Ms | Programme Management Officer | Programme Management Unit, Mixed Projects Portfolio | South East Asia and Pacific Multi--Country Office (EAPMCO)| Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 1172 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTubeSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish",
