                new (
                    "00TQx00000AEd0YMAT",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Doodle for meeting + some additional considerations...",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-06").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Doodle for meeting + some additional considerations...",
                        Description = "To: matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch\nCC: hieber-girardet@un.org; yolanda.nasi@eda.admin.ch; sandya.prasad@un.org; guillaumele@unops.org; benf@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Doodle for meeting + some additional considerations...\nBody:\nDear MatthiasThanks so much for your email and attachments.  This is to let you know our teams are working on the various areas of the PRA and we will submit to you all we can by the end of this week. We want to ensure we give you the highest quality data which means we will need a couple of extra days to gather and consolidate the relevant information from the different teams involved. This means we cannot hit the 7 May deadline, but will respond as fully as we can by Friday 10th. Thanks for your understanding and look forward to speaking with you soon.Best wishes Louise\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Fri, 3 May 2024 at 09:36, Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise, dear Lori, all\n \nFor the mentioned call (or visit, but unlikely), I’m sharing options via Doodle. Please note that Monday 13th of May would be much preferred (Tuesday I could only 90min,\n and Thursday will be late for our internal schedule):\nhttps://doodle.com/meeting/organize/id/e7WWQ7re\n \nTo be on the save side, I propose 2h. If we are efficient, we can do it in less.\n \nI made a first draft of our internal Credit Proposal today and accordingly, identified some further things. I thus added some considerations below in\nred. These should not be too hard to answer I hope (but if you need more time for those, let me know).\n \nBest wishes,\n\nMatthias\n \nPS: the story won’t end here, I’m afraid. As the credit proposal is consulted on different levels in-house, more questions will certainly come up. It is an iterative process.\n \n\n\nFrom: Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH\n\n\nSent: Monday, April 29, 2024 5:50 PM\n\nTo: 'Louise LEECH' <louisel@unops.org>; Loretta Hieber Girardet <hieber-girardet@un.org>\n\nCc: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>; Nasi Yolanda EDA NMX <yolanda.nasi@eda.admin.ch>; Sandya Prasad <sandya.prasad@un.org>\n\nSubject: RE: [EXTERNAL] Santiago Network Swiss contribution\n\n\n \nDear Louise, dear Lori, colleagues\n \nI herewith provide you as announced with the list of questions to be able to draft the main text of our internal “credit proposal” (see here below)\n and the attached questionnaire for the “(partner) risk assessment” (PRA; which contains four “sheets”).\n\n \nFor the PRA, beyond ticking boxes, please put your comments in column K. For Y/N-type questions we often provide further guidance (see where in\nred). Mostly it is about describing “how” something is ensured (or not), while sharing relevant documents (policies/manuals etc.) and indicating specific applicable provisions therein. In rare cases, to alleviate your work, we\n already put (hurriedly) some information we found (there you can revise/add where needed).\n \nPlease share the filled out PRA both in Excel format and a signed PDF, while submitting as annexes the documents (policies, manuals, etc.).\n \nWe would appreciate\nyour feedback until May 7. Meanwhile, should any of this remain unclear with you, don’t hesitate to reach out asap.\n \nBest regards,\n\nMatthias\n \n//\n \nQuestions (or documents) for the main text of the “credit proposal”\n\n-       \nLogframe/theory of change: do you have something going in that direction?\n We customarily require objectives (a usual cascade with impacts/outcomes, outputs…), that come with indicators and corresponding baselines and targets. Also, a theory of change.\n> outcomes, outputs and baselines appear very prominent on the first page of the credit proposal. So in the absence of anything agreed already, we have to think for some proxies.\n\n-       \nI have attached our SDC-internal indicators in the space of climate/DRR. Hopefully, there would be a match (I highlighted those where I think there\n could be one in yellow) and we could report on those (ideally without further work for you, if they (or similar indicators) would be in your results framework anyway). Please let me know where you\n see a match (and also, among the yellow, where not) and potential that you could report to us.\n\n-       \nBudget: could you provide a budget over four years, if possible disaggregated\n by year? We only have a very generic budget for this year. As a bare minimum, we need to know how much our 4 year contribution makes of the total SN resources (at least based on today resources).\nPS: The Swiss contribution does not have to appear in the budget. Since this is a core contribution, we will contribute to the overall-budget. But in any case, the more detailed and multi-year the budget, the better.\n\n-       \nDonors: please share full list. With amounts and possible time frames\n (in case of multi-year contributions). \n\n-       \nIn-kind contributions of UNDRR/UNOPS:\nif possible with amounts.\n\n-       \nOrganisational set-up (chart available?): in the credit proposal we\n need to outline how the SN-Secretariat, UNOPS/UNDRR hosts, Board, UNFCCC/CMA and OBNEs interrelate and corresponding roles/responsibilities. We have the MoU but more detail would be useful if you have. Please share an organisational chart.\n\n-       \nGender equality, “leave no one behind”, governance (strengthening of national/local institutions), and conflict-sensitivity: \n these are our crosscutting themes (in case of gender and governance we have to mark them in a marker system). Please share any information and send us your policies (or other guidance) you have in this regard.\nWe also have to demonstrate how these are measured (for gender, are indicators gender disaggregated? > in any case, according to Decision 12/CMA.4 gender disaggregation has to be done).\n\n\n-       \nWe have to do a “value for money” assessment of the investment. In case you have any ready-made information in this regard, let me know please (but\n do not spend time drafting such an assessment).\n\n-       \nBeyond the “risk assessment” (see attached) which looks at “institutional risks” (financial etc.), we also assess “contextual risks” (e.g. linked\n to the countries SN works in) and “programmatic risks” (cf. Copenhagen Circles). Any thoughts in this regard are welcome.\n\n-       \nWho submits and accesses TA requests: only developing\n country states or can also non-state actors (e.g. civil society organizations) submit requests? Will the SN have, similarly to the climate funds (GCF, AF, GEF, etc.) have designated national contact points, that have to authorize all requests?\n\n-       \nWill developing countries have to chip in with co-financing?\n If so, any rules apply?\n\n-       \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, April 26, 2024 6:54 PM\n\nTo: Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch>\n\nCc: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>; Loretta Hieber Girardet <hieber-girardet@un.org>; Nasi Yolanda EDA NMX <yolanda.nasi@eda.admin.ch>;\n Sandya Prasad <sandya.prasad@un.org>\n\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Santiago Network Swiss contribution\n \n\n\n\nDear Matthias \n\n\n \n\n\nApologies - I found this email in my drafts and don’t think I sent it to you!\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you very much for your message - this is indeed good news. We appreciate your decision and look forward to working closely with you and SDC on this going forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe will wait to hear from you as outlined below and will be ready to respond.  \n\n\n \n\n\nWith best wishes \n\n\nLouise\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 25 Apr 2024 at 15:28, Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise\n \nThanks again for your useful and timely message. We have decided to try the option of having the contract with UNOPS. We\n will thus proceed accordingly with the hope to secure the necessary signatures.\n \nThe planed approval schedule is quite ambitious (the extra-loops were not sufficiently anticipated). A key date is an already\n planned meeting of a committee that discusses the “credit proposal” (and recommends for approval) planned for 27.5. This credit proposal is quite demanding in information. It will come with a considerable list of questions to have the necessary “raw material”\n to draft it (UNDRR already shared with me some useful documents, but these do not get us all the way unfortunately). In addition, and as an annex to this credit proposal, we will have to submit a detailed “(partner) risk assessment”. The process for this annex\n will involve: sending you a (long!) list of questions (related to financial management, procurement, audit, project management and governance) and requests for documents (accounting policies, etc.), then a call or a visit to your offices in GVA (tbd) to discuss\n your written responses of the questionnaire. We will then draft a report (the risk assessment) that also includes potential mitigation measures.\n \nI hope to send you the questions for both the main text of the “credit proposal” and its risk annex early next week. I would\n then kindly request you to respond in a working week so we have enough time to hold the mentioned call/visit and to draft the proposal.\n \nAs for contract drafting, we have more time. I only know that there is a set of “special provisions” that we need to have\n in the contract in any case. Also, I was advised that there will be very close scrutiny of the fee structure.\n \nI will be in touch early next week. If you have any questions meanwhile, let me know please.\n \nBest wishes,\n\nMatthias\n \n \n \n \n \nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, April 24, 2024 8:55 AM\n\nTo: Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch>\n\nCc: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>; Loretta Hieber Girardet <hieber-girardet@un.org>; Sandya Prasad <sandya.prasad@un.org>\n\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Santiago Network Swiss contribution\n \n\nSuper - thanks Matthias. Look forward to hearing from you in due course. \n\n\nBest wishes \n\n\nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Apr 2024 at 08:17, Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise\n \nMany thanks! I aknowledge receipt of this timely message which will feed into our internal discussion.\n \nI’ll let you know what SDC will decide.\n \nBest wishes,\n\nMatthias\n \nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, April 24, 2024 6:20 AM\n\nTo: Bachmann Matthias EDA BAH <matthias.bachmann@eda.admin.ch>\n\nCc: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>; Loretta Hieber Girardet <hieber-girardet@un.org>; Sandya Prasad <sandya.prasad@un.org>\n\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Santiago Network Swiss contribution\n \n\n\n\n\nDear Matthias, \n \nThank you for the call yesterday.  As discussed, I am sending this joint-email on behalf of UNDRR and UNOPS to confirm the following:  \n \nThe MOU signed in March 2024 by the COP/CMA, UNDRR and UNOPS stipulates that funds contributed to the Santiago Network shall be managed through\n UNOPS, and “where required” by UNDRR. \n \nUNDRR could receive funds e.g. to cover its own costs, however UNDRR did not foresee receiving funds to cover the costs of the Secretariat functions\n beyond providing technical assistance to implementing partners / countries (e.g. for staffing, recruitments, office space, procurement, travel, etc.) which are agreed to be contracted and paid for by UNOPS.  In effect, this would lead to parallel fund management\n and implementation structures, one under UNOPS regulations and rules and another  under UNDRR’s regulations and rules, which would negatively impact management effectiveness and cost efficiency of the Santiago network secretariat’s work programme implementation.\n \nUNDRR and UNOPS were selected by the COP/CMA to co-host the Santiago network secretariat in November 2023, with clearly delineated and complementary\n tasks and responsibilities: UNDRR being responsible for providing technical advisory services and UNOPS providing programme management support. It is on this basis that the MOU between the COP/CMA, UNDRR and UNOPS was cleared by the UN Office of Legal Affairs\n and ultimately by the General Assembly\n \nSo far UNDRR has not accepted to receive and manage funds from other donor countries for the Santiago Network.  This was agreed to be done by UNOPS,\n which has already received $7.8 million from the USA and Spain, and is currently discussing the EUR 3 million contribution from the EU. \n \nIntroducing parallel fund management structures would not only lead to duplication of work and inefficiencies, but would also result in additional\n unnecessary costs as UNDRR would need to hire additional resources to manage the funds and implement activities which were not foreseen in the 2024-2025 work programme.  In addition to the direct costs, UNDRR as a Secretariat entity has to charge an indirect\n overhead cost of 13% to all donor funding, which would result in additional operating costs for the Santiago Network. While UNOPS, benefitting from a flexible pricing policy and leveraging economies of scale, would charge a management fee of 4.44% (which could\n further decrease with additional pledges beyond the current $47 million).\n \nFinally, the funds received by UNOPS on behalf of the Santiago Network will be used in accordance with the workplan and annual budget approved by\n the Advisory Board at its first session in Geneva in March.  The workplan and budget will be subject to regular narrative and financial progress reports and an annual financial audit, thus providing full accountability and transparency.\n \nPlease let me know if you would like more information from us or our UNDRR colleagues.\n \nThanks and best wishes,\nLouise\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
