                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-08").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Draft suggestions on setup and budget for building homes for foster families in Ukraine",
                        Description = "To: mett@eifo.dk; msec@eifo.dk; jewe@eifo.dk; mathom@em.dk; slagsg@em.dk; mogblo@um.dk; annkah@um.dk\nCC: arunn@unops.org; janphilipk@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Draft suggestions on setup and budget for building homes for foster families in Ukraine\nBody:\nDear colleagues at EIFO, Ministry of Business and Ministry of Foreign Affairs. \nIn advance of our meeting in half an hour, please find here for your reference, a preliminary overall description of the two potential setups and accompanying budgets for the construction of foster family homes in Ukraine in collaboration between UNOPS and the Olena Zelenska Foundation. \nWe have described in overall terms an option 1, that would entail that UNOPS does the full implementation of the project by which we would also take upon us the full responsibility and liability for the project outcome. The implementation would still happen in close collaboration with the Olena Zelenska Foundation - and we have made suggestions on the concrete division of labour and responsibilities - all of which would have to be described in detail in a legal agreement The UNOPS fee for this option is 6,0%. Our recommendation would be option 1 as it would eliminate the donor's concerns. \nWe have also described in overall terms an option 2 where UNOPS would provide technical advise and supervision of the project implementation. As UNOPS will not be in control of the implementing parts of the project, UNOPS cannot undertake the responsibility and liability for the outcome of the project under option 2. UNOPS' management fee for this option is 13,7%. \nWith regards to the preliminary budget estimates, kindly notice that for option 1 (full implementation) the cost estimate is for the full project while the cost estimate for option 2 is only for the services provided by UNOPS. I understand that different options on how to fund the budget gap are being discussed between Danish stakeholders. At the meeting, we can discuss how these different options could affect the budget estimates from our end. \nWe look very much forward to elaborating out suggestions for potential setups that could realise this project and minimize the donor's concerns. \nSee you all soon. \nBest,AsbjørnAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
