                new (
                    "00TQx00000AUp2bMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: URGENT: SDC - Info on what is being communicated on S3i and UNOPS remediation actions",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-13").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: URGENT: SDC - Info on what is being communicated on S3i and UNOPS remediation actions",
                        Description = "To: claudiar@unops.org\nCC: nathaliea@unops.org; sarahri@unops.org; djenebas@unops.org; gildasp@unops.org; juliack@unops.org; elenage@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: URGENT: SDC - Info on what is being communicated on S3i and UNOPS remediation actions\nBody:\nDear Claudia\nThanks for your message and for updating me on the request from SDC / Tunisia. \nWe have been through similar exercises with a few country offices.  We are now working with UNOPS HQ due diligence colleagues, to centralise our responses going forward.Last week, we submitted the attached PRA (partner risk assessment) to the Swiss, that we have completed for the Santiago Network Agreement.  Feel free to copy and paste the responses that are relevant.  \nRegarding UNOPS Comprehensive Response Plan - please also find attached the latest update that will be provided by our Executive Director to the Executive Board in New York on 3 June. \n\nPlease let me know if you need any further information, I will be more than happy to assist.\nWith thanks and best wishes\nLouise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \nOn Mon, 13 May 2024 at 11:44, Claudia ROSANO <claudiar@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Louise, \nI hope you are doing well! \nWe are discussing a potential new project with SDC in Tunisia and they asked to have a written document describing:the corrective measures that have been taken and the reforms that have been initiated within UNOPS since 2022/ S3i affaire; how they have translated into the implementation of projects by country offices (at the level of the internal control system , procurement procedures and related risks, etc.).I am aware you are also following-up with SDC at central level and think it would be suitable that the document we provide to SDC Tunisia is aligned with discussions you are having with SDC HQ. Therefore, I'd kindly ask you if you could share with us any useful resource you have already sent to SDC HQ and that could answer the points above. \nI am happy to chat to explain to you better; it is quite urgent so a quick feedback from your side would be appreciated. \nThanks a lot in advance and best regards, Claudia\nClaudia Rosano | Partnerships Specialist | UNOPS Tunisia | North Africa Office | Tunis, Tunisia | www.unops.org | Mob.: +216 92 136 991\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
