                new (
                    "00TQx00000AYKhmMAH",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNHCR EOL for 2024 and 2025 - Signed",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2023-11-10").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNHCR EOL for 2024 and 2025 - Signed",
                        Description = "To: \nCC: laurentium@unops.org; louisel@unops.org; arnauds@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNHCR EOL for 2024 and 2025 - Signed\nBody:\nDear colleagues,\nWe are delighted to announce that the Exchange of Letters (EOL) for the provision of HR services to UNHCR has been extended for a duration of two years, valid until December 31, 2025.Please be advised that the updates made to the existing documentation are minimal, primarily cosmetic in nature, and do not affect the functioning parameters of our operations. All previous elements, including budget financial templates and the centralized advance funds mechanism, remain unchanged.Despite the minimal updates, the latest templates for any operations covering 2024-2025 must be used. Similar to the current setup, the following requirements will continue for the next two years:Refrain from advising UNHCR offices on applicable fees, as fee setting remains the sole responsibility of the hiring UNHCR office, as per Section 5 REMUNERATION of Annex II of the Administrative Instruction.The advance funds mechanism will continue to be managed centrally from HQ, and therefore no advances are required to be made by individual operations under DAs\nFor sections in Annex B - The Matrix of Responsibilities where UNOPS is required to act as a depository, please ensure full compliance with the requirement. \nSummary of Changes for the 2024-2025 Documents:01 UNHCR-UNOPS 2024-2025 Exchange of Letters (EoL)Additional sentence to paragraph 6: Contract management and administration (including but not limited to initial contract issuance, amendment, extension, and termination), payroll services and insurance management will be conducted by UNOPS.Financial terminology has been updated in section 2.3.12: LMDC -> LSS,  CMDC-P -> GSS-P, CMDC-NP -> GSS-NP. \n02 UNHCR-UNOPS 2024 - 2025 - ANNEX A - Disbursement Agreement - TemplateNo change.Footnote removed as this requirement is standard “From 2022 onwards no advances are required to be made by individual operations under DAs.” \n03 UNHCR-UNOPS 2024-2025 - ANNEX A1234 - Financial Templates:No change.\n04 UNHCR-UNOPS 2024-2025 - ANNEX B - Roles and Responsibilities of the Parties:Removed the reference of the Personal History Form (PHF) and its Supplementary Sheet, which is now replaced by UNHCR’s online application form (generated from Workday)The coordination of medical evacuations is now shared responsibility and it is done in cooperation with the partner. This was already the case in 2023, but not reflected in the matrix.  Reiterating the importance of ensuring the collection of documents for processes where UNOPS acts as a depository.\n05 UNHCR-UNOPS 2024-2025 - ANNEX B1 - SOP for ICA Contract Processing:Removed the reference of the Personal History Form (PHF) and its Supplementary Sheet, which is now replaced by UNHCR’s online application form (generated from Workday).Added a new paragraph on page 11 reading: “In accordance with UNHCR’s request, UNOPS will place ICA holders to Special Leave Without or Partial Pay. UNOPS will also process salary advance payments upon UNHCR’s request. Such actions need to be clearly communicated to the respective UNOPS office.\"Added references to Workday throughout the document, as it is now the default system used by UNHCR DHR. (The references to Workday are relevant to a great extent to UNHCR personnel providing you with the required information needed for contract issuance),  \n06 UNHCR-UNOPS 2023 - ANNEX C - Business Innovations Group (BIG) Principles:No change.Please refer to the SharePoint folder for the UNHCR ICA administration documentation. The 2024-2025 EOL is now also active in OU. You are able to link new engagements to the respective information 10029-04.\nWith this comprehensive update, we trust that you can now commence the necessary procedures to ensure compliance with the deadlines stipulated by BSSC. \nShould you require any further clarification or assistance during this process, please do not hesitate to reach out.\n\nBest Regards,\nLorraine-- \nLorraine Anabtawi | HR Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group |\nUNOPS | Tel: 972548174189 | Skype:\nlorraine.anabtawi | www.unops.org | Supplying value, delivering results,\nchanging lives\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date\nwith UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to\nour external newsletter in English, French or Spanish",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
