                    "00TQx00000AgOLJMA3",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Documents for upcoming June EB session",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-17").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Documents for upcoming June EB session",
                        Description = "To: Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Documents for upcoming June EB session\nBody:\nHi Agnes\n\nThank you very much for your rapid response. I've sent you a calendar invite for Tuesday at 10 AM UK time. Hope that works for you - otherwise just let me know. \nWith regards to the EB, I agree that we should schedule a time this time around to ensure that we get together. I'll be escorting our two relatively new DEDs around throughout the whole week. At the moment we haven't finalised their schedule yet. but once that is in place, I'll reach out to you with some suggested time slots for us to meet up in NYC. \nUntil then: Wishing you a lovely extended weekend! \nSee you next week. \n/Asbjørn\nOn Fri, 17 May 2024 at 13:43, Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjorn,\n \nThank you very much for sending through the links. I’d be happy to have a chat  - could something like Tuesday or Wednesday at 10am UK time work?\n \nIt would be great to catch up in NYC, but please this time let’s arrange a time to sit down together properly! We’re going to have a larger team covering the Board for the Annual Session so this\n time my schedule will be a little more reasonable! I’m going to be less in demand on the Tuesday and Wednesday during plenaries if any of those could be a good time for you?\n \nLooking forward to seeing you soon,\n \nAgnes\n \n \nAgnes Annells| UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road,\n Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA |  agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk |\nwww.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, May 15, 2024 2:13 PM\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Documents for upcoming June EB session\n\n\n \n\nDear Agnes, \n\n \n\n\nAs we are now fast approaching the next Executive Board Annual session on June 3-7, I wanted to reach out to you to provide you with a brief overview of the (very many) documents and topics to be discussed that relate to UNOPS. \n\n\n \n\n\nI have provided you with a brief overview and links to all the documents below for your convenience and ease of reference. Once you have had a chance to get an overview, I was hoping that we could catch up at one of our usual informal talks\n about your initial and informal take on the topics and documents. If possible during next week? Just let me know what time would be convenient for you. \n\n\n \n\n\nI will also be in NYC for the EB session and I was hoping that we could find a time slot to catch up in between meetings? \n\n\n \n\n\n\nTopics and documents for June EB session \n\n\n \n\n\nInternal Audit and Investigation activities in 2023\n\no  \nThe report contains: (a) an opinion on the adequacy and effectiveness of the UNOPS framework of governance, risk management and control; (b) a summary\n of work and the criteria that support the opinion; (c) a statement of conformance with the internal audit standards being adhered to; and (d) a view on whether resourcing of the function is appropriate, sufficient and effectively deployed to achieve the desired\n internal audit and investigation coverage.\n\no  \nMain\ndocument transmitted to the EB\n\ni.annex\n 1 (audit reports in 2023)\n\nii.annex\n 2 (open actions older than 18 months)\n\niii.annex\n 3 (recommendations closed)\n\niv.annex\n 4 (Charter of IAIG)\n\nv.annex\n 5 (KPIs)\n\nvi.annex\n 6 (investigation cases in 2023)\n\nvii.annex\n 7 (advisory committee report for 2023) \n\n                                              \nviii.UNOPS\n management response\n \n\n2.       \nActivities of the Ethics Office in 2023\n\no\nThe report explains the progress made by the Ethics Office in 2023, that includes (a) implementation of an updated “whistle-blower” protection policy, \n (b) training and awareness-raising among UNOPS personnel, (c) a review of the Ethics Office’s independence, (d) completion of all but one action points in the Comprehensive Response Plan, (e) guidance and advice on 533 matters, (f) collaboration with UN Ethics\n Panel on standardization of ethics-related practices and policies, (g) review of 1,022 statements by UNOPS personnel, and (h) completed the foundational work and led collaborations with stakeholders to drive the reform and change processes\n\no\nMain\ndocument  transmitted to the EB and\n\nUNOPS management response.\n \n\n3.       \nReport on implementation of the Restated Strategic Plan in 2023\n\no\nThe report updates on the implementation of the Restated Strategic Plan showing how UNOPS helps fill implementation gaps.\n\n\nThe report shows that almost 2/3 of UNOPS response was in countries in special or fragile situations. Goal 3, ‘good health and well-being’, and Goal 16, ‘peace, justice and strong institutions’, accounted for about half of UNOPS activities. Demand for Goal\n 13, ‘climate action’, and Goal 7, ‘affordable and clean energy’, has yet to materialize to the extent envisaged.\n\nThe performance indicates good progress towards 2025 targets for contribution and management goals. About three quarters are within 25 %-points of the target. Performance towards 10 targets suggests a need for managerial reinforcement.\n\n\nThe report presents two new types of outcome-based reports: case studies of 10 projects contributing to the most vulnerable people and 13 of the Goals; and country reports illustrating contributions to accelerating achievement of 15 Goals across eight countries.\n\no\nMain\n\ndocument transmitted to the EB\n\no\nannex\n 1 (results framework)\n\no\nannex\n 2 (sustainable implementation approaches)\n\no\nannex\n 3 (gender and geographical balance)\n\no\nannex\n 4 (global reporting index)\n\no\nannex\n 5 (engagement with implementing partners)\n\no\nannex\n 6 (UNOPS report on JIU recommendations)\n\no\nannex\n 7 (internal oversight arrangements)  \n\no\nSDG\n 16 report\n\no\nCountry\n reports on UNOPS contributions to the Goals\n\no\nCase\n studies of UNOPS contributions for the most vulnerable people\n \n\n4.       \nStatus on implementation of the Comprehensive Response Plan\n\no\nThis document summarizes progress in implementing the comprehensive response plan. Out of 43 recommendations, 33 have been completed to planned scope,\n 2 have not been operationalized and 1 is led by OLA. Of the outstanding recommendations, 6 will be completed in 2024 and 1 will continue until 2027.\n\no\nMain\n\ndocument transmitted to the EB, \nToR for external review. \n \n\n5.       \nUNOPS’ efforts on repositioning the UN development system\n\no\nThe information note gives an overview of some of the key developments at UNOPS to support the implementation of the repositioning of the UN development\n system. \n\no\nInformation\n note transmitted to the EB\n \n\n6.       \nWork Plan on Organizational Culture\n\no\nThe information note provides a detailed work plan with clear milestones and targets for reshaping UNOPS organisational culture.\n\n\no\nSee\n\nnote on Reshaping UNOPS Organizational Culture as transmitted to the EB. \n \n\n7.       \nUNOPS’ work on protection from sexual exploitation, abuse and harassment (PSEAH)\n\no\nCommon\n UNDP/UNFPA/UNOPS background note transmitted to the EB and \nAnnex C on UNOPS Corporate Action Plan to prevent and respond to sexual exploitation and abuse \n \n\n8.             \nReview of governance and oversight of the EB \n\no\nSee\n\nreport prepared by the Joint Inspection Unit as transmitted to the EB.  \n\n\n \n\n\n\nEnjoy reading - and let's talk next week! \n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation",
