                        Subject = "Email: Brussels 8 Update",
                        Description = "To: \nCC: dejagher@unhcr.org; sofia.lopezpiqueres@un.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Brussels 8 Update\nBody:\nDear Colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for your patience last week while we finalized the UN’s Delegation to the Brussels 8 Conference for Syria. Kindly ensure that your delegation is made aware of the below.\n\n \nI wanted to share with you all the final list of UN Participants at the Brussels 8 Conference.\n \nSome logistical pieces for your kind attention please:\n\nRegistration confirmation: Elke, Sofia and myself sent out all the registration confirmations last week to individual delegations. Please let us know ASAP if you didn’t receive\n it from us. The EU will be validating registrations this week. \n \n\nRequests for Bilateral Space: If you are intending to have bilateral meetings in the margins of the Ministerial Event, we are managing those requests on behalf of the EU. Please\n fill out the form https://forms.office.com/e/bF40KCeJaB to request space. We will do our best to accommodate everyone in 30 minute slots.  Please ensure your bilateral requests are submitted at the latest\n by 25th May as we have to submit them to the EU. Please note that there will be no flags in the bilateral space this year and that the EU will generously provide, tea, coffee and water to support bilateral meetings.\n\n \n\nBadge Collection: With thanks to our colleagues in UN Brussels, badge collection will take place as follows:\nThe badges will be available for collection from Sofia at the UN Office in Brussels on the 6th floor, on Monday, 27 May, from\n 9h to 13:45h.\n\n \n\nFloater badges: We have submitted a request for each delegation to have at least 1 red floater badge and that everyone who does not receive a red floater badge receive pink\n floater badges for the listening room. We will revert once this is confirmed by the EU partners.\n\n \n\nChanges to the delegation: At this time, it is not possible to add additional members of delegation. The only changes that are permitted are to heads of delegation.  If you\n have a change in HoD, please reach out to \nbxl8accreditation@un.org. \n \nThanks again for all your kind support to the process for the UN’s attendance at BXL8! Please let us know if you have any questions.\n \nWarmly,\nAmierah\n \nAmierah Ismail\n\nHumanitarian Affairs Officer\n\nExternal Relations and Partnerships Section\n\nUN OCHA\nM: 917.514.7280\n\nismail53@un.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000Ao949MAB",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "ismail53@un.org", "bxl8accreditation@un.org", "sofia.lopezpiqueres@un.org", "dejagher@unhcr.org" },
