                        Name = "Email: Re: UK participation in the SIDS4?",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UK participation in the SIDS4?",
                        Description = "To: Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UK participation in the SIDS4?\nBody:\nHi Agnes, \nOur Regional Director for the Latin and Caribbean Region will shortly reach out to Mr. Geere to arrange for a meeting during the SIDS. Unfortunately Jorge's calender has been filled with other obligations in the meantime. But I am confident that the two would be an excellent match to discuss in dept how UNOPS could help the FCDO fulfill SIDS objectives with tangible projects. \nOnce again - thank you very much for your kind help with this. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Thu, 23 May 2024 at 16:26, Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Asbjorn,\n \nFor setting up the meeting between the ED and Malcolm, below you’ll find Malcolm’s contact details including his mobile number which will be easiest for arranging a time.\n\n \nMalcolm Geere\n| Development Director for the Caribbean and UK Director to the Caribbean Development Bank | British High Commission Barbados |\nmalcolm.geere@fcdo.gov.uk | +1 246 256 8127\n \nAll the best,\n \nAgnes\n \n \nAgnes Annells| UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road,\n Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA |  agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk |\nwww.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\nFrom: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> \n\nSent: Wednesday, May 15, 2024 12:39 PM\n\nTo: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: UK participation in the SIDS4?\n\n\n\n \nHi Asbjorn,\n \nOur Development Director for the Caribbean, Malcolm Geere, would like to meet the ED. Prior to this role he was our Alternate ED at the IADB – he’s really great. He will be able to talk quite a lot\n of detail on the practicalities of our work on the climate/infrastructure side but I guess it can also be quite an exploratory conversation?\n \nLet me know if there are specific issues you think the ED would like to cover with him, and I can make sure everyone is prepared. I’m still waiting for advice of how we pin down a time but will let\n you know as soon as I have news. Are there any times that would be better for the ED and I can feed them in to our system?\n \nAgnes\n \n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, May 6, 2024 3:07 PM\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UK participation in the SIDS4?\n\n \n\nHi Agnes, \n\n \n\n\nCould you advise on a senor UK official that might be useful for our ED to meet? He is a bit keen on increasing partnership with the UK - and meeting. :-) \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you!\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 3 May 2024 at 13:07, Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n \n\nHi Asbjorn,\n \nFor the SIDS conference, the UK delegation will be led by the Foreign Secretary and Minister Rutley will be out later in the week after the FS departs.\n \nColleagues working on our participation say that if there is a specific event you would like our participation in, please do share more details and we can consider who might be\n able to attend.\n \nIt is looking unlikely that we would be able to offer a Ministerial meeting to the ED as their programmes are already very tight, but there will be a number of senior officials\n travelling so do let me know if this would be of interest.\n \nFinally, they have been engaging a lot with Simona Marinescu from UNOPS in preparation for SIDS4 who has been working with Antigua closely on identifying partnership opportunities,\n including with philanthropy, and on conference organising support. So that is very much appreciated already!\n \nAll the best,\n \nAgnes\n \n \nAgnes Annells| UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and\n Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road, Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA | \nagnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk |\nwww.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nOFFICIAL\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, May 2, 2024 12:01 PM\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UK participation in the SIDS4? \n\n \n\n\nDear Agnes, \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you very much for your rapid and elaborated response. \n\n\n \n\n\nWith regards to the strategic dialogue thanks a lot for the agenda with UN Women. based on that, I will draft a suggestion for what it could look like for UNOPS and revert to you. \n\n\n \n\n\nOn dates, October seems realistic. Would it be possible for you to check if we could settle on a specific day in\nthe week of October 14? That would be the best option on our end. \n\n\n \n\n\nFinally, might you be able to help me identify who would participate in the SIDS4 from the UK side? Jorge\n will participate in the conference and attend a number of side events on climate financing and effectiveness in development projects. It might be useful to see if this could be of UK interests and/or if a bilateral meeting might be convenient. \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you!\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\n\nOn Thu, 2 May 2024 at 10:57, Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n \n\nDear Asbjorn,\n \nThanks very much for your message and the reminders of the issues I owe you responses on.\n\n \nI’m attaching the agenda for the UN Women dialogue – I think we could use this sort of structure as a starting point but there are some tweaks I would probably make. We started\n the dialogue with a bilateral meeting between our DG Development and Humanitarian and a DED, which was followed by an opening session that looked at the overarching relationship. Then we selected a few areas for a more in depth discussion. In general, I think\n objectives are very well aligned so I think we don’t need to spend too much time talking about that. We could increase the time for discussion if we prepare some discussion papers/background reading in advance and focus the discussion around 3 or so key questions/challenges\n we are each trying to address? It would be great to hear any ideas of areas we should focus on. The UNDP dialogue is happening today so there may be other lessons we can apply.\n \nIn terms of dates, we’ve got some transitions happening in the team over the summer so I would suggest that we look at something from October? That way the Boards/UNGA ministerial\n week etc will be out of the way too. Let me do some initial scoping at my end – the really key person for us to pin down is Melinda Bohannan, our DG Humanitarian and Development.\n\n \nI’m still following up on the Somalia Police Programme, and will find out who is attending the SIDs conference for the UK and who is leading on arrangements and let you know.\n\n \nLook forward to catching up ahead of the Boards - it feels like they’ll be here in no time!\n \nAll the best,\n \nAgnes\n \n \nAgnes Annells| UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and\n Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road, Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA | \nagnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk |\nwww.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \n \n \n\n \nOFFICIAL\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, May 2, 2024 8:22 AM\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UK participation in the SIDS4? \n\n \n\nDear Agnes,\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well. \n\n\n \n\n\nI am reaching out to you with a few of our outstanding questions. \n\n\n\n\nIt would be really good if we could please get a date for the strategic dialogue settled - so that planning can commence. As discussed previously, I would also greatly appreciate it if you could forward me an example of a programme that worked well for inspiration\n for a similar dialogue with UNOPS. \nOn the UK share of the Somalia Police programme I will wait for your colleagues to get back to me with instructions on where to transfer the funds. \nI will soon reach out to you in a separate email with info on the upcoming EB session, where I hope that we could have one of our usual informal chats in advance, to get your initial take on the topics to be discussed. \nFinally, I was wondering if you could help me identify who would participate in the\nSIDS4 from the UK side? Jorge will participate in the conference and attend a number of side events on climate financing and effectiveness in development projects. It might be useful to\n see if this could be of UK interests and/or if a bilateral meeting might be convenient. \n\nThank you very much for your always kind help! \n\n\n\n \n\n\nBest,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n \nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n \nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation",
