                new (
                    "00TQx00000AyMmNMAV",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS support to MOH in KGZ",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-24").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS support to MOH in KGZ",
                        Description = "To: beneso@who.int; vedrascol@who.int\nCC: victorkp@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS support to MOH in KGZ\nBody:\nDear Oleg and Liviu!\nHope you guys are doing well - I had a feeling our paths would cross again and I'm very happy for it :)  !!\nSince I left WHO in 2022 I have been busy helping my UNOPS colleagues understand the global public health world (not always easy to navigate!) and connect them with health partners to help expand implementation capacity, esp to accelerate progress in SDG3.\nYou may know UNOPS is the \"operational arm\" of the UN, mandated in Infrastructure, Procurement and Project Management.  Of our total portfolio (USD 1.3 bn per year) over 1/3 is Health focused, we are self financing, and all our projects are needs-driven based on requests from our Partners (member states, international organisations and financing institutions).\nI understand there has been a request in KGZ for some support with the construction of a national vaccine storage warehouse. We stand ready to help you and MOH / EPI (and other key stakeholders) move this forward, if we can be of assistance, given the time and budget constraints as I understand them (from Gavi). My colleague Victor in copy is our partnerships specialist and also Civil Engineer, so he knows his construction stuff :) and is well placed to support.\nI believe Oleg has provided MOH assistance a while back on needs assessment and there are also some WHO guidelines available for vaccine warehouses. We have significant experience in this type of construction (examples include Kosovo, Panama). I would be happy to convene a call for the four of us, if useful, to see if we can help move this forward as a partnership effort on behalf of MOH. Will either of you be at the WHA in Geneva next week?\nA few capacity statements here in case useful Health facilities / Health supply chain management / WASH for health facilities / Laboratory capacity / Solar for health\nLooking forward to hearing from you! \nThanks and best wishes, Louise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000AyMmNMAV",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "victorkp@unops.org", "beneso@who.int", "vedrascol@who.int" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
                        CreatedBy = paoUserEmailMapping.ContainsKey("louisel@unops.org".ToLower()) ? paoUserEmailMapping["louisel@unops.org".ToLower()] : 0,
