                new (
                    "00TQx00000AymGwMAJ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: GLOBAL FUND Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-24").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: GLOBAL FUND Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment",
                        Description = "To: tidjaniw@unops.org; jakobt@unops.org; rainerf@unops.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; elenage@unops.org; seynaboud@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: GLOBAL FUND Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\nBody:\nDear allGreat to speak with Tidjani and Jakob today with Gavi - country mission will help identify how we can support going forward.On Global Fund - see below - Good news!  I will schedule a call with you guys asap to see how we take this forward.Thanks and best wishes Louise \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Lee Hicks <Lee.Hicks@theglobalfund.org>\nDate: Fri, 24 May 2024 at 14:47\nSubject: RE: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>, Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\nCc: Ayi Hervé D'almeida <Herve.Dalmeida@theglobalfund.org>, Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>, Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>, Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>, Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nI hope you are well. My name is Lee Hicks and I am the Program Officer for the GF Guinea-Bissau portfolio. We are pleased to announce that the warehouse\n is now reaching its final stages, and we would like to revisit this discussion with your team to determine the timing to conduct the warehouse engineering assessment. Our team is hoping to conduct the assessment as soon as possible, preferably sometime in\n June. We acknowledge that the turnaround time for this may be a bit tight however please let me know if this timeline is feasible for you. Additionally, if there are any documents/materials that you would need from the UNDP in order for you to conduct this\n assessment, please let us know, as we are happy to liaise with the UNDP to ensure you have the documents needed for you to conduct the evaluation.\n \nOn our end, we’ve shared the UNOPs concept note with the Ministry of Health to obtain their non-objection for contracting and we should receive a response\n within the next week regarding this request. If you would like to hold a quick call to discuss next actions related to starting this assessment, please let us know.\n \nKind regards,\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLee Hicks\nProgram Officer\nGuinea Bissau\nWestern Africa Team\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41762831664\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nlee.hicks@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> \n\nSent: Wednesday, April 24, 2024 6:50 PM\n\nTo: Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Ayi Hervé D'almeida <Herve.Dalmeida@theglobalfund.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Lee Hicks <Lee.Hicks@theglobalfund.org>; Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>; Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>; Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Bruno\n\n\nOk no worries, thanks for the update and look forward to speaking soon \n\n\nBest wishes Louise \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Apr 2024 at 18:30, Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nHope you are well and apologies for the delay in getting back to you on this.\n \nThe warehouse should be almost finalized, allow me to discuss with the team internally in terms of how/when to proceed with\n this assessment, and we’ll get back to you asap.\n \nMany thanks\n\n\n\n\nBruno\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBruno Viana\nFund Portfolio Manager\nGMD\nWestern Africa Team\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41794354176\n\n\n\n\nT: +41587911147\n\n\n\n\nbruno.viana@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, April 2, 2024 11:48 AM\n\nTo: Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>; Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>;\n Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Bruno\n\n\nI hope this finds you well! Just following up to see where we are with the Guinea Bissau project - our my country team\n are keen to understand if there is any news from your side and if they should reach out to offer support to UNDP or we are still \"holding\" this conversation while the Warehouse Agreement is in progress.\n\n\nThanks for letting me know and hope to speak soon.\n\n\nI will be at GHC tomorrow around lunch time if you are free for a quick catch up.\n\n\nAll best wishes\n\n\nLouise \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 11 Jan 2024 at 11:33, Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nHappy new year!\n \nSorry I missed you at the office yesterday, I am just returning to work. Are you planning on going there again soon?\n \nBest\nBruno\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBruno Viana\nFund Portfolio Manager\nGMD\nWestern Africa Team\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41794354176\n\n\n\n\nT: +41587911147\n\n\n\n\nbruno.viana@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, January 10, 2024 3:56 PM\n\nTo: Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhi Bruno!\n\n\nHappy new year!\n\n\nAre you in the office today?  I am here and was wondering if you were free for a 10 minute catch up on the warehouse\n in Bissau?\n\n\nbest wishes Louise\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 31 Oct 2023 at 09:48, Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise and Seynabou,\n \nTrust this email finds you well.\n \nJust following up on this matter in case it is possible for us to finalize the TORs?\n\nMeanwhile also to inform you that the contract for this service will be with our PR UNDP using their grant funds – hope\n this could accelerate the admin process as well.\n \nThanks in advance and looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest\nBruno\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBruno Viana\nFund Portfolio Manager\nGMD\nWestern Africa Team\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41794354176\n\n\n\n\nT: +41587911147\n\n\n\n\nbruno.viana@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, October 23, 2023 1:18 PM\n\nTo: Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>; Moise Touhon <Moise.Touhon@theglobalfund.org>;\n Lee Hicks <Lee.Hicks@theglobalfund.org>; Filiz Cengiz Karakoyun <Filiz.Cengiz@theglobalfund.org>; Chris Dobosz <chris.dobosz@gmail.com>;\n Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>; Fatou Fifi NDIAYE <fatoufn@unops.org>; Ndende MBAYE <ndenem@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Bruno, Louise,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for your feedback on the proposal.\n\n\nI will review it accordingly and get back to you soon. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n----\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSeynabou DIENG\n| Partnership Specialist\n | UNOPS Francophone and Lusophone West Africa | Dakar, Senegal | Tel: +221784684697 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Oct 23, 2023 at 10:43 AM Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nThanks for sharing the concept proposal and budget for the warehouse assessment in Bissau.\nPlease find below our comments for your consideration and finalization of the proposal.\n\nWe will also in the meantime discuss with the MoH in terms of the next steps for contractualization.\n \n\n\nIndicate Individual Personnel: The GF Scope of Work requests a roster of specific individuals and their qualifications (CVs).  The Proposal lists (5) appropriate\n Roles, but not individuals.\n\n·       \nWe would request UNOPS for specific individuals, with an emphasis on at least (1) individual with demonstrated expertise in warehouse design and construction. A warehouse expert was mentioned during\n previous discussions - It’d be good to confirm if this individual, or a peer, would be part of the UNOPS team.\n\n\nComprehensive Operational Assessment is\nnot in Scope of Work:\nThe Proposal suggests an early November Site Visit.  The Warehouse will not be operational until December at the earliest, and likely later.  Thus, it will not be not feasible, nor expected, that any kind\n of comprehensive operational assessment will be part of this proposal.\n\n·       \nIf such assessment is part of the role of the “Expert in the safe storage of pharmaceutical products”, please revise their scope accordingly.\n\n\nAll Work to be Completed & Invoice by End of Year: Due to GF grant guidelines, all work in the Proposal must be completed and invoiced before the end of\n calendar year 2023, including meetings, site visit, and final deliverables (i.e. final report).\n\nOn-Site Teleconference with Global Fund: GF requests a teleconference with the UNOPS team while they’re on site, to hear their immediate findings and be\n able to collaboratively address any areas of interest or challenges the team is having with access or information. We simply want to use this unique opportunity as best possible.\nProvide Cost & Duration for any Suggested Corrective Measures: For any and all suboptimal findings noted, please provide recommended corrective measures\n along with typical costs and durations for such measures.\n \nThanks in advance.\nBest regards\nBruno\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBruno Viana\nFund Portfolio Manager\nGMD\nWestern Africa Team\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41794354176\n\n\n\n\nT: +41587911147\n\n\n\n\nbruno.viana@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, October 19, 2023 11:23 AM\n\nTo: Bruno Viana <Bruno.Viana@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org>; Moise Touhon <Moise.Touhon@theglobalfund.org>; Lee Hicks <Lee.Hicks@theglobalfund.org>;\n Filiz Cengiz Karakoyun <Filiz.Cengiz@theglobalfund.org>; Chris Dobosz <chris.dobosz@gmail.com>; Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>;\n Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Guinea-Bissau Warehouse Engineering Assessment\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Bruno and team\n\n\nPlease find attached concept proposal and budget for the warehouse assessment in Guinea Bissau.\n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you in due course.\n\n\nWith thanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Oct 5, 2023 at 11:20 AM Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear all\n\n\nThank you for your email. I had a meeting with the GB team yesterday and they are ready to take on the project, but are concerned by the timeframe (end Nov. seems more do-able from\n their side). \n\n\nI would be happy to set up a call once they have developed concept / budget. I understand we have previous used MOU for this type of collaboration, I'm closer to tracking down an\n existing template..\n\n\nPls let me know if you need more at this stage\n\n\nBest wishes Louise.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Oct 3, 2023 at 12:04 PM Scott Dubin <Scott.Dubin@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nAs discussed, I have attached a SoW for an independent engineering assessment of a warehouse being constructed in Guinea\n Bissau. We would like UNOPS to identify and contract with independent engineers to undertake the assessment, ideally in late October or early November.\n\n \nPlease let us know if you have any questions.\n \nRegards,\n\nScott\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScott Dubin\nAdvisor, Supply Chain Private Sector Engagement\nIn-Country Supply Chain Management\nSupply Operations\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41764701538\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nscott.dubin@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nGlobal Health Campus\n | Chemin du Pommier 40 | 1218 Grand-Saconnex | Geneva, Switzerland",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000AymGwMAJ",
