he standards of the United Nations.It is impossible to live in good conditions in an organization that commits abuses, ICs need psychological care because the psychic suffering is so atrocious. You wind in the annex the correspondence of UNOPS addressed to the ICs:1. Memorandum Ref; 002-UNOPS DRC Goma -2017.01(Mathieu VANDAL UNOPS Project Manager)2.   Memorandum, ref: 248.UNOPS-DRC-Goma-2023.07,The same memorandums (2) were given to us by Mrs. ZAINAB (UNOPS) in a participatory meeting of the ICs on 27/10/2023. To let you know that the policy of UNOPS is to silence the ICs who speak out and denounce the authority abuses. We remind you once again that it is evidence that UNOPS constitutes a form of mafia that risks tarnishing the image of this peace keeping mission in the DRC. the way UNOPS seeks to silence us, while forbidding us to be in contact with the mission (MONUSCO) for which we work. Can we ask you the question to know who is the boss of UNOPS?We no longer trust the UNOPS administration, the reason why we ask for the involvement of Human Rights, OMBUDSMAN and Legal Affaire for neutral arbitration to avoid UNOPS abuses, protected by some UN staff. If MONUSCO does not intervene, then it will be perceived that MONUSCO is responsible for all the abuses committed by UNOPS over the past 10 years. Because MONUSCO will be considered in this case as a protector of UNOPS.Thank you and best regards.For the Committee of ICs (UNOPS/MONUSCO) MONUSCO GOMACommittee of ICSTRESOR SAFARI, President of the committeeSerge MUGISA, SpokespersonJohn LUNGI, advisorBaby OWANDJI, advisorMrs. MWAMINI CISHWEKA, Communication +243 993 321 760+243 992 835 208+243 975 944 410  From: Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org> \nSent: Saturday, May 04, 2024 12:06 AM\nTo: Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org>; Alejo EIRIZ <alejoe@unops.org>\nCc: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org>; Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>; Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; Raad GILYANA <raady@unops.org>\nSubject: Re: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Hi Laurentiu,\n\nThanks for the update. I'm looping in @Alejo EIRIZ for his information as well.\nBest\nArnaud On Fri, 3 May 2024 at 12:14, Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org> wrote:Dear David,  Thank you for sharing the below information. As far as we are aware in terms of the Monusco operation, based on current data the situation is as follows: - we provide contract management and administration for 804 personnel under the ICA modality, with the most significant population being in DRC (740 personnel)- speaking about DRC alone the distribution of the workforce is as follows:- in addition to that, particularly for Monusco we manage another workforce category called Short Term Daily Workers (STWA), which do not appear in the standard HR reports, and currently account for another 298 Personnel. They are mainly used for short-term assignments ranging from a few weeks to a few months, and Monusco prefers to keep it this way due to the high degree of flexibility and lower-cost.  If for the LICA the entire setup is standard, the STWA has been subject to several discussions in the past, since the current setup is not ideal.  Under this agreement, STWA personnel are not entitled to leave and medical insurance coverage. However, they are covered by Malicious Acts Insurance and Service-incurred insurance, as outlined in their contract. So far, since those contractors are not registered as personnel in oneUNOPS, they don't have resource IDs, however they are registered as suppliers. These contractors are paid via PO payments by the projects, they are not part of the BSSC regular payroll cycle and the majority of the operations are performed manually. A conversation/proposal was triggered with Monusco in order to attempt a conversion to the LICA regular or retainer setup however this was unsuccessful as per the confirmation from our PM.Aside from the above setup, in terms of the items raised in the attached memo's, we are currently looking into the matter and seeking input from our field colleagues in the region responsible for managing the relationship.Lastly, while UNOPS is responsible for managing the contract, the fee setting and any potential yearly progression, together with the associated benefits and entitlements linked to the contract are agreed upon with Monusco.I will  provide an update as soon as possible, Best regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n  On Fri, May 3, 2024 at 8:50 AM David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> wrote:  From: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> \nSent: Friday, May 03, 2024 1:48 PM\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; 'Raad GILYANA' <raady@unops.org>; Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>\nSubject: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Dear Tatiana,  I hope this email finds you well.  Today BSSC received in our generic ICA administration inbox the below email related to the Technical support services (HR services) project with MONUSCO. I copy partnerships who I hope can help you with this matter, since it seems to me that perhaps the problems are created by the requirements and modus operandi of the partner.  Good Luck and please let me know if you need anything from us. Warm regards, David   David Chillaron-Cortizo | Manager | Bangkok Shared Service Centre (BSSC) | Shared Services Centre (SSC) | Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2614 | Mob : +66 8 1627 9262 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French, or Spanish  ---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: COMMITTEE ICs <icscommittee0@gmail.com>\nDate: Thu, May 2, 2024 at 10:22 PM\nSubject: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nTo: <ceesaye@un.org>, <galinierp@un.org>, <unoms@un.org>, <herrmann1@un.org>, <ulbrich@un.org>, <jessica.davila-ardittis@un.org>, <monusco-legal@un.org>, <keita31@un.org>, <gssc.ica.unops.admin@unops.org>\nCc: <dove@un.org>, <amadut@un.org>, <tatianaW@unops.org>, <haynes2@un.org>, <jeanne.diokhpsadio@un.org>, <duwana@un.org>, <kannehb@un.org>, <rizkallahe@un.org>, <Zeinabth@unops.org>, <kisemboserge1984@gmail.com>, <girukwayo@un.org>, <rocheteau@un.org>, <amelia.hannaford@un.org>, <tjitske.dejong@un.org>, <boite@un.org>, jeannes@unops.org <jeannes@unops.org>, <fredericfr@unops.org>, tresorsafari1@gmail.com <tresorsafari1@gmail.com> Dear all MONUSCO Authorities,  Find on attached below the denunciation from ICs for your perusal: examine and take action please: ICs prefer to be managed by another UN agency rather than UNOPS Because of: 1. violation of Respect of Diversity one of the UN Core Values2. Abuse of authority Your support will be highly appreciated ICs' Committee MONUSCO GOMA+243 99 33 21 760+243 97 59 44 410   Best regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n  \n\n---------- Forwarded message ----------\nFrom: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org>\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>, Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>, Raad GILYANA <raady@unops.org>, Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>\nBcc: \nDate: Fri, 3 May 2024 13:48:23 +0700\nSubject: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nDear Tatiana,  I hope this email finds you well.  