                    "00TQx00000BAOFkMAP",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: IMPORTANT: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-29").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: IMPORTANT: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA",
                        Description = "To: fredericfr@unops.org\nCC: nadians@unops.org; jeannes@unops.org; entelas@unops.org; arnauds@unops.org; davidc@unops.org; tatianaw@unops.org; SarahO@unops.org; dalilag@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; valeriek@unops.org; raady@unops.org; victoriac@unops.org; alejoe@unops.org; laurentium@unops.org; ramouh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: IMPORTANT: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nBody:\nDear Frederic,\nThank you for your clarification and elaboration on the situation. We are reviewing the exchanges shared and will reach out with a date to discuss the challenges and explore ways forward.\nBest regards,Lorraine\n\nOn Fri, May 24, 2024 at 9:12 AM Frederic FRIPPIAT <fredericfr@unops.org> wrote:\nDear all,\n\nIt is important to note that the concerns raised are\nnot new, as similar unfounded and exaggerated complaints have been received\nfrom the ICs Committees since the inception of this project in 2015. This\nproject is a partner personnel HR initiative managed by UNOPS on behalf of the\nUN Mission in DRC. The ICs are provided with full information regarding the\nterms and conditions of their contracts before they agree to them. The issue\noften arises when ICs realize that others working directly for the UN Mission\nhave more favorable contracts. However, it is crucial to understand that the\ncontract modalities differ significantly, with those managed by UNOPS having\ndistinct terms and conditions that are clearly communicated to all parties\ninvolved. Despite continuous efforts by our Project Manager and her team to\neducate the ICs and relevant committees on these facts, there seems to be a\nlack of understanding or acknowledgment on their part.\n\nThe ICs allege that UNOPS hinders their direct\ncommunication with the UN mission but this is due to a request from our partner\nMONUSCO. Despite this, the ICs have still reached out directly, disregarding\nthe official project communication channels in place. It is important to note\nthat the UN Mission is scheduled to close down in 2024/2025 at the request of\nthe Congolese Government, leading to understandable anxiety among the ICs,\nalthough this situation is beyond anyone’s control.\n\nJeanne, the Project Manager (PM), and her team are\nmanaging this challenging situation in close cooperation with the UN Mission.\nHowever, they continue to receive unwarranted letters of complaint\nperiodically.\n\nI hope this provides a bit more context of the situation at\nhand.\n\nThank you,Fred\nOn Thu, May 23, 2024 at 5:19 PM Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Jeanne,\nThank you for your response. In the attached email, \"DENUNCIATION OF ABUSE OF AUTHORITY From ICs committee\", it mentions that there is a letter from UNOPS, could you kindly share a copy with us so we have an overview of what has been communicated to MONESCO? \nThank you and best regards,Lorraine  \nOn Thu, May 23, 2024 at 3:27 PM Jeanne Diokh SADIO <jeannes@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Entela and All,\nPlease be informed that  I have discussed the issue with the MONUSCO Contracts Management section.As per attached exchange emails, the matter is currently being handled by the partner, MONUSCO.The OIC, Contracts management officer will share a draft response to ICs with UNOPS to review.\n\nI will keep you updated on any development.\nWith kind regards,Jeanne\n Jeanne Diokh SADIO\n| Cheffe de Projets  Senior, MONUSCO | UNOPS | Congo Multi Country Office - (CDMCO) | MONUSCO RVA, Room E 23, 100 Av. du Lac, Quartier Katindo, Commune de Goma, RDC | Tel. mobile : +243 (0) 812 394 485 | Ext 195-8388 | Skype:\njeanne.diokh1 | UNOPS is ISO 9001 certifiedKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\n\n \n\nOn Thu, May 23, 2024 at 1:00 PM Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Arnaud, \nThank you for your email and the query. \nI am cc-ing here Jeanne, the PM of this project, who has the details of the specific exchange with MONUSCO. \nBest regards Entela  Entela SULA | Head of Partnerships Development and Communication | AFR CDMCO Bureau Multi-Pays pour RDC, RCA, RC, Angola, Burundi, Cameroun, Comores, Equatorial Guinea, Gabon, Madagascar, Rwanda, Seychelles, Mauritius, Sao Tome & Principe, Capo Verde | 34, Avenue Pumbu, Commune de la Gombe, Kinshasa, RDC | Tel.+243 8311 94911 | Email: entelas@unops.org | www.unops.org/rdc | Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\nOn Thu, May 23, 2024 at 12:29 PM Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org> wrote:\nDear David, \nThank you for forwarding this email. We have followed up internally (see Laurentiu's email of 3 May).\n\nHowever, given the seriousness of the claims outlined in the memo, we believe it is important to have a documented conversation with Monusco to clarify each party's responsibilities and liabilities regarding the contractors. It would be great to hear from CDMCO colleagues about their discussions with MONUSCO regarding the memo and the concerns raised by the ICs. \n\nDear Tatiana and CDMCO colleagues,\n\nPlease let us know whether there have been any discussions with MONUSCO regarding:\n1. the memo and the concerns raised by the ICs\n2. the possibility of transitioning these contractors to a more regular or retainer setup, such as LICA.\nThis conversation should clearly specify who manages and oversees the contractors, including their payment, supervision, and any associated legal or regulatory requirements. It is important to highlight that ICs are personnel governed by explicit terms of service agreements and are considered commercial vendors.\n\nPlease let us know if you have any questions or would like Lorraine and Laurentiu to join the discussions with MONUSCO.\n\nKind regards,\nArnaud\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org>\nDate: Thu, 23 May 2024 at 07:10\nSubject: FW: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>, Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>, Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>, Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>, Raad GILYANA <raady@unops.org>, Alejo EIRIZ <alejoe@unops.org>\n\nDear Arnaud, Laurentiu and colleagues,  Yesterday (22 May 2024) BSSC received in our generic ICA administration inbox another email complaint related to the Technical support services (HR services) project with MONUSCO. Please find the email below.  The email had an attachment called: Memorandum UNOPS Interdit, included in this email.  Further below, I have kept the correspondence related to the first email complaint. The attachments that were included in that first email are also included in this email. I wish you luck in resolving this matter successfully. Thank you and best regards, David   David Chillaron-Cortizo | Manager | Bangkok Shared Service Centre (BSSC) | Shared Services Centre (SSC) | Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2614 | Mob : +66 8 1627 9262 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French, or Spanish  ---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: COMMITTEE ICs <icscommittee0@gmail.com>\nDate: Wed, May 22, 2024 at 9:08 PM\nSubject: DENUNCIATION OF ABUSE OF AUTHORITY From ICs committee\nTo: <galinierp@un.org>, <tjitske.dejong@un.org>, <zervos@un.org>, <vahard@un.org>, <ocholla@un.org>\nCc: <ceesaye@un.org>, <dove@un.org>, <herrmann1@un.org>, <unoms@un.org>, <gssc.ica.unops.admin@unops.org>, <haynes2@un.org>, <Zeinabth@unops.org>, <jeannes@unops.org>, <tatianaW@unops.org> Dear Tjitske de Jong,We were alerted in our letter of May 02, 2024, some abuses of UNOPS, but so far, the services that are supposed to restore us to our rights seem to line up behind those who exploit the ICs and commit abuses by their administration policy that does not respect the standards of the United Nations.It is impossible to live in good conditions in an organization that commits abuses, ICs need psychological care because the psychic suffering is so atrocious. You wind in the annex the correspondence of UNOPS addressed to the ICs:1. Memorandum Ref; 002-UNOPS DRC Goma -2017.01(Mathieu VANDAL UNOPS Project Manager)2.   Memorandum, ref: 248.UNOPS-DRC-Goma-2023.07,The same memorandums (2) were given to us by Mrs. ZAINAB (UNOPS) in a participatory meeting of the ICs on 27/10/2023. To let you know that the policy of UNOPS is to silence the ICs who speak out and denounce the authority abuses. We remind you once again that it is evidence that UNOPS constitutes a form of mafia that risks tarnishing the image of this peace keeping mission in the DRC. the way UNOPS seeks to silence us, while forbidding us to be in contact with the mission (MONUSCO) for which we work. Can we ask you the question to know who is the boss of UNOPS?We no longer trust the UNOPS administration, the reason why we ask for the involvement of Human Rights, OMBUDSMAN and Legal Affaire for neutral arbitration to avoid UNOPS abuses, protected by some UN staff. If MONUSCO does not intervene, then it will be perceived that MONUSCO is responsible for all the abuses committed by UNOPS over the past 10 years. Because MONUSCO will be considered in this case as a protector of UNOPS.Thank you and best regards.For the Committee of ICs (UNOPS/MONUSCO) MONUSCO GOMACommittee of ICSTRESOR SAFARI, President of the committeeSerge MUGISA, SpokespersonJohn LUNGI, advisorBaby OWANDJI, advisorMrs. MWAMINI CISHWEKA, Communication +243 993 321 760+243 992 835 208+243 975 944 410  From: Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org> \nSent: Saturday, May 04, 2024 12:06 AM\nTo: Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org>; Alejo EIRIZ <alejoe@unops.org>\nCc: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org>; Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>; Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; Raad GILYANA <raady@unops.org>\nSubject: Re: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Hi Laurentiu,\n\nThanks for the update. I'm looping in @Alejo EIRIZ for his information as well.\nBest\nArnaud On Fri, 3 May 2024 at 12:14, Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org> wrote:Dear David,  Thank you for sharing the below information. As far as we are aware in terms of the Monusco operation, based on current data the situation is as follows: - we provide contract management and administration for 804 personnel under the ICA modality, with the most significant population being in DRC (740 personnel)- speaking about DRC alone the distribution of the workforce is as follows:- in addition to that, particularly for Monusco we manage another workforce category called Short Term Daily Workers (STWA), which do not appear in the standard HR reports, and currently account for another 298 Personnel. They are mainly used for short-term assignments ranging from a few weeks to a few months, and Monusco prefers to keep it this way due to the high degree of flexibility and lower-cost.  If for the LICA the entire setup is standard, the STWA has been subject to several discussions in the past, since the current setup is not ideal.  Under this agreement, STWA personnel are not entitled to leave and medical insurance coverage. However, they are covered by Malicious Acts Insurance and Service-incurred insurance, as outlined in their contract. So far, since those contractors are not registered as personnel in oneUNOPS, they don't have resource IDs, however they are registered as suppliers. These contractors are paid via PO payments by the projects, they are not part of the BSSC regular payroll cycle and the majority of the operations are performed manually. A conversation/proposal was triggered with Monusco in order to attempt a conversion to the LICA regular or retainer setup however this was unsuccessful as per the confirmation from our PM.Aside from the above setup, in terms of the items raised in the attached memo's, we are currently looking into the matter and seeking input from our field colleagues in the region responsible for managing the relationship.Lastly, while UNOPS is responsible for managing the contract, the fee setting and any potential yearly progression, together with the associated benefits and entitlements linked to the contract are agreed upon with Monusco.I will  provide an update as soon as possible, Best regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n  On Fri, May 3, 2024 at 8:50 AM David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> wrote:  From: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> \nSent: Friday, May 03, 2024 1:48 PM\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; 'Raad GILYANA' <raady@unops.org>; Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>\nSubject: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Dear Tatiana,  I hope this email finds you well.  Today BSSC received in our generic ICA administration inbox the below email related to the Technical support services (HR services) project with MONUSCO. I copy partnerships who I hope can help you with this matter, since it seems to me that perhaps the problems are created by the requirements and modus operandi of the partner.  Good Luck and please let me know if you need anything from us. Warm regards, David   David Chillaron-Cortizo | Manager | Bangkok Shared Service Centre (BSSC) | Shared Services Centre (SSC) | Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2614 | Mob : +66 8 1627 9262 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French, or Spanish  ---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: COMMITTEE ICs <icscommittee0@gmail.com>\nDate: Thu, May 2, 2024 at 10:22 PM\nSubject: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nTo: <ceesaye@un.org>, <galinierp@un.org>, <unoms@un.org>, <herrmann1@un.org>, <ulbrich@un.org>, <jessica.davila-ardittis@un.org>, <monusco-legal@un.org>, <keita31@un.org>, <gssc.ica.unops.admin@unops.org>\nCc: <dove@un.org>, <amadut@un.org>, <tatianaW@unops.org>, <haynes2@un.org>, <jeanne.diokhpsadio@un.org>, <duwana@un.org>, <kannehb@un.org>, <rizkallahe@un.org>, <Zeinabth@unops.org>, <kisemboserge1984@gmail.com>, <girukwayo@un.org>, <rocheteau@un.org>, <amelia.hannaford@un.org>, <tjitske.dejong@un.org>, <boite@un.org>, jeannes@unops.org <jeannes@unops.org>, <fredericfr@unops.org>, tresorsafari1@gmail.com <tresorsafari1@gmail.com> Dear all MONUSCO Authorities,  Find on attached below the denunciation from ICs for your perusal: examine and take action please: ICs prefer to be managed by another UN agency rather than UNOPS Because of: 1. violation of Respect of Diversity one of the UN Core Values2. Abuse of authority Your support will be highly appreciated ICs' Committee MONUSCO GOMA+243 99 33 21 760+243 97 59 44 410   Best regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n  \n\n\n\n\n-- \nLorraine Anabtawi | HR Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group |\nUNOPS | Tel: 972548174189 | Skype:\nlorraine.anabtawi | www.unops.org | Supplying value, delivering results,\nchanging lives\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date\nwith UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to\nour external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\n\n \n\n \n\n-- \n\n\nBest regards, \nFred Frippiat | Head of Programme  | Centre Opérationnel de l’UNOPS | AFR CDMCO| Multi-Country Office: RDC, RCA, RC, Angola, Burundi, Cameroun, Comores, Equatorial Guinea, Gabon, Madagascar, Rwanda, Cape Verde, Sao Tome and Principe, Seychelles and Mauritius | 34 Avenue Pumbu, Commune de la Gombe, Kinshasa, RDC | Portable: +243 823368533 |www.unops.org/rdc | Email: Fredericfr@unops.org\t\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nLorraine Anabtawi | HR Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group |\nUNOPS | Tel: 972548174189 | Skype:\nlorraine.anabtawi | www.unops.org | Supplying value, delivering results,\nchanging lives\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date\nwith UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to\nour external newsletter in English, French or Spanish",
