                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-03").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA",
                        Description = "To: davidc@unops.org\nCC: tatianaw@unops.org; lorrainea@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; raady@unops.org; arnauds@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nBody:\nDear David, \nThank you for sharing the below information.\nAs far as we are aware in terms of the Monusco operation, based on current data the situation is as follows:\n- we provide contract management and administration for 804 personnel under the ICA modality, with the most significant population being in DRC (740 personnel)- speaking about DRC alone the distribution of the workforce is as follows:\n- in addition to that, particularly for Monusco we manage another workforce category called Short Term Daily Workers (STWA), which do not appear in the standard HR reports, and currently account for another 298 Personnel. They are mainly used for short-term assignments ranging from a few weeks to a few months, and Monusco prefers to keep it this way due to the high degree of flexibility and lower-cost.  If for the LICA the entire setup is standard, the STWA has been subject to several discussions in the past, since the current setup is not ideal.  Under this agreement, STWA personnel are not entitled to leave and medical insurance coverage. However, they are covered by Malicious Acts Insurance and Service-incurred insurance, as outlined in their contract. So far, since those contractors are not registered as personnel in oneUNOPS, they don't have resource IDs, however they are registered as suppliers. These contractors are paid via PO payments by the projects, they are not part of the BSSC regular payroll cycle and the majority of the operations are performed manually. A conversation/proposal was triggered with Monusco in order to attempt a conversion to the LICA regular or retainer setup however this was unsuccessful as per the confirmation from our PM.Aside from the above setup, in terms of the items raised in the attached memo's, we are currently looking into the matter and seeking input from our field colleagues in the region responsible for managing the relationship.Lastly, while UNOPS is responsible for managing the contract, the fee setting and any potential yearly progression, together with the associated benefits and entitlements linked to the contract are agreed upon with Monusco.I will  provide an update as soon as possible, Best regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\nOn Fri, May 3, 2024 at 8:50 AM David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> wrote:\n  From: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> \nSent: Friday, May 03, 2024 1:48 PM\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; 'Raad GILYANA' <raady@unops.org>; Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>\nSubject: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Dear Tatiana,  I hope this email finds you well.  Today BSSC received in our generic ICA administration inbox the below email related to the Technical support services (HR services) project with MONUSCO. I copy partnerships who I hope can help you with this matter, since it seems to me that perhaps the problems are created by the requirements and modus operandi of the partner.  Good Luck and please let me know if you need anything from us. Warm regards, David   David Chillaron-Cortizo | Manager | Bangkok Shared Service Centre (BSSC) | Shared Services Centre (SSC) | Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2614 | Mob : +66 8 1627 9262 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French, or Spanish  ---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: COMMITTEE ICs <icscommittee0@gmail.com>\nDate: Thu, May 2, 2024 at 10:22 PM\nSubject: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nTo: <ceesaye@un.org>, <galinierp@un.org>, <unoms@un.org>, <herrmann1@un.org>, <ulbrich@un.org>, <jessica.davila-ardittis@un.org>, <monusco-legal@un.org>, <keita31@un.org>, <gssc.ica.unops.admin@unops.org>\nCc: <dove@un.org>, <amadut@un.org>, <tatianaW@unops.org>, <haynes2@un.org>, <jeanne.diokhpsadio@un.org>, <duwana@un.org>, <kannehb@un.org>, <rizkallahe@un.org>, <Zeinabth@unops.org>, <kisemboserge1984@gmail.com>, <girukwayo@un.org>, <rocheteau@un.org>, <amelia.hannaford@un.org>, <tjitske.dejong@un.org>, <boite@un.org>, jeannes@unops.org <jeannes@unops.org>, <fredericfr@unops.org>, tresorsafari1@gmail.com <tresorsafari1@gmail.com> Dear all MONUSCO Authorities,  Find on attached below the denunciation from ICs for your perusal: examine and take action please: ICs prefer to be managed by another UN agency rather than UNOPS Because of: 1. violation of Respect of Diversity one of the UN Core Values2. Abuse of authority Your support will be highly appreciated ICs' Committee MONUSCO GOMA+243 99 33 21 760+243 97 59 44 410  \nBest regards, Laurentiu Mastacan | HR Partnerships Analyst | PLG, Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7816 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.\n\nOn Fri, May 3, 2024 at 8:50 AM David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> wrote:\n  From: David CHILLARON-CORTIZO <davidc@unops.org> \nSent: Friday, May 03, 2024 1:48 PM\nTo: Tatiana WAH <tatianaw@unops.org>; Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\nCc: Emilie POTVIN <emiliep@unops.org>; 'Raad GILYANA' <raady@unops.org>; Arnaud SGAMBATO <arnauds@unops.org>\nSubject: FW: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA Dear Tatiana,  I hope this email finds you well.  Today BSSC received in our generic ICA administration inbox the below email related to the Technical support services (HR services) project with MONUSCO. I copy partnerships who I hope can help you with this matter, since it seems to me that perhaps the problems are created by the requirements and modus operandi of the partner.  Good Luck and please let me know if you need anything from us. Warm regards, David   David Chillaron-Cortizo | Manager | Bangkok Shared Service Centre (BSSC) | Shared Services Centre (SSC) | Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2614 | Mob : +66 8 1627 9262 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French, or Spanish  ---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: COMMITTEE ICs <icscommittee0@gmail.com>\nDate: Thu, May 2, 2024 at 10:22 PM\nSubject: ICs denunciation trough ICs committee GOMA\nTo: <ceesaye@un.org>, <galinierp@un.org>, <unoms@un.org>, <herrmann1@un.org>, <ulbrich@un.org>, <jessica.davila-ardittis@un.org>, <monusco-legal@un.org>, <keita31@un.org>, <gssc.ica.unops.admin@unops.org>\nCc: <dove@un.org>, <amadut@un.org>, <tatianaW@unops.org>, <haynes2@un.org>, <jeanne.diokhpsadio@un.org>, <duwana@un.org>, <kannehb@un.org>, <rizkallahe@un.org>, <Zeinabth@unops.org>, <kisemboserge1984@gmail.com>, <girukwayo@un.org>, <rocheteau@un.org>, <amelia.hannaford@un.org>, <tjitske.dejong@un.org>, <boite@un.org>, jeannes@unops.org <jeannes@unops.org>, <fredericfr@unops.org>, tresorsafari1@gmail.com <tresorsafari1@gmail.com> Dear all MONUSCO Authorities,  Find on attached below the denunciation from ICs for your perusal: examine and take action please: ICs prefer to be managed by another UN agency rather than UNOPS Because of: 1. violation of Respect of Diversity one of the UN Core Values2. Abuse of authority Your support will be highly appreciated ICs' Committee MONUSCO GOMA+243 99 33 21 760+243 97 59 44 410",
