                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000BCWYuMAP",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Touching base and notice of dinner invitation 28th May 2024",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-05-29").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Touching base and notice of dinner invitation 28th May 2024",
                        Description = "To: timl@unops.org\nCC: emiliep@unops.org; JeromeDT@unops.org; LaetitiaK@unops.org; janphilipk@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; sophiedj@unops.org; mykhailot@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Touching base and notice of dinner invitation 28th May 2024\nBody:\nDear Tim,\nJust a quick update on the dinner I attended yesterday, hosted by Friends of Europe on \" Winning Peace: building a secure and democratic future in Ukraine\".\nThe dinner was attended by some 40 people. Among them, senior diplomats to NATO, the EU, EEAS reps, former Presidents of Croatia and Lithuania, GIZ Rep here and in Ukraine, think tanks and private sector.\nThe keynote speech was made by Olha Stefanishyna, Deputy Prime Minister for European and Euro-Atlantic Integration of Ukraine. I had the opportunity to exchange with her and she said that she knows UNOPS from her role of coordination of humanitarian work there and was glad of our presence and work.\nThe main theme of the dinner was the Summit on Peace in Ukraine on 15-16 June at the Bürgenstock (Canton of Nidwalden), presented by the Deputy head of Switzerland Mission to the EU. The aim of the meeting, which will be at heads of state and government level, will be to develop a common understanding on how to achieve a just and lasting peace in Ukraine. What came out very clearly was the intention to involve as much as possible the global south, to make sure they come onboard as opposed to an evident pro-Russia position. Members of G20 will be invited with the exception of Russia,\nThe discussion was very much politically oriented and about defence issues, also around \"what if Trump wins\"?\nEven though I had gotten great inputs from Mykhailo, I was not able to take the floor (only 1h30 hrs time!) but UNDP Nick Hartmann, Deputy Regional Director of the Regional Bureau for Europe and CIS took the floor to explain what UNDP and the other UN agencies do in Ukraine in terms of energy supply, mine action etc. He even mentioned the EB members upcoming visit to Ukraine. He actually said that UNDP shares the same board with a few other UN agencies but he did not dare mention which ones (and the rep of UNFPA in Brussels and myself were there :). We spoke a bit after the end of the dinner (can tell you more).\nI will have some follow-up meetings with some of the participants at the dinner in the coming days and will keep you informed.\nBest regards,Carmen\n\nAttached is the list of participants.Mariacarmen Colitti | Head of Office and Representative | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Brussels, Belgium | Tel: + 32 2 7881840| www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Fri, May 3, 2024 at 8:47 AM Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org> wrote:\nCarmen\nThanks so much for this - and I really enjoyed the panel with Friends of Europe that I sat on when I was in Brussels a few months ago.\nLogistically this will be a real challenge for me - I am in transition from Kyiv to Geneva and plan to be in Copenhagen that day to start settling in. I do think it is a great showcasing opportunity, so let me mull this over through and see if there is someone else we could consider.\nThanks\nTim\nTim Lardner | Regional Director Europe and Central Asia Region | Director UNOPS Multi Country Office Ukraine | Tel/Whatsapp: +41772464777 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Thu, 2 May 2024 at 21:11, Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org> wrote:\nSorry sent it too quickly.\nCopying also Emilie and BLO team for their information.\nBest regards CarmenMariacarmen Colitti | Head of Office and Representative | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Brussels, Belgium | Tel: + 32 2 7881840| www.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nLe jeu. 2 mai 2024 à 20:09, Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org> a écrit :\nDear Tim,\nJust sharing this invitation I got from Friends of Europe.\nWe believe this would be a good opportunity for you to showcase UNOPS role in Ukraine .\nI did attend one of these events before on the Paris summit and it was really great and helped me to make more friends!\nPlease let me know if you wish me to confirm \nBest regardsCarmen\nMariacarmen Colitti | Head of Office and Representative | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Brussels, Belgium | Tel: + 32 2 7881840| www.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n---------- Message transféré ---------\nDe : Dharmendra Kanani <dharmendra.kanani@friendsofeurope.org>\nDate : jeu. 2 mai 2024 à 14:39\nObjet : Touching base and notice of dinner invitation 28th May 2024\nÀ : Mariacarmen Colitti (mariacarmenco@unops.org) <mariacarmenco@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Maria Carmen,\n \nHow are you? I hope all is well with you and yours. It has been some time since we exchanged and I know you wanted to a month or so before getting back to us but I didn’t want chase.\n \nSeparately, and in advance of inviting other UN agencies, I wanted to let you know that we are organising an exclusive dinner with high level personalities from our Ukraine Initiative Steering Group. They will all be\n in town for our Ukraine Security Forum on 28th May. Given I have interviewed your main colleague/country head in Ukraine and know of the work you are doing, it would be great to have you present if possible. Also, if you think we should invite a\n senior colleague also from UNOPS let me know but they would have to be at your level or above – I hope you understand given the names I list below:\n \nJaap\n de Hoop Scheffer, former NATO Secretary-General;\nŠtefan Füle; former European Commissioner for Neighbourhood and Enlargement;\nKolinda Grabar-Kitarović, former President of Croatia; Oleksandra Matviichuk, Ukrainian Nobel peace prize Winner and European Young Leader alumna;\nDalia Grybauskaitė, former President of Lithuania; Rose Gottemoeller, former Deputy Secretary-General of NATO;\nPhilippe Maze-Sencier, President of Teneo France and former Chair of Global Public Affairs of Hill & Knowlton Strategies;\nMike Ryan, lecturer on world affairs and Russian history, former US Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defence for European and NATO policy.\n \nThey will all be present at the dinner which will be Chatham House as usual. Let me know what you think and if you are able to come. Given the nature of the debate we area planning we will be inviting other UN agencies\n and a host of related Ambassadors. Look forward to hearing from you.\n \nRegards,\nDharmendra \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDharmendra Kanani\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nChief Operating Officer & Chief spokesperson\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFriends of Europe ‑ Connect. Debate. Change.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe think tank for a more inclusive, sustainable and forward‑looking Europe\n\n\n\n\nTransparency register 99436366768‑45\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ndharmendra.kanani@friendsofeurope.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n\n, \nB‑1000 Brussels",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000BCWYuMAP",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "laetitiak@unops.org", "dharmendra.kanani@friendsofeurope.org", "emiliep@unops.org", "janphilipk@unops.org", "mariacarmenco@unops.org", "eleneag@unops.org", "jeromedt@unops.org", "sophiedj@unops.org", "timl@unops.org", "mykhailot@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
                        CreatedBy = paoUserEmailMapping.ContainsKey("mariacarmenco@unops.org".ToLower()) ? paoUserEmailMapping["mariacarmenco@unops.org".ToLower()] : 0,
