                new (
                    "00TQx00000BLlleMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-06-03").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support",
                        Description = "To: tidjaniw@unops.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; jakobt@unops.org; seynaboud@unops.org; fatoufn@unops.org; elenage@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support\nBody:\nDear Tidjani\nThanks for this very positive update and congratulations on project development!  On tripartite - will Gavi set up the meetings with WHO and UNICEF?  For your information we have UN to UN Agreement with both WHO and UNICEF (e.g. see Agreement 21747-DRAFT12)\nOn the waste management / incinerators, UNOPS (GPO Geneva) acts as procurement agent for the Global Fund (non-health product ordered through WAMBO, the Global Fund online market place).  This means Guinea Bissau ministry of health (the Global Fund principal recipient) could use GAVI funding to order through the domestic channel of WAMBO, if they wish. GPO Geneva has vehicles in the procurement pipeline already for Global Fund programmes.  We could help coordinate :)\nLooking forward to hearing moreBest wishes Louise\n\nOn Mon, 3 Jun 2024 at 12:45, Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org> wrote:\nHello Dear colleagues,I hope my message finds you well. \nI would like to share with you the summary of my discussion with Mr. Seydou Ouedraogo, Gavi's Country Manager.\nDuring our meeting, I discussed our contribution to health facilities in Guinea-Bissau, particularly in the areas of infrastructure and procurement, purchase and supply of equipment . \nWe then discussed opportunities for collaboration between UNOPS and Gavi. We agreed that UNOPS could provide its expertise to the vaccination chain by taking over the collection and management of vaccination waste. This includes the construction of incinerators in large cities, the establishment of a waste sorting system, and the collection and transport of waste from small health centers to a central treatment and disposal site.\nMr. Ouedraogo informed me of his intention to also meet with WHO and UNICEF during his mission. He clarified that UNOPS will receive funding from Gavi through WHO or UNICEF. Therefore, it is necessary to organize tripartite meetings between UNOPS, WHO and Gavi, or between UNOPS, UNICEF and Gavi, as soon as possible.\nOverall, we had a fruitful exchange.\n\nThank you very much Have a great day.\n\nBe Safe and Healthy!Best Regards !\nTidjani.\nTidjani  WAHABOU │Senior Project Manager/Head of Office│UNOPS AFR, SNMC, GUINEE-BISSAU│Mob: +245 956 647 964│Skype: wtidjani_1│www.unops.org │\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us\non Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French\nor Spanish\n                  \n\nOn Tue, May 28, 2024 at 8:29 AM Jakob TUBORGH <jakobt@unops.org> wrote:\nBonjour Tidjani,\n\nEst-ce que tu as vu la proposition dans l'e-mail ci-dessous ? Merci de répondre directement à Marius.\n\nBonne journee!\n\nJakob \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Marius Keller <mariuskeller1@outlook.com>\nDate: Mon, May 27, 2024 at 10:52 PM\nSubject: RE: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>, Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>\nCc: Marius Keller <mkeller@gavi.org>, Seydou Mohamed Ouedraogo (Consultant) <souedraogo@gavi.org>, Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>, Fatou Fifi NDIAYE <fatoufn@unops.org>, Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>, Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>, Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>, Ferdinand NZEYE <ferdinandn@unops.org>, Jakob TUBORGH <jakobt@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nThanks for looping me in.\n \nWould your country team be available for lunch on Thursday June 6 at around 12.15pm?\n \nBest,\n\nMarius\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, May 24, 2024 10:18 AM\n\nTo: Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Marius Keller <mkeller@gavi.org>; Seydou Mohamed Ouedraogo (Consultant) <souedraogo@gavi.org>; mariuskeller1@outlook.com; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Fatou Fifi NDIAYE <fatoufn@unops.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>; Seynabou DIENG\n <seynaboud@unops.org>; Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>; Ferdinand NZEYE <ferdinandn@unops.org>; Jakob TUBORGH <jakobt@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support\n\n \n\n\nGreat thanks so much Danielle! Yes I just got Marius' out of office and sent my email to his new address :)\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 24 May 2024 at 12:16, Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise\n \nThanks for the email and organizing the meeting. Please note the new email address of\n@mariuskeller1@outlook.com so that he can also be loop in in the conversation. We look forward meeting with you in country.\n \nBest,\nD\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, May 24, 2024 12:13 PM\n\nTo: Danielle Rosset <drosset@gavi.org>; Marius Keller <mkeller@gavi.org>; Seydou Mohamed Ouedraogo (Consultant) <souedraogo@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Fatou Fifi NDIAYE <fatoufn@unops.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>;\n Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>; Tidjani WAHABOU <tidjaniw@unops.org>; Ferdinand NZEYE <ferdinandn@unops.org>;\n Jakob TUBORGH <jakobt@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Gavi / UNOPS Guinea Bissau support\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know\n the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Seydou and Danielle,\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for the call this morning - it was great to e-meet you and get us all connected at the country, regional and global level! Sorry\n we missed Marius on this occasion!\n\n\n \n\n\nFollowing our discussion, we duly note the upcoming\n3-7 June Gavi mission in Guinea Bissau, and @Marius if possible will find time in the schedule for our country teams to meet. The objective being to discuss some of the operational challenges that UNOPS could support MOH / Gavi / other in-country\n partners with going forward - with a focus on complementary activities, and where we can\nadd value or help expand / accelerate existing activities. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs requested by Seydou please see below a few of our\n\"capacity statements\" to give you an idea of how we are helping countries and their partners expand implementation capacity to improve health infrastructure, health procurement and health programme management. \n\n\n \n\n\nI will keep you updated on the\nUNOPS / Gavi Framework Agreement that is being finalised in case of need (I'm working with Irina Petkova and Laurent in your Legal team on this).\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing back on the in-country discussions - and I am often at GHC in case you are free for a coffee any time :)\n !\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Health\n facilities\n\n\n- Health\n supply chain management\n\n\n- WASH\n for health facilities\n\n\n- Laboratory\n capacity\n\n\n- Solar\n for health\n\n\n- Digital\n health\n\n\n- Capacity\n development\n\n\n- Emergency\n response\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nJakob TUBORGH | Directeur p.i. -  UNOPS - Afrique de l'Ouest francophone, lusophone et du Maghreb | Complexe SICAP, Point E, Immeuble C, 5ème étage  - Dakar, Sénégal | Tel: +221 33 869 3848 | +221.33 869 3838 | Mobile: +221 77 569 8335 | www.unops.org/fr Suivez l’UNOPS sur Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nAbonnez-vous à notre bulletin d’information externe en français, en anglais ou en espagnol.",
