                    "00TQx00000BOzybMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS Gavi collab - capacity statements",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-06-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS Gavi collab - capacity statements",
                        Description = "To: hjohnson@gavi.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS Gavi collab - capacity statements\nBody:\nDear Hope\nHow are you doing?  Hope all is going well :)  \nGood to see you fleetingly at the WHA77 breakfast event Tokunbo invited me to last week. It was an extremely thought provoking and transparent session, please congratulate Sania for me!   Tokunbo had asked me to make an intervention about UNOPS in country implementation support but we ran out of time unfortunately.\nI would love to regroup on some of the info I shared below, and hope to be signing our framework agreement around mid June to help facilitate our engagements going forward, given the growing requests from Gavi!  \n\nIn other news, I see Sania is listed to speak at the World Health Summit in October this year in Berlin - do you know who is organising Gavi participation? \n\nLooking forward to speaking again soon!Thanks and best wishes Louise \n\nOn Mon, 11 Mar 2024 at 18:06, Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Hope\nGreat to see you on Thursday, so nice to catch up after so long and congrats again on the new role! Exciting times ahead :) \n\nAs promised pls see below in case of interest - a few capacity statements covering our support in cold chain, warehousing, programme management, solar and a few others! (there's more if you need :)\nLooking forward to keeping in touch a bit more regularly now!!\nAll best wishes for the week ahead!Louise \nUNOPS - Medical Waste Management\nUNOPS - Health programme capacity building \nUNOPS - Health Programme and Fund Management \nUNOPS - Health supply chain management and warehousing \nUNOPS - Solar for Health",
