                        Subject = "Email: Global Fund and Ethiopia",
                        Description = "To: workneshg@unops.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org; kulenid@unops.org; lydiaat@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Global Fund and Ethiopia\nBody:\nDear WorkneshGreat to hear you are invited to UNCT ad hoc meeting with Global Fund who are in country on mission tomorrow, 20 June.For info / background:  The overall Fund Portfolio Manager is George SAKVARELIDZE - he oversees an 8 person team (in Geneva) - see list below.  \nUNOPS currently provides 3 main types of support to Global Fund Globally:1. as Principal recipient in Asia region - multi country grant of note, Malaria RAI3E project in Mekong2. as Local Fund agent (like independent auditor) in 9 countries, primarily in eastern europe3. as Procurement specialist, providing non health items through the WAMBO platform (Global Fund portal into UNWB+) to help the Principal Recipients implement programmes - see here from slide 9 for additional information on typical procurement demands.  The WAMBO project is managed out of GPO/Geneva (PM - Marion Cassen).  VIP I encourage UNOPS country offices to work with WAMBO team as needed - e.g. procurement of oxygen materials through WAMBO - can be complemented by UNOPS country office support for related logistics / infrastructure / training etc \nLet me know if you need anything else and I look forward to hearing how it goes.Good luck!Louise\nGlobal Fund Ethiopia Country TeamAkmal KarimovLegal OfficerDardane ArifajHealth Product Procurement and Supply Chain ManageEvelyn ZbindenProgram OfficerGeorge SakvarelidzeFund Portfolio ManagerIvandra ChirrimeMonitoring and Evaluations SpecialistMalika El AissiLegal OfficerParvina OdilkhonovaFund Portfolio AssistantPriscah MwaiFinance OfficerRosemary NdibalemaProgram Officer\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
