                new (
                    "00TQx00000C5gxWMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: World Refugee Day: Celebrating strength",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-06-20").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: World Refugee Day: Celebrating strength",
                        Description = "To: andrewk@unops.org\nCC: ecr.gva.all.personnel@unops.org; elenali@unops.org; plg.personnel@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: World Refugee Day: Celebrating strength\nBody:\nThanks for this Andrew! and to complement this information on #WorldRefugeeDay - since December 2023, UNOPS is also now a signatory to the UN Common Pledge. 2.0 where we, along with 20+ UN agencies have commited globally, to renew and strengthen our efforts to promote refugee inclusion. \nWe are working closely with UNHCR, one of the PLG/GLO-managed Partnerships, to review and report back on what UNOPS is doing to \"walk the talk\" to implement this commitment. You can see the UNOPS pledge here (LiD is also included in the dashboard :)\nWe currently have a survey out (thanks @Elena Librino) to gather baseline data from all of UNOPS country offices (9 of whom are already contributing to the UN country pledges) in order to measure our contribution over time.  \nThe first annual resident coordinator webinar on the UN common pledge 2.0 was held on Tuesday 18 June - if interested the recording is available here: UN Common Pledge RC Webinar June 2024 Recording.mp4 (sharepoint.com). \nHappy to provide any further information and look forward to reflecting all of UNOPS work globally in support of refugees and IDPs in the months and years ahead!\nBest wishesLouiseLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Thu, 20 Jun 2024 at 08:01, Andrew KIRKWOOD <andrewk@unops.org> wrote:\nDear colleagues\nToday, on World Refugee Day, let's take a moment to acknowledge the incredible strength and resilience of millions of refugees and host communities whose lives have been impacted by displacement.World Refugee Day serves as a reminder of the ongoing displacement crisis. We are deeply committed to supporting displacement-affected communities. We believe that everyone deserves an opportunity to build a life of their own, choosing and contributing to the societies in which they live. In particular, I want to highlight the great work of three of our engagements that contribute to supporting refugees around the world:The Lives in Dignity Grant Facility funded by the EU, which provides refugees, host communities, and other displacement-affected people with the resources and agency to design and implement solutions that foster self-reliance. Since 2021, LiD has allocated $27 million to a diverse group of implementing partners, half of which are local. The facility's geographic scope includes 14 projects across 15 countries in Asia, Latin America, and Sub-Saharan Africa.Cities Alliance has just launched the Supporting Urban Integration of Displacement-Affected Communities (SUIDAC) programme in Sub-Saharan Africa, supported by a €30 million grant from the EU. This four-year initiative targets cities in DRC, Ethiopia, Somalia, Sudan, and Uganda, aiming to enhance the integration of refugees and their host communities and improving self-reliance, social cohesion, and local governance through infrastructure and sustainable urban planning. The Platform on Disaster Displacement plays a crucial role in advocating for refugees and promoting solutions for governments to welcome and support them. Their work supports those fleeing the devastation of natural disasters, so that they receive the protection and assistance they deserve.On this World Refugee Day, I encourage you to:Watch these inspiring stories of resilience from the LiD-funded project in Uganda and South Sudan. Also this short video on the work of the LiD Grant FacilityBe an advocate: Share World Refugee Day information and resources with your networks using #WithRefugees, #WorldRefugeeDay and #UNOPS.Consider volunteering your time or donating to organizations supporting people affected by displacementAll the best,Andrew\nAndrew Kirkwood (he/him) | Geneva Office Director, Global Portfolios Office | +41 795203669 | www.unops.org",
