                new (
                    "00TQx00000C6m7zMAB",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: INTERNAL - Switzerland - update",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-06-20").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: INTERNAL - Switzerland - update",
                        Description = "To: jorge.moreiradasilva@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; hilaryb@unops.org\nCC: asbjornb@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: INTERNAL - Switzerland - update\nBody:\nDear all\nSummary: This is to update you on my regular informal call with the UNOPS focal point at SDC, the Swiss Agency for Development Cooperation (SDC/Martin Borgeaud, MB) on 19 June. The tone remains tepid but Switzerland continue to sign agreements for existing & related projects (Palestine, Cities Alliance, North Macedonia...) Jorge scheduled to speak with Patricia Danzi and team on 6 August.\nOn the June EB / closed session: SDC feels true dialogue (beyond \"communications exercise\") is still missing and that \"SDC questions are still not answered\". I urged MB/SDC to submit their questions in writing, for us to respond more effectively and help us to move forward. MB will follow up to see if that is desirable. I also reminded that perm rep did not respond, and SDC Head of Agency only recently agreed, to speak bilaterally with JMdS. MB shared they felt \"different bilateral conversations with different EB members / countries are not always useful and cannot replace effective and transparent conversations through existing governance structures\" Recovery of S3i funds\nMB questioned whether paying USD 1 million to OLA for an investigation on the recovery of S3i funds is money well spent and asked what is the realistic chance of recovering any of the misused funds.Partnership / Agreements \nMB repeated \"UNOPS is not a priority organisation for Switzerland\"; they are still not comfortable with \"tone from the top\" (perception  of policy over operations; too quick to turn the page; impunity)  MB is following ongoing negotiations regarding the transfer of Swiss funds to the Santiago Network (GPO) and the Platform on Disaster Displacement (GPO) and others, confirming with the additional step of a PRA (partner risk assessment) Agreements are likely to be approved - though all must be signed off by Head of Agency.SDC/MB welcome the engagement with IAIG, seen as \"very important and always helpful\"MB and I will speak again in July, before Jorge and Patricia's scheduled call (6 August). Following which, we will plan for 2024 dialogue.\nHappy to answer any specific / further questions.Best wishes\nLouise",
