                        Name = "Email: Re: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-03").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire",
                        Description = "To: Claire.Cazeneuve@theglobalfund.org\nCC: Marcus.Deepe@theglobalfund.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire\nBody:\nDear ClaireGreat, how about any time after 14hrs on 10 or 11 July. I can come to GHC.Thanks for letting me know what works best for youBest wishes Louise.\nOn Fri, 28 Jun 2024 at 09:36, Claire Cazeneuve <Claire.Cazeneuve@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n\n \nThanks for your message.\n\nUnfortunately, next Thursday won't work for us, as Marcus will be in Abidjan.\n\n \nCan I suggest the following week, Wednesday 10 or Thursday 11 ? It can be via Teams, no problem for us.\n\n \nThanks.\n\n \nBest,\n\n \nClaire\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nClaire Cazeneuve\nSenior Program Officer\nHigh Impact Africa 1 Department\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41796070264\n\n\n\n\nT: +41587911152\n\n\n\n\nclaire.cazeneuve@theglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, June 27, 2024 3:28 PM\n\nTo: Claire Cazeneuve <Claire.Cazeneuve@theglobalfund.org>; Marcus Deepe <Marcus.Deepe@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: Fwd: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Claire and Marcus\n\n\nHope this finds you well. Following the exchange with Paula, I was reaching out to see if you are free next week for a short meeting. I will be at GHC on thursday 4th afternoon if that works\n for you?\n\n\nOtherwise feel free to suggest an alternative.\n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you\n\n\nBest wishes Louise\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\n\nFrom: Paula Hacopian <Paula.Hacopian@theglobalfund.org>\n\nDate: Fri, 21 Jun 2024 at 09:07\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire\n\nTo: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>, Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>\n\nCc: Claire Cazeneuve <Claire.Cazeneuve@theglobalfund.org>, Marcus Deepe <Marcus.Deepe@theglobalfund.org>\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Louise\nThank you for reaching out.\n\nI will be travelling to Abidjan for two weeks and then I will be on leave.\n\nWe don’t have any specific needs at the moment for the portfolio but it would be a good idea for you to\n touch base with my colleagues Claire and Marcus so they can learn about the services you offer in case the need arises.\nThank you\nPaula\n \n\nPaula Hacopian\n\n\nSenior Fund Portfolio Manager\n\nHigh Impact Africa I\n\nGrant Management Division\n\n\n\npaula.hacopian@theglobalfund.org\norg\n\nM: +41 79 599 6526 \n\n\n\nThe Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria\n\nGlobal Health Campus\nChemin du Pommier 40\n1218 Grand-Saconnex, Switzerland\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\nfacebook.com/theglobalfund\n\ntwitter.com/globalfund\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, 20 June, 2024 17:13\n\nTo: Seynabou DIENG <seynaboud@unops.org>; Paula Hacopian <Paula.Hacopian@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS support to Global Fund Cote d'Ivoire\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Paula \n\n\n \n\n\n Global\n Fund Brown Bag Presentation\n\n \n\n\nApologies for not reaching out sooner! I was hoping you may have been at our \"brown\n bag\" session in February when we had some of our Africa multi country office teams here in Geneva to meet Global Fund colleagues for an interactive session on how UNOPS can support GF / MOH /PRs. Please find attached a few slides if helpful.  \n\n\n \n\n\nI am copying here my colleague Seynebou in Dakar and we were hoping to set up a quick\n call with you to discuss procurement (not available on WAMBO) and distribution support.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe work in many countries supporting GF / MOH / PRs and have well-established modalities\n to engage and partner.\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you and meeting soon - I'm a regular visitor at GHC\n and happy to pop over!\n\n\nThanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
