                    "00TQx00000ClQeUMAV",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Cote d'ivoire",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Cote d'ivoire",
                        Description = "To: seynaboud@unops.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Cote d'ivoire\nBody:\nHi SeynabouThanks for the call the other day, always lovely to catch up as always, and thanks for the clarifications on the Cote d'Ivoire project.  So I spoke with WHO HQ energy expert after we chatted, and he's keen to have a chat with us - can you suggest me a couple of days and times next week that work for you? (and anyone else you think should join)  I have copied his comments below n blue so you get the idea ....I am trying to get us into a more systematic collaboration with WHO to align on approaches and also to get their support / recommendation of our health infra work more broadly. Solarisation of health care facilities is one piece of the broader puzzle :) Looking forward to hearing from youBest wishes Louise \nI completely agree on the critical importance of training. This is indeed a fundamental aspect.In some cases, however, training covers particularly the preventive maintenance, while a budget allocation is still needed in case of future need for spare parts or to pay the curative maintenance interventions from specialized technicians. Often the health facilities do not have the budget to cover these curative maintenance costs, and in many cases project funds do not consider this long-term budget allocation. In some cases this happens because all the grant needs to be spent by a certain date, and this is not compatible with long term and future disbursements. Do you know by any chance if such curative maintenance budget and relevant long-term disbursements have been considered by the donors in the below cases, and what the disbursement arrangements are? I look forward to continuing these conversations with you, and to talking with your colleagues in charge of the health-care facilities solarization project in Cote D´Ivoire at your/their earliest convenience, if helpful.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000ClQeUMAV",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "seynaboud@unops.org", "elenali@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
