                        Subject = "Email: Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC",
                        Description = "To: martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC\nBody:\nDear Martin\nI hope this finds you well, despite the very changeable summer weather conditions !\nDuring Q1 and Q2 I have spoken with a number of colleagues across UNOPS and hosted entities regarding their conversations and negotiations on projects that may (or may not) be supported by SDC funding. Please find here the list, please confirm it aligns with yours:Santiago Network, (Hosted, Geneva)Platform on Disaster Displacement, (Hosted, Geneva)Scaling Up Nutrition, (Hosted, Geneva)Cities Alliance, (Hosted, Brussels)UNOPS Cooperation in Northeast Asia (Mekong office)UNOPS North Macedonia (Serbia office)UNOPS Tunisia UNOPS Jerusalem (for Palestine ASU)UNOPS Mozambique   I understand Partner Risk Assessments (PRA) are either in discussion, in progress or have been completed for each of these project engagements. This week I heard there has been a further revision to the SDC internal memo specifying that external consultants are now being appointed by SDC to undertake the PRAs going forward - would you please confirm this is the case and clarify if this is just for UNOPS projects or broader?   \nGiven ongoing conversations, I have taken the liberty of re-sharing the fee setting methodology as well as a short overview of UNOPS role in the Mozambique Peace Support Secretariat (attached) in case this might be useful background to share internally.\n\nFinally, following our last conversation I was wondering if there was any update on the submission of written questions from you/your colleagues regarding the actions being taken by UNOPS as a result of the S3i crisis, to further clarify what has been shared through formal and informal mechanisms.\nI hope you have managed to get some leave scheduled :) I will be heading out from Wednesday next week for two weeks. Happy to have a quick catch up  Monday/Tuesday, otherwise, otherwise just before Patricia and Jorge meet virtually on 6 August as agreed on our last call.\nLooking forward to hearing from youThanks and best wishesLouise \n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
