                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Partner Risk Assessment (SDC)",
                        Description = "To: anan@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Partner Risk Assessment (SDC)\nBody:\nDear AnaHope all is well with you!  Has the SDC PRA been completed - I saw you mentioned the end of June 2024 in your earlier email.  Is this now a fixed quarterly process? Thanks for letting me know!\nBest wishes Louise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Tue, 7 May 2024 at 13:14, Ana NEDELJKOVIC BELJA <anan@unops.org> wrote:\nDear colleagues, \nFirst, I apologize for the late response,due to the Easter holidays in Serbia last week. \nSince many of you have expressed interest in the SDC Partner Risk Assessment, I am providing all the information about the process as well as links to specific files which you can also find in the corporate drive folder for SDC Partner Risk Assessment:SDC ToR for selecting a firm to carry out the PRA: in Serbia, the PRA was conducted by the audit firm DFK during October-November 2022, before signing the contract with SDC for the PRO programme in December 2022.A questionnaire with 48 questions divided into following areas: legal, governance, accounting and reporting, cash management, budgeting, audit, procurement, HR, PM, Asset, ICT. Note: in addition to the questionnaire, we also had a series of meetings with the DFK, according to these areas where we provided additional information and clarifications about UNOPS rules and regulations, processes, mechanisms, structures, and more. Also, where necessary and possible, we also provided officially available documents as evidence they requested.Initial document with recommendations from the audit firm DFK with UNOPS comments – namely, DFK shared the recommendations with us for review before sending them to SDC, we provided comments, however, in the final version (the following file) we do not see that they have made any changes.PRA recommendations updated by SDC in November 2023PRA recommendations updated by UNOPS in January 2024 SDC in Serbia has asked UNOPS RSMCO to perform a semi-annual update of the PRA recommendations to monitor progress towards the agreed recommendations. The next update is planned for the end of June 2024. \nAlso, I am copying colleagues from RSMCO who participated in the process in North Macedonia (SDC used the PRA from Serbia) and are equally informed about the PRA process. \nIf you have any additional questions or uncertainties, feel free to contact us.\n\nBest regards,Ana\nOn Wed, 1 May 2024 at 12:41, Gilda SENTIES PORTILLA <gildasp@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Ana, \nHope this email finds you well. I am contacting you because of an SDC Partner Risk Assessment that I'm supporting with in HQ. In trying to assess whether another project or unit has already responded to such an assessment from the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation, I came across project 23801, PRO Local Programme for People and Nature. I can see in the project drives you have a subfolder entitled SDC Partner Risk Assessment (see screenshot below), so I wonder if by any chance you'd have that already completed and you could share it with us. It would help us a great deal, also in terms of consistency.\nMany thanks in advance,Gilda Senties Portilla (she/her), PhD | Due Diligence Specialist | Risk and Compliance Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen | www.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
