                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: IPAS-186711 Standardized Agreement UNOPS-GAVI: Question on adding GOV signature box in the template",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: IPAS-186711 Standardized Agreement UNOPS-GAVI: Question on adding GOV signature box in the template",
                        Description = "To: ipas.solution.portal@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: IPAS-186711 Standardized Agreement UNOPS-GAVI: Question on adding GOV signature box in the template\nBody:\nThanks - Gavi came back to me with a request regarding upcoming engagement with DRC. As per the practice so far established with UNOPS, in DRC the GA should be tripartite. Gavi’s suggestion is not to re-open discussion on the template, but just to add a signature box (ideally with a preceding sentence \"acknowledgment of receipt\", as the Government would not technically be a party since all rights and obligations relate to Gavi and UNOPS) for the Government to sign on page 10.\n\nOn Fri, 12 Jul 2024 at 13:23, Clothilde FESTOC <noreply@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n —-—-—-—\n \n \n Reply above this line.\n \n \n \n Clothilde FESTOC commented:\n Dear Louise,\n In order to expedite anything, I need to understand what the request is. Has GAVI expressed a need to renegotiate the tripartite agreement template ? What is the issue we wish to address here ? As mentioned in my previous message, the tripartite mechanism covers a different legal scenario than the template under negotiation.\n Best regards,\n Clothilde\n \n \n View request · Turn off this request's notifications\n This is shared with Beria MUTUNKAME VICTORIA, Fiona MERALI, Frederic FRIPPIAT, and 3 other people.\n Powered by Jira Service Management\n \n Sent on 12 July 2024 13:23:02 CEST",
