                        Subject = "Email: Re: [EXTERNAL] Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC",
                        Description = "To: martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: [EXTERNAL] Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC\nBody:\nOK great, let's do lunch Monday at 13.00 at \"Cuisine Lab\" just round the corner from GHC (you will need security entry badge there, which I can sort out, but it's a bit more fuss!). Sound OK?!\n\nOn Fri, 12 Jul 2024 at 15:01, Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise, I could also do 1PM (lunch?). Let me know what works best for you.\nMartin\n \n\n\nFrom: Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 12, 2024 3:01 PM\n\nTo: 'Louise LEECH' <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: [EXTERNAL] Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC\n\n\n \nDear Louise,\n\n \nWe could meet at 3PM at the GHC (never been there I assume there must be a cafe there?).\n\n \nBest,\nMartin\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 12, 2024 2:39 PM\n\nTo: Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch>\n\nSubject: Re: [EXTERNAL] Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC\n\n \n\nHi Martin\n\n\nAh Thanks good point I will Check and add. \n\n\nMonday can work for me between 13-14h or 15h-17h Anywhere around the Palais / WHO / GHC - let’s me know What works for you \n\n\nBest wishes \n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 12 Jul 2024 at 14:20, Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n\n \nThanks for the list and information. I believe the UN Waters project is missing from the list.\n\n \nRegarding a call next week – sure. Would be happy to touch base before you go on leave. Shall we say Monday\n afternoon (could meet in person or through a call)? \n \nBest,\nMartin\n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 12, 2024 2:03 PM\n\nTo: Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch>\n\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Update and tracking UNOPS/SDC\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this finds you well, despite the very changeable summer weather conditions !\n\n\n\n \n\n\nDuring Q1 and Q2 I have spoken with a number of colleagues across UNOPS and hosted entities regarding their conversations\n and negotiations on projects that may (or may not) be supported by SDC funding. Please find here the list, please confirm it aligns with yours:\n\n\n\n\nSantiago Network, (Hosted, Geneva)\nPlatform on Disaster Displacement, (Hosted, Geneva)\nScaling Up Nutrition, (Hosted, Geneva)\nCities Alliance, (Hosted, Brussels)\nUNOPS Cooperation in Northeast Asia (Mekong office)\nUNOPS North Macedonia (Serbia office)\nUNOPS Tunisia \nUNOPS Jerusalem (for Palestine ASU)\nUNOPS Mozambique   \n\n\nI understand Partner Risk Assessments (PRA) are either in discussion, in progress or have been completed for each of\n these project engagements. This week I heard there has been a further revision to the SDC internal memo specifying that external consultants are now being appointed by SDC to undertake the PRAs going forward - would you please confirm this is the case and\n clarify if this is just for UNOPS projects or broader?   \n\n\n \n\n\nGiven ongoing conversations, I have taken the liberty of re-sharing the\n\nfee setting methodology as well as a short overview of UNOPS role in the Mozambique Peace Support Secretariat (attached) in case this might be useful background to share internally.\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFinally, following our last conversation I was wondering if there was any update on the submission of written questions\n from you/your colleagues regarding the actions being taken by UNOPS as a result of the S3i crisis, to further clarify what has been shared through formal and informal mechanisms.\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope you have managed to get some leave scheduled :) I will be heading out from Wednesday next week for two weeks.\n Happy to have a quick catch up  Monday/Tuesday, otherwise, otherwise just before Patricia and Jorge meet virtually on 6 August as agreed on our last call.\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you\n\n\nThanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
