                    {
                        Name = "Email: Request for meeting with new UNOPS Deputy Executive Director, ASG Kirstine Damkjær",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-25").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Request for meeting with new UNOPS Deputy Executive Director, ASG Kirstine Damkjær",
                        Description = "To: cristina.de-carvalho@sida.se; karl.svensson@gov.se\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Request for meeting with new UNOPS Deputy Executive Director, ASG Kirstine Damkjær\nBody:\nDear Karl and Cristina, \nI hope this email finds you well with at least some sunny days in Stockholm (unlike Copenhagen...). \nAs I briefly mentioned to Karl earlier today, our new Executive Director, ASG Kirstine Damkjær would very much like to go to Stockholm during the fall to pay a visit to her Swedish peers, considering the importance of our partnership with Sweden. \nWith regards to bilateral meetings at the MFA I was thinking that it might be useful for her to meet Carl Hartzell and Michael Hjelmåker. Anyone else that might be relevant to meet?\nWith regards to SIDA perhaps it would be relevant for Kirstine to meet Elisabet Brandberg. Anyone else at SIDA that might be relevant? \nWith regards to meeting topics I was thinking that it might be useful to discuss the status of UNOPS' reform process, the situation in Ukraine and Gaza, status of ongoing Swedish funded UNOPS projects and then perhaps see where there might be possibilities for expanded collaboration - especially in fragile and conflict affected areas. \nAs always I would be very happy to hear your thoughts and suggestions - and then I look very much forward to seeing you in Stockholm! \nThank you very much for your kind help! \nBest regards,Asbjørn\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
