                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: LICA management for UNFPA",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-25").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: LICA management for UNFPA",
                        Description = "To: delagarza@unfpa.org\nCC: waiters@unfpa.org; weidmann@unfpa.org; ArnaudS@unops.org; LaurentiuM@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: LICA management for UNFPA\nBody:\nDear Mayra,\nI hope this email finds you well. Thank you for the updates regarding the policy review and staffing changes at UNFPA. We appreciate the introduction to Ms. Katrina Waiters and look forward to working with her in her new role.\nWe understand the importance of the upcoming changes through the transition to the UNFPA Local Service Contract (LSC) and offer our continued collaboration should UNOPS be the chosen local Country Office service provider. We look forward to receiving the final draft of UNFPA's LSC policy and KPIs. I am also sharing UNOPS’ HR Services presentation as a refresher to our previous discussions and happy to connect for a call next week at your convenience.  We look forward to resuming our conversation, Best,Lorraine\nOn Wed, Jul 24, 2024 at 10:13 PM Mayra De La Garza <delagarza@unfpa.org> wrote:\nDear Lorraine,\nI hope this email finds you well. Since Jan's last email to you, we have had a few updates at UNFPA. First, the policy was reviewed by the UNFPA Executive Committee but still not promulgated. There is an outstanding issue of applicability i.e. whether we will allow the contract to be offered for professional services rather than exclusively for support functions.\nAnother change is related to our staffing. Mr Jan Weidmann has accepted a new role in the Ethics Office effective November 2023. Allow me to introduce you to Ms. Katrina Waiters, who has taken over the role as focal point for the new contract modality. \nWe anticipate making a change from UNDP Service Contracts to the new UNFPA Local Service Contract (LSC) in Q4 of this year, with the idea of offering UNFPA Country Offices the choice of service provider, i.e. LSC to be administered by either UNDP as customized Partner Personnel Services Agreement, or UNOPS as customized LICA.\nTo enable this, we would like to resume our conversation with you for a global service level agreement. Please let us know what information you would require from UNFPA at this stage. We could share the final draft of our LSC policy, and also the KPIs that our Deputy Executive Director has asked for as part of any future agreement.\nKind regards,mayra\nMayra M. De La GarzaChief, Policy and Staff RelationsDivision for Human ResourcesUNFPA\n+1.212.297.5312 | delagarza@unfpa.org\n\nOn Tue, Oct 17, 2023 at 9:50 AM Jan Weidmann <weidmann@unfpa.org> wrote:\nDear Lorraine,\nThank you for following up. The policy was presented at our Policy Committee last week and it was endorsed. However, there is still one item that was considered controversial and the policy will therefore be discussed at our Executive Committee. Therefore, unfortunately, it is not ready to be shared yet, as we do not have the final approval yet. We will keep you posted as things progress.\nBest,Jan\nOn Tue, Oct 17, 2023 at 7:16 AM Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Jan,\nI trust this email finds you well.I am writing to follow up on whether the policy has been approved and ready to share?\nThank you,Lorraine\nOn Wed, Sep 27, 2023 at 6:06 PM Jan Weidmann <weidmann@unfpa.org> wrote:\nDear Lorraine,\nIt was a pleasure meeting you and your colleagues yesterday! \nPlease find attached as promised a table with the locations of our Service Contract holders. We will share the policy with the conditions once it has been approved. \nBest regards,Jan\nOn Tue, Sep 26, 2023 at 11:38 AM Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Jan,Thank you for your time today. As discussed, I am sharing the updated presentation on HR services and look forward to receiving the overview of the contractors/duty stations and locations of UNFPA offices at your convenience. Best regards,\nLorraine\nOn Mon, Sep 18, 2023 at 11:09 PM Jan Weidmann <weidmann@unfpa.org> wrote:\nDear 