                new (
                    "00TQx00000DohnLMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-05").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: isabelaf@unops.org\nCC: solv@unops.org; leyres@unops.org; elsaa@unops.org; arantzazuo@unops.org; josem@unops.org; sylviaac@unops.org; villelyv@unops.org; benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org; mgreco@iadb.org; ALAINLO@iadb.org; JUANITAR@iadb.org; PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org; DENISEC@iadb.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\nBody:\nHi Isabela and colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for returning the documents. We are looking forward to finalizing with you at the earliest. \n\n \nAs the team will not be available next week due to other commitments, we would like to propose another date. Denise will coordinate with you on Monday to find the most convenient\n date and time.\n \nKind regards and have a good weekend.\n\n \nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 5, 2024 1:54 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>; Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>; Sylvia\n AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>;\n Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\nDear Shirley and colleagues, \n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached the latest version of the MoU (v4.0) with our proposal regarding the fee (section 8.1) and the template for project implementation we propose to include annexed to the MoU. This template is based on a project we recently\n signed in Argentina, it is in Spanish, so it would require translation to both English and French once approved. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe'd like to propose next Thursday 11th, 8:30-9:30 AM Panama/9:30-10:30 AM Washington DC for our meeting. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jul 2, 2024 at 1:31 PM Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nHi Shirley, \n\n \n\n\nPlease disregard my previous email as we managed to find a solution.\n\n\n \n\n\nOur teams are reviewing the document and we will add the suggested template at the bottom, in accordance to the previous email. We'll send it back as soon as possible, this will facilitate reviewing it ahead of our next meeting. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best, \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jul 2, 2024 at 7:21 AM Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Shirley, \n\n \n\n\nWould it be possible to re-send the latest version of the MoU in google docs? we didn't have this problem before, but this time around this file in particular isn't being supported by google. We can see the new comments yet we can't add\n anything to the document, and we need to be able to edit the file to include the information that is being requested. \n\n\n \n\n\nThanks in advance for the support. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Jun 28, 2024 at 5:44 AM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\nHappy Friday! Please find attached the draft PFA with our comments.\n\n \nWe have sent the meeting invitation for Monday.\n\n \nHave a good weekend!\n \nShirley\n \n\n\nFrom: Gayle, Shirley Maud\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, June 26, 2024 11:29 AM\n\nTo: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\nCc: Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA\n <isabelaf@unops.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>;\n Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel\n VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>;\n Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n\n \nDear Sol,\nIt was our pleasure to have you here at the IDB and we look forward to meeting other members of the team.\nWe have no objection to the inclusion of some language addressing coverage of UNOPS’ fees as an eligible expense. For\n the Bank however, it is absolutely critical that the agreement is definitive on the fees, either in terms of a range or at the minimum, a cap.\n\n \nWe hope that we can find a meeting point on this key issue. We are inviting your team to a meet this Monday July 1,\n at 10:30 where we can finalize the document.\n \nKind regards,\nShirley\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, June 24, 2024 6:25 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA\n <isabelaf@unops.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>;\n Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel\n VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nDear Shirley, \n \nThank you very much for your time last week, it was a great pleasure to meet you and Patricia in person and discuss topics of mutual interest. Based on our conversation,\n we’d like to move forward with the possibility of avoiding a capped fee in our framework agreement, since this is something that UNOPS doesn’t normally do to ensure consonance with our cost-recovery policy. We hereby share more information on our approach\n to fee setting here.\n This is an external document that we share with our stakeholders so they have a clear understanding of the procedures we follow in terms of fee setting, and ensure transparency. In this sense, we can work on a paragraph that details this information in our\n agreement. \n \nLikewise, we are\nsharing here\n the latest version of our MoU with updated revisions from our team. \n \nWe consider that the framework agreement should reflect that the IDB has no objection to financing the UNOPS fee and eligible expenses within the project, provided\n these are included in the loan account at the borrower's request. In this sense and in alignment with our collaborative goals, we would like to propose that it be stated that the IDB is amenable to covering the UNOPS fee and any eligible expenses related to\n the project. These costs can be incorporated into the loan account upon the borrower's formal request to ensure clarity and mutual understanding.\n \nPlease let us know of any updates on your side in regards to the fee setting. We are happy to work on the aforementioned paragraph so UNOPS’ cost-recovery policies\n and net zero revenue approach are properly showcased in the agreement, to ensure transparency in our operations and with stakeholders. \n \nWarm regards, \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jun 11, 2024 at 10:05 AM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol and colleagues,\n \nI hope you are all doing well. Thanks for our recent meeting.\n\n \nPlease find attached the updated draft.\n\n \nWe look forward to hearing from you. Can we set a date soon to continue the discussions on the agreement?\n \nMany thanks and best regards,\nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, June 5, 2024 10:42 AM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>; Arantzazu\n OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>;\n Elise REICHE PEREIRA <eliserp@unops.org>; Hurwitz, Zachary\n Daniel <zacharyh@IADB.ORG>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria\n <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Pierre-Olivier LANGLOIS <pierreol@unops.org>; Salabie, Denise\n Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>;\n Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>;\nelisabets@unops.org;\njosem@unops.org; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>;\n Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\nDear Shirley,\n\n\n \n\n\nMost grateful for your time and feedback on today's call. We would dearly appreciate it if you could send us as soon as possible the MOU draft discussed today including the new\n comments. We would also appreciate the template draft in order to compare both sets of documents. Meanwhile, if you could send us the MOU draft it would be great so that we can continue our internal process, especially to assess the proposed comments and for\n us to evaluate the fee clause about a cap/ fixed fee which has not been originally included.\n\n\nThanks in advance,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Jun 3, 2024 at 7:00 AM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\n \nPleasant start to the week! Thanks for confirming the meeting. We prefer to use Teams so we will send the invitation.\n \nBest regards,\nShirley\n \n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, May 31, 2024 8:58 AM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>; Arantzazu\n OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>;\n Elise REICHE PEREIRA <eliserp@unops.org>; Hurwitz, Zachary\n Daniel <zacharyh@IADB.ORG>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria\n <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Pierre-Olivier LANGLOIS <pierreol@unops.org>; Salabie, Denise\n Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>;\n Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>;\nelisabets@unops.org;\njosem@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Shirley,\n\n\n \n\n\nGreetings from Panama! Reaching out to confirm availability for a call on\nJune 5th to discuss the agreement that we all reviewed. \n\n\n \n\n\nAccording to the calendars of most of our team members, they are available, so we have put a placeholder to alert everyone about this time slot. Given that we have people in different\n regions and time zones, I propose it to be at 8 am Panama Time / 9 am EDT. \n\n\n \n\n\nPlease confirm if this time is convenient for you and would appreciate it if you could kindly let me know if you would like us to send the invitation for the call (Google Meet)\n or if you have a preferred platform.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to your confirmation.\n\n\n\n\nHave a great weekend ahead!\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nEl El mié, 29 de may de 2024 a la(s) 3:07 p.m., Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n escribió:\n\n\n\nDear Shirley,\n\n \n\n\nI hope you are doing well and had a great Memorial Day weekend.\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks for your prompt response and for reviewing our comments on the document. It's great to hear there are only a few areas left to reconcile.\n\n\nRegarding the meeting, Wednesday, June 5th works well for us as a preliminary call. However, from our end, I'll confirm with our team to ensure everyone is available. I will let\n you know as soon as possible.\n\n\nWe are eager to work together to finalize the details on the draft document and can definitely arrange for negotiations afterwards.\n\n\nLooking forward to a productive discussion and I will formally confirm the date soon.\n\n\nWarm regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, May 29, 2024 at 1:49 PM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\n \nWe have looked at your comments on the document and believe we have only a few areas to reconcile. Would your team\n be available to meet next week Wednesday 5th June for negotiation? If not we could have preliminary call and arrange for the negotiations afterwards.\n \nWe would send you our comments ahead.\n \nBest,\nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, May 27, 2024 10:10 AM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\njosem@unops.org;\nelisabets@unops.org; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez,\n Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE\n MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>;\n Elise REICHE PEREIRA <eliserp@unops.org>; Arantzazu OJINAGA\n <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Tanja CHOPRA\n <tanjac@unops.org>; Hurwitz, Zachary Daniel <zacharyh@IADB.ORG>;\n Pierre-Olivier LANGLOIS <pierreol@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\nGood morning Shirley!\n\n \n\n\nI hope you and the team had a fantastic weekend. I am pleased to attach a copy of the document in Word Format, which includes our comments. Nonetheless, you also have the Google document reviewed by\n our team, if you prefer to view the comments more clearly.\n\n\n \n\n\nHappy Memorial Day! Looking forward to your feedback.\n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, May 27, 2024 at 6:11 AM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\n \nThanks so much for the comments on the draft agreement. To facilitate our internal review, would you please send us\n the document as an attachment to an email?\n \nWe will arrange for review as soon as you send it and return to you regarding next steps.\n \nKind regards,\nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, May 24, 2024 4:50 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\njosem@unops.org;\nelisabets@unops.org; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez,\n Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE\n MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>;\n Elise REICHE PEREIRA <eliserp@unops.org>; Arantzazu OJINAGA\n <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Tanja CHOPRA\n <tanjac@unops.org>; Hurwitz, Zachary Daniel <zacharyh@IADB.ORG>;\n Pierre-Olivier LANGLOIS <pierreol@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\nDear Shirley,\n\n \n\n\nWe are pleased to inform you that the comments from the UNOPS team have been incorporated into the draft document.\n\n\nWe´ll appreciate the feedback provided by the IADB team on the attached\n\ndocument, which is now available for your review.\n\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you soon about the next steps in order to continue the process towards formalizing the partnership between two committed partners.\n\n\nWishing you a great week ahead!\n\n\n \n\n\nWarm regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, May 6, 2024 at 9:26 PM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\nThanks so much for your response. It is good to meet you and your team through this medium and I look forward to meeting in person for\n our talks.\n \nWe look forward to receiving your feedback on the 24th of May. This might necessitate a new date for our negotiation meeting.\n No worries however, we will suggest a new date.  \n \nIt would be good if you could let us know where you figure would be most convenient for you to meet so we can start to arrange.\n\n \nKind regards,\nShirley\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, May 6, 2024 7:35 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\njosem@unops.org; \nelisabets@unops.org; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Elise REICHE PEREIRA <eliserp@unops.org>;\n Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nsolv@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Shirley,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well as we are looking forward to advancing in this partnership process. As Head of Partnerships- LAC at UNOPS, I would be coordinating these efforts\n from our end in our shared goal of contributing to the development and advancement of the peoples of Latin America and the Caribbean.  It is of this spirit that we are looking forward to signing a framework agreement between IADB and UNOPS.\n\n\nWe would dearly appreciate it if the review deadline date can be moved from May 17th to May the 24th as we have to coordinate with internal team members in Denmark (Headquarters),\n and the LAC Regional Office (Panama).\n\n\nInitially, the UNOPS team will be composed by: \n\n\n \n\n\nJose Moscoso, Senior Procurement and Supply Chain Consultant, Business Development\n\n\nLeyre Sastre, Coordinator of Regional Activities, LAC\n\n\nElise Reiche/Elsa Abete, Legal Group\n\n\nArantza Ojinaga, Financial Management Advisor\n\n\nAnne Claire, Director, Procurement Group\n\n\nIsabela Fraiz, Senior Partnerships Associate\n\n\nSol Villa Michel, Head of Partnerships LAC\n\n\n \n\n\nUNOPS participants might eventually change subject to their specialization.\n\n\nLooking forward to your confirmation.\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Apr 26, 2024 at 1:17 PM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Isabela,\n \nThanks for your prompt reply.\n \nWe are looking forward to receiving your comments and scheduling the meetings with you.\n \nHave a great weekend!\nShirley\n \n \n\nFrom: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, April 25, 2024 7:01 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: josem@unops.org; \nelisabets@unops.org; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\nDear Shirley, \n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for this, great to hear from you. I will share this draft internally with our teams for their prompt review; I am looping in Sol, our Head of Partnerships, so she can\n assess these details and get back to you with decisions on how to proceed with the negotiations for this important agreement. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Partnerships & Communications Senior Associate |\nRegional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Apr 25, 2024 at 4:06 PM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n \nDear Isabela and UNOPS colleagues,\n \nPlease receive warm greetings from the IDB.\n \nWe would like to thank you for our previous meetings and exchanges in relation to the forming of an agreement between the IDB and UNOPS and for your patience as we worked through\n many processes\n \nIn follow up, we are reaching out to make arrangements for the negotiations. Please find attached the draft which will be used for our discussions. We kindly invite you to review\n it and send us your feedback by May 17, 2024.\n \nWe know you share our interest in realizing an agreement at the earliest time. Therefore, our preference is to have in-person negotiations, dedicating 1-2 days to agree and finalize\n the text of the agreement. To ensure we gain the most from these sessions, it is important to have the participation of persons empowered to make decisions. We request that you bring the relevant persons from your legal, finance, partnerships, environmental\n and social, procurement, audit and integrity and any other area you consider pertinent.\n\n \nWe would like to propose\nJune 5 to meet with you if that would be convenient. We are prepared to host the meetings here at the Bank. However, if this is not convenient for you, we are willing to meet at your offices.\n \nWe look forward to working together to conclude this important agreement.\n \nBest regards,\nShirley\n \n \nShirley Gayle\n\nLead Procurement Specialist\nFinancial Management and Procurement Services,\nOffice of the Vice Presidency for Countries\nTel: (202) 623-2452\n\n\n\n\n\n1300 New York Avenue, N.W.\n\nWashington, D.C. 20577\n\nUSA\n\nwww.iadb.org",
