                new (
                    "00TQx00000DqcptMAB",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: FW: Side-event forespørgsel til Summit for the Future: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\"",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-30").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FW: Side-event forespørgsel til Summit for the Future: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\"",
                        Description = "To: aro@ms.dk\nCC: skb@ms.dk; noa.valentin.katz.sogaard@undp.org; aca@ms.dk; majatouzari@gmail.com; naimoh@unops.org; amiro@unops.org; aikaterinis@unops.org; hannahsr@unops.org; nadiamo@unops.org; kellymc@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Side-event forespørgsel til Summit for the Future: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\"\nBody:\nDear Annette, \nThank you for your positive feedback and interest in collaborating on an event at the Summit of the Future. \nMy colleagues Amir, Kelly and Hannah from our Peace and Security Cluster will revert to you with suggested time slots for a meeting. \nPSC colleagues: Could I kindly ask for you to take this forward? Don't hesitate to let me know if you need anything from my side! \nThanks!\nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 29 Jul 2024 at 20:10, Annette Rohde <aro@ms.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n\n \nThank you so much for getting back to us on this request. Your suggestions sound very interesting. We would very much like to connect and discuss more\n this. Would it suit you to schedule a meeting mid next week?\n \nI am also here sending you an updated version of the concept note. We also have OHCHR and PBSO on board as well.\n\n \nWe look very much forward to connecting.\n\n \nAll the best,\n\n\nAnnette\n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, July 29, 2024 11:02 AM\n\nTo: Annette Rohde <aro@ms.dk>\n\nCc: Sara Katrine Brandt <skb@ms.dk>; Noa Valentin Katz Søgaard <noa.valentin.katz.sogaard@undp.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Amir OMERAGIC <amiro@unops.org>; Aikaterini SERETI <aikaterinis@unops.org>; Hannah Septembre REES <hannahsr@unops.org>;\n Nadia MOUSSA <nadiamo@unops.org>; Kelly MCAULAY <kellymc@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Fwd: FW: Side-event forespørgsel til Summit for the Future: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\"\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nasbjornb@unops.org. \nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Annette, \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for reaching out regarding a potential side-event during the action days at the summit of the future. \n\n\n \n\n\nHere at UNOPS, our Peace and Security Cluster might be interested in joining forces with you on such a side event. I am therefore putting you in contact with Amir, Hannah and Kelly (all cc this email) to take the dialogue forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nBased on your initial pitch, Amir and his colleagues considered that they might be able to offer a range of topics under a brader angle peace building, conflict sensitivity, community engagement. Some initial thoughts:\n\n\n\nMine Ban Treaty adopted in 1997 is a result of a huge piece of advocacy, predominantly pushed by the CSO/NGOs and the UN. Its a good intro into the mine action framework and results that we see today.\n\nEarlier than the mine ban treaty itself, the work of international and national organisations in places such as Afghanistan was also largely a grass root movement and bottom up solution to a complex problem landmines and ERW pose.\nGenerally, engagement in the affected communities to understand how landmines and ERW affect them help design better project solutions; the principal of do no harm can also be highlighted\nCommunity Based demining - examples in AFG and Somalia, whereby a small core technical team engages in the affected communities, trans, equips and manages community based demining teams to get rid of the problem that hampers life and development;\nDemoblised soldiers and deminers - examples from COlombia (ex-FARC) and Afghanistan showcase how local interest and skillset can be channeled into new institutions (NGOs) that work for the good.\nPreventing Violent Extremism - Risk education/conflict resolution project in Mali.\nIf the above idea fit with your intent, Amir and his colelagues would be very happy to take the dialogue forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom:\nAnnette Rohde <aro@ms.dk>\n\nDate: Thursday, 4 July 2024 at 14.52\n\nTo: Noa Valentin Katz Sogaard <noa.valentin.katz.sogaard@undp.org>\n\nCc: Sara Katrine Brandt <skb@ms.dk>\n\nSubject: Side-event forespørgsel til Summit for the Future: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\naro@ms.dk. \nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHej Noa\n\n\n\nTak, fordi du vil tage dig tid til at videreformidle vores forespørgsel. Vi leder efter en FN institution, som kunne have lyst til at medvært på et Summit of the Future side-event under Action Dagene d. 20-21 september i NY.\nDet har titlen: \"Grassroots Solutions: Transforming Peacebuilding through Social Movements\".\n\n\nVi planlægger side-eventet med blandt andet Danmark, Somalia og Open Society Foundations. Og arbejder tæt sammen med OHCHR, som gerne ville være med, men man kan som FN institution kun være lead/co-lead på\n et event og noget andet er planlagt dér. \nVi leder altså efter en FN institution, som ikke allerede har en side-event planlagt på Summit of the Future og gerne vil være medværter på vores side-event. Vedhæftet er pitch på side-eventet.\nPå forhånd tak for hjælpen.\n\n \nMange hilsener\nAnnette\n\n \n \nAnnette Rohde |\nOrganisational Change Lead |\nDenmark\n\n  \n\n\nTel: +45 7731 0041\n\n\nEmail: aro@ms.dk | Web: www.globalplatforms.org\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\nActionAid is a global movement of people working together to further human rights for all and defeat poverty.\n\n  \n\n  \n\n   \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS\n HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
