                        Subject = "Email: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29",
                        Description = "To: satu.lassila@formin.fi\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29\nBody:\nDear Satu,\nI hope this email finds you well - somewhere warm and sunny!  \nAs usual, I wanted to provide you - and your team - with a brief and informal overview of the UNOPS relevant topics to be discussed at the upcoming Executive Board session on August 26-29. \nPlease feel free to forward my email to Andrea's replacement as I understand he now resides in Algeria. :-) \nYou might already have noticed that all the relevant documents as well as the draft agenda have been uploaded to the UNOPS website and can be found here. \nOn substance the topics relevant specifically to UNOPS relates to the following: A draft terms of reference for the review of UNOPS implementation of the Comprehensive Response PlanAn information note on UNOPS strategy for the implementation of the Process Innovation and Digitalisation ProgrammeInformation note on the estimated amount remaining of undisbursed excess reserve fundsThe annual report on the procurement activities of the UN system in 2023 + annexAd 1) - ToR for review of implementation of the Comprehensive Response PlanAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \nUpon request from the EB, UNOPS' Internal Audit and Investigation Group (IAIG) has prepared a draft ToR for the upcoming second review of UNOPS' implementation of the Comprehensive Response Plan (CPR). This document was also presented to the EB at the June EB session. \nThis second review will seek to validate/dismiss that UNOPS has in fact implemented the remaining action points in the CPR and thereby adhered to the recommendations by KPMG following the S3i independent review. The review is meant to start in 2025 when all but one recommendation will have been concluded (the digitisation programme (PID) - which runs until 2025). \nAd 2) Implementation of the Process Innovation and Digitalisation ProgrammeAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \n\nUpon request from the EB, UNOPS has provided an extensive information note with a roadmap for the PID's scope, progress, milestones, budget, governance and risk management, KPIs and stakeholder engagement. \nThe progress in implementation - as well as challenges - will be reported in the monthly briefings to the EB until the first EB session in January / February 2025. \nAd 3) Estimated remaining excessive reserve fundsAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \nUNOPS estimates that out of the 123.8M USD, only 1.5M will be undisbursed by the end of 2024, which is the deadline provided by the EB. As per June 2024, only 8.5M USD remains in the reserve, which is focused on 10 government partners. \nThe EB will decide on the use of the remaining funds at the first session in 2025. \nAd 4) Estimated remaining excessive reserve fundsAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 23 August. \nThe annual procurement report shows that the UN procured goods and services worth almost 25B in 2023 - a decrease by 15.7%. 5B was procured from least developed countries. \nScheduled Informal Sessions19 August, 10 am - 1 pm: ToR for review on UNOPS implementation of the CRPRoadmap for the PID programmeRemaining funds in excess reserve23 August 10 am - 12 pmProcurement report \nI hope this gives you a somewhat overview of the topics to be discussed at the August EB session. \nI also hope that you - or the new UNOPS focal point in your unit - might be available during next week for an informal chat. where we could go through the topics, clarify potential questions bilaterally and get your initial take on the topics. \nIf so - please do let me know when it might suit you to meet online next week. \nLooking forward to hearing back from you. \nBest regards,Asbjørn\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
