                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-30").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29",
                        Description = "To: karl.svensson@gov.se\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29\nBody:\nDeal!\nI've sent you a calendar invite. \nOn Tue, 30 Jul 2024 at 17:11, Karl Svensson <karl.svensson@gov.se> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi,\n\n\n\nShall we say at 11.00?\n\n\n\nBest,\nKarl \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrån: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\nDatum: tisdag 30 juli 2024 5:04 em\nTill: Karl Svensson <karl.svensson@gov.se>\nKopia: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\nÄmne: Re: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29\n\n\n\n\nHi Karl\n\n\n\nThursday next week is good for me - preferably before 12 if OK for you. \n\n\n\nWhat time would be best for you?\n\n\n\nBest,\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 30 Jul 2024 at 16:43, Karl Svensson <karl.svensson@gov.se> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn,\n \nThe sun is shining in Stockholm today, hope it does in Copenhagen as well!\n \nMany thanks for this valuable update and explanation of the upcoming topics during the SRS in August. Much appreciated to hear your takes on the topics.\n\n \nI will dedicate some time during the week to go through the documentation and discuss the topics internally at our department. Thanks for taking the initiative for an informal call next week, would Thursday work for you?\n\n \nThanks once again!\n \nBest regards, \nKarl\n \n \n\nFrån: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSkickat: den 30 juli 2024 15:44\n\nTill: Karl Svensson <karl.svensson@gov.se>\n\nKopia: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nÄmne: Executive Board, Second Regular Session, August 26-29\n\n \n\nDear Karl, \n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well in sunny, summer-ish Stockholm. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs promised during our conversation last week, I wanted to provide you with a brief and informal overview of the UNOPS relevant topics to be discussed at the upcoming Executive Board session on August 26-29. \n\n\n \n\n\nYou might already have noticed that all the relevant documents as well as the\ndraft agenda have been uploaded to the UNOPS website and can be found\nhere. \n\n\n \n\n\nOn substance the topics relevant specifically to UNOPS relates to the following: \n\n\n\nA draft terms of reference for the review of UNOPS implementation of the Comprehensive Response PlanAn\n information note on UNOPS strategy for the implementation of the Process Innovation and Digitalisation ProgrammeInformation\n note on the estimated amount remaining of undisbursed excess reserve fundsThe annual report on the procurement activities of the UN system in 2023 +\nannex\n\n\n\nAd 1) - ToR for review of implementation of the Comprehensive Response Plan\n\n\n\nAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \n\n\n \n\n\nUpon request from the EB, UNOPS' Internal Audit and Investigation Group (IAIG) has prepared a draft ToR for the upcoming second review of UNOPS' implementation of the Comprehensive Response Plan (CPR). This document was\n also presented to the EB at the June EB session. \n\n\n \n\n\nThis second review will seek to validate/dismiss that UNOPS has in fact implemented the remaining action points in the CPR and thereby adhered to the recommendations by KPMG following the S3i independent review.\n The review is meant to start in 2025 when all but one recommendation will have been concluded (the digitisation programme (PID)- which runs until 2025). \n\n\n \n\n\nAd 2) Implementation of the Process Innovation and Digitalisation Programme\n\n\nAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \n\n\n \n\n\nUpon request from the EB, UNOPS has provided an extensive information note with a roadmap for the PID's scope, progress, milestones, budget, governance and risk management, KPIs and stakeholder engagement. \n\n\n \n\n\nThe progress in implementation - as well as challenges - will be reported in the monthly briefings to the EB until the first EB session in January / February 2025. \n\n\n \n\n\n\nAd 3) Estimated remaining excessive reserve funds\n\n\nAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 19 August. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nUNOPS estimates, that out of the 123.8M USD, only 1.5M will be undisbursed by the end of 2024, which is the deadline provided by the EB. As per June 2024, only 8.5M USD remains in the reserve, which is focused on 10 government\n partners. \n\n\n \n\n\nThe EB will decide on the use of the remaining funds at the first session in 2025. \n\n\n \n\n\n\nAd 4) Estimated remaining excessive reserve funds\n\n\nAn informal session about this topic is scheduled for 23 August. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nThe annual procurement report shows that the UN procured goods and services worth almost 25B in 2023 - a decrease by 15.7%.\n5B was procured from least developed countries. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nScheduled Informal Sessions\n\n\n·\n19 August, 10 am - 1 pm: \no\nToR for review on UNOPS implementation of the CRP\no\nRoadmap for the PID programme\no\nRemaining funds in excess reserve\n·\n23 August 10 am - 12 pm\no\nProcurement report \n\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this gives you a somewhat overview of the topics to be discussed at the August EB session. \n\n\n \n\n\nI also hope that you might be available during next week for an informal chat. where we could go through the topics, clarify potential questions bilaterally and get your initial take on the topics. \n\n\n \n\n\nIf so - please do let me know when it might suit you to meet online next week. \n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing back from you. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe\n Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
