                    "00TQx00000DthOMMAZ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Update from Bangladesh",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-31").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Update from Bangladesh",
                        Description = "To: sudhirm@unops.org\nCC: charlesc@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Update from Bangladesh\nBody:\nDear Sudhir\nThanks so much for your message - what a lovely welcome back from my leave!!  Great news and Kudos to you and the team for this great collaboration with GF.\nCharlie and I attempted to connect with Gyongyi when we went met Global Fund/Sri Lanka colleague together a couple of weeks ago.  I will reach out to her to say hi ( I haven't met her as part of regular networking / engagements yet )\nHow does your 13-15 October look ?  We have the World Health Summit coming up in Berlin on those dates, where all my GLO partners will be present, including Peter Sands speaking about replenishment with Gavi (WHO is also replenishing.... lots of players, finite funds ... another conversation!)  Anyway, my point is, we could if I can generate interest, highlight the GREAT work in Bangladesh on Oxygen?  sound interesting?  Please let me know, and I will start preparing ground work....\nLet's speak soonBest wishesLouise\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Wed, 31 Jul 2024 at 08:39, Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Louise,\nI am reaching out to you from Bangladesh with some exciting news. Following Peter Sands' visit to our PSA Plants Project last month, it has been recognized as a flagship project globally by GFATM. The executive director has instructed that the project be well covered from a visibility standpoint as it is considered one of GFATM's most successful projects in a non-traditional area, not directly related to the three diseases. Please find below the minutes of a recent meeting we had with the FPM for Bangladesh.\nWe greatly appreciate your continued support. Thank you.\nBest regardsSudhir\nSudhir Muralidharan | Country Manager | AR, SAMCO | UNOPS Bangladesh & Bhutan| Dhaka, Bangladesh| Tel: +880 1324536524 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org>\nDate: Tue, Jul 30, 2024 at 2:27 PM\nSubject: Re: 29 PSA Plant Project Bangladesh - Update - 23rd July 2024\nTo: Gyongyver Jakab <Gyongyver.Jakab@theglobalfund.org>\nCc: Mohamed Infiyaz HYDER <mohamedh@unops.org>, James Wariero <James.Wariero@theglobalfund.org>, Kevin Luthi <Kevin.Luthi@theglobalfund.org>, Caroline Mubangizi <Caroline.Mubangizi@theglobalfund.org>, Kuldip MALLA <kuldipm@unops.org>, Charles Rochford CALLANAN <charlesc@unops.org>\n\nSorry, here is the attachment. \nBest regardsSudhir\nSudhir Muralidharan | Country Manager | AR, SAMCO | UNOPS Bangladesh & Bhutan| Dhaka, Bangladesh| Tel: +880 1324536524 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Tue, Jul 30, 2024 at 2:02 PM Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Gyongyi,\nIt was wonderful catching up with you yesterday. I will capture the main aspects of our conversation below, but please feel free to correct me if I have missed something.\nVisibility of PSA Plants Project. It is understood that the ongoing PSA Plants project is now a flagship project for the Global Fund, and UNOPS supports GF in any efforts to enhance the project's profile. TB Diagnostics financed from GF Funding- Currently, these are entirely sourced from GDF, which is part of Stop TB Partnerships, which is a hosted entity of UNOPS, Geneva. MOH has expressed a desire to source these through the UNOPS Bangladesh Country office if the commercial terms remain the same or are more advantageous to the GoB. The Ministry is preparing the business case, and the process for internal approvals to request this change is already in progress. The main advantages cited by MOH are the ease of follow-up and interaction with a local UNOPS office in the local language. GF clarified that the CCM would have to approve the request before the GF considers it, and then the CCM will again need to approve the changed implementation arrangements should the GF approve this. Both GF and UNOPS will keenly follow progress and keep each other praised on progress. GF cannot comment further on this until a formal request reaches them from the CCM.Medical Waste Management: The investment committee of the GF has yellow-lighted a potential medical waste management project for Bangladesh from the remaining Covid 19 response funds. GF will informally share the proposal which was sent to the IC. The condition placed by the IC is that a more detailed technical proposal be developed and greenlighted by the IC. GF expects the detailed proposal to be developed in August- September to go back to the IC in September for full greenlighting. The implementation end date cannot cross Dec 31, 2025, as things stand. The IC yellow light assumes implementation by UNOPS, and this will be clarified with ADG Flora next week to understand the Government's preference. The next steps should take final shape during the GF mission to Bangladesh in September. UNOPS mentioned that because of the short implementation timeline and UNOPS due diligence in infrastructure projects, it may be good for UNOPS to be involved closely in the next steps. Oxygen Guidelines- DGHS has developed draft oxygen management guidelines for Bangladesh with support from UNICEF. The oxygen guidelines ownership within the DGHS rests with NEMEW & TC. NEMEW & TC has expressed reservations about the guidelines and has informally requested UNOPS to review them to address their concerns. UNOPS has stood firm that we will need a written formal request to consider this. Considering the strategic importance of finalising and operationalising these guidelines, GF supports such an intervention should a formal request be made to UNOPS. GF would consult internally further on this to manage relationships while UNOPS works with NEMEW&TC on the formal request. This intervention can be part of the existing PSA Plant Project, but a budget top-up will be required..Rehabilitation of 35 PSA Plants financed by other sources- UNOPS mentioned that there were 35 PSA plants in the country financed from other sources that were non-operational for various reasons. A feasibility study would need to be undertaken to understand what prevents these from being operationalized. UNOPS offered to do such a study if adequate funds were made available in the ongoing project as a budget top-up. The cost of such a study would be roughly USD 40 K, as per a brief concept note attached. GF will discuss this internally and revert on this. Thank you.\nBest regardsSudhir\nSudhir Muralidharan | Country Manager | AR, SAMCO | UNOPS Bangladesh & Bhutan| Dhaka, Bangladesh| Tel: +880 1324536524 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Thu, Jul 25, 2024 at 4:12 PM Gyongyver Jakab <Gyongyver.Jakab@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sudhir,\n\n \nThanks and I look forward to our discussion. In case the connectivity fails again, we will find an alternative slot later on.\n \nBest,\n\nGyongyi\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGyongyver Jakab\nSenior Fund Portfolio Manager\nHigh Impact Asia\nGrant Management Division\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41 79 829 8948\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ngyongyver.jakab@theglobafund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, July 25, 2024 12:11 PM\n\nTo: Gyongyver Jakab <Gyongyver.Jakab@TheGlobalFund.org>\n\nCc: Mohamed Infiyaz HYDER <mohamedh@unops.org>; James Wariero <James.Wariero@theglobalfund.org>; Kevin Luthi <Kevin.Luthi@theglobalfund.org>; Caroline Mubangizi <Caroline.Mubangizi@theglobalfund.org>; Kuldip MALLA <kuldipm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: 29 PSA Plant Project Bangladesh - Update - 23rd July 2024\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Gyongyi, \n\n\n \n\n\nThanks. Monday 2 pm Bangladesh time is great subject to restoration of internet. I will send you a Google invite. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards\n\n\n\nSudhir\n\n\n\n\n\nSudhir Muralidharan | Country Manager | AR, SAMCO | UNOPS Bangladesh| Dhaka, Bangladesh| Tel: +880 1324536524 |\n\nwww.unops.org \n\n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n\n￼\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 25 Jul 2024, 15:38 Gyongyver Jakab, <Gyongyver.Jakab@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Sudhir,\n\n \nThanks for your email. I am happy to meet with you next week. I have availabilities on Monday 2pm, Wednesday\n 1pm and Friday 1.30pm Bangladesh time. Please let me know if any of those slots are suitable.\n\n \nBest,\n\nGyongyi\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGyongyver Jakab\nSenior Fund Portfolio Manager\nHigh Impact Asia\nGrant Management Division\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41\n 79 829 8948\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ngyongyver.jakab@theglobafund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, July 25, 2024 11:38 AM\n\nTo: Gyongyver Jakab <Gyongyver.Jakab@TheGlobalFund.org>\n\nCc: Mohamed Infiyaz HYDER <mohamedh@unops.org>; James Wariero <James.Wariero@theglobalfund.org>; Kevin Luthi <Kevin.Luthi@theglobalfund.org>\n\nSubject: Re: 29 PSA Plant Project Bangladesh - Update - 23rd July 2024\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Gyongyi, \n\n\n \n\n\nI have been briefed about today's meeting. Thanks for the continued support and encouragement. I was wondering if we could have a short meeting next week at your convenience. Thanks. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards\n\n\n\nSudhir\n\n\n\n\n\nSudhir Muralidharan | Country Manager | AR, SAMCO | UNOPS Bangladesh| Dhaka, Bangladesh| Tel: +880 1324536524 |\n\nwww.unops.org \n\n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n\n￼\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 23 Jul 2024, 20:16 Gyongyver Jakab, <Gyongyver.Jakab@theglobalfund.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Infiyaz,\n\n \nThank you very much for your detailed update. Both Kevin and James are on leave at the moment, but I am\n acknowledging receipt of your message on their behalf. \n \nCaroline and I will be happy to connect with you on Thursday to discuss any issues that we may be able\n to help with and particularly to further discuss the issue of the transformers, the hand-over of the sites with and without power, and the remaining sites that are to be completed.\n\n \nThank you for all your efforts to ensure site security and wishing your team all the very best through\n this difficult period. \n \nBest\n\nGyongyi\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGyongyver Jakab\nSenior Fund Portfolio Manager\nHigh Impact Asia\nGrant Management Division\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM: +41\n 79 829 8948\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ngyongyver.jakab@theglobafund.org\n\n\n\n\ntheglobalfund.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Mohamed Infiyaz HYDER <mohamedh@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, July 23, 2024 8:46 AM\n\nTo: James Wariero <James.Wariero@theglobalfund.org>;\n Kevin Luthi <Kevin.Luthi@theglobalfund.org>\n\nCc: Sudhir MURALIDHARAN <sudhirm@unops.org>; Charles\n Rochford CALLANAN <charlesc@unops.org>; Iftekhar AHMED <iftekhara@unops.org>;\n Sheikh Daud Adnan <adn_dr@yahoo.com>; Shyamol Kumer Das <dpmmalaria.shyamolkdas@gmail.com>;\n Mushfiqur Rahman <musfiqr2003@gmail.com>; Md Mosiqure Rahaman\n <mdmosiqure@gmail.com>; Hashan ALI <hashana@unops.org>;\n Samudika DANANJANI IMBULPE <samudikad@unops.org>; Zahidul\n ISLAM <zahiduli@unops.org>; Mohammad Shahadt Hossain MAHMUD\n <shahadthm@unops.org>; Nicholas Furtado <Nicholas.Furtado@theglobalfund.org>;\n Mahadi Hasan FAHAD <fahadm@unops.org>; Caroline Mubangizi <Caroline.Mubangizi@theglobalfund.org>;\n Gyongyver Jakab <Gyongyver.Jakab@TheGlobalFund.org>;\ndr.azad842492@gmail.com; Shaikh Mohammad ALAVEE <shaikha@unops.org>;\n Bodrudoza ALAM <bodrudozaa@unops.org>; Sarwar ISLAM <sarwari@unops.org>;\n Mohammad Maruf HASAN <marufh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: 29 PSA Plant Project Bangladesh - Update - 23rd July 2024\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear James and Kevin,\n \nI hope this email finds you well.\n \nI apologize for the delay in providing project updates. I was finally able to connect after returning to Sri Lanka this morning. As you're\n aware, the situation in Bangladesh has been extremely challenging, and the lack of internet connectivity, curfew, etc. disrupted our day-to-day work and even internal team communications.\n \nWhile I will be sending the detailed monthly highlight report early next week, I wanted to provide some key updates that I know you are eager\n to hear about.\n \nHanded Over Sites\nAs discussed in our last coordination meeting, we conducted retesting at NIDCH and Manikganj with NMEP operators and engineers present. The\n plants were operational for approximately 6 hours per day over three days, and the purity levels were consistently above 93%. Unfortunately, the planned training sessions requested by NMEP had to be postponed due to ongoing issues. The operators are now more\n confident in running the plants, and we stressed the importance of daily operations to maintain performance.\n\n \nCompleted Sites (With Power)\nFollowing advice from the Line Director - CDC, the NMEP team will take over the three sites where the PSA plant is already connected to the\n existing substation. Our goal was to complete these handovers by July 2024, but this timeline will need to be adjusted.\n \nCompleted Sites (Without Power)\nNMEP's recent decision not to take over sites without power has significant implications for project handovers, site security, the DNP period,\n and our operational expenditure. While we understand the necessity of fully completed sites, we are concerned about the critical impacts of this decision on our plans. I will provide a detailed explanation in a separate email.\n \nThe good news is that there has been no damage to the sites from the ongoing demonstration activities, and our team is working diligently\n to ensure their security as some site locations are really sensitive.\n \nOngoing sites (Ishwardi & Bandarban)\nThe construction activities are underway but slow progress due to the absence of workers due to the movement restrictions in place.\n \nTransformers\nOn behalf of NMEP, I want to update you on the meeting held on 15th July 2024 by LD-CDC with the relevant hospital directors. The roles and\n responsibilities concerning transformers were clearly outlined. Our colleagues Mr.Maruf, Mr.Hashan, and Mr.Fahad attended the meeting, and I will provide a detailed update in the coordination meeting on 25th July 2024. We are hopeful that things will proceed\n smoothly.\n \nUpcoming Meeting\nGiven the current situation in Bangladesh, NMEP's participation in the 25th July 2024 meeting is uncertain. However, I suggest we proceed\n with the meeting so I can provide further updates on the project status.\n \nThank you for your understanding and patience. \n \nWe all pray for the safety of our team and for the situation to be resolved in Bangladesh soon and bring the team together.\n \n\n\n\n\n\nThank You!\n\n\nBest Regards!\n\n\n \n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails outside office hours. I don't necessarily demand responses\n to my emails outside your working hours.\n\n\n \n\nInfiyaz Hyder\nCEng MICE| Project Manager/Civil Engineer | Operational Hub - Bangladesh, Bhutan,\n India, Nepal, Pakistan I SAMCO Sri Lanka | AR BDMCO | Colombo, Sri Lanka | Tel: +94 7135 03812 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
