                    },
                    new List<string> { "003Qx00000N3LlsIAF" },
                    new List<int> { 1193 },
                    new List<string> { "kajsah@unops.org" },
                    new List<string> { "B0047" }
                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000Du2BBMAZ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Meeting with UN Habitat on WCD and WUF 2024",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-01").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Meeting with UN Habitat on WCD and WUF 2024",
                        Description = "To: elenage@unops.org\nCC: kajsah@unops.org; amyn@unops.org; paolanyiramigambom@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Meeting with UN Habitat on WCD and WUF 2024\nBody:\nDear Elena,\nThank you for the update!\n1. I have already discussed this with Sarah Rihane and the project manager of the \n\nPlastic Waste project in Libya. I think I already updated you about this. The project was supposed to be signed in June to start in July. We agreed with the project manager and Sarah that they would identify a protagonist for the story from the civil society organizations working with UNOPS in this project. I am waiting to hear from Sarah. As soon as the protagonist is identified we will hire a local videographer who with our guidelines and guidelines from Elise (as we count on her to edit all the video materials for the campaign) will perform the interview and take the footage. \n2. During my last meeting with \n\nKaterina and Yamila we agreed that apart from the main video, we will collect content for short video pils on other projects. Our comms officers across Africa are already collecting the materials for this.\n\n3. \n\nWorld Urban Forum. About the video, It sounds perfect. About the attendance, my latest discussion with Katerina was to find a slot at the Forum for Dalila to contribute as a speaker. I was waiting for you to send me a list of topics Dalila can discuss to share with Katerina. For your email, I understand that Dalila may not be going.\n\nHappy to discuss all of this when you have time.\nAll the best,\nHilariaHilaria ESPIN | Communication Specialist | Africa Regional Office | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 4533 7542 | Mobile: +45 30 17 75 42| www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Mon, Jun 24, 2024 at 11:55 AM Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Hilaria, \nKajsa and I met with Katerina of UN Habitat last Friday to discuss our collaboration on World Cities Day as well as the World Urban Forum 2024. We essentially picked up the discussion from where you left it and received an update from Katerina which I'd like to share with you to establish our next steps. \n@Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN please add or correct me as needed!\n\nWorld Cities Day Habitat will do a physical event on October 31st at the Library in Alexandria. The focus will be on what you have previously discussed - young people championing climate action in their cities and it will feature a number of events, including (all TBC): 1. High level speeches including by the UN Habitat executive director, the Governor of Alexandria, Ministers2. Panel discussion on stage3. RoundtablesWhile the event may be broadcast online, the idea is to avoid a hybrid set up with all participants being physically present. \nStoriesI am sure you already have ideas about young people campaigning for climate action in their respective cities or that you have already reached out to colleagues from our various offices. My suggestion would be to try and identify good examples from the Tunisia/North Africa office. This is for two reasons: 1. There is a good example of collaboration with UN Habitat in Libya for the development of Tripoli's waste management masterplan. 2. Nathalie, the Tunisia director, is trying to grow our presence in Egypt. She and her office would benefit from the visibility both the WCD event and the WUF would offer. \nOther options include Mozambique and Zimbabwe in the context of reconstruction after natural disasters. Both UNOPS and Habitat are implementing relevant projects there. Can we showcase that voices of young people informed our work? Maybe something to check with Tanja Chopra who leads on safeguards for KEMC?\nAnother idea is to look for cash-for-work examples. \nWe agreed that we will seek to gather all the examples by mid July at the latest. \nWorld Urban ForumIt's unclear who is attending from UNOPS' leadership and having spoken to Katerina, I think we might want to make the case for high level representation. \nIn the lead up to the WUF, Habitat have been doing some brief interviews with leaders from the UN and beyond, e.g. they had Melissa Fleming do something recently. Kajsa is going to look into whether we can contribute a short video of Jorge. The questions are standards and Katerina can share them with us. \nLet me know your thoughts as well as any work done so far and we can touch base as needed. \nBest wishes, Elena \n\nActions for us-Consider whether we want to participate physically in the WCD event. \n\n-- \nElena Georgalla | Partnerships Specialist | Africa Regional Office | Nairobi, Kenya | Tel: +254 700035033| www.unops.org",
