                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000Du94NMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UNH UNOPS Thank you and next steps",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-25").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNH UNOPS Thank you and next steps",
                        Description = "To: ran.wang@un.org\nCC: lucia.kiwala@un.org; AmritaN@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; cherrilyn.auma@un.org; erfan.ali@un.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNH UNOPS Thank you and next steps\nBody:\nDear Ran,\n\nLikewise, it is a pleasure to work together! Thank you so much to both you and Cherrilyn for the quick turnaround time in sharing these documents, and for putting together the workplan. \n\n1. I have reviewed the workplan and it looks great to me - I agree that we can update it as we move forward.\n2. Excellent, I will get back to you with our copy as I proceed with the data collection and mapping.\n3. Thank you so much for putting me in touch with Lucia, much appreciated (and great to meet you, Lucia!). I will write a separate email on the matter and will keep you in copy.\n4. Thank you also for sharing the 2017 MoU, I am additionally attaching our HR services agreement so that we all have a full overview of the existing frameworks for our collaboration.\n\nLooking forward to advancing this together, and to speaking with you again next week.\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\nOn Thu, 25 Jul 2024 at 15:06, Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa,\n\n\n\n\n\nIt's a great pleasure to working with you. And thank you so much for your following-up.\n\nHere are some documents shared for your information:\n\n\nWorkplan: kindly for your amendment and suggestion, it will be a living document to be updated from time to time.\n\nMapping document from UNH: we will keep updating this document as we will involve other divisions from HQ.\n\nUNH policy for implementing partner and legal templates: focal point for partnership is\n\n@Lucia Kiwala. Not sure if this is what you asked about. But keep in touch,  I can also be part of the communication.\n\nMOU btw UNH and UNOPS, for your information.\n\n\nThe weekly coordination meeting invitation is shared, and I saw your confirmation. collaboratively and closely.\n\nThank you so much and looking forward to your follow-up.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\nRan WANG\nAssociate Expert\nRegional Programme Division, HQ, UN-HABITAT\nMobile: +254 (0)702070067\nEmail:\nran.wang@un.org\n\n3rd level, Block 4, North wing\n\nUN Complex\n\nNairobi, Kenya\n\n\n\n \n\nwww.unhabitat.org\n\n \n\n\n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nSent: 25 July 2024 12:38\n\nTo: Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>\n\nCc: Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>; Cherrilyn Wanyangu Auma(Intern) <cherrilyn.auma@un.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNH UNOPS Thank you and next steps\n \n\nDear Ran,\n\n\n\nThank you for the productive call just now. As agreed, I am sharing the UNOPS-UN Secretariat MoU effective from May 2024, which covers our collaboration in terms of a) implementing partner services;\n and b) support services (in addition to our HR agreement).\n\n\n\nIn terms of the data from our system, please allow me a couple of days to consolidate and put it in a presentable format. Grateful if you can share the sheet that you have, so I can also use it to\n inform how I structure our mapping.\n\n\n\nThanks again and looking forward to hearing from you.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Jul 2024 at 13:45, Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org> wrote:\n\nDear Ran,\n\n\n\nThank you, the suggested slot works well. Looking forward to our conversation tomorrow.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Jul 2024 at 13:43, Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org> wrote:\n\nDear Kajsa and colleagues,\n\n\n\n\nKindly for your participation in the discussion on our collaboration.\n\nLet me know if the meeting time works.\n\n\n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\nRan\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nSent: Wednesday, July 24, 2024 11:00:13 AM\n\nTo: Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>\n\nCc: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>; Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>;\n Emilie Potvin [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>; Cherrilyn Wanyangu Auma(Intern) <cherrilyn.auma@un.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps\n \n\nDear Ran,\n\n\n\nThanks for your quick reply. Yes, I am available for a call either tomorrow morning or alternatively from Tuesday onwards next week. Please let me know when would work for you. \n\n\n\nIn the meantime, I would be grateful for any feedback in relation to point 1, as well as any contacts for implementing partner agreements.\n\n\nThanks so much in advance, and looking forward to speaking with you soon.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Jul 2024 at 12:42, Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org> wrote:\n\n\nDear Kajsa,\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you so much for the update. The information has been briefed to Erfan.\n\nTo follow-up the agreed points, would you be available for a meeting so that we can discuss into details?\n\nThank you so much and looking forward to your feedback.\n\n\n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\nRan\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nSent: 24 July 2024 12:23\n\nTo: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>; Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>\n\nCc: Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from \nkajsah@unops.org. \nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n\nI hope that you and the team are well. As promised, I am writing to get back to you on a couple of things:\n\nBilateral meeting between UNOPS & UN-Habitat EDs:\nI've received a green light from our Executive Director to organize a meeting between our EDs during the UNGA/Summit of the Future (he will be in NY from 20-25 September). I will be coordinating a letter from our Executive Director on this soon. While I\n do so, could you please confirm whether your Executive Director's start date is August 1, 2024 and if we should send the letter to Sukhjinder with you in copy?Workshop dates: \nIt would be great to organize our global workshop ahead of the meeting between our EDs, so that the workshop can also inform their conversation. I would like to suggest we find a date in the week of September 9th, if possible on your side? I will be coming\n to Nairobi in September and would be happy to plan my travel dates around the workshop. WUF12: While we are still finalizing our delegation, I can confirm that we will have a senior leader present at WUF12 representing UNOPS. I will inform you of details as I receive them, and\n we can then agree on practicalities with regards to a signing ceremony for the partnership action plan / other representation duties. As mentioned previously, we are also discussing joint visibility opportunities for WUF12 with your Chief of Communications.\nI hope that the above sounds agreeable on your side. On a final note, I was hoping to get your guidance on who to contact within UN-Habitat in relation to project implementing partner agreements.\n Our Infrastructure and Project Management Group are in the process of revising our grant agreements, and are seeking examples of implementing partner agreements with infrastructure clauses from other UN Agencies. Any tips on this would be much appreciated.\n\n\n\nWishing you a great day!\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jul 2024 at 13:58, Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org> wrote:\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n\nThank you for the quick response, sounds great. \n\n\n\nI look forward to working on the mapping exercise with Ran. It would indeed be great to lock down a date for the workshop - please feel free to suggest a few dates that would work on your end.\n\n\n\nThank you also for highlighting the opportunity for UNOPS attendance in the One UN roundtable at WUF12. I will get back to you on this soon, as we still need to lock down some details in relation\n to our presence in Cairo.\n\n\n\nWishing you a great start to the week!\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKajsa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jul 2024 at 11:42, Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org> wrote:\n\nDear Kajsa\nThanks for the note and it was my pleasure to discuss with you and I’m happy to work together to advance the partnership.\nThe only point that I may add is the possible involvement of UNOPS in the One UN round table in the World Urban Forum in Cairo in November.\nI copied here\n@Ran\n Wang who will be liaising with regional and country offices on the mapping exercise. I’ll also suggest possible dates for the workshop in September.\nAll the best\nErfan\n \n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nSent: Monday, July 15, 2024 10:55 AM\n\nTo: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>\n\nCc: Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin\n [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Thank you and next steps\n\n \nDear Erfan,\n \nMany thanks for the meeting last week, it was a pleasure to meet with you and the team.\n \nI have attached short notes of our meeting, and summarized the agreed next steps below:\n\nExpansion of programmatic collaboration\n\n\nJuly-August – UNOPS and UN-Habitat to map joint programming interests (past and potential)September – Conduct global workshop in Nairobi based on identified areas of interestOctober – Finalize joint partnership action planNovember – Formalize action plan (potentially at 12th World Urban Forum)\n\n\nHigh-level engagement\n\n\nSeptember – Organize a bilateral between UNOPS and UN-Habitat Executive Directors at the Summit of the Future.\n\nPlease feel free to add if I missed anything. I would also be grateful if you could share Ran Wang's contact so that I can advance point 1 with her. \n \nThank you again, and I look forward to our continued collaboration!\n \nKind regards,\nKajsa\n \n \n \n--\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n| UNOPS Headquarters\n| Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n| UNOPS Headquarters\n| Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n| UNOPS Headquarters\n| Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\nMicrosoft Teams\nNeed\n help?\n\nJoin\n the meeting now\n\nMeeting ID: 351 429 626 313\n\nPasscode: E9Koe9\n\n\n\n\nJoin on a video conferencing device\n\nTenant key: unitevc@m.webex.com\n\nVideo ID: 125 634 340 1\n\nMore\n info\n\nFor organisers: Meeting\n options\n\n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n| UNOPS Headquarters\n| Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n| UNOPS Headquarters\n| Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\n\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nKajsa Hartman | Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
