                new (
                    "00TQx00000DwRbVMAV",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: FCLP Secretariat: Draft MoU with the UK",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-01").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FCLP Secretariat: Draft MoU with the UK",
                        Description = "To: julieda@unops.org\nCC: naimoh@unops.org; tatianaco@unops.org; isabellav@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FCLP Secretariat: Draft MoU with the UK\nBody:\nHi Julie, \nI fully agree - what was DFID is now FCDO. So obviously we should use that one. \nAlso - I don't really see the problem when we have signed several other engagements with the FCDO without the advanced payment. \nIn any case - I have written to our UK HQ contacts to get the original standard template to ensure that we use the correct one. \nI'll connect to the meeting later today - and hopefully we will have gotten a response from the UK by then. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Wed, 31 Jul 2024 at 23:49, Julie Dahan <julieda@unops.org> wrote:\nThank you AsbjornThis is really appreciated.\nI am receiving the below message from Elsa Abete from Legal.What do you think?From my side, I am a bit surprised by her comment as DFID has closed and been replaced by FCDO.\n\nVery best, Julie\n\"Dear Julie,Thanks for sharing the draft MoU with the UK-DESNZ and the “model” used shared by Partnerships, as confirmed (we note that its a model with UK-FCDO (Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office)).Regarding the “model” and as an initial comment, I discussed internally with LG (HQ) and, as a general rule, it is advised to use the UK-DFID (Department for International Development) corporate template (that was carefully negotiated addressing all the essentials from UNOPS perspective (see below)), instead of the UK-FCDO model (that has not been agreed in the past for general use as a corporate template).https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GYA7eDrjd5AjSM2unVgEE9O6OnmNH5qf/edit#heading=h.gjdgxsCan you confirm if this is something that was contemplated and discussed specifically internally (including LG) and/or with the Partner, please? Has the Partner specifically requested the use of the UK-FCDO model instead of the UK-DFID corporate template?It would be good to discuss tomorrow early morning (NY time) also with Partnerships (before your meeting with the Partner, if possible) about this matter of the templates so we are all on the same page for this case (and future ones) in order to advance using the correct/internally agreed instrument.\"\nOn Tue, Jul 30, 2024 at 3:12 AM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Julie,\nI am super happy to hear that you're progressing well with the upcoming partnership on the FCLP secretariat. \nThe clause on the FCDO not paying in advance is indeed a standard clause used for many of their engagements. I just quickly searched and located this one - signed with the former DEID - and this one that both contains the very same clause about advanced payments - which UNOPS approved, \nI hope this helps getting a fast approval from IPAS Legal. Otherwise don't hesitate to let me know if there is anything at all I can do to help. \nDo let me know when you get to sign the agreement! \nThanks!\nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 29 Jul 2024 at 21:30, Julie Dahan <julieda@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Asbjorn,\nHope this message finds you well.I am glad to inform you that UNOPS is progressing well in its upcoming partnership with the FCLP Secretariat.\nThe UK is looking at the possibility of signing the bilateral agreement/MoU by 15th August.\nWhile Francesca reached out to you, she shared with you the following template, which has been shared with the UK.It was confirmed that it was the correct template.\n\n1. On paragraph 8 \"In line with UK Government financial regulations, FCDO will not pay in advance of operational need, unless this has been justified and approved in writing by both participants. \"Do you confirm that this is acceptable for UNOPS? UNOPS usually does not advance funds\n2. Would you be able to share any MoU signed with the UK on this basis? It will support IPAS Legal review.\nWith many thanks, Julie\nPS: Please note that we are meeting with the donor on Wednesday, and any support by then will be greatly appreciated\n-- \nJulie Dahan \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n-- \nJulie Dahan \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
