                new (
                    "00TQx00000EJjRCMA1",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS SDC high level call - notes follow ups",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-09").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS SDC high level call - notes follow ups",
                        Description = "To: martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS SDC high level call - notes follow ups\nBody:\nDear Martin, please share this email and attachments with meeting participants. Merci. Louise\nDear SDC colleagues,\nThank you very much for the productive call this week. It was a pleasure to see you all (virtually at least) and have the opportunity for a frank exchange. Please find attached draft notes and follow ups for your review and approval. Should we not hear from you by Thursday 15 August ‘close of business’, we will take these as a final record of our conversation. \nRegarding the question of risk assessment, as part of the CRP implementation, the Risk and Compliance Group of UNOPS has carried out a global project portfolio risk overview across its service lines. This covered key risks within Infrastructure, Procurement, Financial Management, Project Management and HR services, as well as associated lessons learned. The internal work was complemented by an external advisory engagement for extended risk data modelling and analysis. Please note that the report itself contains confidential information on individual partnerships and projects, and for that reason cannot be shared as a whole. However, we will prepare a short note that summarises the approach taken, the key observations and lessons learned as well as our overall framework for managing risks within the project portfolio. We will share this summary note with you and the Executive Board Members along with the next monthly update on implementation of the Comprehensive Response Plan that will be issued on 5 September 2024.   \nWe look forward to hearing from you in due course and continuing to strengthen our collaboration going forward. \nWishing you a restful weekend. On behalf of the team,Louise  \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
                        Location = null,
