                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-15").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Progress with USAID on Sunsetting July 2022 Clauses.",
                        Description = "To: emiliep@unops.org\nCC: svene@unops.org; iraklij@unops.org; vineshw@unops.org; elizabethdu@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Progress with USAID on Sunsetting July 2022 Clauses.\nBody:\nDear Emilie,I wanted to update you on our (Sven, Irakli, and myself) productive meeting yesterday with the USAID Office of Development Cooperation (ODC), in the Planning, Learning, and Resource Management Bureau (PLR), the Comptroller’s Office, and the General Counsel.Sven and Irakli delivered a comprehensive briefing on our net-zero budgeting, reserve calculations, and the process for refunding excess reserves. USAID appreciated the discussion and the insight into the significant changes we've made to our financial rules and regulations over the past two years  \nCharles Kiame, the head of ODC, monopolized most of the subsequent discussion. He asked several questions about our approach to managing reserves, cost recovery, and applying indirect costs. We assured him that our costing methodology is fully transparent, with project budgets negotiated openly, reserve levels set by the Executive Board (EB), and excess reserves returned to partners every two years, following the same process as the initial $5.6M refund. He appeared satisfied with the discussion  \nWe also discussed our collaboration with INL to develop standardized language that addresses the Bureau's concerns. I shared the INL language and proposed using a similar approach to sunset the July 2022 clauses. ODC said they will consult internally and follow up with us on the next st  \nCharles also asked about our progress on digitization, organizational culture, and whistleblower protection policies. We outlined the significant changes we've implemented in these areas and offered to provide additional briefings or information. We also noted that these topics are likely to be discussed at the upcoming EB session.  \nOverall, it was a productive meeting. I will talk with my USAID counterparts early next week to develop a plan for sunsetting these clauses this fall. \n\nYour meeting with ODC's Liz Buckingham on the sidelines of the EB will be another opportunity to support this effort, \nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need further information.Best regards,\nPatrick\n-- \nPatrick Ellsworth | Senior Partnerships Advisor | Address: 1775 K Street NW, Washington, DC 20006 |Tel: +1 703 350 2932 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube\nVirus-free.www.avast.com",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000EfRXFMA3",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "elizabethdu@unops.org", "emiliep@unops.org", "svene@unops.org", "iraklij@unops.org", "vineshw@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
