                new (
                    "00TQx00000Er8x9MAB",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Thanks and hope to see you soon!",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Thanks and hope to see you soon!",
                        Description = "To: karl.svensson@gov.se; roger.m.karlsson@gov.se\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Thanks and hope to see you soon!\nBody:\nDear Karl, \nThank you very much for briefly but properly taking good care of UNOPS during the summer time. It was a pleasure working with you and I wish you all the best for the future! \nDear Roger,Welcome onboard and I look very much forward to continuing the constructive and excellent collaboration between the Swedish MFA and UNOPS in your capable hands. \nI do not assume that you will attend the Executive Board in New York next week - but if you do, I would be very happy to invite you for a coffee to get introduced. In case you are not in NYC next week, perhaps we could schedule an introduction call for the first week of September at your convenience? Please let me know when you might be available. \nJumping right into substance, please find attached to this email - for your convenience - the statement that the ASG and Executive Director for UNOPS will give to the Executive Board next week.  \nSecondly, as I have previously discussed with your predecessors, it can be difficult to keep track of / on top of the ongoing UN tribunal involving the former UNOPS DED, Mr. Vanshelboim. \nFor your convenience and ease of reference I wanted to informally let you know that the UN tribunal case is ongoing in Geneva with regular hearings, submissions of requested documentation, etc. The latest hearing took place in Geneva on August 14. Please see here for your info a summary of the latest hearing. \nWhile it is unknown when the case will be finalised, a qualified guess is that the tribunal could present their ruling by the end of september. However, this ruling can be appealed by both parties. \nIn short, the ongoing case relates to Vanshelboim contesting the UN disciplinary measures of: DismissalA fine of 12 months’ salaryRecovering from him 63,626,806 USD - and to withhold his UN pension fund until the 63M USD has been fully recovered  \nIn case you're interested in following developments in the case, you can find all updates here. As you will see, the documents contain very detailed updates on each new document submitted, statements by the contestant, etc. \nI hope this brief overview and status of the tribunal case helps. To be clear, all of these matters are naturally handled by the OLA. The above is merely a way for you to be better capable of keeping track and being up to date. \nOnce again - looking very much forward to meeting you and continuing the excellent collaboration! \nUntil then - I hope you will have an excellent weekend!\nBest regards,Asbjørn\n\nOn Fri, 23 Aug 2024 at 13:38, Karl Svensson <karl.svensson@gov.se> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjörn,\n \nHope everything is well.\n\n \nI am writing to you since this is my last day at the Swedish MFA for this time and I will now hand over the Unops-portfolio to my dear colleague Roger Karlsson (roger.m.karlsson@gov.se).\n\nI would like to take the opportunity to express my gratitude for our cooperation during the summer and your kind and valuable support in matters regarding Unops.\n\n \nI wish you all the best and I hope we see each other soon in the future!\n \nBest regards,\n\n \nKarl Svensson\n\nDesk Officer\n\nDepartment for Multilateral Governance and Humanitarian Policy\n\nMinistry for Foreign Affairs\n\n103 39 Stockholm, Sweden\n\nMob. (+46) 076-7814493\n\nkarl.svensson@gov.se\n\nwww.government.se\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000Er8x9MAB",
