                new (
                    "00TQx00000ErHgzMAF",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Various in advance of EB next week",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Various in advance of EB next week",
                        Description = "To: Satu.Lassila@gov.fi\nCC: aki.enkenberg@gov.fi; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Various in advance of EB next week\nBody:\nDear Satu,\nI hope this email finds you well - rested after the summer break. \nFollowing Andrea's desertion to Algeria, I was wondering who might cover the UNOPS file within your unit? And might I be so lucky as to bump into you and/or that person in NYC next week? \nIn any case, I just wanted to briefly provide you with a couple of information points in advance of the EB next week: \nFirstly, In case you have not yet noticed, please find attached Jorge's statement for the EB session next week. \nSecondly, as we discussed in the past, it can be difficult to keep track of / on top of the ongoing UN tribunal involving the former UNOPS DED, Mr. Vanshelboim. \nThe UN tribunal case is ongoing in Geneva with regular hearings, submissions of requested documentation, etc. The latest hearing took place in Geneva on August 14. Please see here for your info a summary of the latest hearing. \nWhile it is unknown when the case will be finalised, a qualified guess is that the tribunal could present their ruling by the end of september. However, this ruling can be appealed by both parties. \nIn short, the ongoing case relates to Vanshelboim contesting the UN disciplinary measures of: DismissalA fine of 12 months’ salaryRecovering from him 63,626,806 USD - and to withhold his UN pension fund until the 63M USD has been fully recovered  \nIn case you're interested in following developments in the case, you can find all updates here. As you will see, the documents contain very detailed updates on each new document submitted, statements by the contestant, etc. \nI hope this brief overview and status of the tribunal case helps. To be clear, all of these matters are naturally handled by the OLA. The above is merely a way for you and your team to be better capable of keeping track and being up to date. \nBest regards,Asbjørn\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
