                new (
                    "00TQx00000F1zvHMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Thank you and next steps (UNOPS)",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-27").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Thank you and next steps (UNOPS)",
                        Description = "To: aguirres@un.org\nCC: kajsah@unops.org; AmritaN@unops.org; emiliep@unops.org; muna@un.org; habitatny@un.org; annag@unops.org; waingchita@unops.org; mikaelag@unops.org; rahulm@unops.org; draganmi@unops.org; erfan.ali@un.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps (UNOPS)\nBody:\nDear Sarah,\nThank you very much. This is confirmed on my side as well.\nAll the best,KerrieKerrie Tyas | Executive Assistant - Senior Associate to Under-Secretary-General and UNOPS Executive Director | UNOPS Executive Office | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 31 19 49 72 | www.unops.orgKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Tue, 27 Aug 2024 at 16:38, Sarah Maria Rosaria Aguirre-Degidon <aguirres@un.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kerrie,\n \nLikewise, very good to e-meet you and the UNOPS team.  Mon 23 Sept, 11:00 - 11:45 will work for a meeting between\nED Rossbach and ED da Silva.\nWe can have the meeting at UN Habitat New York office, 2 UN Plaza (DC2), East 44th St., bet. 1st/2nd\n Aves (across UNICEF and next to Millenium Hilton), 9th Floor.\nI will send an invite shortly.\n \nThank you,\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Kerrie TYAS <kerriet@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, 27 August, 2024 9:34 AM\n\nTo: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN [UNOPS] <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nCc: Sarah Maria Rosaria Aguirre-Degidon <aguirres@un.org>; Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>; Aye Aye Mun Aung <muna@un.org>; HabitatNY <habitatny@un.org>; Anna Gaarde [UNOPS] <annag@unops.org>; Waing\n Chit Aung [UNOPS] <waingchita@unops.org>; Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>; Mikaela SOLFRID GERKMAN <mikaelag@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps (UNOPS)\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nkerriet@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa and Sarah,\n\n\n \n\n\nKajsa - thank you for connecting us.\n\n\n \n\n\nSarah - it's a pleasure to e-meet you and thank you for sending the available time slots.  I have added a placeholder in our ED's agenda for 23 Sept, 11:00 - 11:45.  Is that time still available?\n\n\n \n\n\nWill this meeting take place at the UN Habitat office, or would you like me to find a meeting room at UNOPS?\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks,\n\n\nKerrie\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nKerrie Tyas\n\n| Executive\n\nAssistant - Senior Associate to Under-Secretary-General and UNOPS Executive Director | UNOPS Executive Office | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 31 19 49 72 |\n\nwww.unops.org\n\nKeep up-to-date with\n\nUNOPS. Follow us on\nTwitter,\n\nLinkedIn,\n\nFacebook,\n\nInstagram,\n\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSubscribe to\n\nour external newsletter in\nEnglish,\n\nFrench\n\nor \nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 23 Aug 2024 at 16:43, Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sarah,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for getting back to us with some time slots, much appreciated. Allow me to add Kerrie Tyas from our Executive Office in the loop, so that she can help identify a suitable slot. \n\n\n \n\n\nDear Kerrie,\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find below some suggested time slots for the proposed bilateral meeting with USG Anacláudia Marinheiro Centeno Rossbach, ED of UN Human Settlements Programme. Grateful if you could let\n us know whether one of these would suit our ED's schedule.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 23 Aug 2024 at 16:23, Sarah Maria Rosaria Aguirre-Degidon <aguirres@un.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa,\n \nTrust this finds you well.  I can help coordinate the meeting request between ED Rossbach and USG Jorge\n Moreira da Silva, ED of UN Office of Project Services (UNOPS).\nNoted that ED da Silva will be in New York from 20-25 September. \n\n \nThe current availabilities are (may be subject to change):\nMon 23 Sept: 11am-12:30pm, 3:00pm – 5:30pm\nTues 24 Sept: 9am-10am, 2:00pm-3:00pm\nWed 25 Sept: open\n \nKindly advise on a suitable time slot.\n \nThank you,\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, 30 July, 2024 9:22 AM\n\nTo: Runze Wang <runze.wang@un.org>\n\nCc: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>; Sarah Maria Rosaria\n Aguirre-Degidon <aguirres@un.org>; Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>;\n Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin [UNOPS]\n <emiliep@unops.org>; Andre Dzikus <andre.dzikus@un.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nkajsah@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Runze,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for taking this forward. \n\n\n \n\n\nOur ED is scheduled to be in New York between 20-25 September 2024, and it would be great to organize the meeting during this time\n frame if possible. We will soon be in touch with you and Sarah together with our Executive Office to identify suitable slots.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 30 Jul 2024 at 14:17, Runze Wang <runze.wang@un.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa,\n\n \nGreetings and well noted the proposed bilateral in NY in Sep. I am looping in my colleague Sarah from our NYO to please capture and propose\n slots when ready.\n \n\n\nBest regards,\nRunze Wang\n \nSpecial Assistant to the Executive Director\nUnited Nations Human Settlements Programme (UN-Habitat)\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nM (K): +254\n 717 080 969 | M (US): +1 917 615 2146\nE: runze.wang@un.org\n | W: www.unhabitat.org\nP: P.O.\n Box 30030, GPO Nairobi 00100, Kenya\n\nA: UNON\n Complex, United Nations Avenue, Gigiri, Nairobi, Kenya\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\nFrom:\nKajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\nDate: Thursday, 25 July 2024 at 09:17\n\nTo: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>\n\nCc: Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>, Runze Wang <runze.wang@un.org>, Amrita NAUL\n [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>, Emilie Potvin [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nkajsah@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n \n\n\nIt is good to hear from you, and many thanks for sharing the updates. Please see my responses below:\n\n\n \n\n\n1. The start date and contact details are well noted and much appreciated, I will also convey this information to our Executive Office.\n Pleasure to meet you, Runze.\n\n\n2. Excellent, let's plan for the week of September 9th. Ran and I will meet today and scope out the details.\n\n\n3. This is well noted from our side, and happy to discuss further with both you and Ran what the appropriate format for the partnership\n action plan should be.\n\n\n4. The standard implementing partner agreement would work great, in case you have a copy to share - particularly any standard clauses\n on infrastructure would be of interest.\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you so much, and have a great start to the day!\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 24 Jul 2024 at 17:21, Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa\n\nThanks for the kind feedback. I discussed yesterday with Rana and I see she’s following up directly with you.\n\nLet me also share the following:\n\n\n\nOn the Bilateral this is highly appreciated and\n@Runze Wang will follow on this. New ED will start officially on 8 August.\n\nThe week of 9th of August should  be fine and I leave it to Ran to confirm date and other details with you\n\nThanks for the update on WUF and I’ll ask Katerina the head of communication to keep us informed. We may need to conclude any draft agreement by end  of September to give sufficient time for legal review.\n\nOn implementing partner agreement, we have an internal policy since 2017 (which is under review and update now), however I could share here the standard implementing partner agreement of the UN secretariat which we\n apply as well. \nAll the best\n\nErfan\n\n \n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, July 24, 2024 12:24 PM\n\nTo: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>; Ran Wang <ran.wang@un.org>\n\nCc: Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin\n [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Thank you and next steps\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope that you and the team are well. As promised, I am writing to get back to you on a couple of things:\n\n\n\n\nBilateral meeting between UNOPS & UN-Habitat EDs:\nI've received a green light from our Executive Director to organize a meeting between our EDs during the UNGA/Summit of the Future (he will be in NY from 20-25 September). I will be coordinating\n a letter from our Executive Director on this soon. While I do so, could you please confirm whether your Executive Director's start date is August 1, 2024 and if we should send the letter to Sukhjinder with you in copy?\nWorkshop dates: \nIt would be great to organize our global workshop ahead of the meeting between our EDs, so that the workshop can also inform their conversation. I would like to suggest we find a date in the week\n of September 9th, if possible on your side? I will be coming to Nairobi in September and would be happy to plan my travel dates around the workshop. \nWUF12: While we are still finalizing our delegation, I can confirm that we will have a senior leader present at WUF12 representing\n UNOPS. I will inform you of details as I receive them, and we can then agree on practicalities with regards to a signing ceremony for the partnership action plan / other representation duties. As mentioned previously, we are also discussing joint visibility\n opportunities for WUF12 with your Chief of Communications.\n\nI hope that the above sounds agreeable on your side. On a final note, I was hoping to get your guidance on who to contact\n within UN-Habitat in relation to project implementing partner agreements. Our Infrastructure and Project Management Group are in the process of revising our grant agreements, and are seeking examples of implementing partner agreements with infrastructure clauses\n from other UN Agencies. Any tips on this would be much appreciated.\n\n\n \n\n\nWishing you a great day!\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jul 2024 at 13:58, Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for the quick response, sounds great. \n\n\n \n\n\nI look forward to working on the mapping exercise with Ran. It would indeed be great to lock down a date for the workshop\n - please feel free to suggest a few dates that would work on your end.\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you also for highlighting the opportunity for UNOPS attendance in the One UN roundtable at WUF12. I will get back\n to you on this soon, as we still need to lock down some details in relation to our presence in Cairo.\n\n\n \n\n\nWishing you a great start to the week!\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jul 2024 at 11:42, Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Kajsa\n\nThanks for the note and it was my pleasure to discuss with you and I’m happy to work together to advance the partnership.\n\nThe only point that I may add is the possible involvement of UNOPS in the One UN round table in the World Urban Forum in Cairo in November.\n\nI copied here\n@Ran Wang who will be liaising with regional and country offices on the mapping exercise.\n I’ll also suggest possible dates for the workshop in September. \nAll the best\n\nErfan\n\n \n\nFrom: Kajsa Johanna HARTMAN <kajsah@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, July 15, 2024 10:55 AM\n\nTo: Erfan Ali <erfan.ali@un.org>\n\nCc: Amrita NAUL [UNOPS] <AmritaN@unops.org>; Emilie Potvin\n [UNOPS] <emiliep@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Thank you and next steps\n\n \n\n\n\n\nDear Erfan,\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for the meeting last week, it was a pleasure to meet with you and the team.\n\n\n \n\n\nI have attached short notes of our meeting, and summarized the agreed next steps below:\n\n\n\n\nExpansion of programmatic collaboration\n\n\n\nJuly-August – UNOPS and UN-Habitat to map joint programming interests (past and potential)\nSeptember – Conduct global workshop in Nairobi based on identified areas of interest\nOctober – Finalize joint partnership action plan\nNovember – Formalize action plan (potentially at 12th World Urban Forum)\n\n\n\nHigh-level engagement\n\n\n\nSeptember – Organize a bilateral between UNOPS and UN-Habitat Executive Directors at the Summit of the Future.\n\n\nPlease feel free to add if I missed anything. I would also be grateful if you could share Ran Wang's contact so that I\n can advance point 1 with her. \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you again, and I look forward to our continued collaboration!\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nKajsa\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\nKajsa Hartman\n| Partnerships Specialist | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS Headquarters | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench or\nSpanish.",
