                new (
                    "00TQx00000F2FAcMAN",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review",
                        Description = "To: mariawe@unops.org\nCC: mohammedameers@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review\nBody:\nDear Maria,\n \nThank you for these inputs, allow me to come back to you when we have the final list of side events ready.\n \nBest regards,\nDenise\n \n\nFrom: Maria WERNEVI <mariawe@unops.org> \n\nSent: Thursday, August 22, 2024 8:26 PM\n\nTo: Denise Laaveri <denise.laaveri@unwomen.org>\n\nCc: Mohammed Ameer SOBHAN <mohammedameers@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review\n\n \n\n\nThank you Denise for the very quick response!\n\n \n\n\nI am very sorry we missed the deadline. Yes gender-sensitive infrastructure is a topic that we know well.\n\n\n \n\n\nI am not sure what was submitted by others but we could for example talk about \n\n\n- how “access” to safe transport and safe roads\nbenefits women and other vulnerable groups\n\n\n- How inclusive and rights-based climate action must be integrated into infrastructure development\n\n\n- infrastructure built on Equitable Principles\n\n\n-Importance of Physical Design for Universal Access and Safety\n\n\n- development of digital systems, data sharing and analysis to protect against GBV\n\n\n \n\n\nand overarching is that a physical infrastructure asset is built to last for a long time - so if done wrong it will cause harm over a long period or be a very costly activity to redo.\n\n\n \n\n\nI think all of the above could fit- depending on the submissions - under\n\na-d in the agenda\n\n\n \n\n\nAgain thank you for the very quick response and happy to meet and discuss if you find that we could contribute.\n\n\n \n\n\nHave a nice evening! Maria\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Aug 22, 2024 at 6:57 PM Denise Laaveri <denise.laaveri@unwomen.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Ameer,\n \nThanks very much and will do. Are you/Maria interested in speaking on a the same topic – gender-sensitive infrastructure?\n \nBest\nDenise\n \n\n\nFrom: Mohammed Ameer SOBHAN <mohammedameers@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, August 22, 2024 6:55 PM\n\nTo: Denise Laaveri <denise.laaveri@unwomen.org>\n\nCc: Maria WERNEVI <mariawe@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nmohammedameers@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMany thanks for the quick response, Denise. That is indeed a pity. \n\n\n\nPlease do feel free to reach out if any of the organizers would like speakers or moderators for any of the panels as UNOPS would be happy to support that too. \n\n\n\nBest wishes,\n\nAmeer \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAmeer Sobhan (he/him) | Change Management Senior Officer | Strategy and Transformation Group\n | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Aug 22, 2024 at 1:45 PM Denise Laaveri <denise.laaveri@unwomen.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Ameer,\n \nThanks so much for reaching out and it’s nice to e-meet you.\n \nI am afraid that I don’t have good news in terms of the side events – the deadline for receiving applications has already passed and we are already in the process of shortlisting\n the proposals submitted. This year, we received almost 50 applications and we can accommodate approx. 20 in total so many will ultimately be rejected.\n \nVery sorry for being the bearer of bad news.\n \nAll the best,\nDenise\n \n\n\nFrom: Mohammed Ameer SOBHAN <mohammedameers@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, August 22, 2024 6:13 PM\n\nTo: Denise Laaveri <denise.laaveri@unwomen.org>; Maria WERNEVI <mariawe@unops.org>\n\nSubject: UNOPS-UN Women collaboration on Asia Pacific MC on Beijing+30 Review\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nmohammedameers@unops.org.\nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Denise,\n\n\n\n\nGreat to connect with you (and many thanks to Joelle for putting us in touch). UNOPS and UN Women previously worked together to organize a side-event during the Beijing+25 Review and given the upcoming Asia Pacific Ministerial Conference on the Beijing+30 Review,\n we wanted to reach out to you to see if we can work together on something again in November. I've attached the flyer for our last event for your reference.\n\n\n \n\n\nWould you be available for a quick call with @Maria WERNEVI , who is the Regional Advisor on Project Management and Gender\n for UNOPS Asia Region? I'm currently based in Copenhagen but happy to help in any way I can!\n\n\n\n\nBest wishes,\n\n\nAmeer\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nAmeer Sobhan (he/him) | Change Management Senior Officer | Strategy and Transformation Group\n | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | www.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n\n\nMaria\n\n\n \n\n\n\nMaria Wernevi (Ms.)\n| Regional Advisor Project Management and Gender Mainstreaming & Social Inclusion | Office of the Regional\n Director | Asia Region | Bangkok, Thailand | Mob: +66 98 282 1402 or +45 2255 9197 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
