                        Name = "Email: Fwd: Request for a consultation on new UK Caribbean Resilient Infrastructure Platform",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-08-28").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: Request for a consultation on new UK Caribbean Resilient Infrastructure Platform",
                        Description = "To: giuseppem@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: Request for a consultation on new UK Caribbean Resilient Infrastructure Platform\nBody:\nFYI :)Isabela Fraiz | Partnerships Senior Analyst, Process Innovation & Digitalisation | Partnerships and Liaison Group (PLG) | UNOPS Headquarters | Tel: +507 64839508 | www.unops.orgKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube. \nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Caroline Fouvet <Caroline.Fouvet@mottmac.com>\nDate: Wed, Aug 28, 2024 at 3:54 PM\nSubject: Request for a consultation on new UK Caribbean Resilient Infrastructure Platform\nTo: antoinel@unops.org <antoinel@unops.org>, williamsg@unops.org <williamsg@unops.org>, isabelaf@unops.org <isabelaf@unops.org>\nCc: Joanna Burton <joanna.burton1@fcdo.gov.uk>, Emma Robinson <Emma.Robinson1@fcdo.gov.uk>, Asia.Williams@mdy.co.uk <asia.williams@mdy.co.uk>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear William, Antoine and Isabela,\n \nAs you may be aware, the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) is currently reviewing options for the next phase of its climate resilient infrastructure programming\n in the Caribbean.  The proposed UK Caribbean Resilient Infrastructure Platform (UK CRIP) will build upon the existing efforts under the UK Caribbean Infrastructure Fund (UK CIF), as well as ongoing programmatic work supported by the UK in Jamaica.\n \nWe have been commissioned by the UK Government to support the scoping and design effort. The FCDO has suggested that we reach out to you to discuss the regional challenges facing\n resilient infrastructure development, and to get your view on the possible options for institutional structure, financing and technical assistance approach for the new facility.\n\n \nTo discuss the above, we would like to arrange a short call with you over the next 2-3 weeks. Please let me know if any of these dates/timeslots could work for you, otherwise\n we can look into alternative options:\n\nSeptember 6th at 5:00pm (Spain time)September 12th at 5:00pm (Spain time)\n \nLet me know if you have any questions. You may also contact FCDO (copied) if you wish to discuss directly with them.  Otherwise, we look forward to speaking with you shortly.\n \nBest wishes,\n \nCaroline\nCRIP - Programme Options Expert\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCaroline Fouvet\n\nSenior Consultant - Climate Policy & Finance\nD +442087742237     \nT +34 910 389 528     \n\ncaroline.fouvet@mottmac.com\nLinkedIn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMott MacDonald\n\nPº de la Castellana, 77\n\nPlanta 9\n\n28046 Madrid \n\nSpain \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWebsite\n  |   LinkedIn\n  |   Instagram\n  |   Facebook\n  |   YouTube\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMott MacDonald Spain, S.L.U.\n\nNIF B88234455 \n\n\n\nThe information contained in this e-mail is intended only for the person or entity to which it is addressed and may contain confidential and/or privileged material. If you are not the intended recipient of this e-mail, the use of this information or any disclosure,\n copying or distribution is prohibited and may be unlawful. If you received this in error, please contact the sender and delete the material from any computer.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMott MacDonald Restricted",
