                    "00TQx00000FGUhaMAH",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-07-26").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: solv@unops.org\nCC: benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org; mgreco@iadb.org; IGNACIOH@iadb.org; robertole@iadb.org; ALAINLO@iadb.org; vivianama@iadb.org; JUANITAR@iadb.org; SAMANTAT@iadb.org; valeriede@unops.org; SARAVI@iadb.org; ESTEBANDE@iadb.org; anneclaireh@unops.org; arantzazuo@unops.org; elisabets@unops.org; elsaa@unops.org; fernandoc@unops.org; giuseppem@unops.org; isabelaf@unops.org; josem@unops.org; leonardoquinteros@unops.org; leyres@unops.org; VITORIAL@iadb.org; PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org; mauricioh@unops.org; pedrogt@unops.org; DENISEC@iadb.org; sofiateresama@unops.org; svene@unops.org; sylviaac@unops.org; vineshw@unops.org; mariabal@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\nBody:\nDear Sol,\n \nThanks for your message and looking forward to receiving the cleared PFA.\n\nCertainly, we will continue working to finalize the template.\n\n \nI will get back to you on the other questions. Let me speak with my colleagues in our partnerships office.\n \nBest regards,\nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, July 25, 2024 6:33 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Anne-Claire HOWARD <anneclaireh@unops.org>; Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Elisabet SOLE PORTERO <elisabets@unops.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>; Fernando COTRIM BARBIERI <fernandoc@unops.org>;\n Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Herrera, Ignacio <IGNACIOH@iadb.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>; Leal Rosillo, Roberto <robertole@IADB.ORG>; Leonardo Aristides\n QUINTERO BELIZ <leonardoquinteros@unops.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Mauricio HIMEDE PALOMO <mauricioh@unops.org>;\n Maya Iglesias, Viviana Mariela <vivianama@IADB.ORG>; Pedro GRACIA TOQUERO <pedrogt@unops.org>; Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sofia Teresa MELENDEZ APARICIO <sofiateresama@unops.org>; Sven ECKERT <svene@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Torres Lasso Samanta Dayann <SAMANTAT@IADB.ORG>; Valerie Alexandra DELLA TOGNA ALARCON <valeriede@unops.org>; Vila Saint Etienne, Sara <SARAVI@IADB.ORG>; Vinesh WINODAN <vineshw@unops.org>; de Dobrzynski, Esteban\n <ESTEBANDE@IADB.ORG>; mariabal@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSubject: Coordination and Next Steps for PFA and Template Review/ Sign off \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nDear Shirley,\n\n\n \n\n\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I want to inform you that internally, we are in the final stage of clearance, just waiting for the Finance Group to approve topics of their competence. Hopefully, we will be able to send it tomorrow morning.\n Regarding the template, we are still in the process of internal review. We hope to share a version with our comments soon, especially since it is a binding document to the PFA and one of the added values we see in the PFA. As you mentioned, this PFA will be\n signed during the IDB General Assembly in September (SoF/ UNGA). On behalf of the IDB, would it be the President's signing? Do you recommend it be the Executive Director of UNOPS to maintain reciprocity? What would be the approximate dates and location? I\n ask because the UNOPS Executive Director's office is already coordinating and scheduling bilateral meetings. I need to share this with colleagues from the OED in Copenhagen HQ to ensure the space within the UNGA framework.  \n\n\n \n\n\nAdditionally, I would like to inquire who you recommend from UNOPS to accompany our Executive Director on this crucial milestone occasion of the signing. Since this agreement is promoted by the LAC region of UNOPS to maintain coherence\n with the benefits to the member countries of IDB and where UNOPS has a presence, it is essential to maintain proportion and reciprocity in the protocol to follow in this process. We can delve into these details further, but it is crucial to start coordinating\n with the respective IDB unit in a timely manner. \n\n\n \n\n\nI would appreciate it if you could provide us with the IDB contacts we should eventually coordinate with. Could you please send the contacts from the Office of the IDB President, and the Partnerships Office to whom we can contact to arrange\n accordingly? This will allow our OED to include this in the ED agenda within the framework of the UNGA, where this PFA/template would be signed. \n\n\n \n\n\nSpecial thanks to you for the progress, leadership, communication, the IDB & UNOPS team's support and commitment to these negotiations for the benefit of the LAC region and its citizens.\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you soon. \n\n\n \n\n\nWarm regards,\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own\n working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507 61695775 | Email:\nSolv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on \nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in \nEnglish, \nFrench or \nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEl El lun, 22 de jul de 2024 a la(s) 7:00 a.m., Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org> escribió:\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol and colleagues,\n \nPlease see attached for the draft Output Template for your attention.\n \nHope to hear from you soon.\n\n\n\n\n \nKind regards,\nShirley\n\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 19, 2024 2:16 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Elisabet SOLE PORTERO <elisabets@unops.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia\n <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Herrera, Ignacio <IGNACIOH@iadb.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>;\n Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>; Leal Rosillo, Roberto <robertole@IADB.ORG>; Leonardo Aristides QUINTERO BELIZ <leonardoquinteros@unops.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>;\n Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Mauricio HIMEDE PALOMO <mauricioh@unops.org>; Maya Iglesias, Viviana Mariela <vivianama@IADB.ORG>;\n Pedro GRACIA TOQUERO <pedrogt@unops.org>; Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>;\n Sofia Teresa MELENDEZ APARICIO <sofiateresama@unops.org>; Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Torres Lasso Samanta Dayann <SAMANTAT@IADB.ORG>;\n Valerie Alexandra DELLA TOGNA ALARCON <valeriede@unops.org>; Vila Saint Etienne, Sara <SARAVI@IADB.ORG>; Vinesh WINODAN <vineshw@unops.org>;\n Xiomara Hernandez <xhernandez@bcie.org>; de Dobrzynski, Esteban <ESTEBANDE@IADB.ORG>;\nmariabal@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\n\nThanks, Shirley, for your prompt response. We will revert soon and accordingly. If you have any other questions or suggestions please let us know. \n\n\n\nFor now, we have a meeting scheduled today at 3:30 PM Panama time to reach an agreement on some clauses in the legal area as discussed today in our Teams meeting.\n\n\n\nWarm regards\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nEl El vie, 19 de jul de 2024 a la(s) 12:53 p.m., Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n escribió:\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol and colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for a productive meeting. I have responded in line in the message you sent.\n \nThanks for you continued cooperation.\n\n \nWishing all a good weekend.\n \nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 19, 2024 12:04 PM\n\nTo: de Dobrzynski, Esteban <ESTEBANDE@IADB.ORG>\n\nCc: Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Elisabet SOLE PORTERO <elisabets@unops.org>; Gayle, Shirley Maud\n <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Herrera, Ignacio <IGNACIOH@iadb.org>;\n Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>; Leal Rosillo, Roberto <robertole@IADB.ORG>;\n Leonardo Aristides QUINTERO BELIZ <leonardoquinteros@unops.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lima de Moraes, Vitoria <VITORIAL@IADB.ORG>;\n Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Mauricio HIMEDE PALOMO <mauricioh@unops.org>;\n Maya Iglesias, Viviana Mariela <vivianama@IADB.ORG>; Pedro GRACIA TOQUERO <pedrogt@unops.org>; Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sofia Teresa MELENDEZ APARICIO <sofiateresama@unops.org>; Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>;\n Torres Lasso Samanta Dayann <SAMANTAT@IADB.ORG>; Valerie Alexandra DELLA TOGNA ALARCON <valeriede@unops.org>; Vila Saint Etienne, Sara <SARAVI@IADB.ORG>;\n Xiomara Hernandez <xhernandez@bcie.org>;\nmariabal@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Shirley, Esteban and Colleagues \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nWe greatly appreciate today's meeting. From our end, we would like to request the following:\n\n\n \n\n\n1. IDB will send the recent version v7 (sent today)  confirming this was sent post meeting by Esteban. Please note the 4 items pending your action in\n his email.\n\n\n \n\n\n2. IDB will send a template that includes clauses 3.2, 3.3, and 12.1 for our review.\nApologies, appears we did not yet send the template as we were still on the PFA. Will send it shortly.\n\n\n \n\n\n3. Will the template be attached as an annex to the PFA, or it will be mentioned in the PFA? We understand it is binding. \nThe template will not be annexed but will be binding. Hence the reference in 10.5 of the PFA\n\n\n \n\n\n4. Clause 10.5 indicates \"that are agreed to,\" assuming that both parties clear the template .\nYes,  the clause anticipates that we will negotiate and agree the template which will be binding.  \n\n\n \n\n\n5. Tentatively, our Regional Director for LAC, Mr. Fabrizio Feliciani would be the person signing on behalf of UNOPS (to be confirmed). On IDB’s side, who would be signing the PFA? The\n IDB President will sign the agreement. We therefore kindly request that his counterpart, the UNOPS Executive Director, sign for UNOPS.\n\n\n \n\n\n6. This afternoon, María, another colleague from Legal, Leonardo, and I will be meeting with Benedetta to define clauses 5.3 and 12.1 OK\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you again for your support and understanding on these matters , and we look forward to receiving the draft of the template as soon as possible.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards\n\n\nHave a great weekend \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, Jul 19, 2024 at 9:49 AM de Dobrzynski, Esteban <ESTEBANDE@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear UNOPS Colleagues,\n\n \nThank you very much for today’s meeting.\n\n \nPlease find attached an updated version of the PFA. I have cleared all the language that we have agreed on, leaving\n only the four issues we await your confirmation on:\n \n(i)              \nRules and Regulations: Paragraph 1.1 (g)\n(ii)             \nIntegrity List of Sanctions: Paragraph 5.3\n(iii)           \nChannel of communication: Paragraph 9.1 (ii)\n(iv)           \nDispute Resolution: Paragraph 12.1\n \nAs mentioned, we are time-pressed to conclude this negotiation today, so we would appreciate a reply as soon as possible.\n\n \nDo not hesitate to let us know should you have any further queries.  \n \nKind regards,\n\nEsteban\n\n \n \nEsteban de\nDobrzynski\nAttorney - Legal Senior Specialist\nSovereign Guaranteed Operations\nLegal Department\nTel: +1 (202) 623-1473\n \n \n\n\n\n1300 New York Avenue, N.W.\n\nWashington, D.C. 20577\n\nUSA\n\nwww.iadb.org\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, July 18, 2024 3:42 PM\n\nTo: Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Leonardo Aristides QUINTERO BELIZ <leonardoquinteros@unops.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Sylvia AGUILAR\n CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Valerie Alexandra DELLA TOGNA ALARCON <valeriede@unops.org>; Xiomara Hernandez <xhernandez@bcie.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Shirley. Hope everything is going well.\n \nPlease find attached the latest version of the MoU (v.6) considering UNOPS suggestions and comments for your review. This version considers proposed changes in some articles (in\n track changes and highlighted for easy reference) and additional comments that we would like to clarify in our meeting.\n \n\nAlso we would like to validate if you have the opportunity to review the template for project implementation that UNOPS shared on July 5. This template was recently\n used in Argentina and we would also be interested in including additional templates tailored to the categories of projects that UNOPS implements. It is very important for us to agree on the templates as part of this MoU.\n \nBest regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, Jul 12, 2024 at 3:00 PM Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\n \nThanks for your response. I have sent a meeting invitation for Friday, July 19 at 8-10 am Panama time.  Kindly send us the reviewed documents prior\n to the meeting so that we have the opportunity to review and address comments in preparation for the meeting.  In doing this, we can use the time more efficiently.\n \nHave a great weekend.   \n \nRegards,\nDenise\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 12, 2024 2:59 PM\n\nTo: Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Leonardo Aristides QUINTERO BELIZ <leonardoquinteros@unops.org>;\n Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\nDear Shirley & Denise\n\n\n \n\n\nAt the moment, I propose a team meeting for Friday, July 16, 8-10 am Panama Time, while we work on the documents reviewed by the IDB and additional comments.\n\n\nPlease let me know if this is suitable for your team.\n\n\nWarm regards\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of\n normal working hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama\n City, Panama | Mobile: +507 61695775 | Email: \nSolv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, Jul 12, 2024 at 8:01 AM Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol and Isabela,\n \nIn follow-up to Shirley’s email, would 2 pm Denmark time (8 am DC time) on July 19th be okay for your team?\n \nRegards,\nDenise\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 12, 2024 8:00 AM\n\nTo: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n\nCc: Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n\n \nDear Sol and Isabel,\n \nGood morning.  Just following up to see if you want to meet on the 19th. I believe we could wrap up the\n PFA in that meeting.  Denise and Pati will schedule with you as I am traveling. I think 9-11 could work.\n \nThanks so much.\n \nShirley\n \n\n\nFrom: Gayle, Shirley Maud\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, July 9, 2024 3:18 PM\n\nTo: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\nCc: Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>;\n Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sven ECKERT <svene@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n\n \nHi Sol,\nThanks for your message. We are in other negotiations this week and have some other commitments early next week. Can\n we set the 2-hour block on Friday, July 19 to finalize the documents? \n \nIn the meantime, we will coordinate with Isabel on the Output Template to make it ready.  We will share a revision\n soon. \n \nThanks for your kind cooperation.\n \nBest regards\nShirley\n \n \n\nFrom: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, July 9, 2024 10:56 AM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>;\n Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>; Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Sven ECKERT <svene@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\n\nDear Shirley, \n\n\n \n\n\n\nGood morning! I hope all is going well on your end. I would like to inquire if a date has been set for our meeting early next week ( preferably 2 hours from 8-10 am Panama time),\n as it would be optimal to advance in these proceedings. Please note that some Unops’ team members will be on annual leave in August, and I hope to avoid any delays in this important process for both parties. I remain at your disposal for any further inquiries. \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI choose to work flexibly and send emails at a time that suits me, which may be outside of normal working\n hours. There is no need to respond outside of your own working hours.\n\n\n \n\nSaludos cordiales / Best regards,\n\n\n\n \n\n\nSol Villa Michel | Head of Partnerships | Latin America and the Caribbean Region | Regional Office | Panama City, Panama | Mobile: +507\n 61695775 | Email: Solv@unops.org | www.unops.org \n\n\n \n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook, \nLinkedIn, \nTwitter, \nInstagram, \nYouTube.  \n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, Jul 5, 2024 at 3:22 PM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Isabela and colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for returning the documents. We are looking forward to finalizing with you at the earliest. \n\n \nAs the team will not be available next week due to other commitments, we would like to propose another date. Denise\n will coordinate with you on Monday to find the most convenient date and time.\n \nKind regards and have a good weekend.\n\n \nShirley\n \n\nFrom: Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, July 5, 2024 1:54 PM\n\nTo: Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n\nCc: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>; Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>; Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>;\n Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>; Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>; Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>;\n Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n \n\nDear Shirley and colleagues, \n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached the latest version of the MoU (v4.0) with our proposal regarding the fee (section 8.1) and the template for project implementation we propose to include annexed\n to the MoU. This template is based on a project we recently signed in Argentina, it is in Spanish, so it would require translation to both English and French once approved. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe'd like to propose next Thursday 11th, 8:30-9:30 AM Panama/9:30-10:30 AM Washington DC for our meeting. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jul 2, 2024 at 1:31 PM Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\nHi Shirley, \n\n \n\n\nPlease disregard my previous email as we managed to find a solution.\n\n\n \n\n\nOur teams are reviewing the document and we will add the suggested template at the bottom, in accordance to the previous email. We'll send it back as soon as possible, this will\n facilitate reviewing it ahead of our next meeting. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best, \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Jul 2, 2024 at 7:21 AM Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA <isabelaf@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Shirley, \n\n \n\n\nWould it be possible to re-send the latest version of the MoU in google docs? we didn't have this problem before, but this time around this file in particular isn't being supported\n by google. We can see the new comments yet we can't add anything to the document, and we need to be able to edit the file to include the information that is being requested. \n\n\n \n\n\nThanks in advance for the support. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMrs. Isabela Fraiz \n| Senior Associate for\nPartnerships & Communications\n| Regional Office for Latin America and the Caribbean | Panama | Tel: +507 306 3638 | Mob: +507 648 39508 |\nwww.unops.org \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Jun 28, 2024 at 5:44 AM Gayle, Shirley Maud <SHIRLEYG@iadb.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Sol,\nHappy Friday! Please find attached the draft PFA with our comments.\n\n \nWe have sent the meeting invitation for Monday.\n\n \nHave a good weekend!\n \nShirley\n \n\n\nFrom: Gayle, Shirley Maud\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, June 26, 2024 11:29 AM\n\nTo: Sol VILLA MICHEL MORALES <solv@unops.org>\n\nCc: Martin-Albo Jimenez, Patricia <PATRICIAMAR@iadb.org>;\n Leyre SASTRE SEBASTIAN <leyres@unops.org>; Isabela FRAIZ SOMOZA\n <isabelaf@unops.org>; Elsa ABETE <elsaa@unops.org>;\n Arantzazu OJINAGA <arantzazuo@unops.org>; Jose MOSCOSO <josem@unops.org>;\n Sylvia AGUILAR CAMACHO <sylviaac@unops.org>; Villely Vivel\n VILLARRUE MITCHELL <villelyv@unops.org>; Benedetta Audia <benedetta.audia@intldevelopment.org>;\n Salabie, Denise Ann <DENISEC@iadb.org>; Greco, Maria Sofia <mgreco@IADB.ORG>;\n Lopez, Alain <ALAINLO@iadb.org>; Riano Londono, Juanita <JUANITAR@iadb.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Negotiation of Procedural Framework Agreement IDB-UNOPS\n\n\n \nDear Sol,\nIt was our pleasure to have you here at the IDB and we look forward to meeting other members of the team.\nWe have no objection to the inclusion of some language addressing coverage of UNOPS’ fees as an eligible expense. For\n the Bank however, it is absolutely critical that the agreement is definitive on the fees, either in terms of a range or at the minimum, a cap.\n\n \nWe hope that we can find a meeting point on this key issue. We are inviting your team to a meet this Monday July 1,\n at 10:30 where we can finalize the document.\n \nKind regards,",
