                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: AEF / UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-09-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: AEF / UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: celiaafricak@unops.org\nCC: ewelina.oblacewicz@africaeuropefoundation.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: AEF / UNOPS\nBody:\nHI Celia,\nWe are on the first floor at Square de Meeus 5-6.\nSee you shortly, my mobile phone is 0499347508, should you need to reach out,\nBest\nHoly\n \n\nHoly Ranaivozanany​​​​Deputy Executive DirectorAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Actionholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.orgSquare de Meeûs 5‑6, B‑1000 Brussels\nFrom: Celia KELLER MARTINEZ <celiaafricak@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, 3 September 2024 15:18\n\nTo: Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nCc: Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>; Andrea Konstantinidi <andrea.konstantinidi@africaeuropefoundation.org>; Taskeen Khan <taskeen.khan@africaeuropefoundation.org>; Ewelina Oblacewicz <ewelina.oblacewicz@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nSubject: Re: AEF / UNOPS\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Holy, \n\n \n\n\nThanks a lot for sharing the concept note, I look forward to discussing everything in detail tomorrow!\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nCelia\n\n\n\n\n\nCelia Keller Martínez\n(she/her) | Senior Partnerships and Communication Officer (OIC) | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | UNOPS |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram, and\nYouTube. \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Sep 2, 2024 at 6:36 PM Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Celia,\n \nThanks for this,\nAhead of our meeting this Wednesday 10.30 at our AEF office  (Square de Meeus 5-6) – (sent the outlook invite), please see attached the\n concept note for our joint event with Amref and PAJCA on Sept 24. We can discuss the general agenda then, on both sides.\nLooking forward to our meeting!\n \nBest\nHoly\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHoly Ranaivozanany​​​​\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeputy Executive Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n, \n\n\nB‑1000 Brussels\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Celia\n KELLER MARTINEZ <celiaafricak@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, 30 August 2024 15:50\n\nTo: Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nCc: Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>; Andrea Konstantinidi <andrea.konstantinidi@africaeuropefoundation.org>;\n Taskeen Khan <taskeen.khan@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nSubject: Re: AEF / UNOPS\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Holy,\n\n\n\nLovely to hear from you! \n\n \n\n\nThank you for sharing the programme with us and congratulations on such an interesting array of events and meetings. We have shared it with our events team in\n HQ so they can support in identifying a suitable UNOPS speaker, and they have expressed interest in the Amref session you propose. Do you have any confirmed speakers that we could share with our team? This would help them assess which UNOPS speaker would be\n best suited. In addition, we think the Africa-Europe Women Leaders Network could be of interest for our Director of Partnerships. If you have any information (concept note or list of speakers/participants) on either event that we could share internally, it\n would be very helpful. \n\n\n \n\n\nFrom our side, our HQ colleagues are planning a session at the UN Goals House on peace and sustainable development on 26 September. I will be able to share more\n info on it next week.\n\n\n \n\n\nIt would be great to meet on Wednesday in person and exchange in more detail. Would 10:30 suit you? I would be happy to come to the AEF office, and you are welcome\n at the UN House, whichever suits you best.\n\n\n \n\n\nWishing you a lovely weekend,\n\n\n \n\n\nCelia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCelia Keller Martínez\n(she/her) | Senior Partnerships and Communication Officer (OIC) | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | UNOPS |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram, and\nYouTube. \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench or\nSpanish.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Aug 29, 2024 at 4:05 PM Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nBCCing Jerome to spare his inbox\n \nDear Celia,\n \nHope all is well and glad to reconnect,\n \nAs mentioned below, would be great to exchange plans for the upcoming UNGA79 / Summit of the Future -sharing below\na more comprehensive and up-to-date agenda of the Africa-Europe Foundation programming for UNGA79 and the Summit of the Future.\n \nWould be great to discuss with you and hear your thoughts on who you would like to recommend to join us in particular for\nour event to be hosting with\n\nAmref on climate / health / finance on September 24, 5pm at CURE, NY – to discuss the\nNew Collective Quantified Goal (NCQG) on climate finance as the main expected outcome of the 2024 UN Climate Change Conference (UNFCCC COP 29) in Baku and hearing UNOPS leadership on the topic would be timely\n and help elevate the conversation (through the angle of implementation support).\n \nHappy to meet in person next week (for instance Wed morning), if you are in Brussels or hop on a call?\n \nThanks!\nBest\nHoly\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Africa-Europe Foundation (AEF) will convene its cross-continental network of experts on the sidelines of the 79th Session of the UN General Assembly and this year's\n UN Summit of the Future in New York from 21‑25 September. Through a series of events, we will challenge silos on sustainable development, bringing into focus the climate-health nexus and innovative financing to support the implementation of the UN Pact for\n the Future via an Africa-Europe lens.\n\n \n\nKey AEF sessions in New York:\n\n \n\n1. Future, Now!\n\n\nSaturday,\n21 September, 11:00am-12:30pm EST\n\n \n\nAs part of the Africa-Europe Foundation’s Partners Initiative Awards Scheme, Alefa Diaspora is hosting a side event to the UN Summit of the Future Action Days between\n youth and political leaders of OACPS countries on expectations for the UN Summit and the resulting Pact for the Future.\nMore info available soon on their\nsocial channels.\n\n \n\n2. Africa-Europe Women Leaders Network\n\n\nMonday, 23 September, 7:30-9:00am EST,\nPermanent Mission of Ireland to the UN (hybrid, invite-only)\n\n \n\nCo-chaired by Presidents Mary Robinson and Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, the meeting will set the tone for next steps following the UN Summit of the Future, and the critical\n role of multilateral trust and finance to reach global goals. Members will discuss actionable recommendations for advancing a holistic approach to climate and health at the UN Climate Change Conference 2024 (COP29) in November and look ahead to key milestones\n in the 2025 multilateral agenda, from Financing for Development to COP30. \nThe opening panel will be live-streamed on AEF social channels (X\n and LinkedIn).\n\n\n \n\n3. Advancing Political Commitments on Climate and Health Financing: Where is the Global South voice?\n\n\nTuesday, 24 September, 5:00-6:30pm EST, followed by Networking Cocktail, Cure (in-person)\n\n \n\nIn partnership with Amref Health Africa and the Pan African Climate Justice Alliance, the convening will forge an Africa-Europe political and financial climate-health\n roadmap, presenting barriers and their concrete solutions, including to the delivery of a robust New Collective Quantified Goal on climate finance whereby health is fully integrated, and facilitating preliminary discourse and alignments ahead of COP29, while\n looking ahead at COP30. Register for in-person participation\nhere.\n\n \n\n4. From Risk to Resilience: Unlocking Climate Financing for Local Heath Adaptation\n\n\nWednesday, 25 September, 11:30am-12:30pm EST,\nStudio Gather Rockefeller Center (hybrid)\n\n\n \n\nThis strategic dialogue, done in partnership with Foundation S and Foreign Policy, aims to address the impact climate change has on global health and to unlock the financing\n to better address local health adaptation efforts. The event will also welcome the launch of the Collective Minds Climate x Health Council’s Report as a call to action to empower local communities in their adaptation efforts.\nRegister for in-person participation or watch online\n here.\n\n \n\nView the detailed event program\nhere.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHoly Ranaivozanany\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeputy Executive Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n, \n\n\nB‑1000 Brussels\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Holy\n Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, 9 August 2024 17:29\n\nTo: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\nCc: Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>; Celia KELLER MARTINEZ <celiaafricak@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: AEF / UNOPS\n\n\n \nMany thanks Jerome and happy to e-meet you Celia!\nWould be lovely to hop on a call / meet in person end of August / early September and exchange plans for UNGA and beyond,\nSpeak soon and enjoy the summer break!\nBest\nHoly\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHoly Ranaivozanany\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeputy Executive Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n, \n\n\nB‑1000 Brussels\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Jerome\n DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, 9 August 2024 17:22\n\nTo: Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nCc: Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>; Celia KELLER MARTINEZ <celiaafricak@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: AEF / UNOPS\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Holy,\n\n\n\nGreat to hear from you . Many thanks for the kind words and the update below which I'm sharing with my colleagues copied. Seizing this opportunity to introduce you to Celia who will cover my responsibilities until January 2025.\n\n\n\n\nMany thanks for the kind invitation related to your event at UNGA79 / Summit of the Future. Kindly liaise directly with Celia on this as UNOPS will be participating and hosting conversations as well.\n\n\n \n\n\nHappy to join a follow up call as well of course or meet with you and Celia around coffee in the coming weeks as I'm still based in Brussels.\n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nJérôme\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Partner Analytics Team Lead (OIC) | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Aug 9, 2024 at 5:13 PM Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Jerome\n \nHope all is well, long time no speak.\n \nFirst of all, congratulations on your new role! Very well deserved and wishing you all the best!\n \nI wanted to share a\ncouple of updates on our end that may be of interest to you:\n\n-in relation to climate and development, covering Carbon Markets, Adaptation, Agri-food,\n Energy\nRealising\n the full potential of carbon pricing and markets: Opportunities for the Africa-Europe Partnership  \nClimate\n Adaptation and The Reform Of The International Financial Architecture: Strategic Pillars Of The Africa-Europe Partnership\nJoint\n Statement: Fostering Africa-Europe Energy Cooperation (Berlin Energy Transition Dialogue) \nAfrica-Europe\n Policymaker Meeting on African Agri-food Systems 1st ATLAS Roundtable (Paris Peace Forum) \n-our renewed commitment on the climate-health nexus, with the support of our Women Leaders network and statement on clean cooking solutions\n\nhere\n-the recent convening we hosted at the sidelines of the WHA77, demonstrating the cost and return on investment of building climate and\n pandemic-resilient health systems \nhere - and a good recap of latest engagement \nhere.\n \nMonths of work with the climate/ health nexus at the center of it, with upcoming report to be launched at UNGA79 / Summit of the Future\n with Foundation S and partners on how to operationalize the guiding principles for financing climate and health solutions announced during COP28 – registration to join the launch event is available\n\nhere. \n \nAttached our draft agenda for\nUNGA79 / Summit of the Future - flagging as well an invite-only convening we will be hosting with Amref on climate / health / finance on September 24, 5pm – it would be great to have you and UNOPS colleagues join this conversation,\nwith a focus on the New Collective Quantified Goal (NCQG) on climate finance as the main expected outcome of the 2024 UN Climate Change Conference (UNFCCC COP 29) in Baku.\n I attach the concept note for your reference, and official invitation will follow. If there is any specific convening in NY that you are hosting, and that could be of interest, please let me know!\n \nWould be good to have a follow up call in the next weeks to exchange on priorities? Leaving on holidays today, but back end of the month.\n \nThanks a lot, enjoy the summer break and speak soon!\nBest\nHoly\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHoly Ranaivozanany\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeputy Executive Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n, \n\n\nB‑1000 Brussels\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Jerome\n DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, 2 April 2024 15:56\n\nTo: Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n\nCc: Andrea Konstantinidi <andrea.konstantinidi@africaeuropefoundation.org>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: AEF at WHA\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside the organization. Do not click links or open attachments\n unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Holy,\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks again for sharing your programme which I have shared with our colleagues in Geneva. \n\n\n \n\n\nI'm glad to introduce you to my colleague Louise, Head of UNOPS Geneva Liaison Office.\n\n\nShe would be happy to meet with you to discuss further.\n\n\n \n\n\nLeaving it to you to take it from there :)\n\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nJérôme\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Senior Communications and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Mar 28, 2024 at 3:26 PM Holy Ranaivozanany <holy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Jerome\n \nHope all is well,\n \nFollowing up on our conversation yesterday, please see below for now our AEF engagement at WHA  – in collaboration with our close partners.\n \n27 May evening at 18h00 – 20h0 CET (TBC) – Permanent Mission of France: Reception hosted by the French Government focused on\n climate and health. \n28 May morning from 8h00 – 9h30 CET – Crowne Plaza Geneva Hotel: Closed door meeting with Collective Mind Climate Council Members\n and Ministers to gain perspectives and insights for our paper focused on ensuring adaptation funding reaches communities and countries most in need and at risk of the health impacts of climate change.  \n28 May late afternoon from 17h30 – 19h CET – Global Health Campus/Global Fund, Geneva: Joint panel session followed by a reception\n with the co-conveners of the \nGuiding Principles for Financing Climate x Health Solutions\n \nWe are exploring as well the possibility of having a specific dialogue on Return on investment: financing climate and pandemic-resilient health systems, particularly\n as despite the fact the world is facing two existential threats, climate change and pandemics, there is little focus on the financing interventions and mechanisms that can make the most impact on the combination of these issues and the implications for international\n financing of prevention versus neglect need to be better understood. \n \nWe would be happy to discuss further on this with you and your Geneva-based colleague, if there is interest there and hear more about UNOPS programming too, so\n we can explore synergies for collaboration?\n \nMany thanks!\nBest\nHoly\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHoly Ranaivozanany\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeputy Executive Director\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAfrica‑Europe Foundation – Transforming Dialogue into Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nholy.ranaivozanany@africaeuropefoundation.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSquare de Meeûs 5‑6\n\n\n, \n\n\nB‑1000 Brussels",
