                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000FTRiZMAX",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Invitation for Lotte Machon to speak at panel discussion on \"How Sustainable Development Can Foster Lasting Peace\"",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-09-09").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Invitation for Lotte Machon to speak at panel discussion on \"How Sustainable Development Can Foster Lasting Peace\"",
                        Description = "To: marweg@um.dk\nCC: julwin@um.dk; tuewes@um.dk; rikoln@um.dk; naimoh@unops.org; aikaterinis@unops.org; events-secretariat@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Invitation for Lotte Machon to speak at panel discussion on \"How Sustainable Development Can Foster Lasting Peace\"\nBody:\nDear Marie-Louise, \nWe are currently waiting for confirmation from David Miliband and the German State Secretary. We are also in dialogue with the Gates Foundation and IFIs to get attendance from them to the panel debate. \nWe will keep you updated on the confirmed panelists. \nLooking forward to your response once you've looked into it. \nOnce again - thank you in advance for your support. \nBest wishes,Asbjørn\n\nOn Fri, 6 Sept 2024 at 15:42, Marie-Louise Koch Wegter <marweg@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n \nThank you for following up. We will look into this and get back to you. Meanwhile, please keep us updated on other panelists\n😊\n \nEnjoy your weekend\n \nMarie-Louise\n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 06 September 2024 12:50\n\nTo: Marie-Louise Koch Wegter <marweg@um.dk>\n\nCc: Lotte Machon <lotmac@um.dk>; Julia Winding <julwin@um.dk>; Tue Kristoffer Westhoff <tuewes@um.dk>; Rikke Enggaard Olsen <rikoln@um.dk>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Aikaterini SERETI <aikaterinis@unops.org>; Events Secretariat UNOPS <events-secretariat@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Invitation for Lotte Machon to speak at panel discussion on \"How Sustainable Development Can Foster Lasting Peace\"\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nHi Marie-Louise\nFollowing up to our brief exchange yesterday regarding the upcoming event that UNOPS is organizing at\nGoals House\n in Central\n Park on Thursday, 26th September.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe event will focus on the connection between sustainable development and lasting peace, a topic that I think could resonate deeply with current global priorities\n - not least Danish.\n\n\n\n\n\nGiven Denmark’s leadership in these areas, our close collaboration and common aim of increasing awareness of the UN agency headquartered in Copenhagen,\nwe would be honored to have State Secretary Lotte Machon speak at our panel discussion and share her insights. Do you think that it might be possible to fit into her calendar?\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe panel will be moderated by\nMr.\n Simon Mundy of the Financial Times, and hosted by Jorge alongside other prominent figures. \n \nPlease find additional details about the event below. Should we have the honor of welcoming Lotte, our excellent events team (cc) will ensure a comprehensive briefing and preparatory\n call are arranged ahead of the event.\n \nThank you very much for considering this!\n \nBest,\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTitle: Missing Peace: How Sustainable Development Can Foster Lasting Peace\nDate:\nThursday 26th\n September\n\nTime: 10.30am – 12.00pm\nVenue:\nTavern on the Green in Central Park, New York\n \nFrom Ukraine to Gaza and Sudan to Mozambique, violent conflict is rife and having far-reaching impacts across the world.\n \nBeyond the immense human suffering caused by conflict, war reverses progress on human development and creates challenges often felt most by already vulnerable\n populations. From food insecurity and disease, to environmental damage and inequality, conflict undermines the foundations of a just and prosperous society.\n \nJoin\nUN Under-Secretary-General and UNOPS Executive Director, \nJorge Moreira da Silva, and partners for a panel discussion on the necessary foundations for lasting peace. The panel will share ideas and experiences on how to respond, recover, and rebuild from conflict and develop long-term sustainable solutions for\n communities around the world. Moderated by Simon Mundy, Moral Money Editor,\nFinancial Times.\n \n \n\n\nBackground & context \n\nIn 2022, more people lost their lives as a result of conflicts than at any time over the preceding 28 years. In the same year, military expenditures globally\n reached a new record of $2.24tn.\n \nPeace is needed across the globe, from Gaza, Ukraine, the Sahel, Sudan, Libya, the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), Yemen, Myanmar, and Haiti. When\n emergencies happen, we must respond, recover and rebuild., from dispatching first responders to coordinating reconstruction. At the same time, we must forge long-term solutions that enable access to essential services, build resilience against future\n shocks, and contribute to a more sustainable future.\n\n \n“In a world facing rising conflict and complex crises, UNOPS works to respond to immediate needs, while laying the foundations for a more sustainable and\n resilient future. Agility, preparedness and resilience are the heart of our humanitarian, development and peace efforts.” \nJorge Moreira da Silva - UNOPS Executive Director\n \n*UNOPS vision is a world where people can live full lives supported by sustainable, resilient and inclusive infrastructure and by the efficient, transparent\n use of public resources in procurement and project management. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head\n of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in\nEnglish,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
