                new (
                    "00TQx00000HUbTPMA1",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: UNOPS SFA Templates",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-10-29").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: UNOPS SFA Templates",
                        Description = "To: alistairs@unops.org; mfikre@worldbank.org; akircher1@worldbank.org\nCC: christinebo@unops.org; elizabethdu@unops.org; vineshw@unops.org; SvenE@unops.org; sofiateresama@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS SFA Templates\nBody:\nHi Alistair,\n \nApologies that I have not been able to respond to the different inputs/comments we have received from different various partners.  I can assure you that this input from Sofia\n has been incorporated into Annex III of the SFA – in the part under Final Financial Statement as a specific bracketed comment for UNOPS.\n \n\nbest, Rajeev\n \n\n\n\n\nRajeev K. Swami\n\n\n\n\nLead Specialist\nOperations Policy & Country Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nT\n\n\n+1 (202) 458-9610\n\n\n\n\nE\n\n\nrswami@worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\nW\n\n\nwww.worldbank.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nrajeevkswami\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, October 29, 2024 8:09 AM\n\nTo: Rajeev K. Swami <rswami@worldbank.org>; Million Fikre <mfikre@worldbank.org>; Andrew C. Kircher <akircher1@worldbank.org>\n\nCc: Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>; Elizabeth DUBY <elizabethdu@unops.org>; Vinesh WINODAN <vineshw@unops.org>; Sven ECKERT <SvenE@unops.org>; sofiateresama@unops.org\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS SFA Templates\n\n\n \n[External]\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Rajeev, Andy and Million,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope you are well. I am writing to follow up on the below, to gauge the Bank’s reaction to the text, and to request updated SFA language for consideration more broadly. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks,\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Oct 10, 2024 at 12:03 PM Sofia Teresa MELENDEZ APARICIO <sofiateresama@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Rajeev, \n\n \n\n\nI hope you are well. As agreed during the meeting, please find here the text proposed by UNOPS for the SFA related to hedging:\n\n\n \n\n\n \"If applicable UNOPS and the government agree to hedge the financial risk of non-usd currency exposure (including from SDR). Any hedging adjustments will be included in the overall revenue reported in the financial statement.\" \n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you, and thank you again for today's productive meeting.\n\n\n \n\n\nkind regards,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSofia Melendez\n| Project Finance Specialist | Finance Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark |\nwww.unops.org \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench or\nSpanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Oct 9, 2024 at 5:23 PM Alistair Peter SOMERVILLE <alistairs@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Rajeev, \n\n \n\n\nThanks for the conversation this morning. Please find attached as requested the Word Doc versions of the marked-up SFAs for your review. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe look forward to the meeting tomorrow, which, as of now, looks like it will work well for our Copenhagen colleagues too.\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for the coordination on this.\n\n\n \n\n\nAlistair \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\n\nFrom: Elizabeth DUBY <elizabethdu@unops.org>\n\nDate: Mon, Oct 7, 2024 at 12:21 PM\n\nSubject: UNOPS SFA Templates\n\nTo: Christine BOWERS <christinebo@unops.org>, Rajeev K. Swami <rswami@worldbank.org>, Andrew C. Kircher <akircher1@worldbank.org>,\n Sofia Teresa MELENDEZ APARICIO <sofiateresama@unops.org>, Sven ECKERT <svene@unops.org>\n\n \n\n\nDear Rajeev, \n\n\n \n\n\nI am pleased to share with you UNOPS' complete comments on the SFA templates for your consideration.  We would greatly appreciate the opportunity to schedule a meeting date, with the aim of concluding the process by November 1.  We have\n taken into account the extensive consultations you have already conducted with UNICEF and have tailored our comments accordingly, focusing on key priorities for UNOPS while seeking to minimize unnecessary adjustments. \n\n\n \n\n\nIn preparation for our upcoming discussions, I would like to highlight a few important agenda points and note that you will find these linked to comments in the template documents shared with you in this email: \n\n\n \n\n\n1. Final Financial Reporting timeline for Output SFA, UNOPS requires 6 months after “UNOPS implementation end date” for issuance of the Final Financial Statement (FFS), which\n in SFA terms means 6 months prior completion date.\n\n\n2. Commitments/Liabilities, Output SFA, General conditions, Article 13. To reinstate the sentence that UNOPS \"shall not be required to assume any liability in excess of such\n payments”. In order to be compliant with UNOPS policy that requires to receive the funds before entering into a commitment. \n\n\n3. Accountability of previous advances must include expenses and commitments. UNOPS takes into account expenses and commitments to determine the project cash balance. Therefore, UNOPS\n would like to ensure that the same understanding is reflected in the conditions for disbursements (Annex II, II. payment schedule).\n\n\n \n\n\nI look forward to scheduling a meeting date at your earliest convenience and to working together towards a mutually satisfactory outcome. \n\n\n \n\n\n\nOutputs SFA Template with UNOPS Comments\n\n\nTA SFA Template UNOPS Comments\n\n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\nElizabeth \n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\nElizabeth Duby | Legal Advisor\n and Commercial Team Lead (Americas) | Legal Group | HQ |\n Washington D.C. | Mob: +1 (202) 391-2817  | IPAS\n Solution Portal  | www.unops.org |\n \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe\n to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\nElizabeth Duby | Legal Advisor | IPAS | HQ | Copenhagen | Mob:\n +45 30177661  | IPAS\n Solution Portal  | www.unops.org |\n \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe\n to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish",
