                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000HynLxMAJ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-11-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project",
                        Description = "To: sungud@um.dk\nCC: vaszal@um.dk; markup@um.dk; tinlun@um.dk; sahadn@um.dk; annkah@um.dk; asbjornb@unops.org; simonp@unops.org; valentynp@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; marysiaz@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\nBody:\nDear Sune,\nWith apologies, please use the enclosed version of the draft agreement and disregard the one attached to my previous email.\nWith best regards,Elene\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2024 at 2:20 PM Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Sune,\nMany thanks for your detailed review and the readiness to proceed with the project from December onwards - subject to the completion of the proposal and the agreement of course.\nOn the proposal: We have so far not extended the scope of works. We still anticipate the major findings from the engineers to be reflected in the needs assessment report, which will follow the launch of the project and will form a basis for the exact scope. Based on the latest trip though, we tentatively estimate that the existing funds will not suffice to cover all anticipated works, hence we would be cautious to add new sites to the project at this stage.\nOn the specific emergency shelters, our engineers have concluded that:City Children Hospital No. 2 - the shelter repair works are at the final stage already, funding is provided by the city authorities and other donors.City Hospital No. 4 - the shelter repair works are in progress, works are finished in more than one-third of the premises.City Hospital No. 3 - anti radiation shelter needs structural construction works and water insulation works the cost of which is beyond the budget.In view of this, we would suggest to perhaps consider the inclusion of the anti-radiation shelter for the Hospital No.3 at a later stage as a further amendment to the project, if additional funds will be available, but refrain from the expansion of the scope for now, but let us know if this approach makes sense.\nIn the draft agreement, we have updated the text as per your comments, added the detailed budget  and the references to respective percentages. We also corrected some detected errors in the draft agreement and streamlined it to better reflect the distinction between the 2 projects. \nI hope these changes respond to your comments and make sense. \nLooking forward to your feedback.\nWith many thanks and kind regards,Elene\n\nOn Thu, Nov 7, 2024 at 6:05 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nThanks again for sharing the draft proposal and the draft agreement. Herewith some comments as we prepare to move ahead – I hope you\n are in agreement: \n \n\n\n1 December 2024 as the date of commencement of the contract should be fine contingent, however, on the finalization of the proposal and draft agreement.\n\n \nRegarding the proposal:\n\n\nHas this been revised since the site visits of the engineers last week? If not, it would be good to enclose with it any relevant findings that the engineers made during\n their visits. \nI note in the proposal that for the following sites, City Hospital no. 4; City Child Hospital no. 2 and; City Hospital no. 3, emergency shelters are not included in the\n planned repairs. Could you kindly include in the proposal confirmation that approved emergency shelters in these locations are already in place and functioning so that to ensure that upon completion of the planned repairs the hospitals will be operational?\n \nRegarding the draft agreement:\n\n\nI would like to include the reporting schedule, similar to the previous agreements with the following text:\n\n \nUNOPS shall provide the Funding Source an interim narrative report, interim financial statement, a final narrative report and a\n final project specific audited financial statement prepared in USD and in accordance with UNOPS’ standard requirements and formats\n\n\n\nThe interim narrative reports will be provided on a quarterly basis within two weeks of the end date of the quarter.\n\nThe interim financial statements will be provided on a quarterly basis within one month of the end date of the quarter.\nAn annual certified financial statement as of 31 December every year to be submitted no later than the 31 July the following year.\n\nA certified financial statement is to be submitted within six months of the Project end date.\nThe final project specific audited financial statement is to be submitted no later than 30 September 2025.\n\n\n \nAmend Annex 1 – the funding source shall transfer Funds as per the following schedule:\n \n\n\nDKK 25,000,000 will be transferred in two tranches with DKK 13,000,000 no later than the 31st of December 2024, and DKK 12,000,000 no later than the 31st\n of July 2025.\n \nAppendix 2:\n\n\n\nCould you kindly include details on the budget for the personnel part?\n\n\nCould you please create an additional column that indicates the percentage of the budget for each of the subtotal lines.\n\n \nKind regards,\nSune\n \n_______________________________________________________\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\nCHIEF ADVISOR\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n \nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n \n\nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message\n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 05 November 2024 13:12\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>; Mariia\n Kupris <markup@um.dk>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune, \n\n \n\n\nI hope your travels to Mykolaiv went well.\n\nI wanted to check in and see if you had a chance to look at the amendment to the Agreement and Proposal on Health support. If possible, it would be helpful to have more clarity on the timing of\n the signing and launch of the project.\n\n\n \n\n\nI'd be happy to discuss any questions you may have.\n\n\n \n\n\nWith thanks and kind regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Oct 28, 2024 at 5:47 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nGreetings from Mykolaiv and thank you for sharing the updated proposal and amended contract. Please\n let me have a close look at both documents with my colleagues and then revert to you shortly.\n\n \nAll the best\nSune\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n \n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\n\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 28 October 2024 15:30\n\nTo: Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>;\n Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>;\n Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>\n\nSubject: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Anne and Sune,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe are happy that the Danish Government is proceeding with the Mykolaiv health project which will be a truly important contribution to the health sector in Mykolaiv region and wider\n Ukraine. To this end, let me share with you the draft Amendment to the Agreement related to the implementation of the UNOPS project on \"Strengthening Health Systems in Mykolaiv, Ukraine\".\n\n\n \n\n\nAs you know, the implementation of this project is closely linked to the project covering procurement services as funded by the Novo Nordisk A/S and both projects need to be synchronized\n to deliver on time. Therefore, I wanted to inquire if you could already confirm the anticipated start date for this project. In the enclosed amendment, I tentatively estimated that the project would be launched on 1st of December, 2024 and would thus last\n until 31st of March 2027, which encompasses a 16 months implementation period with an additional 12 months for the Defects Notification Period. If this is feasible, we would indicate 1st of April, 2025 (4 months following the launch of the health infrastructure\n project) as a start date for the NN health procurement project respectively.\n\n\n \n\n\nLet us know if you have any questions or comments on the project or amendment to the agreement and of course we'd be happy to discuss any outstanding issues with you, if need be.\n\n\n \n\n\nWith thanks and best regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nElene Agladze\n| Partnerships Specialist | UNOPS Ukraine Multi-Country Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel: +380 956 001880 | Mob: +380 956 001880\nWhatsapp: +380 95600 1880 Viber: +995 499 034408\nwww.unops.org \n \nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000HynLxMAJ",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "sungud@um.dk", "vaszal@um.dk", "tinlun@um.dk", "arunn@unops.org", "markup@um.dk", "marysiaz@unops.org", "valentynp@unops.org", "simonp@unops.org", "eleneag@unops.org", "annkah@um.dk", "asbjornb@unops.org", "sahadn@um.dk" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
