                new (
                    "00TQx00000I50d6MAB",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Azerbaijan - introductions",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-11-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Azerbaijan - introductions",
                        Description = "To: timl@unops.org; harmancih@who.int\nCC: FreyaVG@unops.org; sophiedj@unops.org; elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Azerbaijan - introductions\nBody:\nDear Hande \nIt was great to speak with you yesterday and thanks for taking the time - you must be beyond busy in Baku!!\nAs promised, please find here our Health capacity statement, that explains the implementation support we provide to our partners across various health areas, all aligned with the objectives set out in GPW 14 (we even feature in para 18 ;)  \nOur mandate is infrastructure, procurement and project management where we deliver around USD 3 billion per year in around 100 countries - over a third of which is focused in the health sector. As you rightly mentioned, UNOPS has provided limited support in Azerbaijan, primarily for TB drug procurement (we also host Stop TB and AT Scale that AZE govt contributes to). \nWith this email, please also e-meet my UNOPS colleagues, Tim Lardner, the Regional Director for Europe and Central Asia, Freya von Groote Director of the Vienna multi-country office (Azerbaijan falls under her portfolio) and Sophie Djugeli, regional partnerships specialist.\nDear Tim\nPlease meet Hande Harmanci, the WHO Representative in Azerbaijan. During COP29, Hande will spend most of her time at the WHO Pavilion and I have flagged our Friday 9am \"Energising healthcare\" session to her which she said she will try to attend. Jorge met DG Tedros in Copenhagen last week at the European Regional Committee meeting, they discussed our collaboration specifically around solarisation of health facilities, working in fragile settings, health procurement and access to oxygen infrastructure. I understand Jorge is also meeting MOH AZE in Baku.\nI hope you will be able to meet and discuss potential synergies!\nAll best wishesLouise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000I50d6MAB",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "freyavg@unops.org", "elenali@unops.org", "harmancih@who.int", "sophiedj@unops.org", "timl@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
