                new (
                    "00TQx00000ILTEXMA5",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Sudan operational support - Geneva partners",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-11-20").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Sudan operational support - Geneva partners",
                        Description = "To: munierm@unops.org\nCC: elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Sudan operational support - Geneva partners\nBody:\nDear Munier\nHope all is well with you - I had a good chat with Shible Sahbani this morning and was very happy to hear you are already well connected with him !!\nAs an ex WHO staff myself of 20 years, I do like to ensure all my UNOPS colleagues are well connected with WHO colleagues and can engage with them usefully (there is a lot of jargon in global public health! ;)   Dr Tedros (WHO DG) met with Jorge 2 weeks ago in Copenhagen, and they discussed our collaboration in health infrastructure, oxygen and emergencies... good timing :) - and I hear Jorge is coming your way soon :) \nI was happy to hear there seems to be quite a lot of health infrastructure being prioritised, with UNOPS potentially being considered for the rehabilitation of 10 secondary level hospitals (with the primary health hospital infrastructure going to UNICEF)\nShible also mentioned Medical Oxygen support is desperately needed - we have implemented a number of excellent projects in Zambia and Bangladesh, financed by the Global Fund. I have reached out to the Fund Portfolio Manager for Sudan, and will revert to you when he responds. \nI also understand WHO wishes to convert its temporary contract holders (SSAs) potentially to ICAs. We already have a global agreement with WHO on HR, so this should be easy to do @Lorraine ANABTAWI  manages this Agreement.\nShible also mentioned an interest in our Access to health model in Myanmar, the multi donor fund, managed by UNOPS with a consortium of NGOS delivering basic health services in non-state controlled areas. Happy to discuss this further with you / support if I can.\nLooking forward to hearing from you in due course - perhaps time for a quick catch up ?!\nWarmest greetings from GenevaBest wishes Louise \nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Sun, 21 Jan 2024 at 06:43, Munier Gaafar Mohammed <munierm@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Louise\nGood morning, yes still running a very slim structure here in Sudan, hope the situation will change soon and enable us to expand and have other team members. Indeed a catch-up with you will be very helpful and will support the discussion with GAVI, let me know when suitable for you.\nBest Regards,\n\nMunier Gaafar Mohammed (Mr) | Country Manager |  \nSudan | Ethiopia Multi-Country Office | Port Sudan, Sudan | Mobile:  +249 \n(0) 9 121 30005 I Email: munierm@unops.org | Skype: munier2000 | www.unops.org  \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\n\nOn Thu, Jan 18, 2024 at 5:42 PM Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nAh, my bad, I just saw Petronella is new Manager for SOUTH Sudan - please ignore this suggestion (unless useful !!)Looking forward to speaking with you about GAVI and SUDAN!\nBest wishes Louise \n\nOn Thu, 18 Jan 2024 at 16:39, Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nHi MunierHope all is well with you?  Please let me know if you would like to meet before you meet with Anne Cronin from Gavi?  Also happy to see Petronella has joined to hopefully lessen your workload!  Perhaps she will join us?Looking forward to hearing from you soon!Best wishes Louise\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\nOn Wed, 17 Jan 2024 at 07:43, Munier Gaafar Mohammed <munierm@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Anne\nGood morning, next week is fine for me, looking forward to catching up with you on 24th January, lete know what time is convenient for you.\nHave a safe trip back home.\nBest Regards \nOn Tue, Jan 16, 2024, 20:31 Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Munier, \n\n\n\nThank you for the message, I will be departing Port Sudan on the flight you are arriving on. \nUnfortunately, my computer is not working, so a virtual meeting tomorrow is difficult.\n\n\n\nPerhaps we schedule a virtual call next week when I am back in Geneva. Would next Wednesday 24 Jan be a suitable day? \n\n\n\nI look forward to catching up.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nAnne for \n\n\n\n\n\n\nSent from Outlook for iOS\n\nFrom: Munier Gaafar Mohammed <munierm@unops.org>\n\nSent: Tuesday, January 16, 2024 7:25:14 PM\n\nTo: Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Rita Kaali <rkaali@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Sudan operational support\n \n\n\n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\nDear Anne\n\n\n\nGood evening and thank you for your email, I'm travelling back to Port Sudan, my flight will arrive Port Sudan on 18th January @12:30 afternoon, we can meet anytime late afternoon, alternatively on 17th we can catch-up virtually, anytime late\n afternoon.\n\n\n\nBest Regards\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Thu, Jan 11, 2024, 15:49 Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Munier, \n \nI am visiting Port Sudan next week; would you have availability on 17 Jan to meet?\n \nKind regards, \n \nAnne \n \n\n\nFrom: Munier Gaafar Mohammed <munierm@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, January 11, 2024 12:48 PM\n\nTo: Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org>\n\nCc: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Rita Kaali <rkaali@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Sudan operational support\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Anne \n\n \n\n\nGoing afternoon and looking forward to meeting you FTF or virtual, anytime.let me know when suitable for you.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards\n\n\nMunier\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Jan 11, 2024, 13:44 Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise, \n \nThank you for the introduction. \n \nDear Munir, \nRita and I look forward to meeting you in early February following my return from mission to Port Sudan. Happy to schedule the meeting FTF or virtually.\n\n \nWarm regards, \n \nAnne \n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, January 11, 2024 12:41 PM\n\nTo: Munier Gaafar Mohammed <munierm@unops.org>; Anne Cronin <acronin@gavi.org>\n\nSubject: Sudan operational support\n\n\n \n\nCAUTION : This email originated from outside of Gavi. Please do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\n\nDear Anne, \n\n\nPlease e-meet my colleague Munier, our Country Manager in Sudan. Munier oversees all our in-country operations, implementing projects that focus on conflict resolution, emergency\n relief, WASH and Health - expanding quality health care delivery in Kassala Health Citadel (total USD 28 million partner projects delivered since 2022).  He will be back in country after 15th January and very happy to meet with you to see if UNOPS can support\n Gavi with your mandate to e.g. expand your implementation capacity for vaccination coverage / health system strengthening.\n\n\n \n\n\nDear Munier\n\n\nPlease e-meet Anne, a dear previous colleague of mine, from Gavi, the Vaccine Alliance.  Anne is the Country Manager for Sudan and oversees the portfolio of Gavi investments\n to expand vaccination coverage and strengthen the health system, with a focus on reaching every child with life saving vaccines.\n\n\n \n\n\nI do hope you will be able to meet, and remain at your disposal for further conversation / support!\n\n\n \n\n\nWith thanks and best wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
