                new (
                    "00TQx00000IpKgtMAF",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-12-03").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: workneshg@unops.org\nCC: ekaterinapo@unops.org; sonjav@unops.org; mariacarmenco@unops.org; basazinewt@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS\nBody:\nGood Worknesh.I will take the discussion with the legal team and check with the Italians.\nCheers,\nMartín Arévalo de León | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 | www.unops.org Manténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \n\nOn Tue, Dec 3, 2024 at 12:23 PM Worknesh Mekonnen GONET <workneshg@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Martin,\nYes we have seen this. It was the position from them that our legal team insisted that it is only for five years and the agreement will not be valid until reviewed otherwise we should use the system based calculation which is 7%.  \nWhat I was expecting is that you take the discussion with the legal colleagues based on their argument below.   We are lost at this stage on how to go forward.\nRegards,\n\n \n\nWorknesh Mekonnen | Director, Multi Country Office (MCO) (Ethiopia, Sudan, South Sudan, Djibouti) and Representative to the AU  | Addis Ababa, Ethiopia | Tel:\n+251 115 181960 | EXT: 1960 | Mobile: +251 911512306 |\nSkype: worknesh.mekonnen2 | www.unops.org  \n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow\nus on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, \n\nYouTube\nSubscribe\nto our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\n\nOn Tue, Dec 3, 2024 at 2:06 PM Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\nDear all:\nI sent a message only to Franesco Ceravolo asking him if they had a reaction to the email previously sent.I got this answer and asked to see him personally on Thursday.Glado to talk to you all to discuss position and next steps.\nCheers,\nMartín Arévalo de León | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 | www.unops.org Manténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it>\nDate: Mon, Dec 2, 2024 at 4:28 PM\nSubject: R: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS\nTo: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\n \nSorry for the late reply and thank you for your below email regarding the validity and application of the MoU between UNOPS and the\n Government of the Italian Republic.\n \nWe have carefully reviewed the situation and wish to provide the following clarification.\n \nIn accordance with\nArticle XII of the MoU, titled “Entry into Force, Amendments, and Duration,” the MoU states: \"The MoU shall remain into force until the Parties agree, upon consultation, to terminate its validity or either Party provides a two months prior written\n notice to that end.\"\n \nWe interpret this provision to mean that the MoU remains valid in the absence of explicit notice of termination from either party. While\nArticle VI refers to an initial five-year period for proposed cooperation, we believe that it does not override the broader provisions of Article XII, which explicitly govern the MoU’s duration and termination.\n \nFurthermore, we note the following points:\n\nContinued Reference in Recent Arrangements:\n Between November 2023 and today, three Arrangements were signed for projects implemented in Ethiopia, Sudan, and Tunisia. These arrangements either directly reference the MoU in their preambles or annexes, further supporting its continued applicability. Notably,\n the Arrangements included indirect costs set at 6%, aligning with the practice consistently followed under the MoU framework.Consistency of Practice:\n UNOPS itself has continued to adhere to the terms of the MoU in its operations. This consistency strengthens the position that the MoU’s provisions have remained applicable.Cost Considerations:\n For ongoing and future Arrangements, we propose maintaining indirect costs at 6%, as this aligns with established practices and will facilitate timely approval of pending projects. In fact we are in the process of formalizing one Arrangement in Ethiopia and\n one in Burkina Faso.\n \nFinally, we wish to make a small but important clarification. While the\nDirectorate General for Development Cooperation (DGCS) under the Ministry of Foreign Affairs is the actual donor for projects implemented by UN agencies, the\nItalian Agency for Development Cooperation (AICS) serves as the operational arm of Italian development cooperation with offices in various countries. As such, negotiations are conducted directly with DGCS, though AICS plays a key role in liaison, coordination\n and monitoring during project implementation.\n \nWe hope this clarifies our position and underscores the mutual commitment to ensuring smooth collaboration. Please let us know if further\n discussions or clarifications are needed.\n \nKind regards,\nFrancesco\n \n \n\nDa: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nInviato: lunedì 2 dicembre 2024 16:05\n\nA: Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it>\n\nOggetto: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\nMITTENTE ESTERNO. Prestare attenzione nell'apertura di eventuali link e/o allegati.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nDear Francesco,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope my message finds you well.\n\n\nI wanted to know if we could talk about this project and the consideration of your department.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nManténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Nov 15, 2024 at 11:53 AM Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Francesco, we have been checking this matter with our Legal Department. Let me share their response on the issue with you.\n\n\n \n\n\n\"UNOPS has been queried by its country Office in Ethiopia on the validity of the attached Memorandum of Understanding between the United Nations Office for Project\n Services (UNOPS) and The Government of The Italian Republic executed on 5 April 2018 (the “MoU”) and its application in relation to the Project in Ethiopia “Construction of primary schools in Gazanche primary school and Ambo Secondary school. For the right\n to education in Gurage and West Shewa Zones. ”\n \nArticle VI of the MoU sets out that “the proposed cooperation under this MoU shall have an initial duration of five years from its entry into force, unless terminated\n earlier by either Party upon two months’ notice in writing to the other party. The Parties may agree to extend this MoU in writing for subsequent periods. ” In the absence of the provision on the automatic MoU renewal,  to the best of our knowledge, the\n MoU has not been extended. Additionally, it is to be noted that Article XII refers to the cases of termination only, as opposed to the expiration of the term and therefore, does not deem to apply. \n \nIt is also understood that the MoU’s expiration was a subject of discussion in 2022 during the exercise of the renewal of the project arrangement template, however,\n the MoU has not been renewed. \n \nIn view of the above-mentioned, UNOPS considers the MoU to be expired and not applicable to the ongoing projects between the AICS  and UNOPS. UNOPS has applied this\n practice consistently for the last year, and it has been accepted by the AICS in the past. \n \nIt would be highly appreciated if the above information on the expiration of the MoU could be shared with AICS field offices to avoid any further misunderstanding\n and operational delays. \n \nWe trust your understanding of the above, and stand ready to provide any additional information on the above.\"\n \n\n\nYou may see there is a technical and definitive legal issue here, and a previous application of other formats, accepted by AICS since the expiration of the MoU.\n\n\n \n\n\nI understand that there is a Template Discussion between UNOPS and AICS, stalled for some time, but we are eager to retake the talks.\n\n\n \n\n\nI remain at your disposal.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nManténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Nov 13, 2024 at 3:14 PM Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Francesco:\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for your message and your comments.\n\n\nLet me check with our Legal Department on their stand and I will get back to you as soon as possible.\n\n\n \n\n\nCheers,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nManténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2024 at 3:53 PM Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\n \nthank you for your feedback. I understand that the MoU between Italy and UNOPS is still\n valid, so we would propose to revert to the previous version of the Arrangement with regard to the fee calculation and to keep the 6% fee rate.\n \nMay I kindly ask you to confirm the above?\n\n \nI look forward to your response.\n \nKind regards,\nFrancesco\n\n \nDa: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nInviato: giovedì 7 novembre 2024 16:16\n\nA: Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it>\n\nCc: Genzano Donatella <donatella.genzano@esteri.it>; Worknesh Mekonnen GONET <WorkneshG@unops.org>; Sonja VARGA <sonjav@unops.org>\n\nOggetto: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS\n \n \n\n\n\n\nMITTENTE ESTERNO. Prestare attenzione nell'apertura di eventuali link e/o allegati.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nDear Franesco,\n\n\n \n\n\nYou will find hereto attached the new version of the document and budget for your consideration.\n\n\n \n\n\nAs you may notice the total budget remains the same.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 |\nwww.unops.org \nManténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Nov 7, 2024 at 3:06 PM Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\n \nMay I kindly ask you to send me the new version of the budget document?\n \nMany thanks, best\nFrancesco\n \nDa: Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it>\n\n\nInviato: mercoledì 23 ottobre 2024 20:20\n\nA: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\nCc: Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Genzano Donatella <donatella.genzano@esteri.it>; Worknesh Mekonnen GONET\n <WorkneshG@unops.org>; Sonja VARGA <sonjav@unops.org>\n\nOggetto: Re: AID 013062 – Etiopia - Per il diritto all'educazione delle zone Gurage e West Shewa – UNOPS\n \n\nDear Martin,\n\n \n\n\nthank you for the update, really appreciated. Looking forward to receiving the new budget, in order to finalize our internal procedures for the signing of the Arrangement.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest\n\n\nFrancesco\n\n\n\n\n---\n\nInviato da Workspace ONE Boxer\n\n\nIl 22 ottobre 2024 alle ore 11:15:31 CEST, Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> ha scritto:\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMITTENTE ESTERNO. Prestare attenzione nell'apertura di eventuali link e/o allegati.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nGentile Dottor Ceravolo:\n\n\n \n\n\nI'm writing regarding your message sent on 11th October past.\n\n\nThe team has conducted today a meeting with the AICS focal point (Chiara Biffi), and have agreed on some changes regarding the distribution of budget, not its agreed amount.\n\n\nAs soon as I receive the document with their comments I will forward it to you.\n\n\n \n\n\nCheers,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Representative and Head | Cel +502 3024-0126 |\nwww.unops.org \nManténgase al día con UNOPS. Síganos en\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Oct 11, 2024 at 11:47 AM Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\nCarissimo Francesco \n\n\n \n\n\nGrazie de messaggio.\n\n\n \n\n\nI am switching into English to include my colleagues of the Ethiopia office so that they review the arrangements.\n\n\n \n\n\nBy the same occasion please note that UNOPS has recently opened an office in Rome and my colleague Martin ARÉVALO is now in charge of the Rome Liaison Office. Please refer to him\n for any future communications.\n\n\n \n\n\nGrazie e buona giornata\n\n\nCarmen\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMariacarmen Colitti | Head of Office and Representative | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Brussels, Belgium | Tel: + 32 2 7881840|\nwww.unops.org \n\n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nLe ven. 11 oct. 2024 à 11:35, Ceravolo Francesco <francesco.ceravolo@esteri.it> a écrit :\n\n\n\n\n\nCara Carmen,\n \nspero che questa mia ti trovi bene.\n \nA seguito dell’approvazione dell’iniziativa in oggetto da parte del Comitato Congiunto del 30 settembre scorso, ti scrivo dall’Ufficio Africa della DGCS per sottoporti il testo dell’Arrangement (con i relativi annessi) recante due proposte\n di modifica in TC rispetto alla versione che abbiamo ricevuto da Addis Abeba.\n \nSe concordate con queste modifiche, procediamo a chiedere l’autorizzazione alla firma dell’Arrangement.\n \nGrazie mille per quanto potrai farci sapere.\n \nBuon fine settimana\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrancesco Ceravolo\nSegretario di Legazione\nDirezione Generale per la Cooperazione allo Sviluppo\nUfficio IV – Politiche di cooperazione allo sviluppo in Africa\n \nMinistero degli Affari Esteri\ne della Cooperazione Internazionale\nPiazzale\n della Farnesina, 1 – 00135 Roma\nwww.esteri.it\n \nT +39 06.3691.3702",
