                new (
                    "00TQx00000JIaILMA1",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Fwd: New report: Infrastructure for climate action",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2021-11-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: New report: Infrastructure for climate action",
                        Description = "To: scottt@unops.org\nCC: dorothyl@unops.org; samanthas@unops.org; LaetitiaK@unops.org; mariacarmenco@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: New report: Infrastructure for climate action\nBody:\nDear Scott,\nI'm happy to inform you that Nov 26th is confirmed for the presentation of the report.\nMs Elena Visnar, Head of Unit Climate Adaptation of DG CLIMA, has kindly agreed to co-host the event and will provide an introduction statement.\nWe'll circulate the invitation with the login details next week (platform: Webex hosted by the EU). It's an invitation only event, so pls let me know if you have suggestions of UNOPS colleagues that would be interested in attending the session.\nPls see below the draft agenda:Welcoming remarks by Mariacarmen Colitti (UNOPS, Head of Brussels Liaison Office and Representative) - 2 minIntroduction by Veronika Sfrankova (UNEP, Head of Brussels Office) - 3 minIntroduction statement by Elena Visnar (Head of Unit Climate Adaptation of DG CLIMA) - 5 minMariacarmen introduces the speakers (1 min)Presentation by Scott Thacker (UNOPS Infrastructure Specialist and Honorary Research Associate of the Environmental Change Institute, University of Oxford). - 15 minPresentation by Rowan Palmer (UNEP Lead Sustainable Infrastructure Investment Team) - 8 minQ/A - Moderation by Mariacarmen - 25 minConclusion - 2 min (tbc)Pls let me know if you have any questions.\nKind regards,JérômeJérôme de Thysebaert | Senior Communications Officer and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 | www.unops.orgKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: AHLGREN Christofer <Christofer.AHLGREN@ec.europa.eu>\nDate: Fri, Nov 12, 2021 at 1:46 PM\nSubject: RE: New report: Infrastructure for climate action\nTo: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>, FANTASIA Anais <Anais.FANTASIA@ec.europa.eu>\nCc: Monika Oczkowska <monika.oczkowska@un.org>, CLIMA-A03-ARES@ec.europa.eu <CLIMA-A03-ARES@ec.europa.eu>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Jerome (cc Monika and Anaïs)\n \nThank you for your email about the meeting on 26th November. I think your proposed agenda looks good, and I think the 3-5min\n allocation to Elena is perfect. If you want her to connect more to the EU Adaptation Strategy, then perhaps best to reserve 5 minutes.\n\n \nOn the technical side, yes, we should be able to host the meeting with our unit’s WebEx account. I’ve copied in Elena’s Secretary Anaïs\n FANTASIA that can help you set up the web-ex link once you have sent out the calendar invitation.\n\n \n@Anaïs,\n could you please send a photo and short bio of Elena to Jerome? And then help him set up the WebEx link for this meeting? Molte grazie!\n \nKind regards,\n\nChristofer\n\n \nChristofer Ahlgren\nPolicy Officer\n \nEuropean Commission\nDirectorate-General for Climate Action\nCLIMA.A3 – Adaptation to Climate Change\nAvenue de Beaulieu 31, Bruxelles, Office 06/47\nTelephone: +32 2 29 82506\n\n \nFrom: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, November 12, 2021 12:20 PM\n\nTo: AHLGREN Christofer (CLIMA) <Christofer.AHLGREN@ec.europa.eu>\n\nCc: Monika Oczkowska <monika.oczkowska@un.org>\n\nSubject: Re: New report: Infrastructure for climate action\n \n\n\n\nDear Christopher,\n\n\n\nI'm coordinating the presentation of the report \"Infrastructure\n for Climate Action\" together with Monika from\n UNEP Brussels. We're delighted that Ms Visnar is available to co-host the event.\n\n\n \n\nPlease see below the draft agenda we had in mind. Do you think that 3 to 5 minutes is enough for Ms Visnar intervention?\n\n\n\nOn the technical side, would it be possible to host the conversation on the EU Webex account? We can do it on our Zoom account, but usually Webex works better for EU staff.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe'll prepare a SAVE THE DATE to send early next week. Could you pls share a picture of Ms Visnar and if possible a short bio?\n\n \n\n\nDraft agenda (Nov. 26th, 12h30-13h30)\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n·      \nWelcoming remarks by Mariacarmen Colitti (UNOPS, Head of Brussels Liaison Office and Representative) - 2 min\n\n·      \nIntroduction by Veronika Sfrankova (UNEP, Head of Brussels Office) - 3 min\n\n·      \nIntroduction statement by Elena Visnar (Head of Unit Climate Adaptation of DG CLIMA) -\n3-5 min\n\n·      \nMariacarmen introduces the speakers (1 min)\n\n·      \nPresentation by \nScott Thacker (UNOPS\nInfrastructure Specialist and Honorary Research Associate of the Environmental Change Institute, University of Oxford). -\n15 min\n\n·      \nPresentation by \nRowan Palmer\n(UNEP Programme Management Officer, Lead Sustainable Infrastructure Investment Team) -\n8 min\n\n·      \nQ/A - Moderation by Mariacarmen -\n25 min\n\n·      \nConclusion - 2 min\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nWe wish to keep 25 minutes for the Q/A as we look forward to having a lively conversation, and might also have a contribution from DG INTPA (tbc).\n\n\n \n\n\nPls let us know if you have any questions/comments.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nJérôme\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Senior Communications Officer and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Nov 12, 2021 at 11:49 AM Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Mariko,\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for your response. \n\n\n \n\n\nDelighted to hear that Ms Visnar is available to join us. I'll follow up with Christofer in a separate email to arrange the technical details.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease feel free to suggest names of NEAR (or other DGs) colleagues to include them in the guest list. As discussed, we'll follow-up on our side with DG INTPA. \n\n\n \n\n\nIn line with the Team Europe initiatives, we also wish to invite relevant MS institutions to attend (KfW, AFD, etc.) to attend the presentation.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe'll send the invitation next week, and look forward to a successful event. \n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nJérôme\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Senior Communications Officer and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Nov 11, 2021 at 5:48 PM PETERS Mariko (EEAS) <Mariko.PETERS@eeas.europa.eu> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Jerome,\n\n\nIn the meantime we spoke. While thanking you for your patience I am now happy to confirm that Head of Unit Climate Adaptation of DG CLIMA Elena Visnar has kindly agreed to co-host\n as suggested by you. Please also add CLIMA colleagues Christofer Ahlgren, Claus Kondrup and Stella Brozek-Evereart to the invitation list, in addition to my EEAS colleagues Wouter Wormgoor, Iina Lietzen and FPI colleague Roisin Drury Tully (all in cc).\n\n\n \n\ngreat that you will also invite INTPA colleagues. happy to also suggest names of NEAR colleagues if you have not yet included them in your list.\n\n\n \n\nfeel free to arrange any further details with CLIMA directly; Christofer Ahlgren will be point of contact for that purpose.\n\n\n \n\nI hope this works out and I look forward to attending the event!\n\n \n\nKind regards,\n\n\nMariko\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 04 November 2021 09:54\n\nTo: PETERS Mariko (EEAS) <Mariko.PETERS@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: MORETTINI Marco (EEAS) <Marco.MORETTINI@eeas.europa.eu>; LIETZEN Iina (EEAS) <Iina.LIETZEN@eeas.europa.eu>; Monika\n Oczkowska <monika.oczkowska@un.org>; Veronika Safrankova <veronika.safrankova@un.org>; Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>;\n Alexa Froger <alexa.froger@un.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>; DRURY TULLY Roisin (FPI) <Roisin.DRURY-TULLY@ec.europa.eu>;\n WORMGOOR Wouter (EEAS) <Wouter.WORMGOOR@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: Re: New report: Infrastructure for climate action\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Mariko,\n\n \n\nI’m glad to get back to you about the presentation of the Infrastructure for Climate Action report.\n\n \n\nThe main authors of the report, Dr Scott Thacker (UNOPS) and Rowan Palmer (UNEP), are available to join us for a one-hour online conversation on\nFriday 26 November at 12:30 (CET). Please let us know if this date suits you. The presentation of the key insights from the report and policy recommendations by Scott and Rowan will be followed by a Q/A session to ensure a lively conversation. Mariacarmen\n Colitti, UNOPS Head of Brussels Liaison Office and Representative, and Veronika \nHunt Safrankova, UNEP Head of Brussels Office, will also join the conversation.\n\n \n\nWe would like to invite EEAS to co-host this presentation, and would be honoured if an EU representative could provide a statement (eg: EU position further to the COP26, reflection on the role of infrastructure\n for climate action, etc.) at the beginning of the presentation. Since a project funded by DG INTPA is featured in the report (see page 43 -\nWorking\n with nature to protect Sri Lanka’s population from floods), we would be happy to extend the invitation to a representative of DG INTPA as well.\n\n\n \n\nWe would like to send a save the date early next week, so could you kindly\nlet us know your thoughts on this by Monday Nov. 8th COB? Thank you.\n\n \n\nIf you have any questions, please do not hesitate to reach out. \n\n \n\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\n\n \n\nKind regards,\n\nJérôme\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Senior Communications Officer and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\nOn Fri, Oct 22, 2021 at 3:57 PM Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Mariko,\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nThank you for your message and interest in the report 'Infrastructure for Climate Action'.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nWe're looking forward to organising a presentation for the EU. However, due to time constraints, we recommend setting a date right after the COP26. Since this is a cross-cutting topic, we will also invite EU colleagues from other DGs (CLIMA, ENV, INTPA, NEAR,\n ENER,..) to join us.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nWe'll get back to you as soon as possible with all the necessary details.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nMany thanks again for your interest and quick response.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\nJérôme\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJérôme de Thysebaert\n| Senior Communications Officer and Liaison Associate | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Brussels Liaison Office | Tel: + 32 (0) 499 197 497 |\nwww.unops.org\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on\nFacebook,\nLinkedIn,\nTwitter,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n Subscribe to our external newsletter in English,\nFrench\n or Spanish. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\nOn Wed, Oct 20, 2021 at 4:07 PM PETERS Mariko (EEAS) <Mariko.PETERS@eeas.europa.eu> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Jerome, Monika,\n\n\nThank you very much for the update and sharing the materials with us. We would be very interested in such a briefing! I added a few key colleagues on our side; once a date has been\n identified we can forward to more colleagues who might be interested in joining. Agendas look pretty full already on this end, but perhaps Friday Oct 29th is an option?\n\n\n \n\nbest regards,\n\n\nMariko\n\n\n \n\n \n\nMariko Peters\n\nSr Peace and Conflict Advisor\n\nEuropean External Action Service (EEAS)\n\nIntegrated Approach for Security and Peace Directorate\n\n\nConflict Prevention, Early Warning and Mediation Division (ISP.2)\n\nBrussels\n\nMob +32-460 84 5150\n\nWhatsapp +32-470 362822\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\nFrom: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <jeromedt@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 20 October 2021 12:31\n\nTo: MORETTINI Marco (EEAS) <Marco.MORETTINI@eeas.europa.eu>; LIETZEN Iina (EEAS) <Iina.LIETZEN@eeas.europa.eu>; PETERS\n Mariko (EEAS) <Mariko.PETERS@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: Veronika Safrankova <veronika.safrankova@un.org>; Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>; Monika Oczkowska <monika.oczkowska@un.org>;\n Alexa Froger <alexa.froger@un.org>; Laetitia KRAUS <LaetitiaK@unops.org>\n\nSubject: New report: Infrastructure for climate action\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn behalf of Mariacarmen Colitti and Veronika Hunt Safrankova\n\n***\n\n \n\nDear Mr Morettini, Mr Peters and Ms Lietzen,\n\n \n\nOn\n behalf of UNEP and UNOPS, we are pleased to inform you about the launch of the new Infrastructure for climate action report, co-published\n by UNOPS, UNEP and the University of Oxford on the 12th of October ahead of the COP26 in Glasgow.   \n\n \n\nThe report calls for a radical change in how governments plan, deliver and manage infrastructure - emphasising the often-overlooked role infrastructure plays in combating climate change, mitigation, and adaptation efforts  –\n being responsible for 79% of all GHG emissions and 88% of all adaptation costs. The objective of the report is to guide decision-makers so that infrastructure can accelerate progress towards the Paris Agreement and Sustainable Development Goals.  Better\n and more resilient infrastructure planning decisions made today will determine the quality of our common future.\n\nYou can find the press release here and\n read the full report under the following link.  \n\n \n\nIn the case of your interest we could organize a presentation of key findings and a joint discussion with the team of authors with the European Commission. Please contact monika.oczkowska@un.org at\n UNEP  and jeromedt@unops.org at UNOPS in the UN Brussels Office for further information.\n\n \n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\n\n \nVeronika Hunt Safrankova\nHead of Brussels Office\n\n\n\nUnited Nations Environment Programme\n\nBoulevard du Regent 37-40 | 1000 Brussels | Belgium\nTelephone: +32 2 213 3056\nSkype: vsafrankova\nwww.unep.org\n\n \n\n\n\nMariacarmen Colitti\n\nHead of Office and Representative \n\nUNOPS\n\nPartnerships and Liaison Group\n\nBrussels Liaison Office \n\nTel: + 32 2 7881840 | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000JIaILMA1",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "laetitiak@unops.org", "veronika.safrankova@un.org", "mariko.peters@eeas.europa.eu", "alexa.froger@un.org", "scottt@unops.org", "christofer.ahlgren@ec.europa.eu", "clima-a03-ares@ec.europa.eu", "iina.lietzen@eeas.europa.eu", "wouter.wormgoor@eeas.europa.eu", "mariacarmenco@unops.org", "monika.oczkowska@un.org", "dorothyl@unops.org", "roisin.drury-tully@ec.europa.eu", "jeromedt@unops.org", "anais.fantasia@ec.europa.eu", "marco.morettini@eeas.europa.eu", "samanthas@unops.org" },
