                new (
                    "00TQx00000JIxI8MAL",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Fwd: FW: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-06-18").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: FW: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note",
                        Description = "To: jeromedt@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: FW: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\nBody:\nWilliam Muchira | Project Manager | South Sudan Country Office |\nJuba, South Sudan | Tel: +211 (0)922 666 016; |\nSkype: williammuchira | www.unops.org\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: William MUCHIRA <williamm@unops.org>\nDate: Mon, Jun 10, 2024 at 11:12 AM\nSubject: Fwd: FW: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\nTo: Laetitia KRAUS <laetitiak@unops.org>, Mariacarmen COLITTI <mariacarmenco@unops.org>\n\nWilliam Muchira | Project Manager | South Sudan Country Office |\nJuba, South Sudan | Tel: +211 (0)922 666 016; |\nSkype: williammuchira | www.unops.org\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>\nDate: Fri, May 17, 2024 at 2:17 PM\nSubject: FW: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\nTo: William MUCHIRA <williamm@unops.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear William,\n \nThis is for your information only. We might have more money for corridor 11.\n\n \nYou could begin to think of what we can add to the already drafted proposal.\n \nRegards,\n \nSunday\n \n\n\nFrom: STALMANS Marc (INTPA) <Marc.STALMANS@ec.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: 16 May 2024 08:34\n\nTo: LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: ZAPOROWSKI Piotr (INTPA) <Piotr.ZAPOROWSKI@ec.europa.eu>; LEONTE Gabriel Octavian (EEAS-JUBA) <Gabriel-Octavian.LEONTE@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\n\n\n \nThanks a lot Sunday. This project is very welcome and awaited on our side. We will push for it. Definitely. At A4, we are not in the position to comment technically the proposal and will leave it to A2/F4 colleagues. This being said, I’m\n wondering if we cannot scale-up the proposal/project. We could have more than 10 MEURO from regional envelope….\nM\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, May 16, 2024 12:15 AM\n\nTo: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>\n\nCc: STALMANS Marc (INTPA) <Marc.STALMANS@ec.europa.eu>; NAVARRO Lluis (INTPA) <Lluis.NAVARRO@ec.europa.eu>; BOELEN Martijn (INTPA) <Martijn.BOELEN@ec.europa.eu>;\n GEORGELIN Lenaic (INTPA) <Lenaic.GEORGELIN@ec.europa.eu>; HURJUI Madalina (INTPA) <Madalina.HURJUI@ec.europa.eu>; GAVILAN MARIN Jesus (INTPA) <Jesus-Manuel.GAVILAN-MARIN@ec.europa.eu>;\n DE RUYT Virginie (INTPA) <Virginie.DE-RUYT@ec.europa.eu>; RUIZ SAN JOSE Macarena (INTPA) <Macarena.RUIZ-SAN-JOSE@ec.europa.eu>; GRAPSAS Georgios (INTPA)\n <Georgios.GRAPSAS@ec.europa.eu>; MURAILLE Berenice (INTPA) <Berenice.MURAILLE@ec.europa.eu>; DERIDDER Lennart (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Lennart.DERIDDER@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KILOMBE Kenyi (EEAS-JUBA) <Kenyi.KILOMBE@eeas.europa.eu>; RODENAS RODRIGUEZ Adela (EEAS-JUBA) <Adela.RODENAS-RODRIGUEZ@eeas.europa.eu>; LEONTE Gabriel\n Octavian (EEAS-JUBA) <Gabriel-Octavian.LEONTE@eeas.europa.eu>; WOLIT William (EEAS-JUBA) <William.WOLIT@eeas.europa.eu>; VAN DER PLOEG Johannes (EEAS-KAMPALA)\n <Johannes.VAN-DER-PLOEG@eeas.europa.eu>; MULIISA Simon (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Simon.MULIISA@eeas.europa.eu>; NAKASIGA Fiona (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\n\n\n \nDear Fabio,\n \nPlease find attached the draft proposal for Corridor 11 - South Sudan with a view to contracting before the end of the year, focusing on improving trade facilitation and transport infrastructure\n to increase cross-border trade. \n \nPlease note that we have received this version only today after a previous version yesterday. Some basic issues should now be corrected but it should still be work in progress. We are\n looking forward to comments from you and our colleagues in the Ugandan delegation to improve further.\n\n \nWe have decided to work with two implementing partners (UNOPS and ITC). UNOPS will work on the infrastructure components, while ITC will work on the soft components of trade and markets.\n UNOPS has extensive experience in implementing EU-funded infrastructure projects and ITC has experience of working on trade issues in South Sudan.\n \nWe would be grateful if you could indicate the way forward after this submission to secure this regional funding for South Sudan. Please, let us know if you would like to have a follow\n up meeting to discuss any comments and consolidate a common response for UNOPS/ITC.\n \nKind regards,\n \nSunday\n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA)\n\n\nSent: 15 May 2024 23:18\n\nTo: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>\n\nCc: STALMANS Marc (INTPA) <Marc.STALMANS@ec.europa.eu>;\n NAVARRO Lluis (INTPA) <Lluis.NAVARRO@ec.europa.eu>; BOELEN Martijn\n (INTPA) <Martijn.BOELEN@ec.europa.eu>; GEORGELIN Lenaic (INTPA)\n <Lenaic.GEORGELIN@ec.europa.eu>; HURJUI Madalina (INTPA)\n <Madalina.HURJUI@ec.europa.eu>; GAVILAN MARIN Jesus (INTPA)\n <Jesus-Manuel.GAVILAN-MARIN@ec.europa.eu>; DE RUYT\n Virginie (INTPA) <Virginie.DE-RUYT@ec.europa.eu>; RUIZ SAN\n JOSE Macarena (INTPA) <Macarena.RUIZ-SAN-JOSE@ec.europa.eu>;\n GRAPSAS Georgios (INTPA) <Georgios.GRAPSAS@ec.europa.eu>;\n MURAILLE Berenice (INTPA) <Berenice.MURAILLE@ec.europa.eu>;\n DERIDDER Lennart (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Lennart.DERIDDER@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KILOMBE Kenyi (EEAS-JUBA) <Kenyi.KILOMBE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n RODENAS RODRIGUEZ Adela (EEAS-JUBA) <Adela.RODENAS-RODRIGUEZ@eeas.europa.eu>;\n LEONTE Gabriel Octavian (EEAS-JUBA) <Gabriel-Octavian.LEONTE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n WOLIT William (EEAS-JUBA) <William.WOLIT@eeas.europa.eu>;\n VAN DER PLOEG Johannes (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Johannes.VAN-DER-PLOEG@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MULIISA Simon (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Simon.MULIISA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n NAKASIGA Fiona (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take Aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\n\n\n \nDear Fabio,\n \nPlease find attached the draft proposal for Corridor 11 - South Sudan with a view to contracting before the end of the year, focusing on improving trade facilitation and transport infrastructure\n to increase cross-border trade. \n \nPlease note that we have received this version only today after a previous version yesterday. Some basic issues should now be corrected but it should still be work in progress. We are\n looking forward to comments from you and our colleagues in the Ugandan delegation to improve further.\n\n \nWe have decided to work with two implementing partners (UNOPS and ITC). UNOPS will work on the infrastructure components, while ITC will work on the soft components of trade and markets.\n UNOPS has extensive experience in implementing EU-funded infrastructure projects and ITC has experience of working on trade issues in South Sudan.\n \nWe would be grateful if you could indicate the way forward after this submission to secure this regional funding for South Sudan. Please, let us know if you would like to have a follow\n up meeting to discuss any comments and consolidate a common response for UNOPS/ITC.\n \nKind regards,\n \nSunday\n \n \n\n\nFrom: NAKASIGA Fiona (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: 15 March 2024 14:33\n\nTo: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>\n\nCc: STALMANS Marc (INTPA) <Marc.STALMANS@ec.europa.eu>;\n NAVARRO Lluis (INTPA) <Lluis.NAVARRO@ec.europa.eu>; BOELEN Martijn\n (INTPA) <Martijn.BOELEN@ec.europa.eu>; GEORGELIN Lenaic (INTPA)\n <Lenaic.GEORGELIN@ec.europa.eu>; HURJUI Madalina (INTPA)\n <Madalina.HURJUI@ec.europa.eu>; GAVILAN MARIN Jesus (INTPA)\n <Jesus-Manuel.GAVILAN-MARIN@ec.europa.eu>; DE RUYT\n Virginie (INTPA) <Virginie.DE-RUYT@ec.europa.eu>; RUIZ SAN\n JOSE Macarena (INTPA) <Macarena.RUIZ-SAN-JOSE@ec.europa.eu>;\n GRAPSAS Georgios (INTPA) <Georgios.GRAPSAS@ec.europa.eu>;\n MURAILLE Berenice (INTPA) <Berenice.MURAILLE@ec.europa.eu>;\n DERIDDER Lennart (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Lennart.DERIDDER@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KILOMBE Kenyi (EEAS-JUBA) <Kenyi.KILOMBE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n RODENAS RODRIGUEZ Adela (EEAS-JUBA) <Adela.RODENAS-RODRIGUEZ@eeas.europa.eu>;\n LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>;\n WOLIT William (EEAS-JUBA) <William.WOLIT@eeas.europa.eu>;\n VAN DER PLOEG Johannes (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Johannes.VAN-DER-PLOEG@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MULIISA Simon (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Simon.MULIISA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 First Concept Note\n\n\n \n\nDear Fabio and Colleagues,\n\nThank you for your email below on the intervention logic for Corridor 11 and your kind remarks.\n\n\nPlease find attached our first concept note on Corridor 11 (both MS Word and pdf versions), submitted by DEL-UGANDA, for your kind action. Our colleagues in DEL-SOUTH SUDAN are also working on a second concept note\n which we hope to submit in the 2nd round i.e. 15th May 2024.\n\n\nWith regard to the preparatory work for hard infrastructure projects, we confirm, for the moment, that DEL-UGANDA does not have any funding needs for the feasibility/ preparatory studies as these studies are funded\n from national MIP.\n\nWe remain at your disposal should require any clarifications on our concept note.\n\n \n\n \n\nKind regards,\n\nFiona NAKASIGA\n \n\n\nFrom: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: 26 February 2024 14:13\n\nTo: NAKASIGA Fiona (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n DERIDDER Lennart (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Lennart.DERIDDER@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KILOMBE Kenyi (EEAS-JUBA) <Kenyi.KILOMBE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n REJADO ALBAINA Sergio (EEAS-JUBA) <Sergio.REJADO-ALBAINA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n RODENAS RODRIGUEZ Adela (EEAS-JUBA) <Adela.RODENAS-RODRIGUEZ@eeas.europa.eu>;\n LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>;\n WOLIT William (EEAS-JUBA) <William.WOLIT@eeas.europa.eu>;\n VAN DER PLOEG Johannes (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Johannes.VAN-DER-PLOEG@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MULIISA Simon (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Simon.MULIISA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: STALMANS Marc (INTPA) <Marc.STALMANS@ec.europa.eu>;\n NAVARRO Lluis (INTPA) <Lluis.NAVARRO@ec.europa.eu>; BOELEN Martijn\n (INTPA) <Martijn.BOELEN@ec.europa.eu>; GEORGELIN Lenaic (INTPA)\n <Lenaic.GEORGELIN@ec.europa.eu>; HURJUI Madalina (INTPA)\n <Madalina.HURJUI@ec.europa.eu>; GAVILAN MARIN Jesus (INTPA)\n <Jesus-Manuel.GAVILAN-MARIN@ec.europa.eu>; DE RUYT\n Virginie (INTPA) <Virginie.DE-RUYT@ec.europa.eu>; RUIZ SAN\n JOSE Macarena (INTPA) <Macarena.RUIZ-SAN-JOSE@ec.europa.eu>;\n GRAPSAS Georgios (INTPA) <Georgios.GRAPSAS@ec.europa.eu>;\n MURAILLE Berenice (INTPA) <Berenice.MURAILLE@ec.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: Re: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 Intervention Logic\n\n\n \nDear Fiona, dear colleagues,\n \nMany thanks for the note and the work on developing this logic of intervention\nWe really appreciated the efforts in putting together i) the ongoing existing work with future proposals  ii) and including and making the link between hard infra and soft measures.\n\n \nWe had a discussion in HQ with all the concerned corridor units (A4, E2,F4) to look at all intervention logics. Given the current political context, we understand and agree with your proposal\n of limit the scope of interventions on the Uganda- South Sudan border for the moment.\n \nWith regards to the trade and transport facilitation measures, we suggest to plan in 2024 an action (indicative envelop 15M)  focusing\non small-scale cross border traders (including also the relevant border post activities mentioned), which links very well with the context and logic of intervention explained. Please go ahead on the project preparation and share with us a concept note\n as soon as ready and indicative contracting period.\n \nWith regards to the hard measures please go ahead with the preparatory work for hard infra projects and let us know if there are any needs for the feasibility/preparatory works.\n\nKind regards,  \nFabio and colleagues\n\n \n\n\nFrom: NAKASIGA Fiona (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: Friday, January 19, 2024 7:52 AM\n\nTo: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>;\n RUIZ SAN JOSE Macarena (INTPA) <Macarena.RUIZ-SAN-JOSE@ec.europa.eu>;\n GRAPSAS Georgios (INTPA) <Georgios.GRAPSAS@ec.europa.eu>\n\nCc: DERIDDER Lennart (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Lennart.DERIDDER@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KILOMBE Kenyi (EEAS-JUBA) <Kenyi.KILOMBE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n REJADO ALBAINA Sergio (EEAS-JUBA) <Sergio.REJADO-ALBAINA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n RODENAS RODRIGUEZ Adela (EEAS-JUBA) <Adela.RODENAS-RODRIGUEZ@eeas.europa.eu>;\n LOTIDAK Aryemo Sunday Ocaya (EEAS-JUBA) <Aryemo-Sunday-Ocaya.LOTIDAK@eeas.europa.eu>;\n WOLIT William (EEAS-JUBA) <William.WOLIT@eeas.europa.eu>;\n VAN DER PLOEG Johannes (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Johannes.VAN-DER-PLOEG@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MULIISA Simon (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Simon.MULIISA@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: RE: Central Africa coordination & pipeline – Take aways meeting 6th December - Corridor 11 Intervention Logic\n\n\n \n\nDear Fabio, Macarena, Georgios,\n\nPlease find attached the intervention logic for Corridor 11\n(as requested in the email below) which has been prepared in agreement with the Delegation in South Sudan (also in cc) for your kind action.\n\n\n \n\nRegards,\nFiona NAKASIGA\nOperations Adviser - Infrastructure\n| Global Gateway and Refugee Response | Delegation of the European Union to Uganda | 15th Floor Crested Towers, P. O. Box 5244, Kampala,\n Uganda | Tel: +256 312 701000 (switchboard) | Fiona.NAKASIGA@eeas.europa.eu\n |\nhttp://www.eeas.europa.eu/delegations/uganda/\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: DI STEFANO Fabio (INTPA) <Fabio.DI-STEFANO@ec.europa.eu>\n\n\nSent: 20 December 2023 12:51\n\nTo: MEREL Cedric (EEAS-DAR ES SALAAM) <Cedric.MEREL@eeas.europa.eu>;\n GIRIBALDI Irene (EEAS-NAIROBI) <Irene.GIRIBALDI@eeas.europa.eu>;\n LOCK Stefan (EEAS-ADDIS ABABA) <Stefan.LOCK@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KIVUMBI Dorian (EEAS-NAIROBI) <Dorian.KIVUMBI@eeas.europa.eu>;\n TOMASELLA Michela (EEAS-KIGALI) <Michela.TOMASELLA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n SCHLEDE Simona (EEAS-DJIBOUTI) <Simona.SCHLEDE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n ADRIAENSEN Caroline (EEAS-KAMPALA) <Caroline.ADRIAENSEN@eeas.europa.eu>;\n TASSIN-PELZER Cecile (INTPA) <Cecile.TASSIN-PELZER@ec.europa.eu>;\n LEONTE Gabriel Octavian (EEAS-JUBA) <Gabriel-Octavian.LEONTE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n ROUSSET Elisabeth (EEAS-KHARTOUM) <Elisabeth.Rousset@eeas.europa.eu>;\n PONS Jerome (EEAS-YAOUNDE) <Jerome.PONS@eeas.europa.eu>; VANDENBROUCKE\n Wim (EEAS-BANGUI) <Wim.Vandenbroucke@eeas.europa.eu>;\n BARBE Jean (EEAS-LIBREVILLE) <Jean.BARBE@eeas.europa.eu>; WIESE\n Martin (EEAS-NDJAMENA) <martin.wiese@eeas.europa.eu>; ILLING\n Patrick (EEAS-YAOUNDE) <Patrick.ILLING@eeas.europa.eu>; CHUMBE\n TOUONDOUNKO Rachidetou (EEAS-YAOUNDE) <Rachidetou.CHUMBE-TOUONDOUNKO@eeas.europa.eu>;\n KEMBOU Jules (EEAS-YAOUNDE) <Jules.KEMBOU@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MALINOWSKA-FACCI Kinga (EEAS-YAOUNDE) <Kinga.MALINOWSKA-FACCI@eeas.europa.eu>;\n DEL GIUDICE Roberta (EEAS-BANGUI) <Roberta.DEL-GIUDICE@eeas.europa.eu>;\n SPERANDEO Valeria (EEAS-BANGUI) <Valeria.SPERANDEO@eeas.europa.eu>;\n GUERENDEBO Godefroy (EEAS-BANGUI) <Godefroy.GUERENDEBO@eeas.e