                new (
                    "00TQx00000JORypMAH",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Amnesty International report",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-12-18").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Amnesty International report",
                        Description = "To: timl@unops.org; peterb@unops.org\nCC: emiliep@unops.org; freyavg@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Amnesty International report\nBody:\nHi Tim and Pete,\n\nThank you very much for looping me in on this issue - which unfortunately comes on top of a few other problematic cases we have with the Norwegians these days. \nI would greatly appreciate it if you could keep me in the loop to ensure consistent communication with the Norwegians at all levels. \nI assume that contact with the Norwegians was so far handled locally? Ie. with the Belgrade embassy? As I am often in contact with the Norwegian MFA HQ in Oslo, it would be good for me to know who spoke with who (and about what) in the Norwegian MFA. \nThanks!\n/A\nOn Tue, 17 Dec 2024 at 16:27, Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org> wrote:\nThanks Pete. \nAsbjorn, I’m heading north now on leave but of course can connect if needed\nTim\nTim Lardner | Regional Director Europe and Central Asia Region | Tel/WhatsApp: +41772464777 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\nOn Tue, 17 Dec 2024 at 15:13, Peter BROWNE <peterb@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Asbjorn\n\nAs discussed, below are details of the Amnesty report, the request from Norway and the Reuters questions are here \n\nTim, I am folding in Asbjorn to join the dots as in parallel we seem to have another potential instance involving Norway in Ethiopia where it seems investigations have been called for. \n\nBest,\nPete\n\nOn Mon, 16 Dec 2024 at 09.32, Kirstine DAMKJAER <kirstined@unops.org> wrote:\n\nDear all\nForwarding below from a case that developed on Friday. It seems that we are all in the loop, but I am forwarding none the less for collective knowledge, in case there is a missing flow of information. \nBest, Kirstine\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Tim LARDNER <timl@unops.org>\nDate: Sat, Dec 14, 2024 at 12:27 PM\nSubject: Amnesty International report\nTo: Kirstine DAMKJAER <kirstined@unops.org>\n\nDear Kirstine,\nA quick heads up that we have had some back and forth around an Amnesty International report that they plan to release on Monday.\nIt appears that the report hones in on alleged widespread spyware abuses in Serbia targeted at journalists, acivists and civil society. The report highlights equipment purchased by UNOPS (Serbia office) in 2018/9 on behalf of the Norwegian government and says both parties “had a responsibility to exercise oversight and due diligence when procuring highly invasive technology and handing it over to Serbian institutions.” \nRSMCO has been in touch with CG who have prepared and delivered a response to Reuters who are preparing an article that will be published in parallel to the reports release. The response from UNOPS is that we followed all due processes expected at the time (which did not include any HRDDP due diligence). Pete has the lead and has everything he needs.\nNorwegian MFA have also responded directly to Amnesty in a rather unfortunate manner - essentially passing the buck to us. Norway have also asked UNOPS to undertake an investigation - and Michela is speaking with IAIG Monday.\nMy assessment is that while this is not catastophic, it may well be an uncomfortable week - in Serbia as well as globally (Reuters will publish gloablly). PG is fully aware and prepared, and Jorge is also aware.\nHappy to talk if you like, but not much more to add at this point.\nBest from a 12 hour delay returning home :(\nThanks\nTimTim Lardner | Regional Director Europe and Central Asia Region | Tel/WhatsApp: +41772464777 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube.Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000JORypMAH",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "freyavg@unops.org", "kirstined@unops.org", "emiliep@unops.org", "peterb@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "timl@unops.org" },
