                    {
                        Name = "Email: Remaining excess reserve allocated to UK",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-12-20").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Remaining excess reserve allocated to UK",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Remaining excess reserve allocated to UK\nBody:\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjorn,\n \nI’ve just now received confirmation from my Director that she is content for the remaining excess reserve allocated to the UK to be divided between the Resident Coordinator System and the SDG Fund in line with the Executive Board decision.\n \nWe’ll try to get a letter to you confirming this, but with the Christmas period approaching fast I fear we may not manage in time. I hope having this message helps a bit – and we’ll try to get the letter out asap.\n \nAll the best, and hope you and Naimo have some well deserved rest coming up!\n \nAgnes\n \n \nAgnes Annells|\n UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road, Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA |  agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk\n | www.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \nMy working week is Tuesday to Friday.\n \n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL",
