                        Subject = "Email: Re: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: graced@unhcr.org\nCC: argitab@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS\nBody:\nDear DominicWishing you a happy and healthy 2025!Just dropping you a line to see if we should have another conversation soon?Looking forward to hearing from youBest wishes Louise\n\nOn Wed, 11 Dec 2024 at 15:03, Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Dominic\nSo there is a mix of project staff and partner personnel in Spain. The project staff in Valencia are covered by the UN secretariat peacekeeping agreement that has been in place for several years.  I don’t imagine UN fleet staff could fall under that agreement. Thus Should we wish to proceed with unops contracting UNHCR and WFP staff for the UN fleet in Valencia a discussion with Spanish MOFA and letter of agreement would be needed to enable this project by-  Understanding Spain is a signatory to the UN convention on privileges and immunities. Please advise if you want to pick up the discussion again next week to clarify next steps. \nBest wishesLouise\n\nOn Wed, 4 Dec 2024 at 11:39, Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Louise,\n \nHope all is well with you!\n \nFollowing up on the call this week – can you/your team, give me some more info on the FTA contracts you have in Valencia?  Are they partner personnel?  What Host Country Agreement do they fall under?\n \nOur legal team, as well as MoFA, is stressing the importance of the HCA, so I need to understand that and tick the box.\n \nMany thanks\nDominic  \n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, November 28, 2024 5:23 PM\n\nTo: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org>\n\nSubject: Re: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS\n\n \n\nOk thx. Totally understand. L\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 28 Nov 2024 at 16:58, Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nStruggling with convincing ‘the others’ about hosting.  Think its early days, and possibly I could change perceptions, but a little too early at this point.\n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, November 28, 2024 4:25 PM\n\nTo: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org>\n\nSubject: Re: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS\n\n \n\nlol yup!  See you there. Do you have a view on the appetite for hosting ? A board can be organized fairly easily right ? It seems the FTA wouldn’t solve the issues we discussed\n the other day I. E. separate ERP, own agency line mgmt etc \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 28 Nov 2024 at 16:09, Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nYes, with the big guns!\n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, November 28, 2024 10:49 AM\n\nTo: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org>\n\nCc: Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\nHi Dominic\n\n\n\nThanks for following up, I understand a call has now been scheduled for Monday 2 December\n\n\nBest wishes\n\n\nLouise\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 22 Nov 2024 at 16:17, Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Louise,\n \nThanks for the email and updates.\n \nI was just discussing with Hans, and it seems to boil down to a question of\n‘Can UNOPS offer FTA contracts in Spain?’.\n \nNot sure if you have a HCA which may facilitate that.\n \nGrateful for your views on this.\n \nKind regards\n \nDominic\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Louise LEECH <louisel@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, November 22, 2024 2:18 PM\n\nTo: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org>\n\nCc: Lorraine ANABTAWI <lorrainea@unops.org>;\ncamilla.dupont@wfp.org; Farrell BRODY <farrell.brody@wfp.org>; Lance Bartholomeusz <bartholl@unhcr.org>;\n Maria Arethousa Kyprouli <KYPROULI@unhcr.org>; Laura Sanchez Fernandez <sanchezf@unhcr.org>; Miroslav Medic <medic@unhcr.org>;\n Gergo Gelsei <gelsei@unhcr.org>; Mariam Mansouri Moayed <moayedm@unhcr.org>; Claudie Barrat <barrat@unhcr.org>;\n Krisztina Szollas <szollas@unhcr.org>; Francisco Navarro <navarrof@unhcr.org>; Brynna CONNOLLY <brynna.connolly@wfp.org>;\n Laurentiu MASTACAN <laurentium@unops.org>; Phil Jones <phil.jones@unfleet.org>; Nicolai Von Hoyningen-Huene <huene@unhcr.org>;\n Aurelie Lucrece ARMYNOT DU CHATELET <aureliear@unops.org>; Elena Librino <elenali@unops.org>\n\nSubject: [For review] Key points from the meeting: FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nAttention: This email is from an external sender. Please be careful with any links or attachments.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Dominic\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for convening the meeting on the UN Fleet and sharing the notes. We have made one of two small edits (nothing\n major!)\n\n\n \n\n\nIn response to the section on \"more information needed\", please find attached a few slides we put together in case\n useful, outlining the terms, conditions, fees and potential pros and cons of our HR and Hosting support, for your further consideration.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you in due course and wish everyone a restful weekend.\n\n\n \n\n\nAll best wishes, on behalf of UNOPS colleagues in copy, \n\n\nLouise \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  \n\n\nUNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\n\n\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow\n us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 19 Nov 2024 at 14:38, Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear colleagues,\n \nThank you for participating at the meeting on FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS on 11 November.\n \nBelow please find the link to the key points from the meeting. We would be grateful for your track changes by Friday 22\n November 12:00 noon. Afterwards, I’ll share a final version.\n \nThis is a shared file so you can edit the same version in parallel.\n\n \nWe granted you with access. If you cannot access the file, please email Nicolai (huene@unhcr.org).\n \nPlease consider\nnot copying colleagues to minimize email traffic. \n \nLink to the notes:\n241111\n Key points, FTA contracts for UN Fleet from UNOPS, DRAFT.docx\n \n\nBest regards,\nDominic\n\n \n\n-----Original Appointment-----\n\nFrom: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace <graced@unhcr.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, 8 November 2024 15:44\n\nTo: Dominic Paul Sheldon Grace; Lorraine ANABTAWI; Louise LEECH; Phil Jones;\ncamilla.dupont@wfp.org; Farrell BRODY; Lance Lorenz Bartholomeusz; Maria Arethousa Kyprouli; Laura Sanchez Fernandez; Nicolai Von Hoyningen-Huene\n\nCc: Miroslav Medic; Gergo Gelsei; Mariam Mansouri Moayed; Claudie Barrat; Krisztina Szollas; Francisco Navarro; Brynna CONNOLLY; Laurentiu MASTACAN\n\nSubject: FTA contracts for UNFLEET/UNOPS\n\nWhen: Monday, 11 November 2024 11:00-12:00 (UTC+01:00) Amsterdam, Berlin, Bern, Rome, Stockholm, Vienna.\n\nWhere: Microsoft Teams Meeting\n\n \nDear Colleagues,\n \nAs discussed, we would like a preliminary meeting to discuss whether UNOPS could provide a service to manage a limited number of FTA contracts for UNFLEET, which is managed by both\n UNHCR and WFP jointly.\n \nAgenda:\n \n\n\nSetting of the scene and requirements: Dominic/Phil 10-15 mins\nUNOPS preliminary reaction: Lorraine/Louise\nHR and/or legal implications\nOther matters\nNext steps\n \n@Laura Sanchez Fernandez, please forward to the relevant HR colleagues at UNHCR.\n \nKind regards\nDominic\n \n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n\nMicrosoft Teams\nNeed help?\n\n\n\nJoin\n the meeting now \n\n\nMeeting ID:\n392 778 230 693\n\n\n\nPasscode:\nYd4e5P\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJoin on a video conferencing device\n\n\n\nTenant key:\nunhcr2@m.webex.com\n\n\n\nVideo ID:\n128 459 932 6\n\n\n\nMore\n info \n\n\nFor organizers:\nMeeting\n options \n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________",
