                new (
                    "00TQx00000KWXqdMAH",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Partnering on the DESNZ Climate Innovation Pull Facility",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-20").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Partnering on the DESNZ Climate Innovation Pull Facility",
                        Description = "To: edward.coleridge@sustainableventures.co.uk\nCC: danb@unops.org; joseph.seal-driver@sustainableventures.co.uk; eleanorg@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Partnering on the DESNZ Climate Innovation Pull Facility\nBody:\nDear Edward\nThank you very much for your email and apologies for the late response. \nMy colleague Elanor will reach out to you bilaterally soon - as she has been working on UNOPS' potential engagement in the Climate Innovation Pull Facility. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nOn Fri, 20 Dec 2024 at 16:50, Edward Coleridge <edward.coleridge@sustainableventures.co.uk> wrote:\nDear Asbjørn and Dan, \n\nI work for Sustainable Ventures, the largest climate tech startup ecosystem in Europe based in London. I saw you were also on the DESNZ Climate Innovation Pull Facility call back in September and wanted to reach out.\n\nWe are experts at supporting early stage innovators to scale and bring their products to market. We are looking to partner with a larger organisation such as UNOPS on the bid. We would love to set up a call with you or a member of your team to discuss the bid and if there is an opportunity for us to work together.\n\nFor context: We specialise in supporting and accelerating early-stage UK Climate Tech businesses through a combination of venture support, workspaces, and investments. We have a long-standing track record of working with government (central and regional) and established corporations (e.g Barclays and Google), fostering climate tech innovation, and delivering jobs and economic results. \n\nOur four core business units are:\n\nVenture support: Through our programmes, accelerators, and commercial services, we've supported over 800 climate tech businesses. These are free to startups and funded by corporate partners, local authorities, or philanthropic trusts. We work with London and partners, The Carbon Trust, and various National and Local Authorities. \n\nCorporate Innovation: We run bespoke innovation challenges that connect corporate challenges with start-up innovators. Notably, we built the world's first Net-Zero Home with Schneider Electric and have a growing partnership with Google. \n\nInvestments: Operating at pre-seed and seed, we're one of the most active investors in Europe and the winner of the Business Green Early Stage Investor or the Year. \n\nWorkspaces: We're home to the largest Climate Tech Cluster in Europe, with more than 1,200 Entrepreneurs onsite in our flagship County Hall London workspace based opposite parliament.\n\nWe would love the opportunity to meet your team, either virtually or in person, and we’d be delighted to host you at County Hall for a tour of our sustainable workspace.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you. \n\nBest\n\nEdward\n-- \n\nEdward Coleridge    Corporate Innovation Senior Associate\n\nSustainable VenturesCounty Hall, 5th FloorLondon\nSE1 7PBsustainableventures.co.uk \n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
