                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000KYYoYMAX",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Outputs SFA: Agreed understanding of General Condition 21(b)(ii)",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-16").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Outputs SFA: Agreed understanding of General Condition 21(b)(ii)",
                        Description = "To: bkuba@worldbank.org\nCC: christinebo@unops.org; vineshw@unops.org; alistairs@unops.org; gkassem1@worldbank.org; akircher1@worldbank.org; mfikre@worldbank.org; nmunzberg@worldbank.org; vmosoti@worldbank.org; dgreco@worldbank.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Outputs SFA: Agreed understanding of General Condition 21(b)(ii)\nBody:\nDear Birgit, \nHappy New Year to you as well! \nThank you for sending the text of the email exchange to formalize our understanding of the interpretation of article 21 b) ii) of the SFA.  We confirm our agreement to this interpretation, and please accept this email as formalizing our understanding of that clause.  I wasn't able to open the attachment in your first email but I see the text in the body of your subsequent message below. \nBest regards, \nElizabeth \n--\nElizabeth Duby | Legal Advisor | Legal Group | HQ | Washington D.C. | Mob: +1 (202) 391-2817  | Solution Portal  | www.unops.org | Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish\nOn Wed, Jan 15, 2025 at 11:33 AM Birgit Kuba <bkuba@worldbank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe purpose of this exchange of emails is to formally document the agreed understanding of General Condition 21(b)(ii) of the Standard Form of Agreement for the Delivery of Outputs of November 2024, which refers to the obligation of the\n UN Partner to “ensure that the Contractor and/or Implementing Partner has the capacity to comply with such E&S Obligations”.\n\n \nRepresentatives of the World Bank and UNOPS agreed that this obligation requires UNOPS to conduct an E&S capacity assessment of Contractors and Implementing Partners before they are engaged in the Delivery of Outputs, identify any measures\n required to fill capacity gaps, if any, and thereafter supervise the implementation of such measures. UNOPS will not engage Contractors or Implementing Partners that cannot achieve sufficient E&S capacity in a timely manner.\n \nPlease confirm your agreement with this understanding by responding to this email.\n \nBirgit Kuba\nSenior Counsel\n\nEnvironment and International Law Practice\nLegal Vice Presidency\n\nThe World Bank\n1818 H Street, N.W. Washington DC 20433\n\nEmail:  bkuba@worldbank.org\n \n\n \nThis message may contain privileged and confidential information. If you have received this message by mistake, please keep it confidential and return it to the\n sender. \n \n\n\n\n\n-- \nElizabeth Duby | Legal Advisor | IPAS | HQ | Copenhagen | Mob:\n+45 30177661  | IPAS\nSolution Portal  | www.unops.org |\n\n \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our\nexternal newsletter in English, French or Spanish",
