                new (
                    "00TQx00000KZu0cMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Under-claimed and over-claimed VAT/MOMS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-21").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Under-claimed and over-claimed VAT/MOMS",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: astrug@um.dk; naimoh@unops.org; vilhelmk@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Under-claimed and over-claimed VAT/MOMS\nBody:\nDear Asbjørn,\n \nAs previously mentioned in correspondence between us, we have been in contact with the Danish Tax Agency (Skattestyrelsen) and their Department for Legal Affairs, Tax Process\n and Administrative Law (Jura, Skatteproces og Forvaltningsret). They have informed us that pursuant to the Danish Law on Tax Administration (Skatteforvaltningsloven) §31 (2) the person/entity liable for MOMS/VAT has a period of 3 years (after the expiry of\n the declaration period) for ordinary resumption of VAT liability, i.e. to apply for reimbursement of MOMS.\n\n \nIn regards to your under-claimed MOMS from 2016-2017 (expenses amounting to DKK 909,203.81) the deadline for ordinary request for reimbursement of MOMS has been exceeded.\n\n \nUNOPS has informed us that the expenses in question were not submitted to the Protocol Department within the 3 year period due to mistakes by one or more staff members. The\n Danish Tax Agency furthermore referred to §32 (1)(4) (i.e. § 32, stk. 1, nr. 4) of the Law on Tax Administration, which refers to a possibility for extraordinary resumption (after the 3 year period) if special circumstances exist. The Tax Agency mentioned\n that it would not be considered special circumstances if the error/mistake is caused by the business/entity or one of its representatives. UNOPS may also see the legal guide,\nA.A.8.3.2.2.2.4\n Særlige omstændigheder - info.skat.dk, regarding special circumstances. There is nothing in the legal guide to suggest the presence of special circumstances and thereby justify\n extraordinary resumption of the reimbursement claims. The Protocol Department adheres to the information and guidance provided by the Tax Agency and cannot on the grounds mentioned extraordinarily receive and process the expenses in question for reimbursement.\n \nHowever, the Tax Agency mentioned that if UNOPS, after familiarizing itself with the relevant legislation and the legal guidance mentioned above, were in doubt about its rights\n and/or options, it might consider acquiring the services of a lawyer or other specialized adviser to look into whether there are possibilities to pursue the matter within the framework of the Law on Tax Administration. Should UNOPS wish to pursue the matter\n regarding under-claimed VAT/MOMS, the Tax Agency advised that a request for a legally binding opinion should be submitted to the Protocol Department (cf. VAT Act/MOMS-loven § 45 (7)), and the Protocol Department should in turn forward the request to the Tax\n Agency for such an opinion.\n \nIn the matter of over-claimed VAT/MOMS, relating to four duplicated expense submissions from 2015, 2016 and 2018 respectively (amounting to DKK 42,308.75), the Protocol Department\n refers to information provided by the Tax Agency, according to which such a matter/request should also be assessed pursuant to the Danish Law on Tax Administration §31 (2). The expenses in question are from 2015, 2016 and 2018, and consequently the deadline\n for ordinary resumption has been exceeded. In dialogue with the Tax Agency the Protocol Department has assessed the request for repayment of duplicated VAT/MOMS reimbursement pursuant to the Law on Tax Administration §32 (1)(4) regarding special circumstances\n for resumption. On the basis of the information provided by UNOPS and scrutinization of the reimbursement process carried out by the Protocol Department (in regards to the four expenses in question), it is the assessment of the Protocol Department that no\n special circumstances exist in this matter. The abovementioned legal guide does not offer opinions to the contrary. The Protocol Department will not pursue the matter of over-claimed VAT/MOMS further.\n \nShould UNOPS have any questions to the above, please do not hesitate to contact the Protocol Department.\n \nKind regards,\nSøren\n \n_______________________________________________________\n \nSØREN SÆRMARK-THOMSEN  /\nSORSAR@UM.DK\nCONSUL / TEAMLEADER / PROTOCOL DEPARTMENT\nDIRECT +45 3392 1191 / MOBILE +45 2156 6253\n \nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN\nPHONE +45 3392 0000 /\nWWW.UM.DK\n \nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n \nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message",
