                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: FCLP: Norway",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: FCLP: Norway",
                        Description = "To: julieda@unops.org\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FCLP: Norway\nBody:\nDear Julie, \nThank you very much for reaching out. \nSuper happy to hear about the interest from Norway in contributing to FCLP! Could I ask how much they are considering? \nIt has indeed been difficult to sign new engagements with Norway for some time due to the fallout of the S3i and the fact that the former ED was of Norwegian nationality. For your background information, the Norwegian Court of Auditors published a report in December containing a rather severe criticism of the Norwegian MFA for their lack of critical scrutiny of UNOPS at the Executive Board. \nLast engagement with Norway was a 34K top-up for the implementation of the maputo accord in April 2024. The last new engagement with Norway was back in April 2021 to support EU accession process for Western Balkans. So quite some time ago... \nNorway does not have any formal restrictions on engagements with UNOPS. But due to the salience of the S3i fallout in Norway, some skepticism may remain among some personnel that are not in the loop on the global relationship between the Norwegian Government and UNOPS. We have a very good and constructive dialogue with the HQ based persons within NORAD and the Norwegian NFA that are responsible for Norway's relationship with UNOPS. They follow our reform process closely and have been complementing UNOPS on our progress, the transparency, etc. \nA way to ease the resistance of your counterpart might be to:I reach out to our Norwegian HQ focal points at NORAD / MFA to make them aware of your ongoing conversations regarding a potential Norwegian contribution to FCLP - and encourage them to explain to your counterpart that it is perfectly legitimate to engage with UNOPS since we have implemented the reforms. \n\nThat you kindly refer your counterpart to the persons responsible for NORAD's / MFA's relationship with UNOPS - to get their take on Norwegian engagements with UNOPS. To initiate this, could I kindly ask for the name, email, position and division/unit of the person you're in contact with? I assume it is someone from NORAD? If so - you could refer your counterpart to Mr. Stein Erik Horjen (Stein.Erik.Horjen@norad.no). Stein Erik is following UNOPS' reform process very closely and knows that there is a great relationship between NORAD's Director General and our Executive Director. In fact, Jorge was invited to be a keynote speaker at the annual NORAD conference last week (unfortunately Jorge couldn't attend as he has to participate in the Executive Board). \nIn case you're dealing with the Norwegian MFA, the relevant person to refer your counterpart to, would be Mr. Constantin Nicolaysen (Constantin.Nicolaysen.Karame@mfa.no) who is a Chief Advisor in their UN Division and responsible for the Norwegian Government's relationship with UNOPS. He is also the Norwegian member of our Executive Board. \nI hope this helps - and as mentioned I would be more than happy to jump on a call to discuss how to approach if you would find it useful. \nIn any case, it would be super good if we could get the Norwegians to contribute to the FCLP - as it would be the first new engagement with them in years. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 3 Feb 2025 at 21:53, Julie Dahan <julieda@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Asbjorn,\nHope this message finds you well.I am glad to inform you that Norway would like to potentially contribute to the pool funds of the FCLP, but they have been a bit hesitant since the UNOPS drama of 2022.\nWould you be able to let me know if any bilateral agreements have been signed between Norway and UNOPS since that time?\nWhat language UNOPS has been using in this situation? How UNOPS is presenting that the situation of 2022 is now resolved ? How UNOPS has been reassuring donors in that situation?\nWith many thanks, Julie\n-- \nJulie Dahan \n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube. Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish. \n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
