                    "00TQx00000L9dwMMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Helsingor Dialogue",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Helsingor Dialogue",
                        Description = "To: msh@di.dk\nCC: JHN@di.dk; CLHA@di.dk; freyavg@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Helsingor Dialogue\nBody:\nDear Marie, \nThank you very much for your feedback and excellent suggestions on how to get some tangible, and concrete examples from the private sector that could inspire the attendants for more action. \nPlease give us a few days to touch base internally with relevant stakeholders to discuss your suggestions after which we will revert to you. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 3 Feb 2025 at 11:13, Marie Gad <msh@di.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn and Freya\n \nThank you for the opportunity to provide input to your concept note on the Helsingor Dialogue.\n\n \nI am happy to send you a few suggestions with this e-mail, and if your calendar allows it, I would suggest a short meeting where we can discuss further how we can support you in\n organizing this very important and timely event.\n \nWith the focus on the need for implementation and results, it would be great to showcase some of the ways in which cross-sector partnerships between international organizations/UN\n agencies and the private sector work together to achieve results. We have a number of concrete examples that could inspire more action.\n \nHere are a few concrete suggestions:\n\n \n\nFor session 1: From Implementation Gaps to Implementation Solutions, it would great to include a private sector actor to\n provide insights on the private sector is pushing implementation for the SDGs. \n\nIt could be the CEO of DI Lars Sandahl Sørensen with a perspective on the private sector as a key partner in reaching the\n SDGs. We are working closely with our member companies on the issue, but also together with our sister organisations across the globe – in Africa, Asia, Latin America and countries in the European neighboring region: read more here\nUdviklingssamarbejder - DI arbejder for økonomisk vækst i verden - DIIt could be Maersk CEO Vincent Clerc or Chairman of the Board Robert Uggla to provide insights on how Maersk is driving\n a sustainable decarbonization of the entire maritime industry – and how cross-sector partnerships can help to overcome some of the barriers that is facing the drive to CO2 neutrality for the private sector.It could be CEO of Novo Nordisk Fonden Mads Krogsgaard Thomsen with a focus on how private foundations can team up with\n development partners in innovative partnerships. One recent example is a new alliance between Novo Nordisk Foundation, Lego Foundation, Grundfos Foundation, the Danish ministry of foreign affairs and UNHCR to ensure lasting and inclusive solutions in humanitarian\n settings.\n\n \n\nFor session 2: Building and bridging: The case of infrastructure, it would also be great to include a private sector angle\n on how to ensure sustainable solutions that create local jobs and knowledge as well as a focus on blended finance solutions\nIt could be Copenhagen Infrastructure Partners Managing Partner Jakob Barüel Poulsen. CIP are driving some innovative projects\n to ensure access to clean energy, e.g. this: Renewable\n Energy Initiative - Global Fashion Agenda\n\n\n \n\nFor session 3: From fragmentation to scale the suggestion above with a focus on the role of private foundations could also\n fit well here, so I copied it in below. Relevant speakers could also be CEO of Lego Foundation Sidsel Marie Kristensen or Executive Director of Grundfos Foundation Kim Nøhr Skibsted\nIt could be CEO of Novo Nordisk Fonden Mads Krogsgaard Thomsen with a focus on how private foundations can team up with\n development partners in innovative partnerships. One recent example is a new alliance between Novo Nordisk Foundation, Lego Foundation, Grundfos Foundation, the Danish ministry of foreign affairs and UNHCR to ensure lasting and inclusive solutions in humanitarian\n settings.\n\n \nFor the list of participants, we would suggest the following additions:\n\nCEO of DI Lars Sandahl SørensenMads Kann-Rasmussen, CEO of VKR HoldingChairman of the Board Robert UgglaExecutive Director of Grundfos Foundation Kim Nøhr SkibstedManaging director of Bestseller Foundation Tine Fisker Henriksen\n \nFinally, we have good experiences with organizing side events or exhibitions of concrete solutions for these types of high-level events, and that could also be a possibility. We\n would be happy to discuss these possibilities further with you, if you have time for a meeting during one of the coming weeks.\n \nPlease do not hesitate to reach our if there is anything else that we can assist you with.\n \nAll the best,\n \nMarie\n\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nMarie Gad\nGlobal Development and Sustainability\nDirector\n\n\n(+45) 3377 3789\n(+45) 2949 4447\n (Mobil)\n\nmsh@di.dk\n\ndi.dk\n \n\n \nRead how DI treats\n and protects \n\npersonal data in DI Privacy Policy\n \n\n\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
