                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000LIo41MAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Potential projects in Gaza",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-07").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Potential projects in Gaza",
                        Description = "To: Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk\nCC: Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Potential projects in Gaza\nBody:\nDear Agnes, \nThank you in advance for putting us in touch with your colleagues in Jerusalem. I was a bit unsure if dealings with Gaza and Syria was an HQ based thing due to the political attention to the matters. \nWith regards to the US funding pause, our preliminary estimates is that 26 of our projects are affected with an estimated impact on delivery in 2025 around 150M USD - which is about 5% of the total projected delivery for this year. \nIt may be of particular interest to the UK, that in addition to the UNOPS hosted engagements, two of the projects are multi-donor where the UK is a donor. These are the UNVM (Yemen) and Access to Health (in Myanmar). In those cases, use of UK funds is on pause for the time being, as required by the Executive Order and the subsequent State Department directives. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nOn Tue, 4 Feb 2025 at 13:52, Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Asbjorn,\n \nMany thanks for being in touch.\n\n \nWe’re still recovering from last week’s Boards! Although I think the UNOPS decisions came out in a decent place in the end.\n \nThis is definitely one to raise with our BCG in Jerusalem who manage that portfolio of work – let me look up who the best people to speak to are and come back to you.\n \nI also wanted to check in with you on any info you can share about how the US EOs might be affecting UNOPS?\n \nAll the best,\n \nAgnes\n \nAgnes Annells| UN Development Agency Coordination and UN Women/UNOPS Lead | UN Partnerships Unit | Education, Gender, and Equalities\n Directorate | Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office | Abercrombie House, Eaglesham Road, Hairmyres, East Kilbride, G75 8EA |  agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk\n | www.fcdo.gov.uk\n\n \nMy working week is Tuesday to Friday.\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 04 February 2025 12:12\n\nTo: Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Sally Clifford <Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Potential projects in Gaza\n\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Agnes,\n\nI am writing to you to initiate a dialogue about potential projects in Gaza. I hope that you might be able to connect me with your colleagues dealing with UK interventions in Gaza? \n\nAs you know, the situation in Gaza remains dire, with ongoing humanitarian needs and a fragile security situation. There is a massive and urgent need for humanitarian aid. At UNOPS we are currently\n exploring several projects that directly address these needs and might be in the interest of the UK:\n\n\nStrengthening the Electricity Supply System: This project aims to improve living conditions and address interrupted critical\n and essential services for the most affected Palestinians in Gaza by reconstructing and strengthening the electricity supply system with renewable energy. This aligns with the UK's commitment to promoting stability and supporting essential services in Gaza.\nSafe Rubble Removal and Recycling: This project focuses on clearing away war debris, a critical prerequisite for early recovery\n and reconstruction interventions, and the provision of essential services in Gaza. This project aligns with the UK's commitment to supporting reconstruction and recovery efforts in Gaza.\nHumanitarian Fuel for Gaza Project: This project aims to procure and deliver fuel to Gaza in support of humanitarian operations\n and essential services. This aligns with the UK's commitment to supporting humanitarian relief efforts in Gaza.\n\nI have attached a brief overview of these potential projects for your review. All of them are scalable. We believe these projects have the potential to make a significant impact on the lives of the\n Palestinian people in Gaza while aligning with UK objectives.\n\nWe would be grateful for the opportunity to discuss these projects further with you and explore potential UK support. \n\nPlease let me know if you or your relevant colleagues would be  available for a call in the coming weeks.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nAll the best,\n\nAsbjørn\n\n-- \n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation\n\n\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
