                        Name = "Email: Summary from ED meeting with PR of Finland, 30 January 2025",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-10").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Summary from ED meeting with PR of Finland, 30 January 2025",
                        Description = "To: rahulm@unops.org; freyavg@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nCC: annag@unops.org; mikaelag@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Summary from ED meeting with PR of Finland, 30 January 2025\nBody:\nDear Rahul, Freya, Asbjorn and Naimo,\nPlease see below a summary from the recent meeting between Jorge and the PR of Finland in New York:\n Meeting with H.E. Ms. Elina Kalkku, Permanent Representative of Finland (30 January 2025 / Briefing)UNOPS participants: Jorge, Freya, OonaThe PR was accompanied by Mr. Ramses Malaty, Deputy Director General, Department for Development Policy, and Mr. Antti Virtanen, First Secretary, Permanent Mission of Finland.The ED briefed the PR on his upcoming mission to the Middle East. He shared updates on the UN2720 Mechanism, highlighting its success in promoting transparency and accountability. Additionally, he noted that UNOPS has scaled up its fuel operations in Gaza, now assuming responsibility for fuel distribution inside Gaza. The ED underscored the critical importance of the early recovery phase, particularly activities such as the removal of rubble and debris. As UNOPS celebrates its 30th anniversary in 2025, the ED reflected on this milestone as an opportunity for UNOPS and Member States to evaluate the progress of the reforms achieved through the Comprehensive Response Plan (CRP). He reported that the CRP has been successfully completed (with the exception of PID), and that recovery efforts of the funds related to S3i  led by OLA are advancing well. UNOPS is looking forward to the third party review on the CRP which will confirm its completion and be addressed at the 2025 Annual Session. The PR congratulated the ED on the reform agenda and expressed appreciation for the informative closed session on the recovery efforts held earlier in the week. The PR and ED discussed the letter sent by anonymous UNOPS personnel to the Board.Finally, the PR and ED reflected on the role of the Executive Board and agreed on the importance of strengthening collaboration and coherence among agencies sharing the Board. The ED and PR discussed initiatives such as organizing joint interactive dialogues and showcasing project stories from the country level to enrich the quality of the discussions at the Board. The Joint Meeting of the Boards in June 2024 (focused on the HDP Nexus) was highlighted as a successful example of these efforts. Additionally, the PR shared insights from her weekly meetings with EU and Nordic delegations, noting a shared concern that a communication gap appears to exist between the information available to delegates and PRs on Board-related topics.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions!\nKind regards,Oona\n-- \nOona Anttila | Management Specialist | Executive Office | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +4553589617 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000LOReBMAX",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "freyavg@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "annag@unops.org", "asbjornb@unops.org", "rahulm@unops.org", "mikaelag@unops.org" },
