                new (
                    "00TQx00000LOSP4MAP",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Summary from ED/DED meeting with DPR of Denmark, 28 January 2025",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-10").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Summary from ED/DED meeting with DPR of Denmark, 28 January 2025",
                        Description = "To: freyavg@unops.org; rahulm@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nCC: annag@unops.org; hilaryb@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Summary from ED/DED meeting with DPR of Denmark, 28 January 2025\nBody:\nDear Freya, Rahul, Asbjorn and Naimo,\nPlease see below the summary of the meeting between the DPR and ED/DED on 28 Jan in New York:\n Meeting with H.E. Mr. Erik Laursen, Deputy Permanent Representative of Denmark (28 January 2025 / Briefing)UNOPS participants: Jorge, Kirstine, OonaThe DPR apologized on the PR’s behalf as she was not able to join the meeting due to an urgent Security Council meeting. The DPR expressed his appreciation of the closed briefing to the Executive Board on the funds recovery related to S3i (with UN OLA), organized on the same morning (28 Jan). He also commended the UNOPS reform process and expressed his full support.The ED thanked the DPR for the strong partnership between Denmark and UNOPS. He provided an update on the preparations for the week of the CEB meeting and the Copenhagen Dialogue in May 2025. The aim is to establish the Copenhagen Dialogue as an annual forum to discuss the implementation gap and address bottlenecks in delivering solutions at scale. UNOPS plans to invite the Minister for Foreign Affairs of Denmark to open the dialogue alongside the Deputy Secretary-General, who has already confirmed her participation.The ED briefed the DPR on UNOPS activities supporting the humanitarian response in Gaza, emphasizing the real-time online tracking of consignments going through the UN2720 Mechanism to ensure accountability and transparency. The ED expressed his readiness to update the Security Council with USG Kaag if members found it useful. Additionally, the ED shared details of his upcoming mission to Syria, Lebanon and Gaza to explore how UNOPS can further support the region. The DPR and ED discussed the implications of the US funding pause. The ED explained that the biggest impact of the pause on UNOPS operations is in the Middle East (to which we expect waivers) and the Hosted Entities (e.g. StopTB). The DPR and ED discussed the letter sent by anonymous UNOPS personnel to the Board.The DED D&P provided an update on her upcoming mission to Myanmar to visit UNOPS teams and projects. Action Point: Share data on the percentage of international and local personnel in Myanmar with the Permanent Mission. Oona ANTTILA\nKind regards,Oona\n-- \nOona Anttila | Management Specialist | Executive Office | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +4553589617 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
