                new (
                    "00TQx00000LQNeTMAX",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: FA comments Feb 2025: UNFPA MOU Discussion",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-07").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: FA comments Feb 2025: UNFPA MOU Discussion",
                        Description = "To: Rebecca.White@fcdo.gov.uk\nCC: stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk; linda.sloan@fcdo.gov.uk; onile-ere@unfpa.org; obezo@unfpa.org; kortekaas@unfpa.org; rhona.mcdonald@fcdo.gov.uk; rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org; stephan.ulrich@undp.org; lbarusya@unicef.org; xiaoman.zhang@unwomen.org; ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk; kevin.leitch@fcdo.gov.uk; Gareth.Bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk; Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk; Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk; asbjornb@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: FA comments Feb 2025: UNFPA MOU Discussion\nBody:\nDear Rebecca and colleagues, \nWe are pleased to share with you attached further comments and feedback on the draft Framework Agreement, in response to the latest comments provided by the FCDO.\nWe also note the feedback from Louise at the time that, as FCDO is now a fully merged department, some policies relating to the framework have changed and in the absence of further context from us, it is difficult for you to agree to revert to historic positions when FCDO policy has moved on. There are, however, a couple of areas where extensive discussions resulted in agreement ( such as the audit discharge annex)  and where we would appreciate not reverting and re-negotiating, further delaying this process.\nWe have flagged some areas where further clarity is needed; though there may be others after UN agencies review; on the financial reporting (33),  procurement (para 76) and asset management (para 78). \nOn communication and Branding -Para 90 and related annex, we would highly recommend keeping the detailed planning of communications efforts and assets to the programme document, rather than a legal agreement. \nOrganization Payment Request Form - Annex 1, the form has a number of issues ( as discussed our financial rules stipulate that payment must be in advance, our operational currency is USD, for payments in full or a first tranche this information is not available). Can we revert to the simpler form of the payment request form agreed previously. \nAudit discharge certification - Annex 2 - this form has been discussed and removed. We do not  audit all projects automatically and we cannot implement a pre-arranged audit. \nVisibility statement - Annex 3 -  we would request keeping the detailed planning of communications efforts and assets to the programme document, rather than a legal agreement. \nOne the Due Diligence assessment, Annex 4 a separate call was held on 7 November and the draft is attached. \nPlease note, we are sharing these comments in order to move this process along. However, while our approach on most items are in line with that of other UN agencies based on the history of the negotiations,  we stress that considering the long lapse in time, other UN agencies still need to review the draft FA after we have feedback from FCDO and hopefully a cleaner document.All the best, \nAsa\n\nOn Mon, Jan 13, 2025 at 6:31 AM Rebecca White <Rebecca.White@fcdo.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Asa,\n\n \nHappy New Year.\n\n \nI just wanted to follow up on the below about anticipated timelines, please could you let us know when to expect comments?\n \nThanks,\n\n \n\nBest Regards,\n\n \nBecca White\n \nCommercial Lead- Grants and Multi-Laterals- Grants Hub\n\nProgramme Delivery Commercial, Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office, KCS\n \nPlease follow\n@FCDOProcurement\non X!\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n\n\nFrom: Rebecca White <Rebecca.White@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\n\nSent: 27 November 2024 15:15\n\nTo: Gareth Bartlett <Gareth.Bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk>; Stephen Berwick <stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk>; Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>; Linda Sloan <linda.sloan@fcdo.gov.uk>; Oladele Onile-Ere <onile-ere@unfpa.org>; Maria Monica Obezo <obezo@unfpa.org>;\n Vanessa Kortekaas <kortekaas@unfpa.org>; Sally Clifford <Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk>; Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>; Rhona McDonald <rhona.mcdonald@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>; Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>; Leona Barusya <lbarusya@unicef.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Xiaoman Zhang <xiaoman.zhang@unwomen.org>; Ellie Young <ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nSubject: RE: UNFPA MOU Discussion\n\n\n\n \nHi Asa,\n\n \nI hope you’re having a good week.\n\n \nI just wanted to follow up on anticipated timelines, have legal colleagues advised on when we can expect their comments?\n \nThanks,\n \n\nBest Regards,\n\n \nBecca White\n \nCommercial Lead- Grants and Multi-Laterals- Grants Hub\n\nProgramme Delivery Commercial, Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office, KCS\n \nPlease follow\n@FCDOProcurement\non X!\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Gareth Bartlett <Gareth.Bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\n\nSent: 11 November 2024 14:11\n\nTo: Rebecca White <Rebecca.White@fcdo.gov.uk>; Stephen Berwick <stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk>; Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>;\n Linda Sloan <linda.sloan@fcdo.gov.uk>; Oladele Onile-Ere <onile-ere@unfpa.org>; Maria Monica Obezo <obezo@unfpa.org>; Vanessa Kortekaas\n <kortekaas@unfpa.org>; Sally Clifford <Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk>; Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>; Rhona McDonald\n <rhona.mcdonald@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>; Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>; Leona Barusya <lbarusya@unicef.org>;\n Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Xiaoman Zhang <xiaoman.zhang@unwomen.org>; Ellie Young <ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nSubject: Re: UNFPA MOU Discussion\n\n\n \nOFFICIAL\n \n\nDear all, \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you again for your time on Thursday. It was a really useful discussion. \n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached the updated DDA annex based on the conversation. I have also attached separate guidance that will be shared with FCDO programme teams setting\n out the due diligence process when working with the UN. If you have any additional thoughts or considerations on either document, please do let us know. It may also be useful to have similar guidance for your colleagues to raise any issues with the relevant\n UK Partnerships Lead. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe look forward to hearing about timelines for receipt of the next round of comments and anticipated agreement date. Thank you for all of your work on this to date.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nGareth\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\nGareth Bartlett\n| Senior Commercial Officer\n| Multilaterals & Grants | Grants Hub\nForeign, Commonwealth & Development Office | Abercrombie House \nE-Mail:\nGareth.Bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk\nMobile: +447917209261 \n \n \n\n\n \n\n \nOFFICIAL\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Rebecca White\n\nSent: 30 October 2024 3:41 PM\n\nTo: Rebecca White <Rebecca.White@fcdo.gov.uk>; Gareth Bartlett <Gareth.Bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk>; Stephen Berwick <stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk>;\n Aasa Dahlvik <dahlvik@unfpa.org>; Linda Sloan <linda.sloan@fcdo.gov.uk>; Oladele Onile-Ere <onile-ere@unfpa.org>; Maria Monica Obezo\n <obezo@unfpa.org>; Vanessa Kortekaas <kortekaas@unfpa.org>; Sally Clifford <Sally.Clifford@fcdo.gov.uk>; Agnes Annells <Agnes.Annells@fcdo.gov.uk>;\n Rhona McDonald <rhona.mcdonald@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nCc: Rafael Martinez Gil <rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org>; Stephan Ulrich <stephan.ulrich@undp.org>; Leona Barusya <lbarusya@unicef.org>;\n Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Xiaoman Zhang <xiaoman.zhang@unwomen.org>; Ellie Young <ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk>\n\nSubject: UNFPA MOU Discussion\n\nWhen: 07 November 2024 15:30-16:30.\n\nWhere: Microsoft Teams Meeting; UK_AH_241_Hybrid VC (6) \n\n \n\n\n \n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n\nMicrosoft Teams\nNeed help?\n\n\nJoin\n the meeting now\n\n\nMeeting ID:\n327 534 746 922\n\n\nPasscode:\nbjiAjU\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDial in by phone\n\n\n+44 20 7660 8164,,919130001#\nUnited Kingdom, City of London\n\n\nFind a local number\n\n\nPhone conference ID:\n919 130 001#\n\n\nJoin on a video conferencing device\n\n\nTenant key:\nteams@fcdo2.onpexip.com\n\n\nVideo ID:\n128 187 425 3\n\n\nMore info\n\nFor organizers:\nMeeting\n options\n|\nReset dial-in PIN\n\n\nYour activity on Teams may be monitored in line with relevant UK legislation.\n\n\nPrivacy and security\n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n \n\n\n\nFollow us online: www.gov.uk/fcdo\n\n\nThis email is intended for the addressee(s) only: All messages sent and received by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office may be monitored in line with relevant\n\nUK legislation",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000LQNeTMAX",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "linda.sloan@fcdo.gov.uk", "stephen.berwick@fcdo.gov.uk", "rafael.martinezgil@unwomen.org", "stephan.ulrich@undp.org", "onile-ere@unfpa.org", "xiaoman.zhang@unwomen.org", "lbarusya@unicef.org", "dahlvik@unfpa.org", "ellie.young@fcdo.gov.uk", "kortekaas@unfpa.org", "teams@fcdo2.onpexip.com", "rebecca.white@fcdo.gov.uk", "asbjornb@unops.org", "kevin.leitch@fcdo.gov.uk", "rhona.mcdonald@fcdo.gov.uk", "sally.clifford@fcdo.gov.uk", "gareth.bartlett@fcdo.gov.uk", "obezo@unfpa.org", "agnes.annells@fcdo.gov.uk" },
