                new (
                    "00TQx00000LQToqMAH",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Feedback from meeting with Human Practice Foundation?",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-21").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Feedback from meeting with Human Practice Foundation?",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: elenage@unops.org; rainerf@unops.org; freyavg@unops.org; sharonle@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; amyn@unops.org; emmaak@unops.org; agnesw@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Feedback from meeting with Human Practice Foundation?\nBody:\nDear Asbjorn\nThank you for the follow up.\nThere was no disagreement as such. I think we are still at a stage where we are learning about each other. We took them through our process of how we implement infrastructure projects and the specific procurement processes for works. At the moment we only see a potential to offer transactional procurement services. It’s entirely up to them to decide to engage us and we are here to support in any way we can. We suggested that they send us the specs for procurement of items for schools that we can source from the UN Web Buy when they are ready to share the information, and we can share the procurement and our costs with them. We heard that they are considering to target around 160 schools, each having distinct requirements. The CD is also facing a dilemma of how many schools to reach and what we provide to them with available resources because the need always seems to outweigh the available financial resources.\nEmma, Agnes, Mariko, Gash and I attended the meeting. I copy Emma and Agnes in case they would like to add further observations.\nBest regards,Fumie Arimizu | Partnerships Advisor | Partnerships Development Office | UNOPS East and Southern Africa | Nairobi, Kenya | Tel:+254 701 821 256 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n2025年1月21日(火) 20:46 Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>:\nDear colleagues in Nairobi\nI understand that yesterday you met with the country director from Human Practice Foundation in Nairobi. I hope this meeting went well, that we have started the due diligence process and that we would soon be able to outline the division of labour between UNOPS and Human Practice Foundation as we discussed with them before the Christmas break. \nEarlier today I was contacted by the CEO of Human Practice Foundation as she had the impression from her feedback that there was a disagreement on the potential collaboration. \nAs the LEGO Foundation will have their board meeting on March 25, it would be important that we can present a concept note / proposal to the board that has been agreed between Human Practice Foundation and UNOPS. \nMight it be possible to outline the disagreements that occurred during your meeting yesterday - so that I can also try to align expectations with the CEO of the foundation here in Copenhagen? I am naturally available to meet online at your convenience if easier. \nThank you very much in advance. \nBest regards,Asbjørn\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
