                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000Lfpc5MAB",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Follow-up on proposal discussion",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-17").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Follow-up on proposal discussion",
                        Description = "To: aslnal@um.dk\nCC: claudiar@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org; nathaliea@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Follow-up on proposal discussion\nBody:\nDear Aslak,\n\nThank you for your email. It was a pleasure to meet you as well, and I appreciate you forwarding the proposal to the relevant units.\n\nRegarding the new embassy in Tunisia, we look forward to its opening. Once settled, my colleagues Nathalie Angibeau, Country Manager for Tunisia and Claudia Rosano, Partnerships Specialist would be pleased to arrange a courtesy visit.\nThank you again and wishing you a lovely week ahead. \n\nBest regards,\nNaimo\nOn Fri, Feb 7, 2025 at 3:40 PM Aslak Alexander Schou Nalepa <aslnal@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Naimo,\n \nThanks a lot for your email, and thank you for taking the time to meet me in the autumn. It was very helpful for me to hear about your\n engagements in Tunisia and a pleasure to meet you.\n \nMy apologies for the very late response to your follow-up suggestions. As I might have mentioned we don’t have any available funds\n in our unit. But I will transmit the proposal and suggestions to the relevant other units here at the MFA and then they will get back directly to you if there is an interest as well as available funds.\n \nWishing you a good weekend.\n \nBest regards,\nAslak\n\n\n\n\n________________________________________________\nASLAK ALEXANDER SCHOU NALEPA\nHEAD OF SECTION /\nMIDDLE EAST AND NORTHERN AFRICA (MENA)\nDIRECT:\n+45 3392 1795\nMOBILE: +45 2153 0438\n \nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS OF DENMARK\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 KØBENHAVN K\nTLF. +45 3392 0000 /\nUM.DK\n \nSÅDAN\n BEHANDLER VI PERSONOPLYSNINGER\n \nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message\n \n \n \n\n\nFra: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\n\nSendt: 10. januar 2025 10:55\n\nTil: Aslak Alexander Schou Nalepa <aslnal@um.dk>\n\nCc: Claudia ROSANO <claudiar@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nEmne: Follow-up on proposal discussion\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Aslak, \n \nWishing you a happy 2025!\n \nIt was an absolute pleasure meeting you and once again thank you so much for welcoming me at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. \n \nI wanted to kindly follow-up on our recent discussion regarding the proposal focused on developing technical and financing models to maximize access to solar energy\n and energy-efficient cooling solutions in the date and dairy value chains across five areas in Tunisia. For reference, please find attached the proposal as well as an overview of UNOPS’ presence in North Africa. \n \nTo summarise, the proposal focuses on enhancing access to solar energy and energy-efficient cooling solutions in Tunisia's date and dairy value chains. It aims\n to develop technical and financing models that will benefit over 3,000 farmers, fostering sustainable livelihoods and addressing root causes for migration. Agriculture contributes 10% to Tunisia’s GDP and employs 16% of the workforce, with dates accounting\n for 12% of the total value of agricultural exports. The proposal is developed in collaboration with UNEP and incorporates a multi-donor funding model, making it easy for Denmark to take part in together with other partners. \n \nAs we discussed, there is much alignment between this project and the DAPP priorities; climate action, youth employment, and migration. \n \nIn the meeting, I also noted that Denmark could potentially be interested in supporting initiatives such as these projects carried out by UNOPS on behalf of our\n partners in Tunisia: Support to Tunisia's Border Control and Management of Migration Flows (Italy), \nSupport for Maritime Border Management (EU), and Procurement Service Project for land border control (Italy). Adding additional support to successful and well-established projects offers significant value for money for Denmark. \n \nMy colleagues Claudia, Asbjørn and I would very much appreciate a virtual meeting with your team and relevant colleagues at MIGSTAB in week 2 or 4 to explore these\n collaboration opportunities. Could you kindly let us know when this might work for you? \n \nBest regards,\nNaimo\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\nNaimo Hassan Hirsi\n| Partnerships Analyst | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Tel: +45 2683 4878 |\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n.",
