                new (
                    "00TQx00000LirJAMAZ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UTP PD feedback",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-18").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UTP PD feedback",
                        Description = "To: eleneag@unops.org\nCC: erik@consultantsfordevelopment.dk; nsl@tanacph.com; marysiaz@unops.org; valentynp@unops.org; marthaas@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; massimodi@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UTP PD feedback\nBody:\nDear Elene,\nThis is very well received. Let me go through and then get back to you later this week with comments and suggestions.\nAll the best,\n- Erik\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com\n\n\nDen 18. feb. 2025 kl. 11.25 skrev Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>:Dear Erik,\nThank you for this note. Enclosed please find our updated programme document for your review. We tried to clean the text as much as possible, but we look forward to your feedback.\nLet us know if a joint discussion would be helpful.\nWith thanks and kind regards,Elene\nOn Mon, Feb 10, 2025 at 10:50 PM Erik Bryld <eb@tanacph.com> wrote:\nDear Elene,\nThank you for the heads up and for this first draft. \nOne comment that you should consider is whether you can find wording that accommodates the wish for EU-compliant processes and products. Denmark is a strong advocate for Ukraine’s EU accession. This is part of the Danish strategy for Ukraine. So, while UNOPS will use its own rules and procedures, there must be some sort of guarantee that processes and output quality are EU compliant. \nI look forward to receiving the draft document. \nAll the best,\n- Erik   \n\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com<Tana_logo_turkis_e-mailsignatur.jpg>\n\n\nDen 10. feb. 2025 kl. 17.03 skrev Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>:\nDear Erik,\nMany thanks for your swift feedback and great to hear that we have a bit more time to continue working on this. \nOur HQ is still reviewing the document and more comments may follow, but I thought to share with you the document as it stands now. Let me also please keep the reservation on the status of the document, since it may cause some complications down the road. Also note that throughout the text we have removed references to compliance to EU rules and regulations, since UNOPS can only commit itself to its own rules.\nI'm sure there will be more questions and we'd be happy to discuss it in more detail.\nWith kind regards,Elene\nOn Sat, Feb 8, 2025 at 1:03 PM Erik Bryld <eb@tanacph.com> wrote:\nDear Elene,\nThanks for the mail and feedback.\nIn terms of timing, we have a bit more time on our hands, so you can wait till the end of next week with forwarding the updated document.\nOn the status of the document. You sign the funding agreement, which is a separate document with all the legal aspects including disbursements etc. The project document provides the basis for the funding, which the Minister signs. It should be implemented as described. However, the document is very flexible and changes from outputs, outcomes and other aspects may happen based on e-mail exchange with the MFA.\nOn the procurement element. We discussed this yesterday and it can likely be waved. So, do delete it for now.\nThe UTPCC has now changed its name to become the Mykolaiv Steering Committee. This will be identical to the current SC. This means the composition will be Mykolaiv City, region and the MFA. Note that all final decisions are made by the MFA (EUNABO). Legally, the Committee is only advisory. The Committee will meet at least quarterly, but can also meet anytime there is a need to do so. It should not have significant ifluence on the timelines. But, in light of your considerations, I will take this up with the MFA. The details concerning the Committee are still being assessed by the MFA.  \n\nI hope this clarifies it and look forward to reading your inputs.\nAll the best,\n- Erik\n\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com\n<Tana_logo_turkis_e-mailsignatur.jpg>\n\n\n\n\n<EC UTP PD UNOPS - Draft 02.docx>\n\n<18 Feb UTP PD UNOPS - Draft 02.docx>",
