                new (
                    "00TQx00000OGcDMMA1",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: Proposal for Meeting_ Thank you and follow up",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-04-09").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: Proposal for Meeting_ Thank you and follow up",
                        Description = "To: eleneag@unops.org\nCC: massimodi@unops.org; valentynp@unops.org; marysiaz@unops.org; arunn@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Proposal for Meeting_ Thank you and follow up\nBody:\nDear Elene,\nI suggest we meet on Friday at 14:00. We can arrange it online, because my colleagues form Paris will be connected as well.\nWould that work for you?\nThank you.\nRegards,\nKateryna\n\n \nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, April 8, 2025 1:58 PM\n\nTo: ELISHYIEVA Kateryna <Kateryna.ELISHYIEVA@coebank.org>\n\nCc: Massimo DIANA <massimodi@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Proposal for Meeting_ Thank you and follow up\n \n\n\nDear Kateryna,\n\n\n \n\n\nSo good to hear from you and thank you for exploring the partnership with UNOPS on the HOME project. \n\n\n \n\n\nWe would be happy to meet you. Would Thursday's (April 10) first half of the day work for you (10 am or noon)? or Friday (April 11) 11 am or 2 pm? Massimo is on the mission this week and will return on Saturday, so we will come together with\n our Head of Programme Marysia Zapasnik and Infrastructure Advisor Arun Narayanan.\n\n\n \n\n\nLet us know what works best for you and we'll adjust.\n\n\n \n\n\nLooking forward to working with you closely in the coming weeks.\n\n\n \n\n\nWith kind regards,\n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Apr 7, 2025 at 8:36 PM ELISHYIEVA Kateryna <Kateryna.ELISHYIEVA@coebank.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Massimo, dear Elene,\nThank you once again for the meeting we had.\nI would like to reach out to propose another meeting with you to better understand your expertise and capacity related to the new TA project I briefly mentioned\n during our discussion. I am referring to the HOME Project, which we are implementing together with the Ministry of Development on the compensation scheme for destroyed houses (EUR 100 million loan). Our future the technical assistance (TA) to the Ministry\n will cover:\n- Support for the work undertaken by the Ministry and local commissions involved in implementing the compensation mechanism, and technical expertise required\n to support beneficiaries (Ukrainians).\n- Operationalization of the next phase of the compensation mechanism, focusing on construction of housing units.\nPlease let me know if you would be interested in meeting to share more about your experience in implementing similar projects. I would be happy to learn more.\nThank you very much.\nBest regards, \n\nKateryna\n \nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, March 21, 2025 5:14 PM\n\nTo: ELISHYIEVA Kateryna <Kateryna.ELISHYIEVA@coebank.org>\n\nCc: Massimo DIANA <massimodi@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Thank you and follow up\n \n\n\nDear Kateryna,\n\n \n\nIt was a great pleasure to meet yesterday. Thank\n you for sharing your views and vision for CEB support to the recovery of Ukraine, particularly in the health sector.\n\n \n\nAs discussed, I've attached our initial concept\n note on supporting Prosthetic and Orthotic capacity building in Ukrainian medical universities. This is a preliminary draft, and we're happy to develop and present a more targeted intervention for Kharkiv or other universities like Ternopil, should this area\n be of interest to you.\n\n \n\nRegarding HEAL, our overall budget is USD 7.6 million,\n and the UNOPS management fee for this intervention is 6.18%. Please note, this fee can vary depending on the specific engagement. Let me also say that our colleagues at the Ministry of Health and the World Bank mentioned they would rather be sharing HEAL-related\n information with you directly, which I trust you will receive shortly.\n\n \n\nPlease don't hesitate to reach out if you have any\n questions about our services or if we can be of further assistance.\n\n \n\nWishing you a great weekend ahead.\n\n \n\nWIth kind regards,\n\n \n\nElene\n\n\n\n\nElene Agladze\n|Partnerships Specialist | Ukraine Multi-Country Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel: +380 956 00 1880 |\nFollow us on\n social media and subscribe to\n our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDISCLAIMER: \n\nLes informations contenues dans ce message et/ou toutes les pièces jointes sont\n\nréservées à l'attention et à l'utilisation de leur destinataire et peuvent être\n\nconfidentielles. Si vous n'êtes pas destinataire de ce message, vous êtes\n\ninformé que vous l'avez reçu par erreur et que toute utilisation en est\n\ninterdite. Dans ce cas, vous êtes prié de le détruire et d'en informer la\n\nBanque de Développement du Conseil de l'Europe. Tout message électronique est\n\nsusceptible d'altération. La CEB décline toute responsabilité au titre de ce\n\nmessage s'il a été altéré, déformé ou falsifié.\n\nThe information in this message and/or any attachments is intended solely for\n\nthe attention and use of the named addressee and may be confidential. If you are\n\nnot the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that you have received this\n\ntransmittal in error and that any use of it is prohibited. In such a case please\n\ndelete this message and kindly notify the Council of Europe Development Bank\n\naccordingly. E-mails are susceptible to alteration. CEB shall not be liable\n\nfor the message if altered, changed or falsified.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000OGcDMMA1",
