                    "00TQx00000OuEc7MAF",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: UNOPS - WFP CPO Meeting",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-25").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: UNOPS - WFP CPO Meeting",
                        Description = "To: anneclaireh@unops.org\nCC: betty.ka@wfp.org; martina@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: UNOPS - WFP CPO Meeting\nBody:\nDear Anne-Claire,\n \nI hope this message finds you well. I wanted to take a moment to thank you for your time and the insightful discussion we had recently.\n \nDuring our conversation, we agreed to exchange our spend profiles to jointly recommend categories that could potentially be transferred, sub-delegated to either of our agencies for more efficiencies.\n \nFrom the initial discussion we have had between our Director Supply Chain, Betty Ka and Martin Arevalo, there were indications of opportunities within\nagricultural practices, including but not limited to equipment, infrastructure, and road maintenance.\n\nAdditionally, I would like to request that we also consider the\nengineering and construction, professional services (such as consultancy) and Technology categories in our recommendations.\n\nI believe these could provide further benefits and efficiencies.\n\nI have also added the food procurement overview for your information and potential queries.\n \nThank you once again for your time and collaboration. \n\nWith thanks,\nRainatou\n \n \n \nRainatou Baillet\nChief Procurement, SCDP\nSupply Chain and Delivery Division\n \nVia Cesare Giulio Viola 68/70 – 00148 Rome, Italy\nT +39 066513 4241  M +39 344 015 4010  FoodSat 1301-4241\n\nrainatou.baillet@wfp.org\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nThe information contained in this electronic message and any attachments is intended for specific individuals or entities, and may be confidential, proprietary or privileged. If you are not the intended recipient, please notify the sender immediately, delete\n this message and do not disclose, distribute or copy it to any third party or otherwise use this message. The content of this message does not necessarily reflect the official position of the World Food Programme. Electronic messages are not secure or error\n free and may contain viruses or may be delayed, and the sender is not liable for any of these occurrences. The sender reserves the right to monitor, record and retain electronic messages.",
