                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Reunião sobre os projectos FSIP e FNPP Angola",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-19").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Reunião sobre os projectos FSIP e FNPP Angola",
                        Description = "To: entelas@unops.org\nCC: elenage@unops.org; carolinaq@unops.org; martina@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Reunião sobre os projectos FSIP e FNPP Angola\nBody:\nHi Entela, \nHere are the budget for each ot the options.\n1 - Full PMU support 60 months2 - BoT for 24 months3 - Project Kickoff 12 months4 - TA for 60 months\nThe partner FAO requested proposals for the 3 scenarios and we proposed the 4th one. These are draft proposals for their understanding of how we can collaborate with them, thus in case of any forth moving we need to redo the budgets accordingly and then hold the PAC. My suggestion is that IPAS, PAC and all formal procedures should take place once we have some sort of green light from the partner, but confirm if so or not. \nCom os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Mon, 19 May 2025 at 15:01, Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Nuno, \ncan you share also the budgets with us please? Google sheet version. \nSo, just to understand, of these versions will be chosen only one? \nAre we going to organize a PAC for these propositions? \nThank you Entela \nEntela Sula | Head of Partnerships Development and Communication | Central Africa Multi-Country Office - RDC, RCA, RC, Angola, Burundi, Cameroun, Comores, Equatorial Guinea, Gabon, Madagascar, Rwanda, Seychelles, Mauritius, Sao Tome & Principe, Capo Verde | Yaounde, Cameroun | Tel: +237 698 403050 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Tue, May 13, 2025 at 5:56 PM Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org> wrote:\nDear colleagues\nWe have prepared the 3 proposals with budget to present to FAO.12 Month Project kickoff24 Month Back on track60 Month full scope PMU\nThe 4th option of Technical assistance has been discarded by FAO, despite that it remains a possibility that we could continue to develop if they request. \nNotes:1 - The budgets are shown in a GEF/UNDP format2 - The fees are calculated from the Pricing tool, but we still need to know if we can lower the fees to 6% as in UNDP GEF projects. 3 - The documents need final revision before submission. 4 - FAO is anxiously waiting for these documents, so the faster we revise these documents the better.\n@Entela SULA The budgets need revision from a partnerships specialist to ensure congruence with our policy, please inform who could do this checking. \n\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Mon, 12 May 2025 at 15:04, Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org> wrote:\nGood afternoon Entela and Elena, \nFollowing this morning's meeting between the FAO team and UNOPS, we are now sharing the highlights of the meeting and actions to develop in the next few days. \n1- Meeting held to present the four forms of collaborations taylored for this project. (only the slides were presented so far, no proposal or budget was yet shared with FAO)2 - In the meeting there were four FAO's HQ colleagues but also from one Asia office liaison where they have been discussing UNOPS collaborations in Timor-Leste.3- FAO informed that the proposals are exactly aligned with their expectations except the Technical Assistance modality that would be difficult to adapt to GEF type of funding and requirements. 4 - In GEF9, GEF will allow for Capacity building budget lines and then this TA option could be designed to fit.5 - Until now they have shared 2 projects for Angola (just the budgets) but there are 2 others that will be shared in the near future.6 - FAO made a few comments/questions :           a) are these budgets just for one project or for a project portfolio that could share the allocated resources?           b) Can the PM for this TA be also a M&E expert to assist them do the Terminal reports?           c) For the TA can it be part-time support from the PM Expert.           d) Each of the collaboration forms is very much what is needed and what they are looking for, but the budgets are higher than the available funds for the project, so they need to assess internally how to adapt to the GEF budget format and for that they need the details of each budget. 7  - They are expecting the documents to be sent no later than tomorrow, and they will respond no later than this week. 8 -  They have urgency in advancing with this collaboration and the expectation is also that this collaboration could expand to  other countries at regional level. \nWe will now develop the budgets in a customized high level format and share them with our team later today or tomorrow so we can discuss before sharing with FAO.   @Martin AREVALO please add any subject/comment that I might have missed in my notes. \nCom os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Fri, 9 May 2025 at 11:41, Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org> wrote:\nDear MArtin,\nThank you for the very good discussion on the strategies and here is the presentation with the links to the documents of all 4 types of contract. \nCom os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Thu, 8 May 2025 at 11:08, Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\nPerfect.Check my calendar.\nMartín Arévalo de León | Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 | www.unops.org Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Thu, May 8, 2025 at 12:03 PM Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Martin, just spoke to the local team. The update is that the government signed the document and they were not expecting, they were expecting the government on board only 1 year or so from now. What I understood is that the door is not shut and we can still propose our services, especially because the time frame has been reduced and they need our efficiency.Let's have a meeting tomorrow morning to go through the 4 proposals, we are creating a presentation summarizing each one.Com os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Thu, 8 May 2025 at 07:31, Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\nCheers Nuno,I'll send the invite for Monday if that works for you.\nMartín Arévalo de León | Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 | www.unops.org Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Wed, May 7, 2025 at 6:13 PM Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Martin, \nHere is the latest news on the project.There seems to be a turn around in this project.Com os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: AmadoJacinto, Josina (FAOAO) <Josina.AmadoJacinto@fao.org>\nDate: Wed, 7 May 2025 at 17:06\nSubject: RE: Reunião sobre os projectos FSIP e FNPP Angola\nTo: Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>\nCc: Carolina QUINTAS TABOADA MEIRELES COSTA <carolinaq@unops.org>, Goncalves, Anastacio (FAOAO) <Anastacio.Goncalves@fao.org>, Watangua, Miguel (FAOAO) <Miguel.Watangua@fao.org>, PalmaDosSantos, Pedro (FAOAO) <Pedro.PalmaDosSantos@fao.org>, Carvalho, Helinton (FAOAO) <Helinton.Carvalho@fao.org>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Nuno Rodrigues,\nHead of Country Office\n\nUNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde e S.Tome\n \nMuito obrigada pelo contacto.\nReceio informar, mas creio que a nossa reunião fica adiada\npara uma outra oportunidade a anunciar, em virtude de uma recente “reviravolta” na estratégia do\nProjeto GEF 7 Miombo Mopane “Integrated landscape management to reduce land degradation and enhance community resilience in Angola?s Miombo-Mopane dry forests (FSP)”.\n\n \nEstamos neste momento em contacto com a nossa Sede/HQ, em Roma, para receber novas orientações sobre a contribuição (ou não) do UNOPS no plano de trabalho do referido projeto.\n Dar-lhe-emos um feedback brevemente.\n \nEntretanto, aproveito a oportunidade para apresentar virtualmente a equipa do Programa da FAO:\n\nos senhores Miguel Watangua e\nPedro Palma (aqui em CC), coordenados pelo Assistente do Representante, Sr.\nAnastácio Roque.\n \nMais uma vez gratos pela vossa disponibilidade,\nAtt\n \nJosina Amado\nBudget and Operations specialist\n\n \nPhone: +244 924 322 085\nFood and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations\nAntonio Jacinto street. Ministry of Agriculture building.\nLuanda – Angola\n\n \n \n \n\nFrom: Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, May 7, 2025 2:00 PM\n\nTo: AmadoJacinto, Josina (FAOAO) <Josina.AmadoJacinto@fao.org>\n\nCc: Carolina QUINTAS TABOADA MEIRELES COSTA <carolinaq@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Reunião sobre os projectos FSIP e FNPP Angola\n\n \n\n\nEstimada Josina\n\n\n \n\n\nEspero que se encontre bem.\n\n\nGostaria de saber se a nossa reunião pode ser amanhã às 10:00AM.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,\n\nNuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS\n Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 |\nwww.unops.org \n Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter,\nLinkedIn,\nFacebook,\nInstagram,\nYouTube.\n\n\n\nError! Filename not specified.",
