                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000PeQX3MAN",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi\nCC: Sara.Alanen@gov.fi; devorahfd@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; radhav@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\nBody:\nDear Riikka,\n\nThank you. This is very good\nnews! From our side, we have made some minor formatting adjustments and adjusted\nthe definition in Article 14.1.b, concerning unethical practices, to ensure it\naligns with the definition we agreed upon for the same term in Article 13.1.f.\nPlease find attached the draft agreement. \n\nIn addition, we wanted to confirm whether,\nonce we have a final version, it would be okay from your end to treat this agreement\nas a template for future engagements between Finland and UNOPS. \n\nFinally, since we'll need to\namend our current signed agreement for this engagement in Nepal to mirror the\nterms we've agreed, we'll reformat the draft into an \"amendment\ndocument.\" Would it be okay with you if we do this work once we have a\nfinal agreement and then share it with you and/or your embassy in Kathmandu?Have a nice weekend. \n\nBest,\n\nFranciscoFrancisco de Asis Camps Bas | Legal Specialist | Legal Group | IPAS Solution Portal | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Fri, May 16, 2025 at 6:21 AM Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Francisco,\n \nI have accepted all the suggested changes. Our legal advisers also approved your new wording related to Article 18. We have consulted Ilija in UNOPS Nepal and he approves\n the wording (added draft reports). \n \nI will check one more time carefully this sent agreement next week. On our behalf we can sign the agreement when the addendum and budget is updated as agreed in Katmandu,\n if that is fine also with you?\n \nKind regards,\n \nRiikka\n \n\n\nFrom: Miettinen Riikka (UM)\n\n\nSent: sunnuntai 4. toukokuuta 2025 15.51\n\nTo: 'Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS' <franciscoca@unops.org>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Alanen Sara (UE) <Sara.Alanen@gov.fi>; Radha VERMA <radhav@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n\n\n \nDear Francisco,\n \nthank you for second round of your suggestions. I will consult our legal advisors and be back to you after that.\n\n \nGreetings from Nepal,\n \nRiikka\n \n\nFrom: Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS <franciscoca@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: torstai 1. toukokuuta 2025 15.13\n\nTo: Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Alanen Sara (UE) <Sara.Alanen@gov.fi>; Radha\n VERMA <radhav@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nDear Riikka,\n\nI hope this email finds you well. Please find attached the draft agreement, which includes our follow-up comments and suggestions. We have accepted the suggestions that were acceptable to us.\n\n\nRegarding Article 13, on financial irregularities, I have adjusted two of the definitions to align them with our internal definitions. For your reference, please see the UNOPS Operational Instruction on Vendor Sanctions,\n where these definitions are detailed.\n\nWith regards to Article 18, concerning counter-terrorism and sanctions, please note that we are unable to accept the proposed language. However, we have proposed alternative wording that the UN Office of Legal Affairs\n (OLA) recently approved for a similar request from another donor.\n\nFinally, please note that we are available to discuss any of our comments and suggestions in more detail via a call at your convenience.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nBest,\n\nFrancisco\n\n\n\n\n\nFrancisco de Asis Camps Bas | Legal\n Specialist | Legal Group | IPAS\n Solution Portal |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Apr 11, 2025 at 4:42 PM Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS <franciscoca@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Riikka,\n\nThank you for your emails. We will review the suggestions and revert to you shortly.\n\nWishing you a pleasant weekend.  \n\nBest,\n\nFrancisco\n\n\n\n\n\nFrancisco de Asis Camps Bas | Legal\n Specialist | Legal Group | IPAS\n Solution Portal |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Apr 11, 2025 at 1:37 PM Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Francisco,\n \nwe have accepted two more of your suggestions. The 5.3 is acceptable the way you suggest. Your annual accounts of the project show at\n which exchange rate the funds have been transferred from the EUR account to the USD account, right?\n \nHave a nice weekend,\n \nRiikka\n \n\n\nFrom: Miettinen\n Riikka (UM) \n\nSent: torstai 10. huhtikuuta 2025 15.28\n\nTo: 'Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS' <franciscoca@unops.org>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Alanen Sara (UE) <Sara.Alanen@gov.fi>;\n Radha VERMA <radhav@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n\n\n \nDear Francisco,\n \nthank you very much for your comments. I have consulted our legal advisers. I have accepted your suggestions that are fine with us. We\n are suggesting some changes to some of your suggestions and also include some comments.\n \nCould you please reply in written to our comments and suggestions one more time? Could you also send me the document where your financial\n irregularities are defined?\n \nThank you in advance and with kind regards,\n \nRiikka\n \nPs. There are too big empty spaces etc., but I will correct them later.\n \n \n\nFrom: Francisco\n De Asis CAMPS BAS <franciscoca@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: perjantai 4. huhtikuuta 2025 11.29\n\nTo: Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>; Alanen Sara (UE) <Sara.Alanen@gov.fi>;\n Radha VERMA <radhav@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n\n \n\n\n\n\nDear Riikka,\n\nI hope this email finds you well. Please accept my apologies for the delayed response. We needed to consult with our internal departments to ensure a thorough review. As promised, we've aimed to keep our comments\n to a minimum. \n\nRegarding Articles 13 and 14, a key point of concern, I'm pleased to inform you that our internal oversight body has approved the proposed language, with the following adjustments: i) The definitions in Article 13\n have been aligned with our internal definitions for consistency; ii) References to the UN oversight body and UN rules and procedures have been updated to reflect the IAIG/UNOPS oversight body and UNOPS/Recipient's rules and procedures.\n\n\nAs discussed during our call, the primary change concerns the \"Counter-terrorism measures and sanctions\" article. We understand this has been a point of negotiation with other UN entities as well. We have revised\n the language to ensure alignment with UNOPS/UN rules and regulations. \n\nWe are available for a call to discuss any of our comments and suggestions in more detail. Thank you.\n\nBest,\n\nFrancisco\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nFrancisco de Asis Camps Bas | Legal\n Specialist | Legal Group | IPAS\n Solution Portal |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 19, 2025 at 9:53 AM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Rikka, \n\n \n\n\nOur colleagues from the legal department are currently making sure that we have gathered all relevant input from our other departments such as audit, risk, finance, etc. to ensure\n that we can provide full feedback on your draft. We will try to gather this as fast as possible - and I hope that we can revert to you by next week. \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for your understanding, \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\nAsbjørn \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 19 Mar 2025 at 07:19, Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear\nAsbjørn,\n \nIt was very nice to meet you online March 7th. Do you have an estimation when\n you could send your comments to our new agreement model as agreed in our meeting?\n \nKind regards,\n \nRiikka\n \nFrom: Asbjorn\n BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: tiistai 4. maaliskuuta 2025 15.02\n\nTo: Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS <franciscoca@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>;\n Luomanperä Sanna (UM) <Sanna.Luomanpera@gov.fi>\n\nSubject: Re: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n \n\n\nDear Riiikka\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for your rapid response and availability on Friday. \n\n\n \n\n\nI have sent a calendar invite for Friday at 13.30 CET that I hope works for all. We use Google Meet but can also log onto other platforms in case Google Meet does not work on your\n end. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 4 Mar 2025 at 13:18, Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear\nAsbjørn,\n \nThank you for your mail. This week on Friday we could have an on-line meeting any time\n good for you, please suggest the best time for you, if Friday is OK in general for you?\n \nIf you have your comments or suggestions for change, please send them to me beforehand\n or otherwise we can mainly discuss about the process of updating the Cities4women agreement. I need to consult our legal advisors related to possible changes in the agreement.\n \nLooking forward to seeing you on-line.\n \nKind regards,\n \nRiikka\n \n \nFrom: Asbjorn\n BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: tiistai 4. maaliskuuta 2025 12.44\n\nTo: Miettinen Riikka (UM) <Riikka.Miettinen@gov.fi>\n\nCc: Devorah Flax-Davidson <devorahfd@unops.org>; Francisco De Asis CAMPS BAS <franciscoca@unops.org>; Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>;\n Luomanperä Sanna (UM) <Sanna.Luomanpera@gov.fi>\n\nSubject: Standard Template for engagements between Finland and UNOPS\n \n\n\nDear Riikka \n\n\n \n\n\nI am reaching out following initial dialogue with your colleague Sanna (cc) regarding the need to initiate a dialogue to update the current standard template for engagements between\n Finland and UNOPS as the current one seems to be outdated. This has become clear at a recent engagement in Nepal. \n\n\n \n\n\nI am looping in my colleagues from our legal department, Devorah and Francisco, who will be leading the conversation on updating the template from our end. \n\n\n \n\n\nTo get things started, I was hoping that you might be available to meet online this week at your convenience. Might you be able to propose some time slots that would work on your\n end? \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you in advance!\n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nAsbjørn \n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nTämä viesti on osoitettu ainoastaan sen tarkoitetulle vastaanottajalle ja se saattaa sisältää salassa pidettävää tietoa. Jos et ole viestissä tarkoitettu vastaanottaja, tuhoa viesti ja ilmoita asiasta välittömästi viestin lähettäjälle.\n Viestin sisällön, välitystiedon ja viestin olemassaolon hyväksikäyttäminen ja ilmaiseminen on kielletty laissa (laki sähköisen viestinnän palveluista 136 § 4. mom).\n\n\n\n\nDetta meddelande gäller endast den avsedda mottagaren och kan innehålla sekretessbelagd information. Om du inte är den avsedda mottagaren ska du radera meddelandet och informera avsändaren omedelbart. Det är enligt lag förbjudet att utnyttja eller röja meddelandets\n innehåll, förmedlingsuppgifterna eller uppgifterna om meddelandets existens (136 § 4 mom. i lagen om tjänster inom elektronisk kommunikation).\n\n\n\n\nThis email message is intended only for the person(s) named in the message header and may contain privileged information. If you are not the intended recipient of this message, please delete the message and notify the sender immediately. Any disclosure or use\n of the content or traffic data of this message or the knowledge of its existence is prohibited by law (Act on Electronic Communications Services, section 136, subsection 4).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
