                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000PeZAVMA3",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Request for Sida contacts at the Swedish Embassy in Tunisia - Migration unit",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-26").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Request for Sida contacts at the Swedish Embassy in Tunisia - Migration unit",
                        Description = "To: Katarina.Zinn@sida.se\nCC: asbjornb@unops.org; roger.m.karlsson@gov.se; claudiar@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Request for Sida contacts at the Swedish Embassy in Tunisia - Migration unit\nBody:\nDear Katerina,Thank you always for your very quick reply and for your suggestion to approach your regional MENA team in Amman. Could I kindly ask for your suggestion on who I should reach out to? In the meantime I will suggest our Tunisia team (Claudia - cc this email) to touch base with your colleague Roger from the Swedish Embassy in Tunis.For your background information, UNOPS is currently delivering projects for $180 million in Tunisia, Morocco, Algeria and Libya on behalf of our partners. Our efforts in the region primarily focus on strengthening land and border control, maritime border management, counter terrorism etc., which might be of interest for Sweden.To further maximize impact on the region’s challenges with migration, we are looking at a Nordic multidonor approach on migration management, where we are not only looking at direct border control but also building local capacity and infrastructure for re-integration of returnees as well as communities vulnerable to migration.This initiative will address not only direct border control but also vital areas such as re-integration infrastructure, support for communities vulnerable to migration, and resources for returnees.Finally, to clarify your question on who is the “demandeur” of the project, this is with the respective program countries - e.g. Tunisia, Algeria, Morocco, Libya, etc. in this case. The projects are co-developed among beneficiaries, donors and UNOPS as the middle man. I hope this clarifies. Beyond migration, UNOPS has a significant presence in Northern Africa, covering areas such as health, private sector development, sustainable energy, climate and environmental action, and institutional capacity building. For this purpose, my colleagues from UNOPS Tunisia Office would like to connect with the SIDA Regional MENA team in Amman.Best regards, Naimo \n\nOn Fri, May 23, 2025 at 12:48 PM Katarina Zinn <Katarina.Zinn@sida.se> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Naimo,\n\n \nThanks for reaching out.  Sida does not to my knowledge  have presence and funding managed in Tunisia. The strategy you refer to is\n managed in Stockholm, but it I am thinking that may be more accurate to approach regional MENA team  in Amman if the scope is regional. I would welcome your advise in this regard.\n \nMay I kindly also ask whom is in charge of this project - is it a project initiated and managed by UNOPS itself or is the idea that\n UNOPS should provide services at the request of the Nordic countries, or  national institutions in the targeted countries?  It would be helpful if you could please clarify if you are approaching Sida for funding, or if you are approaching us with the expectation\n that we would be  co-creators and have a role as demandeur for the services UNOPS will be providing.\n \nSweden has an embassy in Tunisia, so I am putting my MFA colleague Roger in copy, in case he would suggest  to connect you with the\n embassy in Tunisia .\n \nKind regards.\n \nKatarina\n \n \n \n \n \n\nFrom: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: den 23 maj 2025 11:39\n\nTo: Katarina Zinn <Katarina.Zinn@sida.se>\n\nCc: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Request for Sida contacts at the Swedish Embassy in Tunisia - Migration unit\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Katerina\n\nI hope that all is well. \n\nOn behalf of our UNOPS Tunisia Office, I'm reaching out to request\ncontact information for the relevant focal points at Sida within the Swedish Embassy in Tunisia. We are specifically  interested in connecting with colleagues who manage\nSweden's\n development cooperation on migration, returns, and voluntary repatriation.\n\nThis request is part of a broader joint Nordic-UNOPS initiative to explore potential collaboration on migration. UNOPS is well-positioned to support efforts in\nstrengthening local capacity and infrastructure to facilitate return and sustainable reintegration of returnees, as well as\nimproving border infrastructure for better migration management. Also an area of interest for both Denmark and Norway. \n\nThank you so much in advance. \n\nBest regards, \n\nNaimo\n\n-- \n\n\n\n\nNaimo Hassan Hirsi\n| Partnerships Analyst | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Tel: +45 2683 4878 |\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDet här mailet har scannats för spam & virus. Om du anser att det borde ha stoppats av våra filter, klicka\n här för att rapportera det",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000PeZAVMA3",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "katarina.zinn@sida.se", "naimoh@unops.org", "roger.m.karlsson@gov.se", "claudiar@unops.org", "asbjornb@unops.org" },
