                        Subject = "Email: RE: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract",
                        Description = "To: juanca@unops.org\nCC: williamsg@unops.org; Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu; antoinel@unops.org; gabriellar@unops.org; maxencen@unops.org; giuseppem@unops.org; Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu; antonioba@unops.org; Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\nBody:\nDear Juan and UNOPS team, \n\nThank you very much for the response.\nOnce we have received  the documents which have been vetted by your legal team , we will  review same and thereafter convene a meeting with your team  to discuss\n the next steps.                    \n \n \nRajesh Majeed (Mr.)\nProgramme/Policy Manager\nCooperation Section\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDelegation\n of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, St Barthelemy, St Eustatius and St Maarten\n\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\nContacts: (+592) 226-4004 ext 2112 |\nrajesh.majeed@eeas.europa.eu\nhttp://www.eeas.europa.eu/delegations/guyana\n \nFrom: Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 26 May 2025 14:11\n\nTo: MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: William SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>; CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>; DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>;\n Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>; Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>; NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; Antonio BAIO <antonioba@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n \n\n\nDear Rajesh and all\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\n\n \n\n\nOn behalf of William Saquier, please find attached a document compiling the EU comments provided on May 8th to the different documents (DoA, BoA, Letter of Agreement). You will find the respective UNOPS response to each comment on columns\n G and H. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs you will see from the file, we as the negotiation team are preliminarily accepting several of your comments and requests. However, please note that we are in the process of consulting them with the UNOPS Legal review team. Once we get\n the respective green light on the proposed changes, we will share the updated documents with the requested approved changes.\n\n\n \n\n\nRegards,\n\n\nJuan\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nJuan José Castro Cerdas | Project Support Officer | PAMCO, LCR | San José, Costa Rica |\nFollow us\non social media and\nsubscribe to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, May 8, 2025 at 3:23 PM MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear William,\n                         Good afternoon. Please note that while the Delegation had  intended  to send the attached\n comments and observations as contained in the attached documents  prior to your mission to Sint Maarten, it was not  possible. The  comments and observations are herewith presented for your consideration. Thereafter , we can convene a meeting during week 19-23\n May 2025 to facilitate a discussion.\nBest regards,\n \nRajesh Majeed (Mr.)\nProgramme/Policy Manager\nCooperation Section\n\n\n\nDelegation\n of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, St Barthelemy, St Eustatius and St Maarten\n\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\nContacts: (+592) 226-4004 ext 2112 |\nrajesh.majeed@eeas.europa.eu\nhttp://www.eeas.europa.eu/delegations/guyana\n \nFrom: William\n SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 31 March 2025 12:08\n\nTo: NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>; CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>; Kenson, Plaisimond <Kenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org>;\n DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>; MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>;\n Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>; Labega, Noreen <Noreen.Labega@sintmaartengov.org>; BAL Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN)\n <Laurent.BAL@eeas.europa.eu>; BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>;\n Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>; Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>; Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n \n\n\nDear colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\n\n \n\n\nA kind reminder on the above as we finalize preparations for the mission.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | IsCMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\n\n\nFollow us on social media and\nsubscribe to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 26, 2025 at 9:41 PM William SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Joan,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you for the update.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe kindly await the invitation for this additional conversation.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | IsCMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\n\n\nFollow us on social media and\nsubscribe to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 26, 2025 at 1:24 PM NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear William, colleagues,\n\n \nRajesh and Teodora will reach out to you as another vc is needed to go through the comments we still\n have and hopefully close the gap. \n \nThey will reach out directly so it well before your visit to SXM.\n\n \nUn saludo,\n\n \nRegards to all from Brussels, I am behind with my emails,\n \nJoan\n\n \n \nJoan NADAL SASTRE (Mr.)\n\n\nFirst Counsellor – Head of Cooperation\nDelegation of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao,\n Saba, Saint-Barthélemy, St Eustatius and St Maarten \n_____________________________________\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\n\nPhone: +592 226 400\nMobile: +592 684 7365\n\njoan.nadal-sastre@eeas.europa.eu\n\n\n \n \n\n \n \n \nFrom: William\n SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 25 March 2025 16:46\n\nTo: Gumbs, Angelique <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org>\n\nCc: Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>; CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>; Kenson, Plaisimond <Kenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org>;\n DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>; MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>;\n Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>; Labega, Noreen <Noreen.Labega@sintmaartengov.org>; NADAL SASTRE Joan\n (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; BAL Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Laurent.BAL@eeas.europa.eu>; BORIKOVA\n Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>;\n Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>; Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n \n\n\nDear team,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\n\n \n\n\nI would like to follow-up on my previous email and kindly request an update on the previously shared.\n\n\n \n\n\nI will be travelling to SXM on the 6th of April and look forward to meeting key stakeholders as we advance towards the implementation.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | IsCMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\n\n\nFollow us on social media and\nsubscribe to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 19, 2025 at 3:52 PM Gumbs, Angelique <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nGood afternoon,\n \nReceived, with thanks.\n \nWe will review the attached documents, however pls. note that internal processes and procedures of government must be adhered too. Including\n where it pertains to competent authority in signing letters of agreement. \n\n \nKR,\nAngelique Gumbs\n \n\n\nFrom: William\n SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, March 17, 2025 5:29 PM\n\nTo: Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>\n\nCc: CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>; Kenson, Plaisimond <Kenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org>;\n DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <teodora.deaconu@eeas.europa.eu>; MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <rajesh.majeed@eeas.europa.eu>;\n Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>; Labega, Noreen <Noreen.Labega@sintmaartengov.org>; Gumbs, Angelique\n <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org>; NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <joan.nadal-sastre@eeas.europa.eu>; BAL\n Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <laurent.bal@eeas.europa.eu>; BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <jirina.borikova@eeas.europa.eu>;\n Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>; Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>;\n Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nDear Representatives of the Government of Sint Maarten and the European Union delegation,\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well. \n\n\n \n\n\nFollowing the various inputs that we have been receiving through our consultations in the past days we have been able to optimize the documentation in order to collectively\n work towards a positive outcome for the reformulation of Amendment 1. We hope that this effort will contribute to facilitate conversations between Prime Minister Mercelina and Ambassador Van Nes.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached the most recent\ndraft versions as of today March 17th 2025 of the following documents (word documents include track changes to reflect the changes between the original agreement and the Addendum 1):\n\n\n\n1.      Addendum 1 - CA 700002784 (170325): Addendum 1 document that a) removes article 4.4 from Special Conditions to align reporting\n with General Conditions, b) introduces an updated Annex I, and c) introduces an updated Annex III.\n\n2.      Annex I: Description of the Action (24793_SxM_11th_EDF_Proposal)_Amendment 1 (170325): updated Annex I with track changes on background,\n timeline, project inputs, budget, governance, reports, and annexes sections\n\n3.      Annex III: Budget for the Action_March 2025_Amendment 1_(170325): updated budget\n\n4.      24793_250305_Beneficiary Letter of Agreement_UNOPS_SxM - 11thEDF (DRAFT)_170325: draft beneficiary Letter of Agreement to be signed between\n UNOPS and VROMI\n\n\n\nI take this opportunity to highlight that considering the recent changes discussed during our meeting in Georgetown, Guyana, UNOPS would require the\nbeneficiary letter of agreement to be signed by the Prime Minister Luc Mercelina, aligning with the overarching PFA established between the Government of Sint Maarten and the European Union.\n\n\n \n\n\nWe remain available to discuss any pending points on the proposed updated instruments, and we look forward to the clearances from both the Government of Sint Maarten\n and the EU delegation to proceed with our internal review cycles.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards and a pleasant week ahead.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | ICMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\n\n\nFollow us on social\n media and subscribe to our newsletter.\n | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 12, 2025 at 11:29 AM Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear all\n\n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well. Following superior instructions, please find below the draft versions of the following documents to continue our discussions towards\n the signing of Addendum 1 of the 11th EDF Contribution Agreement (word documents include track changes to reflect the changes between the original agreement and the Addendum 1):\n\n\n\n\nAddendum 1 - CA 700002784: Addendum 1 document that a) removes article 4.4 from Special Conditions to align reporting with General Conditions,\nb) introduces an updated Annex I, and c) introduces an updated Annex III.\nAnnex I: Description of the Action (24793_SxM_11th_EDF_Proposal)_Amendment 1: updated Annex I with track changes on background, timeline, project inputs, budget, governance, reports, and annexes sections\nAnnex III: Budget for the Action_March 2025_Amendment 1_DRAFT FOR DISCUSSION: updated budget\n24793_250305_Beneficiary Letter of Agreement_UNOPS_SxM - 11thEDF (DRAFT): draft beneficiary Letter of Agreement to be signed between UNOPS and VROMI\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\nJuan\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nJuan José Castro Cerdas | Project Support Officer | PAMCO, LCR | San José,\n Costa Rica | Follow us\non social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Feb 25, 2025 at 7:09 AM CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear All,\n \n\nGood morning and thank you for your emails on respective availability for this meeting.\n\n\n \n\nAfter careful review, this online discussion is now scheduled for\nWednesday, 5 March at 9:30am Guyana time. WebEx invitation was a few minutes ago for the same.\n\n \n\nBest regards,\n\n \n \n\nDeslyn Croney (Ms)\nCooperation Section Assistant\nDelegation of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao,\n Saba, Saint-Barthélemy, St Eustatius and St Maarten \n_____________________________________\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\n\nPhone: +592 226-4004 ext. 2107\ndeslin.croney@eeas.europa.eu\n\n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Kenson,\n Plaisimond <Kenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org>\n\n\nSent: 20 February 2025 12:22\n\nTo: William SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>; CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>; Labega, Noreen\n <Noreen.Labega@sintmaartengov.org>\n\nCc: Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>;\n Gumbs, Angelique <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org>; Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>; Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>;\n NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>;\n BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>; BAL Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Laurent.BAL@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n\n\n \n\nDear All,\n\n\n \n\n\nFirst of all,\nexcuse me for my contribution to this planning mishap.\n\n\nI have included Ms. Labega who assist me in managing my agenda to this email thread.\n\n\nIn an attempt to remdy this as efficiently as possible I am sharing the following timeslots (all UTC-4).\n\nI am assuming that many stakeholders are operating in European time zones, therefore I focussed on the morning hours here on Sint Maarten.\n\n\n\n\nFriday, 21 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n10:00 to 11:00 <-- still available for VROMI\n\n\n\n\n\nMonday, 24 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 10:00\n\n\n\n\n\nTuesday, 25 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 10:00\n\n\n\n\n\nWednesday, 26 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 12:00\n\n\n\n\n\nThursday, 27 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 12:00\n\n\n\n\n\nFriday, 28 February:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 12:00\n\n\n\n\n\nMonday, 3 March:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 12:00\n\n\n\n\n\nWednesday, 5 MArch:\n\n\n\n\n\n8:30 to 12:00\n\n\n\n \n\n\nSincerely,\n\nKenson Plaisimond\n\nSecretary General VROMI\n\n\n\nSoualiga Road 1, Pond Island\n\nGreat Bay, Sint Maarten\n\nhttp://www.sintmaartengov.org\n\nConfidentiality Notice: This email and any attachments are intended solely for the use of the individual or entity to whom they are addressed. If you have received this\n email in error, please notify the sender immediately and delete it from your system. Unauthorized use, disclosure, or copying of this email or any part thereof is strictly prohibited.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: William\n SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\nSent: Thursday, February 20, 2025 12:01\n\nTo: CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Kenson, Plaisimond <Kenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org>; Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>;\n Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>; Gumbs, Angelique <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org>; Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>;\n Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>; NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; DEACONU Teodora\n (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>; BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>;\n BAL Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Laurent.BAL@eeas.europa.eu>; MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nwilliamsg@unops.org. \nLearn why this is important\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Deslyn,\n\n\n \n\n\nOn the UNOPS end we will not be able to attend on the 7th of March,\n\n\n \n\n\nMay I kindly request that you suggest an alternative, coordinated between the parties before Wednesday 5th of March ?\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regard and a pleasant rest of the day ahead\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | PAMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\nFollow us on\n social media and subscribe to\n our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\nOn Thu, Feb 20, 2025 at 9:50 AM CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>\n wrote:\n\n\nDear All,\n \nDue to unforeseen circumstances, this online discussion will now be re-scheduled to\nFriday, 7 March at 10:00am to 11:00am. As such, revised WebEx invitation will be sent shortly.\n \nThank you and kind regards,\n \n \nDeslyn Croney (Ms)\nCooperation Section Assistant\nDelegation of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, Saint-Barthélemy, St Eustatius\n and St Maarten\n_____________________________________\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\n\nPhone: +592 226-4004 ext. 2107\ndeslin.croney@eeas.europa.eu\n\n\n \n \n\n \n\nFrom: CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN)\n\nSent: 20 February 2025 10:18\n\nTo: 'William SQUIER GONZALEZ' <williamsg@unops.org>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>;\nKenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org; Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>;\nAngelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org; Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>; Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>\n\nCc: NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; DEACONU Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>;\n BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>; BAL Laurent (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Laurent.BAL@eeas.europa.eu>;\n MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nSubject: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n\nImportance: High\n\n \nDear All,\n \nPlease be advised the online discussion will be held on\nFriday, 21 February at 10:00am to 11:00am. WebEx calendar invitation will follow shortly.\n \nWarm regards,\n \n \nDeslyn Croney (Ms)\nCooperation Section Assistant\nDelegation of the European Union to Guyana, for Suriname and with responsibility for Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, Saint-Barthélemy, St Eustatius\n and St Maarten\n_____________________________________\n11 Sendall Place, Georgetown, Guyana\n\nPhone: +592 226-4004 ext. 2107\ndeslin.croney@eeas.europa.eu\n\n\n \n \n\n \nFrom: William SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\nSent: 18 February 2025 11:32\n\nTo: MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Rajesh.MAJEED@eeas.europa.eu>\n\nCc: Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org; Ellis, Hasani <Hasani.Ellis@sintmaartengov.org>;\nKenson.Plaisimond@sintmaartengov.org; NADAL SASTRE Joan (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Joan.NADAL-SASTRE@eeas.europa.eu>; DEACONU\n Teodora (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Teodora.DEACONU@eeas.europa.eu>; CRONEY Deslyn (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <Deslin.CRONEY@eeas.europa.eu>;\n BORIKOVA Jirina (EEAS-BRIDGETOWN) <Jirina.BORIKOVA@eeas.europa.eu>; Juan CASTRO <juanca@unops.org>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>;\n Maxence Alexandre NICOUX <maxencen@unops.org>; Gabriella REMY <gabriellar@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Re 700002784 Implementation Support for the Water and Sanitation Project for the Sint Maarten Dutch Quarter (Contribution Agreement) - Signature of the contract\n \nDear Rajesh,\n \nThank you for the update.\n \nOn the UNOPS end we confirm availability for this friday 21st of February.\n \nKind regards\n \nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | PAMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\nFollow us on\n social media and subscribe to\n our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n \n \nOn Tue, Feb 18, 2025 at 9:30 AM MAJEED Rajesh (EEAS-GEORGETOWN) <<a href=\"mailto:Rajesh.",
                        Location = null,
