                        Description = "To: mariapa@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\nBody:\nGrazzie!\nMartín Arévalo de León | Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 | www.unops.org Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Tue, Sep 30, 2025 at 3:14 PM Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org> wrote:\nFYI\n\n\nMaria Cristina Palamini | Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 |\nSkype: mcpalamini |Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\nDate: Tue, 30 Sept 2025 at 13:54\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\nCc: Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP) <HangThiThanh.Pham@fao.org>, Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP) <Chongguang.Liao@fao.org>, Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>, Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>, Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>, Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>, Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>, Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>, Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>, Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>, Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>, Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nDear YurieThanks to you and all FAO colleagues for the active participation. I hope the session was useful.I will respond to your questions within the next few days.Kind RegardsCristina\n\n\nMaria Cristina Palamini | Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 |\nSkype: mcpalamini |Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Tue, 30 Sept 2025 at 12:34, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina\n \nMany thanks for today’s meeting with FAO country offices.\n \nGrateful to receive your feedback on the list of questions that Zette shared.\nAlso, look forward to receiving the PPT.\n \nBest wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Saturday, September 27, 2025 10:09\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP) <HangThiThanh.Pham@fao.org>; Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP) <Chongguang.Liao@fao.org>; Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>; Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>;\n Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>; Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>; Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Yurie\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find here linked a\n\nrevised draft of the FAO-UNOPS Regional Agreement.\n\n\n \n\n\nKindly note, we have included the possibility to receive Implementation support in the areas of Project implementation, Advisory, Grant Management, and Infrastructure\nat a fixed fee of 5.3% (indirect cost only).\n\n\n \n\n\nAs offering these services is more complex than HR and Procurement - which can be offered through a simple Request for Services - we have included a provision that they be subject to a separate\n agreement detailing the respective responsibility and support from both parties. At the same time, we are working with our HQ trying to explore ways to further simplify how FAO could engage UNOPS for these services, including the development of standard templates,\n which we will share with you, once finalised.\n\n\n \n\n\nI look forward to our session next Tuesday and to hearing feedback from FAO offices. \n\n\n\nIn the meantime, could you kindly let me know if your legal office has provided any comment on the Agreement we shared earlier,\n which already coveres HR and Procurement?\n\n\n \n\n\nWishing you a great week-end.\n\n\nBest Regards,\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 2 Sept 2025 at 11:15, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina,\n \nPlease note that the attached version was shared with FAO HQ and received a green light to proceed with finalization as the document is the standard template for UNtoUN agreement\n as per \nUN2UN-Transfer-Agreement-Template-FINAL-3-June-2021.pdf\n \nBest wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, August 1, 2025 17:42\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nHi Yurie \n\n\nthe inclusion of FTAs will need to be 1) agreed with your HQ and 2) justified (in terms of efficiency, cost, speed etc) in order for\n my HQ to agree.\n\n\nI can help draft a justification, if needed. Please let me know once you discuss with your HQ.\n\n\nRegards and have a great week-end\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 1 Aug 2025 at 17:35, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for your message and the revised draft agreement. I'll use this version to discuss with HQ colleagues.\n\n\n \n\n\nI understood that if we want to include FTE personnel in the agreement, HQ level discussion and agreement, especially from HR team, is required.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest wishes, Yurie\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Maria\n PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\nSent: 01 August 2025 16:32\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear FAO Colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nIn the interest of time, and as agreed separately with Yurie, I share a\n\nrevised draft AGREEMENT without the inclusion of Fixed Term Contracts, which requires additional HQ to HQ consultation.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease feel free to share your comments. Grateful if you could work in revision mode so as to make it easier to track changes.\n\n\nThanks a lot for your patience. Have a great week-end\n\n\n \n\n\nRegards\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 1 Aug 2025 at 10:26, Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Yurie and FAO colleagues\n\n\n \n\n\nI would like to update you on where we stand on the Legal Agreement - which I was planning to share with you today.\n\n\n \n\n\nI have a semi-final draft from my Legal department where the\nonly part still pending is the inclusion of Fix Term Contracts.\n\n\nI have been asked to provide more justifications before being allowed to proceed - I have requested more details and  I will get back\n on this as soon as I have more clarity.\n\n\n \n\n\nRegards\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 30 Jul 2025 at 11:09, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHello Cristina\n \nThank you very much for your feedback.\nI’ll discuss further with the HQ GEF team and come back if they have additional questions.\n \nThank you and best wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, July 30, 2025 11:04\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nHi Yurie,\n\n\nHere below answers to your questions in blue:\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nBudget file: as we make updates to the unit cost etc. during design and implementation, (1) could we use the Excel file’s TAB1 or TAB2 to calculate the\n total cost and (2) should we consult you to check the calculation is correct – maybe not each time, how often would you recommend?\n\n \n\n\nLet me attach the Excel file so we are sure the file is not damaged. Please feel free to modify either TAB, the reason to provide the two calculations was to show you the difference of having Travels\n as reimbursement or as procurement. \n\n\nPlease feel free to share the calculation for our confirmation whenever needed. \n\n\n \n\n\n\nCould you please confirm that “Pacific Region” includes Timor-Leste?\n\nYes, sorry I did not specify it. The Pacific includes Timor Leste.\n\n\n \n\n\n\nCould you please remind us about travel arrangements? When a traveller purchases tickets and books accommodations, when will he/she get reimbursed? I assume the traveller will receive DSA before travel.\n\nThe payment will be processed upon FAO request. Either before, during or after the trip. \n\n\n \n\n\n\nTalking points: Could you please include examples of the average number of working days for the following processes: (a) contracting under RFQ, (b) contracting\n under ITB, (c) contracting under RFP, (d) arranging in-country travel, and (e) under international travel\n\nI will do this and share it with you as soon as possible.\n\n\n\n\n\nUNtoUN Agreement: We’ll come back on your query shortly.\n\n\nThanks a lot.\n\n\nRegards\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 30 Jul 2025 at 10:24, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHello Cristina and colleagues,\n \nThank you for your message and documents. Very much appreciated. One note – when I downloaded the budget file, it says “repaired”. Hope there is no issue.\n \n\n\nBudget file: as we make updates to the unit cost etc. during design and implementation, (1) could we use the Excel file’s TAB1 or TAB2 to calculate the total cost and (2) should we consult you to check the calculation is correct – maybe not each time,\n how often would you recommend?\nCould you please confirm that “Pacific Region” includes Timor-Leste?\nCould you please remind us about travel arrangements? When a traveller purchases tickets and books accommodations, when will he/she get reimbursed? I assume the traveller will receive DSA before travel.\nTalking points: Could you please include examples of the average number of working days for the following processes: (a) contracting under RFQ, (b) contracting under ITB, (c) contracting under RFP, (d) arranging in-country travel, and (e) under international\n travel\nUNtoUN Agreement: We’ll come back on your query shortly.\n \nThanks and best wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, July 29, 2025 16:57\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nHi  Yurie and colleagues\n\n\n \n\n\nI am glad to share with you the presentation\nwe used during our last meeting (attached as a PDF) and a few Talking Points on UNOPS's added value (attached as PDF).\n\n\n \n\n\nI am also attaching the\nrevised budget based on your latest request. Kindly note that there are two tabs: \n\n\n- TAB 1 - Considering Travels as \"Procurement\" (UNOPS procures flights, Hotels and so on) \n\n\n- TAB 2 - Considering Travel as \"Transactional reimbursement of travel cost\" - in or outside the payroll - (UNOPS reimburse\n the cost for travel to the personnel upon FAO request).  Please consider this option is only possible if the person has a valid ongoing contract with UNOPS.\n\n\n \n\n\nAs for the bank charges; kindly note that bank charges related to payroll are covered under UNOPS cost; any additional bank charges for payment outside the payroll - if any - will have to be charged to\n the FAO project separately.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find here below the list of Countries covered under this Agreement and their grouping:\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nSouth Asia MCO (SAMCO) - Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Iran, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan, SriLanka.\n\n\nSouth East Asia and Pacific MCO (EAPMCO) - Cambodia, China, Indonesia, Laos PDR, Malaysia, Mongolia, North Korea, Pacific Region\n (all PSIDS), Papua New Guinea, Philippines, Thailand, Vietnam.\n\n\nAfghanistan.\n\n\nMyanmar.\n\n\nI've been informed by my Legal colleagues, with whom I shared your\nUNtoUN Agreement, that the FMOG-related agencies have adopted the 2021 UN transfer agreement. The\nUNSDG website lists FAO as one of these Agencies. Could you please confirm with your Legal office if there are any objections or reasons why we should not apply this 2021 version of the Agreement?\nDuring our meeting we also discussed\nreporting. Let me share two examples of \ninterim reports and two final reports. The interim reports could be provided on a quarterly basis and the final reports at the end of the project. It would be great to hear your feedback on these. Once approved, we can add the templates to the Agreement.\nLast but not least, I have made changes to the draft Agreement to include: 1 quarterly reporting, 2 clarification on the bank charges and 3 the possibility to recruit Fixed terms; once we have the go ahead from\n our Legal office we will share a draft - hopefully within a couple of days.\nI hope I did not forget anything. In case please feel free to let me know.\nMy Kindest Regards\nCristina\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 29 Jul 2025 at 12:59, Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Yurie.\n\n\nI am checking with my colleagues and I hope to be able to get back by COB today or, at the latest, tomorrow.\n\n\nRegards\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 29 Jul 2025 at 10:24, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina,\n \nApologies – I was reminded to also inquire about below:\n \nAs bank charges related to payroll payments are not included in the draft Agreement, FAO assumes that there is an arrangement with the bank whereby either no charges apply or such charges are covered under the UNOPS service fees. We kindly request UNOPS\n to confirm this understanding. UNOPS also promised to confirm whether a similar arrangement could be applied to non-payroll payments, such as travel for project personnel.\n \nThanks and best wishes, Yurie\n \n\n\nFrom: Naito, Yurie (OCB)\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, July 29, 2025 07:46\n\nTo: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n\n \nDear Cristina,\n \nThank you for the summary below. Together with the updated budget table, grateful to receive the PPT used during our meeting.\n \nBest wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Sunday, July 27, 2025 16:14\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Yurie,\nThanks for your follow-up email and the budget.\nOur team will update the budget and share it with you by Tuesday.\nRegarding our next steps, I'd like to confirm the following points from our meeting to ensure we have a common understanding:\n\n\nUNOPS will include the option to issue Fixed-Term Contracts in the Agreement.\nUNOPS will change the reporting frequency from monthly to quarterly.\nUNOPS will provide the list of countries under the APR region, including their grouping (e.g., under MCOs). This information is important for charging GSS for Procurement projects.\nUNOPS will share talking points to help FAO explain UNOPS's fees and added value to government counterparts.\nUNOPS will include a clause in the Agreement allowing for the transactional reimbursement of travel costs outside of payrolls (additional bank charges incurred by UNOPS from the recipient bank - if any - will be\n charged to the FAO project).\nOnce the Agreement is finalized, UNOPS will develop and share HR and Procurement SOPs with FAO.\nFAO has requested to use a different version of the UNtoUN agreement. We will share the FAO version with UNOPS Legal, and both agencies will ask their respective legal services to connect and finalize the agreement.\nPlease let me know if you have anything to add to the above.\nMy Kindest Regards\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 25 Jul 2025 at 08:03, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDears,\n \nThank you, UNOPS team, for the meeting today.\n \nAs for the below request, my understanding is that we wait for UNOPS' revised UN agreement, which is being reviewed by the legal team, and connect the legal teams of both agencies to finalize the template. Please let us know how\n we want to proceed.\n \nAlso, grateful if you could kindly update the attached template by including the annual fee associated to the procurement. The sections in BLUE are the ones I updated (original total month and actual monthly payroll before UNOPS\n fees). The ORANGE sections are additional items we foresee being included in the UN agreement.\n \nFinally, we look forward to receiving the PPT, list of countries, and other info I can share with the FAO HQ team.\n \nThanks and best wishes, Yurie\n \n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, July 24, 2025 21:43\n\nTo: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>\n\nCc: Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>; Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>;\n Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Zhao Wei and FAO colleagues\n\n\n \n\n\nIt was a pleasure to meet you all in person today. Thanks a lot for the open and fruitful discussion and for sharing this UN2UN template. I will share it with my Legal department and let you know. \n\n\n \n\n\nRegards\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\nFollow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, 24 Jul 2025 at 16:31, Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina,\n \nNice to meet you this morning! May I share again the FAO template of UN to UN agreement? It is much appreciated if you could check with your legal department if it is acceptable. As mentioned earlier, there is no major difference with the UNOPS template\n at all. Thank you very much.\n \nBest regards,\nZhao Wei\n \n\n\nFrom: Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP) <Chongguang.Liao@fao.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, March 7, 2025 11:19\n\nTo: Pranapom, Supakorn (FAORAP) <Supakorn.Pranapom@fao.org>; Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>;\n Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>; Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>;\n Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n\n \nDear all, \n \nNice to meet UNOPS colleagues this morning. \n\n \nKindy find attached the standard UN to UN Agreement template.   It looks the UNOPS example is similar but modified a bit.  If they are basically the same in nature, then it would help us a lot.\n\n \nBest regards, \nLiao \n \n\n-----Original Appointment-----\n\nFrom: Pranapom, Supakorn (FAORAP) <Supakorn.Pranapom@fao.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 4, 2025 08:36\n\nTo: Pranapom, Supakorn (FAORAP); Naito, Yurie (OCB)\n\nCc: Akira MORETTO; Thazin AUNG; Maria PALAMINI; Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP)\n\nSubject: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\nWhen: Friday, March 7, 2025 10:00 AM-11:00 AM (UTC+07:00) Bangkok, Hanoi, Jakarta.\n\nWhere: FAORAP Room B101\n\n \n\n\n\nLooking forward to our meeting.\n \n\n\nMicrosoft Teams\nNeed help?\n\n\n\nJoin\n the meeting now\n\n\n\nMeeting ID:\n325 789 739 908\n\n\n\nPasscode:\ncE7dV9eZ\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFor organizers:\nMeeting\n options\n\n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000UpsWzMAJ",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "akiram@unops.org", "sameer.karki@fao.org", "saminak@unops.org", "hangthithanh.pham@fao.org", "wei.zhao@fao.org", "supakorn.pranapom@fao.org", "chongguang.liao@fao.org", "yurie.naito@fao.org", "fatimaahm@unops.org", "azusac@unops.org", "mariapa@unops.org", "jennifera@unops.org", "thazina@unops.org", "ilhom.muhomediev@fao.org", "trangthun@unops.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
                        CreatedBy = paoUserEmailMapping.ContainsKey("martina@unops.org".ToLower()) ? paoUserEmailMapping["martina@unops.org".ToLower()] : 0,
                        CreatedDate = new DateTime(2025, 10, 2, 13, 45, 58, DateTimeKind.Utc),
                        LastModifiedBy = 0,
                        LastModifiedDate = DateTime.UtcNow,
                        IsDeleted = false,
                        DeletedBy = 0
                    },
                    new List<string> {  },
                    new List<int> { 1244 },
                    new List<string> { "martina@unops.org" },
                    new List<string> { "B0047" }
                )
            };

            // Begin transaction to ensure atomicity
            await using var transaction = await context.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();

            try
            {
                // Step 1: Process all interactions (create or update)
                foreach (var (gmailMessageId, interactionData, _, _, _, _) in interactionsToProcess)
                {
                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(gmailMessageId))
                        continue;

                    // Check if interaction already exists based on GmailMessageId
                    var existingInteraction = await context.Interactions
                        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(i => i.GmailMessageId == gmailMessageId);

                    // Check if interaction already exists based on Subject and Description
                    var existingInteractionBySubDesc = await context.Interactions
                        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(i => i.Subject == interactionData.Subject && i.Description == interactionData.Description);

                    if (existingInteraction != null)
                    {
                        // Update existing interaction - only update CreatedDate & Type fields
                        existingInteraction.CreatedDate = interactionData.CreatedDate;
                        existingInteraction.Type = interactionData.Type;
                    }
                    else if (existingInteractionBySubDesc != null)
                    {
                        //Update existing interaction
                        existingInteractionBySubDesc.CreatedDate = interactionData.CreatedDate;
                        existingInteractionBySubDesc.Type = interactionData.Type;
                        existingInteractionBySubDesc.GmailMessageId = gmailMessageId;
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // Add new interaction to context
                        context.Interactions.Add(interactionData);
                        newInteractionsCount++;
                    }
                }

                // Save all interactions at once
                await context.SaveChangesAsync();

                // Step 2: Process all junction table records in batch
                var interactionContactsToAdd = new List<InteractionContact>();
                var interactionPartnersToAdd = new List<InteractionPartner>();
                var interactionUsersToAdd = new List<InteractionUser>();
                var orgUnitRelationshipsToAdd = new List<OrganizationUnitRelationship>();

                foreach (var (gmailMessageId, _, contactIds, partnerErpValues, ownerEmails, orgCodes) in interactionsToProcess)
                {
                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(gmailMessageId))
                        continue;

                    // Get the interaction (now guaranteed to exist with an ID)
                    var interaction = await context.Interactions
                        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(i => i.GmailMessageId == gmailMessageId);

                    if (interaction == null)
                        continue;

                    // Track unique relationships to avoid duplicates
                    var uniqueContactIds = new HashSet<int>();
                    var uniquePartnerIds = new HashSet<int>();
                    var uniqueUserIds = new HashSet<int>();

                    // Process Contact relationships from Who.Id (ContactNumber)
                    foreach (var contactId in contactIds)
                    {
                        if (contactMapping.ContainsKey(contactId))
                        {
                            var dbContactId = contactMapping[contactId];
                            uniqueContactIds.Add(dbContactId);

                            // Also get the parent Partner for this Contact
                            if (contactPartnerMapping.ContainsKey(dbContactId))
                            {
                                var parentPartnerId = contactPartnerMapping[dbContactId];
                                uniquePartnerIds.Add(parentPartnerId);
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    // Process Partner relationships from What.AccountNumber (ErpDimValue)
                    foreach (var erpValue in partnerErpValues)
                    {
                        if (partnerMapping.ContainsKey(erpValue))
                        {
                            uniquePartnerIds.Add(partnerMapping[erpValue]);
                        }
                    }

                    // Process email addresses from interaction.EmailAddresses
                    if (interaction.EmailAddresses != null && interaction.EmailAddresses.Any())
                    {
                        foreach (var email in interaction.EmailAddresses)
                        {
                            var emailLower = email.ToLower();

                            // Find contacts by email
                            if (contactEmailMapping.ContainsKey(emailLower))
                            {
                                var dbContactId = contactEmailMapping[emailLower];
                                uniqueContactIds.Add(dbContactId);

                                // Also get the parent Partner for this Contact
                                if (contactPartnerMapping.ContainsKey(dbContactId))
                                {
                                    var parentPartnerId = contactPartnerMapping[dbContactId];
                                    uniquePartnerIds.Add(parentPartnerId);
                                }
                            }

                            // Find users by email
                            if (paoUserEmailMapping.ContainsKey(emailLower))
                            {
                                uniqueUserIds.Add(paoUserEmailMapping[emailLower]);
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    // Process Owner.Email for User relationships
                    foreach (var ownerEmail in ownerEmails)
                    {
                        var emailLower = ownerEmail.ToLower();
                        if (paoUserEmailMapping.ContainsKey(emailLower))
                        {
                            uniqueUserIds.Add(paoUserEmailMapping[emailLower]);
                        }
                    }

                    // Create InteractionContact records
                    foreach (var contactId in uniqueContactIds)
                    {
                        // Check if relationship already exists
                        var existingRelationship = await context.Set<InteractionContact>()
                            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(ic => ic.InteractionId == interaction.Id && ic.ContactId == contactId);

                        if (existingRelationship == null)
                        {
                            interactionContactsToAdd.Add(new InteractionContact
                            {
                                InteractionId = interaction.Id,
                                ContactId = contactId
                            });
                        }
                    }

                    // Create InteractionPartner records
                    foreach (var partnerId in uniquePartnerIds)
                    {
                        // Check if relationship already exists
                        var existingRelationship = await context.Set<InteractionPartner>()
                            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(ip => ip.InteractionId == interaction.Id && ip.PartnerId == partnerId);

                        if (existingRelationship == null)
                        {
                            interactionPartnersToAdd.Add(new InteractionPartner
                            {
                                InteractionId = interaction.Id,
                                PartnerId = partnerId
                            });
                        }
                    }

                    // Create InteractionUser records
                    foreach (var userId in uniqueUserIds)
                    {
                        // Check if relationship already exists
                        var existingRelationship = await context.Set<InteractionUser>()
                            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(iu => iu.InteractionId == interaction.Id && iu.UserId == userId);

                        if (existingRelationship == null)
                        {
                            interactionUsersToAdd.Add(new InteractionUser
                            {
                                InteractionId = interaction.Id,
                                UserId = userId
                            });
                        }
                    }

                    // Process OrganizationUnitRelationship from SF_Organisation__r.SF_EntityCode__c
                    foreach (var orgCode in orgCodes)
                    {
                        if (orgHierarchyMapping.ContainsKey(orgCode))
                        {
                            var orgHierarchyId = orgHierarchyMapping[orgCode];

                            // Check if relationship already exists
                            var existingRelationship = await context.OrganizationUnitRelationships
                                .FirstOrDefaultAsync(r => r.EntityType == nameof(Interaction) && 
                                                          r.EntityId == interaction.Id && 
                                                          r.OrganizationHierarchyId == orgHierarchyId);

                            if (existingRelationship == null)
                            {
                                orgUnitRelationshipsToAdd.Add(new OrganizationUnitRelationship
                                {
                                    OrganizationHierarchyId = orgHierarchyId,
                                    EntityId = interaction.Id,
                                    EntityType = nameof(Interaction),
                                    Name = $"Interaction-{interaction.Id}-{orgHierarchyId}",
                                    Status = EntityStatus.Active,
                                    CreatedBy = 0,
                                    CreatedDate = DateTime.UtcNow,
                                    LastModifiedBy = 0,
                                    LastModifiedDate = DateTime.UtcNow,
                                    IsDeleted = false
                                });
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // Add all junction table records at once
                if (interactionContactsToAdd.Any())
                    await context.Set<InteractionContact>().AddRangeAsync(interactionContactsToAdd);
                
                if (interactionPartnersToAdd.Any())
                    await context.Set<InteractionPartner>().AddRangeAsync(interactionPartnersToAdd);
                
                if (interactionUsersToAdd.Any())
                    await context.Set<InteractionUser>().AddRangeAsync(interactionUsersToAdd);
                
                if (orgUnitRelationshipsToAdd.Any())
                    await context.OrganizationUnitRelationships.AddRangeAsync(orgUnitRelationshipsToAdd);

                // Save all junction table records at once
                await context.SaveChangesAsync();

                // Commit transaction if everything succeeded
                await transaction.CommitAsync();

                Console.WriteLine($"Successfully seeded {interactionsToProcess.Count} interactions");
                Console.WriteLine($"Created {newInteractionsCount} new Interactions");
                Console.WriteLine($"Created {interactionContactsToAdd.Count} InteractionContact relationships");
                Console.WriteLine($"Created {interactionPartnersToAdd.Count} InteractionPartner relationships");
                Console.WriteLine($"Created {interactionUsersToAdd.Count} InteractionUser relationships");
                Console.WriteLine($"Created {orgUnitRelationshipsToAdd.Count} OrganizationUnitRelationship records");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // Rollback transaction if any error occurred
                await transaction.RollbackAsync();
                Console.WriteLine($"Error seeding interactions: {ex.Message}");
                throw;
            }
        }
    }
}